/src/plan.rs:27-118` — `PublishPlan` and `ReleaseEntry{package,tag_name,sha,changelog_section}` (with `skip_serializing_if`) match.\n- `crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:17` — `Package.changelog: Option&lt;PathBuf&gt;` confirmed; `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:148` confirmed as the cited co-usage.\n- `crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs:59-72,97-160` — `Diagnostic` fields and `DiagnosticCode` variant list (21 existing variants) match T6's insertion point and T10's hardcoded baseline set exactly.\n- Ran `cargo run -p callisto-cli -- schema --type tag|plan-publish|status` live and diffed the actual JSON against T10's hardcoded `required`/`properties`/`DiagnosticCode` sets — **all match byte-for-byte**, including the `oneOf`/`enum[0]` shape T10's extraction code assumes.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs` (full file read) — T3/T4's `old_string`s match the live file exactly, including exact indentation; the introduced `sha` binding is used consistently and compiles logically; `git` and `already_existed` remain in scope.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:427` and surrounding release-push block — T7's `old_string`/`implementation_2` match live code exactly; `diagnostics` vec is already threaded to the final `PublishPlan` construction (line 471).\n- `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml:85-98` — T1's `old_string` matches the live bug exactly (no exit-1 branch, exit-0 wrongly true, `exit $STATUS_EXIT` passthrough); the extracted run-body between `::group::`/`::endgroup::` references no external variables (`INPUT_CWD` etc. are outside the extracted range), so the bash-test mechanism is sound.\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs:19-21` — T2's `old_string` matches exactly.\n- Traced `plan_publish`'s `is_release`/`ver` derivation (publish.rs:152-181): an untagged, changeset-less package at workspace root is correctly treated as a release candidate at its current manifest version — confirmed by an existing, already-passing