- `crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs:27-118` — `PublishPlan` and `ReleaseEntry{package,tag_name,sha,changelog_section}` (with `skip_serializing_if`) match.\n- `crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:17` — `Package.changelog: Option&lt;PathBuf&gt;` confirmed; `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:148` confirmed as the cited co-usage.\n- `crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs:59-72,97-160` — `Diagnostic` fields and `DiagnosticCode` variant list (21 existing variants) match T6's insertion point and T10's hardcoded baseline set exactly.\n- Ran `cargo run -p callisto-cli -- schema --type tag|plan-publish|status` live and diffed the actual JSON against T10's hardcoded `required`/`properties`/`DiagnosticCode` sets — **all match byte-for-byte**, including the `oneOf`/`enum[0]` shape T10's extraction code assumes.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs` (full file read) — T3/T4's `old_string`s match the live file exactly, including exact indentation; the introduced `sha` binding is used consistently and compiles logically; `git` and `already_existed` remain in scope.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:427` and surrounding release-push block — T7's `old_string`/`implementation_2` match live code exactly; `diagnostics` vec is already threaded to the final `PublishPlan` construction (line 471).\n- `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml:85-98` — T1's `old_string` matches the live bug exactly (no exit-1 branch, exit-0 wrongly true, `exit $STATUS_EXIT` passthrough); the extracted run-body between `::group::`/`::endgroup::` references no external variables (`INPUT_CWD` etc. are outside the extracted range), so the bash-test mechanism is sound.\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs:19-21` — T2's `old_string` matches exactly.\n- Traced `plan_publish`'s `is_release`/`ver` derivation (publish.rs:152-181): an untagged, changeset-less package at workspace root is correctly treated as a release candidate at its current manifest version — confirmed by an existing, already-passing test (`plan_publish_populates_release_entry_via_command_runner_fallback_when_gix_unavailable`, publish_tests.rs:828-900) using the identical fixture shape T7 introduces. T7's fixture is constructible, not a repeat of the \"unconstructible fixture\" defect class.\n- T5, T8, T9's \"no red phase\" claims verified: T5 exercises only the AC-07/AC-08 branches T3/T4 already implement (tag-not-existing, idempotent match) with real git, not stubs — genuinely unchanged by the fix. T8/T9 verified `extract_section` (write.rs:131-136) already collapses empty-section and no-heading to `None` uniformly, and T7's helper already has a distinct `Err(e)` arm using the T6 variant — so both are legitimately non-red regression pins, not disguised new behavior.\n\nAll 16 spec acceptance criteria (AC-01, 02, 04, 05, 06, 06b, 06c, 06d, 07, 08, 10, 10b, 11, 12, 12c, 13) appear in exactly one task's `covers_criteria`; no orphans. Task ordering is dependency-correct (T6 before T7/T9, T3/T4 before T5, action-script/doc-comment/tag/changelog/schema-guard clusters are independent). No task leaves a crate in a broken compilation state — each task's edits are bundled and verified together before commit.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T7\",\n      \"type\": \"under-specified\",\n      \"description\": \"The new resolve_changelog_section doc comment in the implementation new_string contains a full-width comma '，' (U+FF0C) instead of ASCII ',' in 'ChangelogSectionNotFound for the first three (AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12），'. Harmless inside a /// comment (compiles fine) but is a stray non-ASCII character that should not ship in source.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Replace the full-width '，' with an ASCII ',' in the doc comment text before implementation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"pass\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Performed live-code verification (not just plan-internal review) of every symbol cited: CommandRunner/CommandOutput/CommandError, GraphError::Vcs, VcsError::RefNotFound, GitDataSource::resolve_commit signature, ApplyPermit::force_for_tests, CreatedTag/TagReport/ReleaseEntry/PublishPlan field names and skip_serializing_if placement, Package.changelog, Diagnostic fields, DiagnosticCode's full 21-variant baseline (confirmed byte-identical to T10's hardcoded set via `cargo run -- schema --type tag` diffed against actual live JSON output), tag.rs's exact current buggy lines (verified old_string matches char-for-char), publish.rs's exact hardcoded-None line and diagnostics-threading, action.yml's exact current branching bug, main.rs's exact doc comment, and the T7 fixture's constructibility (validated against an existing passing test using the identical shape). T1's bash-extraction mechanism was traced for external-variable leakage and found self-contained. T5/T8/T9's 'no red phase' claims were verified against the actual preceding implementation to confirm they are genuine regression pins, not disguised new behavior. Found zero blocking issues across all seven review dimensions; only one cosmetic non-ASCII character in a doc comment.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>137509</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>56</tool_uses><duration_ms>389390</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"0ad1febe-b1b6-464e-ae3d-63f34c9c4b0c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:47:34.262Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
