, as expected for this regression-proof task (no red phase per plan)\",\n    \"Ran full `cargo test -p callisto-graph`: all 8 tests in the file pass, 0 failures workspace-wide\",\n    \"Ran `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph -- --check`: found formatting diffs in the newly appended code, applied `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph`, re-checked clean\",\n    \"Ran `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\",\n    \"Re-ran full test suite after fmt to confirm still green\",\n    \"Staged and committed with the plan's exact commit message\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"5e02f0c9\",\n  \"concerns\": \"The plan's test fixture (plain `git tag &lt;name&gt; &lt;sha&gt;` in the pre-existing-tag test) initially failed in this environment due to the developer's global git config (tag.gpgsign=true), not due to any defect in the implementation under test. Fixed by adding repo-local `git config commit.gpgsign false` / `tag.gpgsign false` to init_git_repo so the fixture is hermetic. This is a test-fixture-only change; no assertions or scope were altered.\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-07\",\n      \"test_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 346,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 86\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-08\",\n      \"test_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 387,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 77\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"T5 is a pure regression-proof task per the plan: T3/T4 (already committed as 5166d601/3bcc91e2) implement the complete apply-path and dry-run-path logic in tag.rs lines 75-112. This task adds no implementation, only two new tests exercising the two cases the fix must leave unchanged (tag absent -&gt; AC-07; tag present at exactly release.sha -&gt; AC-08), using a real git repo fixture with a PanicRunner to prove the native gix path is used, not the CommandRunner shell fallback. Both new tests passed on first successful run (after fixing the unrelated git-config fixture issue), consistent with the plan's documented no-red-phase expectation. Full crate test suite, fmt --check, and clippy -D warnings all passed before commit.\"\n}\n```\n\nRelevant file: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>71386</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>30</tool_uses><duration_ms>439213</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"676ff658-9000-4828-94e7-1b7b2ae19b22","timestamp":"2026-08-19T22:11:21.734Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
