{"parentUuid":"25b7ec7d-6b11-4cd3-93c5-ddf3deae57d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCuSa6X9b4Gz8uGGEZSp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019J6WmZmBhtA7XvJyaV8pkm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement Track 4 T7","subagent_type":"lambda:implementer","prompt":"Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (Rust cargo workspace, moon-managed). Execute exactly task T7 from the plan at .claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json — read the plan from disk and pull T7's exact steps from there (test content, implementation old_string/new_string and implementation_2). T1-T6 are already committed (2e6f25c5, 442ceeb6, 5166d601, 3bcc91e2, 5e02f0c9, fa038214) — DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError now exists.\n\nWorkspace manifest (baseline green after T6, spec hash matches): { \"workspace_root\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\", \"language\": \"rust\", \"test_runner\": \"cargo test\", \"build_tool\": \"cargo\", \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json\" }\n\nT7 in one sentence: replace the hardcoded `changelog_section: None` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's plan_publish (around line 427, may have shifted slightly) with a new `resolve_changelog_section` helper function that reads the package's already-resolved `pkg.changelog: Option<PathBuf>` path (always Some by construction, per walk.rs), calls `callisto_changelog::extract_section`, and reports the two non-fatal outcomes this task covers (AC-10: found with content; AC-11: file doesn't exist) via a Warning-severity `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic — the helper also has match arms for the empty-section and unreadable-file cases (AC-10b/AC-12/AC-12c) that T8/T9 will separately test as pure regressions, since they're implemented in this same helper.\n\nThis is the plan's most substantial remaining task — verify EVERY symbol you use against live code before writing anything (Package.changelog's exact field, Diagnostic's exact field names and construction pattern used elsewhere in this file or nearby files, extract_section's exact signature in crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs, how `diagnostics` is threaded through plan_publish to the final PublishPlan construction). Read the plan's exact test content (crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs additions: write_release_candidate_pkg helper plus two new tests) and the plan's exact implementation content before writing anything — this spec/plan went through 5 exit-gate rounds specifically because of drift between what was assumed and what's actually in the code, so re-verify rather than trust.\n\nFollow RED (add the two tests, confirm they fail against the current hardcoded-None code) then GREEN (add the helper function, wire it into the release-push block). Before committing, run the FULL `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite (this touches publish.rs, a file with substantial existing coverage), `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph -- --check`, and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings`. If any existing test breaks, diagnose whether it's a genuine sibling-fixture gap (like T3 hit with tag.rs) or a real regression, and fix accordingly rather than reverting. Commit with the plan's exact commit message when everything is clean. Single, self-contained task — do not start T8 or T9."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":526076,"output_tokens":1382,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":51},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":526076