{"parentUuid":"395f84fc-f6ed-4f6b-900b-2f9dcc982c36","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeD64aGc1C9t85eu1Zf7c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QmAcLcikh2y3hWGGRjgW72","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix StatusReport field mismatches","subagent_type":"lambda:implementer","prompt":"Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (Rust cargo workspace, moon-managed). This is a Track 6-mechanical fix — lighter TDD loop tier (no formal spec/plan, this task IS the full scope), matching the established pattern in .claude/plans/ACTIVE.md for narrow, well-scoped correctness fixes. Do the work directly: red test → minimal fix → green → full suite → fmt → clippy → commit. Do not batch unrelated report types into this commit — this task is StatusReport/StatusPackageRecord ONLY.\n\nContext: an earlier research pass found StatusReport/StatusPackageRecord (crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs, roughly lines 298-336) has field-shape mismatches against the documented wire contract in docs/01-spec.md §M.12.4 area (search for \"StatusReport\" and \"StatusEntry\"/\"StatusPackageRecord\" in that doc). Reported findings (RE-VERIFY every one against live code and the live doc before acting — this research is from earlier in a long session and code may have drifted):\n1. `has_changesets: bool` — the doc mandates this field (used by the Action's mode dispatch), but the current struct is missing it entirely.\n2. The doc's package-record type is missing from the current struct: `last_released_version: Option<Version>` and `release_trigger: ReleaseTrigger` fields the doc documents but the code doesn't have.\n3. `changed_since_last_tag: bool` — doc says this is mandatory/always-serialized; current code has `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"std::ops::Not::not\")]`, which omits the field from JSON when false, contradicting \"always present.\"\n4. Code may have an extra field not in the doc: `pending_changesets: 