{"parentUuid":"062beae5-0869-4cef-a0ee-5ab7b040ead4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEVyHTUf4QV8qkSnmG2Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed both findings are still live. Track 5 has three real components, and the scale differs a lot depending on how much you take on:\n\n1. **`pr_body.rs` hand-rolls Markdown instead of calling `callisto_changelog::render_section`** — a real consolidation, moderate risk (touches PR-body output format).\n2. **`ChangeSource::Commit`/`ChangeSource::NewGroupMember` are matched but never constructed** — meaning inference-driven bumps and fixed-group new-member joins never actually produce a changelog entry citing their real cause today. This is a genuine gap, not just a code-tidiness issue.\n3. **`ChangelogInput.entries` silently drops all but one cause when a package has multiple contributing changes in one run** (changeset + cascade + peer-escalation) — a real data-loss bug in changelog accuracy.\n\nGiven how Track 4 and Track 9 both went (multiple rounds of adversarial review each), a full canon pipeline for this — as the master plan originally tiered it — is a real time commitment, not a quick pass like the Track 6 fixes."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":662186,"output_tokens":1200,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":362},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":662186,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEVyC5mXpUJvEJu5DjcV","ty