let Some(mut agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs.get(id).cloned()`) is a hard if/else against the non-changeset synthesis branch (lines 156-195) -- when a changeset entry exists, the synthesis branch never runs at all, silently dropping any real non-changeset cause for the same package in the same run. Fix scope: append a second synthesized ChangelogEntry to agg_input.entries when both a changeset-sourced entry AND a genuine outcome.reasons value exist for the same package -- outcome.reasons remains readable inside the changeset branch since it's a separate map from agg.changelog_inputs.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- when a package's bump has no changeset AND no synthesizable reason in outcome.reasons (e.g. a bump whose cause genuinely can't be attributed), ChangelogInput.entries for that package must not panic, error the whole command, or silently omit the package from the changelog entirely -- the existing fallback behavior for this case (verify what it currently is) must be preserved.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- render_section (already implemented) returns Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput) when given a ChangelogInput with zero entries; pr_body.rs's new integration with render_section must handle this without crashing the whole PR-body composition for one package's empty-entries edge case (verify whether this case is actually reachable given done_when's other criteria, and handle it gracefully either way).\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"A FULL multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package (e.g. two independent cascade paths, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, contributing to the same package in the same run) -- outcome.reasons/agg.reasons are single-valued (BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason>, not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>) all the way up through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. Fixing this fully would require changing that data model throughout cascade.rs -- a genuinely separate, larger 