the collapsible '#### Release Reason' block inside each package's `<details>` (pr_body.rs:175-218) is replaced with reused ChangelogInput + render_section output.\",\n    \"Constructing BumpReason::NewGroupMember (or any new BumpReason variant) is not required by this spec -- the NewGroupMember gap can be closed by directly constructing ChangeSource::NewGroupMember in version.rs's changelog-entry synthesis without necessarily threading a corresponding BumpReason through outcome.reasons; the implementer may choose either path as long as AC-004's observable behavior holds.\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-001\", \"criterion\": \"For every bump in VersionPlan.bumps whose package has a matching entry `w` in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (i.e. some `w` where `w.input.package == bump.package`), the '#### Release Reason' block inside that package's `<details>` element in ComposePrBodyReport.body contains, verbatim, the exact string returned by `callisto_changelog::render_section(&w.input)` (including render_section's own '## <version>' or '## Unreleased' heading line) -- not a hand-matched reconstruction. After this change, crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs contains no `match` arm on `BumpReason::Cascade`, `BumpReason::PeerEscalation`, `BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion`, or `BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion` that independently builds descriptive Markdown text (the block previously at pr_body.rs:184-216 is deleted, not duplicated) -- verified by `grep -c 'BumpReason::Cascade\\\\|BumpReason::PeerEscalation\\\\|BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion\\\\|BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` returning 0. Test method: a new unit test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and one matching ChangelogWrite (built the same way version.rs builds it, with a real ChangeSource::Changeset entry), calls `render_pr_body_from_plan`, independently calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` on the same ChangelogInput in the test body, and asserts `report.body.contains(&expected_section)` where `expected_section` is that independently-computed render_section output.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-002\", \"criterion\": \"For a bump whose package has no entry in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (the package declares no changelog file, i.e. `pkg.changelog` is `None` in the versioning pipeline, so version.rs's changelog-write loop at ~lines 148-215 never runs for it), that package's `<details>` block in ComposePrBodyReport.body still contains a non-empty '#### Release Reason' section (the pre-existing per-BumpReason descriptive text is preserved for this case) -- render_pr_body_from_plan does not error, panic, or emit an empty '#### Release Reason' heading with no following text for such a package. Test method: unit test in pr_body.rs constructing a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` and an empty `changelog_writes` Vec (simulating no changelog file for that package); assert `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and `report.body` contains '#### Release Reason' followed by non-whitespace content before the next `</details>`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-003\", \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run is driven by `BumpReason::Inference` (i.e. `outcome.reasons.get(id) == Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`) and the `InferenceOutcome` returned by the `SeverityInference` implementation for that package has a non-empty `commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)>`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in the resulting `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject }` entry where `sha` and `subject` equal `commits[0]`'s `CommitSha` and `String` respectively -- `commits[0]` because `callisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs:141-174, and the native gix path it documents itself as matching field-for-field) shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag, which is git's default newest-first order, so index 0 is the most recent commit. This choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site explaining why index 0 (not the last index) was chosen. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangeSource::Commit` entry with `sha == sha_recent` and `subject == \\\"feat: recent\\\"` (not `sha_older`).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-004\", \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`), the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` entry where `group` equals that `GroupName` key. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member, drives a bump for the fresh member (e.g. via a changeset or the group's fixed-union bump), calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` contains `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: <the fixed group's GroupName> }`.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-005\", \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains: (a) every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, followed by (b) exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. Total `entries.len()` equals the changeset-only entry count plus 1. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run (both `agg.changelog_inputs` and `outcome.reasons` populated for the same package ID), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-006\", \"criterion\": \"When a package has a bump this run (severity > None), `pkg.changelog` is `Some`, `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `None` (no changeset), AND `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is either `None` or a variant with no direct `ChangeSource` mapping (falls to the catch-all currently at version.rs:188-199), `plan_version` does not panic and does not return `Err` attributable to this condition -- `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains exactly one `ChangelogWrite` for that package whose `input.entries.len() >= 1`, preserving the existing fallback: a single `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Version bump ({})\\\", <severity as major|minor|patch|none>) }` entry. Test method: integration test in version.rs's test module constructs a fixture package with a bump whose `reason` is `None` and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, asserts it returns `Ok`, and asserts the package's `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` has exactly 1 entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary` starts with `\\\"Version bump (\\\"`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-007\", \"criterion\": \"render_pr_body_from_plan's call to `callisto_changelog::render_section` for a given package never causes the overall `compose_pr_body`/`render_pr_body_from_plan` call to panic or return `Err` because that one package's `ChangelogInput.entries` was empty (which would make `render_section` return `Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput)`) -- on such an error for one package, that package's `<details>` block still renders (falling back to the AC-002 pre-existing per-BumpReason text, or if no `reason` is available either, a literal fallback line `_No changelog entries available._`) and every other package's block in the same PR body renders normally and completely. Note: this scenario is confirmed unreachable through the normal `plan_version` -> `pr_body` pipeline as of AC-006 (changelog_writes entries are never empty), so this criterion is tested by calling `render_pr_body_from_plan`'s per-package rendering path directly with a hand-constructed `VersionPlan` whose matching `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` is an empty `Vec` (bypassing `plan_version`), and asserting the call returns `Ok` with a body containing both the fallback text for that package and the normally-rendered block for a second, unaffected package in the same plan.\", \"is_error_case\": true}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\"\n}\n\nReturn the challenger's standard JSON output (issues array with criterion_id/type/description/suggested_fix per issue, plus overall pass/fail).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/ae6100ae9691448b1.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60b24856-dab8-45a1-8871-c59657fd9470","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
