{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:29:48.500Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af8e282e18727300a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01EvVMx7qZ3Sci5aYgGtn5hH</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/af8e282e18727300a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate Track 5 spec round 3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Verdict: **FAIL** (confidence: high, retry_count 2)\n\nVerdict file: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/verdict-track5-r3.json` (validates against `verdict@1`; summary 288/300 chars).\n\n### Round-2 fixes: 4 of 5 hold\n\nI re-derived every type and citation from live code rather than trusting the spec or your summary.\n\n- **Fix 1 (AC-001/AC-002)** — holds. AC-001 is now a dispatch-priority claim, consistent with `non_goals` items 6/11/14. I also confirmed the negative assertion is genuinely discriminating: `\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\"` occurs only at `pr_body.rs:191`; the Executive Summary's Cascade arm emits `\"Cascade from \\`X\\`\"`, so it can't false-positive off the table.\n- **Fix 2 (AC-004/AC-005 arithmetic)** — the arithmetic holds. Your requested trace (matching ChangelogWrite + changeset + cascade + new group member) resolves unambiguously to `[Changeset, DependencyUpdate, NewGroupMember]`. AC-005's fixture is constructible: `cascade.rs:501` `raise` returns early unless `sev &gt; cur_sev`, so a Patch changeset plus a Minor cascade does yield `reason == Cascade` with `changelog_inputs` still `Some`.\n- **Fix 3 (AC-003 empty commits)** — **incomplete.** See below.\n- **Fix 4 (`pkg.changelog` precondition)** — holds, matches the `version.rs:148` gate.\n- **Fix 5 (AC-007 any-Err)** — holds. `ChangelogError` has exactly 4 variants; only `EmptyInput` (`render.rs:6`) and `SeverityNoneEntry` (`group.rs:19`, via `group_entries`) are reachable from `render_section`. AC-007's unreachability note is also true: `version.rs:106` skips `Severity::None` and `aggregate.rs:309` gates on `severity != None`.\n\n### Blocker 1 — AC-003 (primary)\n\nRound 2's fix moved the defect rather than eliminating it. I enumerated the full state table `changelog_inputs {Some,None} × reason {9 variants}`. AC-005 requires `changelog_inputs` is `Some`; AC-006 requires `None`. **AC-003 constrains neither** — and `{Some, Inference}` is reachable:\n\n`aggregate.rs` runs the inference loop *first* (223-236), setting `reasons[P] = Inference`. The later changeset loop overwrites the reason only when `entry.severity &gt; cur_sev` (:297) but pushes into `changelog_inputs` whenever `entry.severity != None` (:309). So a package with inferred Major + Patch changeset keeps `reason == Inference` **and** owns a changeset entry.\n\nIn that cell, `version.rs:149` takes the `agg_input` branch, AC-005 excludes Inference from its four enumerated reasons, AC-006 is excluded by `changelog_inputs == Some` — yet AC-003 still literally demands a `Commit` entry, saying nothing about whether the changeset entries survive. AC-003's own test fixture says \"no pending changeset\", so neither reading is tested, and the natural implementation (Commit only in the else branch) silently violates the criterion.\n\nSecondary, same criterion: AC-003 says only \"contains\" and pins no count. AC-005 pins exactly N+1, AC-006 pins exactly 1 — AC-003 is the only synthesis criterion left unpinned, so leaving the catch-all `\"Version bump (major)\"` entry in place *and* appending `Commit` passes both mandated tests while emitting a junk changelog line.\n\nThree required changes are spelled out in the blocker: add `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id) is None` to the precondition, pin both clauses to `entries.len() == 1`, and add `Inference` to AC-005's reason list with its explicit `ChangeSource` mapping plus a fourth test case.\n\n### Blocker 2 — AC-004 (test-method rationale)\n\nThe parenthetical \"so AC-005's changeset-sourced entry also applies\" is **false**. In that fixture the fresh member's reason is `BumpReason::Changeset`; `union_fixed` does not overwrite it because `aggregate.rs:421` only reassigns when `target &gt; cur`, and the fresh member is what set `target`. The changeset entry arrives via `version.rs:149`'s pre-existing branch, not AC-005 — so the fixture never exercises additive ordering against any spec-added entry, which is exactly what the parenthetical claims it proves. The length-free assertion lets both the described and a corrected fixture pass, leaving vector:planner free to build either. Fix: correct the mechanism, pin `entries.len() == 2`, and add a second case with a cascade strictly exceeding the changeset severity (required by `cascade.rs:501`) asserting the 3-entry ordering.\n\n### Non-blocking notes\n- `group_check` call spans `version.rs:87-94`, spec says 87-93 (closing paren). Trivial.\n- Spec conforms to `spec@1`; no TBD/TODO/vague-language tokens; three `is_error_case: true` criteria; scope is one planning cycle, so no split blocker.\n\n`retry_count` is 2, which does not exceed 3 — this is a fail, not an escalate. **The next submission is the last automated round.**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>92325</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>458179</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
