uired changes are spelled out in the blocker: add `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id) is None` to the precondition, pin both clauses to `entries.len() == 1`, and add `Inference` to AC-005's reason list with its explicit `ChangeSource` mapping plus a fourth test case.\n\n### Blocker 2 — AC-004 (test-method rationale)\n\nThe parenthetical \"so AC-005's changeset-sourced entry also applies\" is **false**. In that fixture the fresh member's reason is `BumpReason::Changeset`; `union_fixed` does not overwrite it because `aggregate.rs:421` only reassigns when `target &gt; cur`, and the fresh member is what set `target`. The changeset entry arrives via `version.rs:149`'s pre-existing branch, not AC-005 — so the fixture never exercises additive ordering against any spec-added entry, which is exactly what the parenthetical claims it proves. The length-free assertion lets both the described and a corrected fixture pass, leaving vector:planner free to build either. Fix: correct the mechanism, pin `entries.len() == 2`, and add a second case with a cascade strictly exceeding the changeset severity (required by `cascade.rs:501`) asserting the 3-entry ordering.\n\n### Non-blocking notes\n- `group_check` call spans `version.rs:87-94`, spec says 87-93 (closing paren). Trivial.\n- Spec conforms to `spec@1`; no TBD/TODO/vague-language tokens; three `is_error_case: true` criteria; scope is one planning cycle, so no split blocker.\n\n`retry_count` is 2, which does not exceed 3 — this is a fail, not an escalate. **The next submission is the last automated round.**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>92325</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>458179</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"9ddd4a68-7b1a-4aa2-9c81-d56dfb349ebc","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:29:48.522Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1