allisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag -- git's default newest-first order -- so index 0 is the most recent commit; this choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site), AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used to construct the corresponding `PlannedBump`). If instead `commits` is empty (a state `InferenceOutcome`'s type does not itself prevent, even though `commit_count` is nonzero), the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Inferred version bump ({} commit(s))\\\", commit_count) }` and `severity` equal to the resolved bump severity -- mirroring AC-006's fallback pattern rather than leaving this state unhandled. Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with `pkg.changelog` set and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Commit { sha: sha_recent, subject: \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string() }` (not `sha_older`) and `severity == Severity::Minor`. (2) same fixture but `InferenceOutcome { commit_count: 2, commits: vec![], .. }` (empty commits, nonzero count), asserting the entry instead matches `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary == \\\"Inferred version bump (2 commit(s))\\\"`.\",","+      \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run has `pkg.changelog` 