{"parentUuid":"c980ef07-59de-480a-91b4-d64c0a752dd6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f9228b9f-6b1d-4089-9cd1-4a252f727cbb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019W9Znuc2Qurr7dS9MRrzsy","type":"tool_result","content":"34:      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`) AND `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains, as its LAST entry (appended after any entries AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 already contributed for the same package -- this criterion is always additive, never a replacement, since GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map and is not subject to AC-005's non_goals limitation), a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset with no other reason for the same package this run (so `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `None` or a Changeset-derived reason with no AC-005 mapping, and AC-005 does not independently contribute a second entry), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `entries.len() == 2`: the changeset entry first (arriving via the pre-existing `agg.changelog_inputs` branch at version.rs:149, NOT via AC-005, since AC-005 requires a genuine non-changeset `outcome.reasons` value which this fixture does not have), and the `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember` entry last. (2) same fixture, but the fresh member is ALSO a cascade target this run with a cascade-driven severity strictly greater than the changeset's own severity (satisfying cascade.rs:501's `target > cur_sev` gate so the cascade path actually fires and `outcome.reasons.get(id)` becomes `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` without being overwritten back), exercising AC-005's additive entry too; asserts `entries.len() == 3` in order: `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}`, `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (AC-005's Cascade mapping), `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember{..}` (this criterion, appended last).\",","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2b9e9053-2156-42b6-92be-0a4ceb98e239","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:30:58.407Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"34:      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`) AND `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains, as its LAST entry (appended after any entries AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 already contributed for the same package -- this criterion is always additive, never a replacement, since GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map and is not subject to AC-005's non_goals limitation), a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset with no other reason for the same package this run (so `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `None` or a Changeset-derived reason with no AC-005 mapping, and AC-005 does not independently contribute a second entry), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `entries.len() == 2`: the changeset entry first (arriving via the pre-existing `agg.changelog_inputs` branch at version.rs:149, NOT via AC-005, since AC-005 requires a genuine non-changeset `outcome.reasons` value which this fixture does not have), and the `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember` entry last. (2) same fixture, but the fresh member is ALSO a cascade target this run with a cascade-driven severity strictly greater than the changeset's own severity (satisfying cascade.rs:501's `target > cur_sev` gate so the cascade path actually fires and `outcome.reasons.get(id)` becomes `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` without being overwritten back), exercising AC-005's additive entry too; asserts `entries.len() == 3` in order: `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}`, `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (AC-005's Cascade mapping), `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember{..}` (this criterion, appended last).\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c980ef07-59de-480a-91b4-d64c0a752dd6","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
