{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:34:07.270Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad0e75777a0429e9b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WKWrFR47Rem3ivKsG62wSW</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/ad0e75777a0429e9b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Challenge Track 5 implementation plan\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Confirmed correct. This completes my adversarial verification. All type/field/method usages, scope, ordering, and error-handling paths check out against the live codebase. Final verdict below.\n\n## Review Summary\n\nI read both files from disk and cross-verified every claimed Rust symbol against the live source (`crates/callisto-graph/src/{aggregate,cascade,groups,infer}.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/{version,pr_body}.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs`, `crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs`, `crates/callisto-model/src/{report.rs,identity.rs}`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/{raw,resolve}.rs`).\n\nFindings: `BumpReason` (8 variants incl. `Inference{commits:usize,remapped:bool}`), `ChangeSource` (7 variants incl. `Commit{sha,subject}`, `NewGroupMember{group}`), `Aggregation`/`CascadeOutcome`/`GroupCheckOutcome`/`InferenceOutcome`/`VersionPlan`/`PlannedBump`/`ChangelogWrite`/`GroupName` all match the plan's literal constructions field-for-field. The insertion point in `version.rs`'s `for (id, &amp;sev) in &amp;outcome.severities` loop confirms `group_check`, `outcome`, `agg`, `sev`, `id`, `to`, `from` are all genuinely in scope where T3/T4/T5 insert code. `pr_body.rs`'s real fallback match (line 176) matches T6/T7/T8's cited insertion points exactly, and T8's replacement code is an unambiguous literal swap of T7's block. The `[cascade] bump-severity` TOML key and fixed-group convergence math in `cascade.rs`/`groups.rs` (aligned_base from the released member, not the fresh member) confirm the T4/T5 fixture reasoning about when the convergence overwrite branch does/doesn't fire. Test helper imports (`git_init_with_commit`, `commit_all`, `tag`, `IgnoreWalkLocator`, `NoInference`, and `callisto_fixtures::git::{init_repo,run_git}` for T2) all exist exactly as referenced. All 7 acceptance criteria (AC-001 through AC-007) appear in exactly one task's `covers_criteria`; none orphaned.\n\nThe only defect found is a minor process risk, not a correctness bug:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T1\",\n      \"type\": \"under-specified\",\n      \"description\": \"T1's own reasoning and expected_failure text acknowledge the AC-006 test passes with zero production-code changes (the existing catch-all already satisfies it). lambda:implementer's protocol treats a test that passes before implementation as a signal of a broken test and stops. The task relies on the implementer reading the reasoning field to understand this is an intentional regression-pin, but there is no explicit directive telling the implementer to proceed past that stop condition.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Add an explicit field or a leading sentence in test_first.description such as: 'This test is expected to pass immediately with no implementation change — this is intentional (a regression pin for T4's later refactor of this same match), not a broken test; proceed to commit without adding implementation code.'\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"pass\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Deep verification against live source for all four requested checks: (1) every referenced type/field/variant/signature in the plan's hand-constructed test literals matches the real struct/enum definitions exactly (BumpReason, ChangeSource, Aggregation, CascadeOutcome, GroupCheckOutcome, InferenceOutcome, VersionPlan, PlannedBump, ChangelogWrite, GroupName, SeverityInference trait). (2) Traced cascade.rs's fixed-group convergence block (lines ~416-442) and groups.rs's fixed_group_target: aligned_base is computed from the released member's base version, and when both group members share an identical base version, the independently-computed member target equals the group-wide winner, so the overwrite condition `out.targets.get(&amp;id) != Some(&amp;winner)` is false for the fresh member and its reason survives -- confirms T4/T5's fixture claims and entries.len()/ChangeSource-sequence assertions hold. (3) Confirmed group_check/outcome/agg/sev/id/to/from are all live identifiers in scope at version.rs's insertion point via direct read of the real function body -- no wrong-scope compile risk. (4) T7's dispatch and T8's fallback restructuring compose unambiguously: T8 explicitly quotes and replaces T7's exact inner block, leaving a single deterministic final code shape. Only issue found is a minor TDD-process risk on T1 (immediately-green test conflicting with lambda:implementer's red-phase heuristic), which is non-blocking since it's explainable from the task's own reasoning field and does not affect correctness of the resulting code.\"\n}\n```\n\nGiven this is presumably a first review pass and the single issue found is advisory (not a missing/wrong-order/missing-error-handling/orphaned-criteria defect), overall verdict is **pass**. Relevant files: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/plan-track5-draft.json`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION.json`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>110395</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>210650</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
