{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:17:48.299Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a43673d042893a83e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LT5t6zhSFQD3C9MQQEEB8y</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a43673d042893a83e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit locate/ dir diff for regressions\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All lines already accounted for (moved inside the new membership `if` gates, verified in the earlier diff view). No other deletions in ignore_walk.rs beyond what I've already traced. My scope is done.\n\n## Report\n\n**Directive:** Audit locate/ignore_walk.rs, locate/membership.rs, locate/git.rs, locate/mod.rs, locate/root.rs for deleted invariants without a re-established replacement.\n\nFindings (JSON):\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"The entire `locate/git.rs` module (function `probe_git`) was deleted, and `mod.rs` no longer declares `pub mod git;` or `pub use git::probe_git;`. `probe_git` was the single call site that invoked `check_git_version` (still defined and unit-tested in callisto-model/src/exec.rs:153) against a real `git --version` output.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"docs/01-spec.md (current branch, still present) documents §G.2.4 `probe_git` as mandatory architecture: 'Git capability probing ... called once per invocation before the first real git call, producing CommandError::IncompatibleVersion identically on either surface' (lines 9099, 10338, 5824-5831). Grepping the whole crates/ tree for `IncompatibleVersion` and `check_git_version(` shows zero call sites outside callisto-model's own definition/tests — nothing in the shipped binary ever invokes this check anymore. A user running callisto against a too-old git (e.g. pre-2.20, per the check_git_version floor tests) will no longer get the documented early, clear `CommandError::IncompatibleVersion` failure; instead they'll hit whatever confusing lower-level git-invocation failure (or silent wrong behavior) occurs downstream, with no version gate at all. This is a removed guard with no replacement — confirmed by cross-checking both the deleted file and the still-standing spec text that assumes it exists.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nEverything else in these 5 files checks out: `dunce::canonicalize` swap (ignore_walk.rs:24, root.rs:5) is a benign Windows-path-formatting change, not a containment/symlink regression; the `PackageId::parse`/`ProjectRoot` push blocks that appear deleted in the diff are simply moved verbatim inside the new `cargo_membership.admits(...)` / `npm_membership.admits(...)` guards, not dropped. `membership.rs` is new code (no prior membership filtering existed), so it adds restrictions rather than removing any — its fallback rules (malformed glob/TOML/YAML → admit-all or exclude-nothing) are consistently the \"fail open\" direction and are exercised by its own test suite, so no silent-narrowing bug found there.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>78956</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>12</tool_uses><duration_ms>63375</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
