{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:18:37.157Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae12458d5fbd754e6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01ABbNY2piKrLRGuF7a2gZBA</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/ae12458d5fbd754e6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit walk.rs and matrix.rs diff for regressions\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings assembled. Reporting to parent.\n\n**walk-matrix-audit report**\n\nScope: walk.rs, matrix.rs, tags.rs, infer.rs, plan.rs, error.rs + matrix_tests.rs/tags_tests.rs/walk_comment_grep_test.rs/cascade_tests.rs.\n\nTraced every `-` line in these files. Result: **no unrefuted regressions found**. All deletions are refactors with the invariant re-established elsewhere and covered by tests:\n\n- `error.rs`: `ConfigError::ParseYaml` variant deleted, diagnostic codes E117→ shuffled to E113. Checked: `ParseYaml` was already unused in `config/resolve.rs` on `origin/main` (dead code removal, not a dropped path). Code renumbering has no collision (only one `E113` occurrence). Not a regression.\n- `matrix.rs`: `read_napi_targets`/`read_maturin_targets`/`read_engines_node`/`read_requires_python` were split into `parse_*` (does the I/O + existence check) + `read_*` (pure extraction from an already-parsed `Value`), so `build_matrix_report` parses each manifest once instead of twice. Same error returns (`ManifestError::Read`/`Parse`) preserved verbatim in the new `parse_*` functions; all deleted test call sites have equivalent tests still present and passing against the new two-arg signatures. Also added a new `DuplicatePlatformTriple` diagnostic (additive, not a removal).\n- `tags.rs`: `fetch_all_tags`/`TagIndex::build` changed from taking `(runner, root)` and discovering `GitAccess` internally, to taking a caller-supplied `&amp;GitAccess` — pure dependency-injection refactor (avoids double discovery), same fallback error path (`VcsError::Command`) still tested.\n- `infer.rs`: `CommitInference` changed from owning `(runner, root)` and discovering `GitAccess` itself, to receiving the caller's `&amp;GitAccess` per call — same pattern as tags.rs, no behavior change to `infer_severity` call.\n- `plan.rs`: purely additive (`PlatformWrite.from` field + test).\n- `walk.rs`: the one substantive behavior change is that a duplicate `primary_id` insert into `package_manifest_decls` no longer unconditionally errors (old: `-return Err(GraphError::DuplicatePackage{...})` at the old single call site) — it now only errors when the two paths' \"claiming ecosystem\" sets are **not disjoint** (`walk.rs:159`, `walk.rs:243`, gated by `claiming_sets_disjoint` at `walk.rs:49`), otherwise it promotes both to `PackageId::Prefixed` (identity-promotion feature, `SPEC-TRACK3B1-IDENTITY-PROMOTION-CORE`). This is a real narrowing of the old duplicate-package guard, but it's the PR's stated feature (multi-ecosystem same-name packages), and it's exercised by dedicated tests (`ac16a_*`, `ac03_fixed_group_member_naming_absent_ecosystem_is_missing_group_member`, and a same-ecosystem-conflict test hitting `walk.rs:159`/`243` directly) — I could not construct a scenario where a genuine same-ecosystem duplicate now silently passes. Not filing as a finding; flagging only for awareness since it's the highest-blast-radius change in this file set.\n\nNo candidate findings to escalate from this file set.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>95786</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>22</tool_uses><duration_ms>105199</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
