ce.\n\n**Rule 4 (Layer Isolation)**: `callisto-model/Cargo.toml` and `callisto-format/Cargo.toml` diffs only add `path-slash`, `schemars`, `proptest`, `serial_test`, `tempfile` (all MIT/Apache-2.0), no license changes (both remain `MIT OR Apache-2.0`). `callisto-manifests/Cargo.toml` gained `serial_test.workspace = true` etc., but `callisto-manifests` itself is licensed `AGPL-3.0-only` (per its own Cargo.toml and reaffirmed in the `ARCHITECTURE.md` diff, which explicitly clarifies it is not part of the protected \"must stay MIT/Apache-2.0, never depend on AGPL\" set) — it is not a Layer 1 crate under the enforced invariant, so this is not a violation.\n\n**Rule 5 (No Emojis in Documentation)**: Scanned all added lines in `docs/00-design.md`, `docs/01-spec.md`, `docs/release-paradigms.md`, `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Found only arrows (→, ↳) and a single ✓ checkmark in a comparison table (`ARCHITECTURE.md` line \"commands::matrix ... | ✓ |\") — standard technical/table notation, not emoji in the sense the rule targets (no colorful pictographs like 🎉/✅/🚀 anywhere).\n\n**Conclusion**: No clear CLAUDE.md violation found in this diff.\n\n```json\n[]\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>79343</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>135739</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
