forms); no caller matches on the old specific variant.\n- `IdentityIndex::resolve_native_with_fallback` lost a `1 =&gt; Some(...)` arm (now always warns + returns `None` on any cross-ecosystem miss, even unambiguous single-candidate). Initially looked like a real finding (feeds `DepEdge` construction in `walk.rs:540`, so it affects cascade-graph edges), but it's a deliberate, tested tightening from commit `de83f6f5` (T13a) with an explicit end-to-end regression test (T13b) — not an accidental deletion.\n- `error.rs`: removed unused `ConfigError::ParseYaml` (dead code, no callers) and fixed a duplicate `E117` diagnostic code collision by renumbering one to `E113` — a bug fix, not a regression.\n\nNo candidate findings to report from this scope.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>101379</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>150789</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:19:43.694Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3a777b0a05379de3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01D61gd8hZGhnP8S2JUeJak2</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a3a777b0a05379de3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review graph core diff for cleanup\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've reviewed the graph-core diff (version.rs, config/*, identity.rs, matrix.rs, tags.rs, infer.rs, plan.rs, error.rs, lib.rs). Most changes are legitimate fixes (e.g. matrix.rs and tags.rs already implement the exact efficiency improvements the audit would otherwise flag). Found 4 real issues in the newly added `plan_version` platform-write logic and `Workspace::load`:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 314,\n    \"summary\": \"plan_version re-derives cargo_workspace/npm_workspace_kind/OpenContext from scratch (Cargo.toml exists check, WorkspaceCargoResolver::load, detect_npm_workspace_kind) instead of reusing a shared discovery helper.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The identical ~15-line OpenContext-construction block already exists in walk.rs:101, apply.rs:132, and lib.rs:198. A 4th independent copy means any future fix to workspace-inheritance detection (e.g. a new npm workspace kind) must be patched in four places; missing one silently reintroduces stale behavior in just this command.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 351,\n    \"summary\": \"Platform-manifest and owner-manifest handles are opened via the raw callisto_manifests::open() call instead of Workspace's existing manifest_cache (manifest_cache::open_cached, already used by Workspace::base_versions in lib.rs:209).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Bypasses the per-command-run manifest cache lib.rs's own doc comment says exists precisely so 'a given manifest is opened at most once per command run' -- any manifest already opened by base_versions is now read and parsed a second time here.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 367,\n    \"summary\": \"Inside the per-platform-member loop, the owner's canonical manifest is opened and parsed fresh for every platform sibling that owner has.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"For an owner with N platform-manifest siblings (exercised by the new test plan_version_merges_two_platform_siblings_optional_dep_updates_into_one_entry), the same owner package.json/Cargo.toml is read from disk and re-parsed N times in one plan_version call instead of once, hoisted out of the loop.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs\",\n    \"line\": 132,\n    \"summary\": \"Workspace now stores `pub identity: IdentityIndex` as a full clone of graph.identity(), just so version.rs can pass `identity: &amp;ws.identity` into CascadeInput.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Duplicates data already reachable via `ws.graph.identity()` (used everywhere else, e.g. walk.rs:1233/1350) -- every Workspace::load now pays to clone the entire IdentityIndex (bare/native/prefixed/platform BTreeMaps) instead of passing the existing reference through.\"\n  }\n]\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>117652</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>22</tool_uses><duration_ms>147345</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:19:43.702Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3a777b0a05379de3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01D61gd8hZGhnP8S2JUeJak2</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a3a777b0a05379de3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review graph core diff for cleanup\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've reviewed the graph-core diff (version.rs, config/*, identity.rs, matrix.rs, tags.rs, infer.rs, plan.rs, error.rs, lib.rs). Most changes are legitimate fixes (e.g. matrix.rs and tags.rs already implement the exact efficiency improvements the audit would otherwise flag). Found 4 real issues in the newly added `plan_version` platform-write logic and `Workspace::load`:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 314,\n    \"summary\": \"plan_version re-derives cargo_workspace/npm_workspace_kind/OpenContext from scratch (Cargo.toml exists check, WorkspaceCargoResolver::load, detect_npm_workspace_kind) instead of reusing a shared discovery helper.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The identical ~15-line OpenContext-construction block already exists in walk.rs:101, apply.rs:132, and lib.rs:198. A 4th independent copy means any future fix to workspace-inheritance detection (e.g. a new npm workspace kind) must be patched in four places; missing one silently reintroduces stale behavior in just this command.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 351,\n    \"summary\": \"Platform-manifest and owner-manifest handles are opened via the raw callisto_manifests::open() call instead of Workspace's existing manifest_cache (manifest_cache::open_cached, already used by Workspace::base_versions in lib.rs:209).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Bypasses the per-command-run manifest cache lib.rs's own doc comment says exists precisely so 'a given manifest is opened at most once per command run' -- any manifest already opened by base_versions is now read and parsed a second time here.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 367,\n    \"summary\": \"Inside the per-platform-member loop, the owner's canonical manifest is opened and parsed fresh for every platform sibling that owner has.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"For an owner with N platform-manifest siblings (exercised by the new test plan_version_merges_two_platform_siblings_optional_dep_updates_into_one_entry), the same owner package.json/Cargo.toml is read from disk and re-parsed N times in one plan_version call instead of once, hoisted out of the loop.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs\",\n    \"line\": 132,\n    \"summary\": \"Workspace now stores `pub identity: IdentityIndex` as a full clone of graph.identity(), just so version.rs can pass `identity: &amp;ws.identity` into CascadeInput.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Duplicates data already reachable via `ws.graph.identity()` (used everywhere else, e.g. walk.rs:1233/1350) -- every Workspace::load now pays to clone the entire IdentityIndex (bare/native/prefixed/platform BTreeMaps) instead of passing the existing reference through.\"\n  }\n]\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>117652</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>22</tool_uses><duration_ms>147345</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:20:26.153Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>afcc23500e9b47639</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01511M7j2iPSm6VxFa3Z3UDc</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/afcc23500e9b47639.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit version.rs diff for altitude bandaids\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task complete — report delivered above (2 findings in groups.rs and version.rs; all other assigned files checked clean).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>144511</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>86547</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:20:29.825Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7a0288fe8b5dcbd3</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a7a0288fe8b5dcbd3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Angle D/E/F: reuse, simplification, efficiency\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## PR #5 Code-Quality Review — Changed Code Only\n\nFour parallel passes covered callisto-manifests, callisto-graph/locate+walk, callisto-graph core (commands/version.rs, config, identity, matrix, tags), and callisto-model+callisto-vcs. 13 candidates surfaced; the 6 below were selected for impact and verified directly against the current file contents.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs\",\n    \"line\": 37,\n    \"summary\": \"New redact_git_stderr wrapper (calls callisto_model::redact_known_secrets + known_credential_env_values(std::env::vars())) is a verbatim copy of the same 4-line body added by this same diff in at least 3-4 other files: callisto-cli/src/commands/pre.rs, callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, callisto-conventional/src/pre_cursor.rs, and callisto-graph/src/commands/publish_client.rs (as redact_stderr).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The identical stderr-redaction call sequence is hand-copied into 5 places instead of one shared callisto_model::redact_process_stderr(text) helper. Any future change to the redaction convention (e.g. caching the env snapshot instead of re-reading it per call, or adding a new credential source) must be made in 5 files, and a 6th call site is likely to reinvent it again rather than find the existing one.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 314,\n    \"summary\": \"plan_version re-derives the OpenContext from scratch (Cargo.toml exists check, WorkspaceCargoResolver::load, detect_npm_workspace_kind) instead of reusing the equivalent discovery logic already present in walk.rs, apply.rs, and lib.rs.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A 4th independent copy of ~15 lines of workspace-inheritance-detection logic; a future fix (e.g. supporting a new npm workspace kind) must be patched in four places, and missing this one silently reintroduces stale behavior only in the version-planning path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 351,\n    \"summary\": \"Platform-manifest and owner-manifest handles are opened via the raw callisto_manifests::open() call instead of the Workspace's manifest_cache::open_cached (defined in callisto-graph/src/lib.rs and already used by Workspace::base_versions, lib.rs:209).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Bypasses the per-command-run manifest cache that lib.rs documents as existing precisely so a given manifest is opened at most once per command run; any manifest already opened elsewhere in the same run (e.g. by base_versions) is read from disk and re-parsed a second time here.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 367,\n    \"summary\": \"Inside the per-platform-member loop, the owner package's canonical manifest is opened and parsed fresh for every platform sibling that owner has, rather than once per owner.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"For an owner with N platform-manifest siblings (the new test plan_version_merges_two_platform_siblings_optional_dep_updates_into_one_entry exercises this), the same owner Cargo.toml/package.json is read and re-parsed N times within a single plan_version call instead of once, hoisted out of the loop.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n    \"line\": 244,\n    \"summary\": \"read_npm_membership reads and JSON-parses root package.json twice per call: once in package_json_declares_name(root) (line ~244), then again in read_package_json_workspaces(root) (line ~283) whenever no pnpm-workspace.yaml governs.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"read_npm_membership runs once per IgnoreWalkLocator::projects() invocation, which is on the hot path for every graph/matrix command. The parsed serde_json::Value from the first read is discarded and re-derived rather than threaded through, doubling I/O and JSON-parse cost on every npm-ecosystem workspace scan for no behavioral gain.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs\",\n    \"line\": 132,\n    \"summary\": \"Workspace::load now stores `let identity = graph.identity().clone();` — a full clone of the IdentityIndex — purely so version.rs can pass `identity: &amp;ws.identity` into CascadeInput, duplicating data already reachable via `ws.graph.identity()` (the pattern used everywhere else, e.g. walk.rs).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Every Workspace::load (i.e. every command invocation) now pays to clone the entire IdentityIndex (bare/native/prefixed/platform BTreeMaps) instead of passing through the existing reference, adding an unnecessary allocation on the startup path of every command.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Notable non-findings**: the manifests fork confirmed the mutate/persist split and the three ecosystem `*_package_name` functions are deliberate, well-justified duplication (doc comments explain why) — not flagged. The graph-core fork confirmed matrix.rs and tags.rs already implement the efficiency improvements an audit would otherwise ask for. Runner-up candidates not included in the final 6 (available on request): a 4x-duplicated error-fallback block in `cargo.rs` (~line 373), a duplicated PEP-503 name-equivalence check in `python.rs` (~line 452), a redundant map lookup in `walk.rs` (~line 146), a per-iteration allocation in `napi_linux_abi_from_package_name` (`walk.rs:658`), and a leftover duplicate test module in `membership.rs` (~line 545).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>61591</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>16</tool_uses><duration_ms>238675</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
