{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:22:00.508Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>afcc23500e9b47639</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NvZLMQpaK6gqzGXpXZ5YKD</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/afcc23500e9b47639.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit version.rs diff for altitude bandaids\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>FILE: crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs\nLINE: 143 (and duplicated at line ~197, in `GroupTable::resolve`)\nSUMMARY: The new cross-group \"already claimed by a different group\" conflict check (`claimed_by` BTreeMap lookup + `ConflictingGroupMembership` error) is implemented as two verbatim copies of the same ~9-line block — one inside the `for rg in &amp;raw.fixed` loop, one inside the equivalent `for rg in &amp;raw.linked` loop — rather than being factored into a single helper (e.g. `fn claim_member(claimed_by, id, group_name) -&gt; Result&lt;(), GraphError&gt;`) called from both loops.\nFAILURE_SCENARIO: If a third group category is ever added (or the conflict rule needs to change, e.g. to also detect a package claimed by two *linked* groups with different constraints), the fix has to be applied in two separate physical locations that already drifted apart once in this diff (the `platform.get(name)` destructuring changed independently in both copies too); a future editor patching only one copy would silently leave the other loop's membership conflicts unchecked or checked differently.\n\nFILE: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\nLINE: 337-380 (`plan_version`, platform-write / optional-dep-update block)\nSUMMARY: The newly added platform-manifest version-write and optional-dependency-update logic iterates only `ws.config.groups.fixed.values()` — no equivalent pass over `ws.config.groups.linked`. Likely intentional (platform/native-addon siblings are architecturally always fixed-group members), but nothing in the code or a doc comment states that invariant explicitly at this call site, so the omission of a `linked` pass reads as an implicit special case rather than a documented contract.\nFAILURE_SCENARIO: If linked groups are ever extended to carry `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` members (nothing in `GroupMember`'s type prevents this), those platform manifests would silently never receive version writes or optional-dep updates here, and the bug would only surface as \"my linked-group platform package didn't get bumped\" rather than a compile-time or validation-time error — because the loop scope was narrowed by omission, not by an enforced type-level constraint. Low confidence this is a real bug rather than settled architecture; flagging because the boundary isn't documented.\n\nNo other genuine altitude-bandaid candidates found in my assigned scope (commands/version.rs, config/groups.rs, infer.rs, tags.rs, plan.rs, config/raw.rs).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>158451</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>180999</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
