ck does check: `head_sha` (lines 78-84), `commits_since` (lines 165-171), `create_tag` (lines 197-203), and `create_floating_major` (lines 218-224) all guard with `if !output.success() { return Err(VcsError::Git(...redact_git_stderr(&amp;output.stderr)...)) }`. (`resolve_commit` intentionally treats failure as `Ok(None)`, which is a documented, different design choice, not a silent-swallow bug.) So a failing `git tag --list` (e.g., not a git repo, corrupted repo) with empty/non-empty stderr and empty stdout falls through `stdout_lines()` on empty stdout and returns `Ok(vec![])` — indistinguishable from \"repository has zero tags\" — with no error surfaced and no stderr redaction/reporting path exercised at all.\n\n**Files read (absolute paths):**\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md` (checked — none of these three are already logged as CONFIRMED)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>53255</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>52544</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
