mpirically: running this suite without `--test-threads=1` produced\n197-/// spurious failures from one test's fixture directory bleeding into\n198-/// another's assertions). `PATH_MUTEX` provides that serialization;\n199-/// `PathGuard` holds the lock for its entire lifetime, only releasing it\n200-/// (in `Drop`, after `PATH` has been restored) once the owning test is\n201-/// done with it.\n202-static PATH_MUTEX: tokio::sync::Mutex<()> = tokio::sync::Mutex::const_new(());\n203-\n204-struct PathGuard {\n205-    previous: Option<std::ffi::OsString>,\n206-    _lock: tokio::sync::MutexGuard<'static, ()>,\n207-}\n--\n501-/// (unreleased), not an error. This is arguably the *correct*, more robust\n502-/// behavior for a brand new/pre-git package -- so this test asserts that\n503-/// real, graceful-success behavior rather than forcing a fabricated\n504-/// \"failure\" assertion that doesn't match reality.\n505-#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]\n506:async fn execute_extension_no_git_repo_succeeds_with_no_last_tag_not_panic() {\n507-    resolve_wasm_file();\n508-\n509-    let sandbox = create_empty_moon_sandbox();\n510-    let root = sandbox.root.clone();\n511-\n512-    // Deliberately no `git init` here -- that's the point of this test.\n513-    fs::write(","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"99fb6a86-0179-4f5e-9edc-ac6bd6132e94","timestamp":"2026-08-21T15:31:00.765Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"162-/// identically whether the underlying command succeeded, failed cleanly, or\n163-/// returned garbage.\n164-///\n165-/// For a test that drives this same \"basic args\" (`args: [\"status\"]`) case\n166-/// and actually asserts something about the resulting report, see\n167:/// `execute_extension_no_git_repo_succeeds_with_no_last_tag_not_panic` below\n168-/// (same args, but against a fixture with no `.git` directory, and it\n169-/// asserts on `exit_code`/`report`) and\n170-/// `execute_extension_status_succeeds_against_real_repo_fixture` (asserts a\n171-/// real success shape