{"parentUuid":"8d27c958-f5af-4127-b848-c54419287cc2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGFFgy3XoAxuNgkbmGoR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1021,"cache_read_input_tokens":668820,"output_tokens":3434,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2688},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1021,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3434,"cache_read_input_tokens":668820,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1021},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGFFbLiVkTXsq3ZcG43g","type":"assistant","uuid":"4ed957c8-c204-4429-9d0c-e1f93bb74b55","timestamp":"2026-08-21T16:57:19.084Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"4ed957c8-c204-4429-9d0c-e1f93bb74b55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGFFgy3XoAxuNgkbmGoR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ran the dry-run and found something important — **this reveals a real bug in `callisto` itself**, not just a changeset organization question.\n\n**What I found:** every crate shares one literal `[workspace.package].version` field (confirmed earlier — `version.workspace = true` everywhere). But the dry-run computed *different* target versions per package: `0.3.4` for the patch-severity crates, `0.4.0` for the minor-severity ones. That's physically impossible — they can't end up at two different numbers when they all read from one field.\n\nI traced it to `apply.rs`'s `apply_version_plan` (line 208-212): for every bump whose write target is `CargoWorkspacePackage`, it reloads the root `Cargo.toml` fresh and calls `ws_res.write_version(&bump.to, permit)` — once per package, each with that package's *own* independently-computed target. This is last-write-wins on one shared field. In this specific case the final on-disk value would happen to land on `0.4.0` (callisto-vcs, alphabetically last, computes minor), but:\n- The generated changelog/report would still say `callisto-changelog` bumped to `0.3.4` — which won't match what's actually in `Cargo.toml` (`0.4.0`) once the dust settles.\n- This isn't guaranteed to coincidentally work out — a different mix of severities/iteration order could silently *under*-version the whole workspace.\n\n**So, no — I'm not confident this produces a clean release as configured**, and this is exactly what your \"shouldn't versions be lined up\" instinct was pointing at.\n\n**On the changeset-splitting question**, you're right in general — a changeset's per-package severity map is meant for genuinely related work that happens to hit different packages at different severities. But for *this* repo specifically, since every package shares one physical version number, giving them different severities is actually meaningless (and is what exposed this bug) — they're always going to land on the same number regardless. The fix for the changeset is to make it uniform (all `minor`), not split it further.\n\nWant me to:\n1. Fix the changeset now (uniform `minor` for all touched packages), and\n2. File/fix the `apply_version_plan` last-write-wins bug for shared-workspace-version packages (a real correctness issue, independent of this PR)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1021,"cache_read_input_tokens":668820,"output_tokens":3434,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2688},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1021,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3434,"cache_read_input_tokens":668820,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1021},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGFFbLiVkTXsq3ZcG43g","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa2b747a-ca24-47b6-9f70-2003fa49c5d4","timestamp":"2026-08-21T16:57:26.111Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
