{"parentUuid":"0ee683d4-5a19-4145-a0bb-a7dfc0bb7d68","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a254f192-f991-43d4-85e4-802bb6fad84e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GcXCgGkxPUFiSb2QZ8dmam","type":"tool_result","content":"3905\t    /// Always `WorkspaceInheritance::root_manifest`. Carried on the result rather than\n3906\t    /// re-read from the snapshot at the call site so that `DepEdge::from_manifest` and\n3907\t    /// `DepWriteTarget::CargoWorkspaceDependency` (§G.7.3) are populated from one value.\n3908\t    pub declared_in: &'a Path,\n3909\t}\n3910\t\n3911\t/// The mutable editor for the workspace root's `Cargo.toml` — the only type in this crate\n3912\t/// that writes `[workspace.package]`/`[workspace.dependencies]`. A member `CargoToml`'s two\n3913\t/// write methods handle an inherited field very differently from each other, and neither\n3914\t/// actually surfaces `ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited` to do it (see the prose below the\n3915\t/// method list) — `write_version` pins an explicit value into the member itself rather than\n3916\t/// touching the root at all; `update_dependency_spec` transparently delegates to this type.\n3917\tpub struct WorkspaceCargoResolver {\n3918\t    root_path: PathBuf,\n3919\t    document: toml_edit::DocumentMut,\n3920\t}\n3921\t\n3922\timpl WorkspaceCargoResolver {\n3923\t    /// Reads and parses the workspace root's `Cargo.toml`. A root with no\n3924\t    /// `[workspace.package]` and no `[workspace.dependencies]` table is valid —\n3925\t    /// `inheritance()` then returns `WorkspaceInheritance::default()`, meaning no member can\n3926\t    /// legally use `.workspace = true` (a member that does anyway is a Cargo-level error, not\n3927\t    /// this resolver's to catch — `cargo metadata`/`cargo check` will refuse it before\n3928\t    /// callisto ever runs).\n3929\t    pub fn load(root_manifest_path: &Path) -> Result<Self, ManifestError>;\n3930\t\n3931\t    /// Cheap: extracts and parses the current `[workspace.package].version`/\n3932\t    /// `[workspace.dependencies]` into an owned snapshot. Called once per invocation, then\n3933\t    /// wrapped in `Arc` for `OpenContext` (§CM.2).\n3934\t    pub fn inheritance(&self) -> Result<WorkspaceInheritance, ManifestError>;\n3935\t\n3936\t    /// Writes `[workspace.package].version`. *Intended* as the single write that satisfies\n3937\t    /// every member inheriting `version.workspace = true` at once (§18 Q2) — but as of this\n3938\t    /// writing, a member's own `CargoToml::write_version` never delegates here; it pins an\n3939\t    /// explicit version directly into the member instead (see the prose below the method\n3940\t    /// list). This method is reachable only through `apply_version_plan`'s\n3941\t    /// `VersionWriteTarget::CargoWorkspacePackage` dispatch arm, and that write target is\n3942\t    /// itself never constructed by the real planner today (§G.10.2 step 3's note) — so this\n3943\t    /// method has no live production caller.\n3944\t    pub fn write_version(&mut self, v: &Version) -> Result<(), ManifestError>;\n3945\t\n3946\t    /// Writes one `[workspace.dependencies]` entry. Two real, independent callers reach this:\n3947\t    /// (1) the apply-phase target for every `SpecRewrite` whose `DepWriteTarget` is\n3948\t    /// `CargoWorkspaceDependency` (§G.7.3, §G.10.2 step 6) — `cascade.rs`'s real rewrite\n3949\t    /// planning does construct this target for a genuinely inherited dependency edge, unlike"}]},"uuid":"227ef349-3552-4ce8-8204-58a9e098df9b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:32:56.100Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"    /// Always `WorkspaceInheritance::root_manifest`. Carried on the result rather than\n    /// re-read from the snapshot at the call site so that `DepEdge::from_manifest` and\n    /// `DepWriteTarget::CargoWorkspaceDependency` (§G.7.3) are populated from one value.\n    pub declared_in: &'a Path,\n}\n\n/// The mutable editor for the workspace root's `Cargo.toml` — the only type in this crate\n/// that writes `[workspace.package]`/`[workspace.dependencies]`. A member `CargoToml`'s two\n/// write methods handle an inherited field very differently from each other, and neither\n/// actually surfaces `ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited` to do it (see the prose below the\n/// method list) — `write_version` pins an explicit value into the member itself rather than\n/// touching the root at all; `update_dependency_spec` transparently delegates to this type.\npub struct WorkspaceCargoResolver {\n    root_path: PathBuf,\n    document: toml_edit::DocumentMut,\n}\n\nimpl WorkspaceCargoResolver {\n    /// Reads and parses the workspace root's `Cargo.toml`. A root with no\n    /// `[workspace.package]` and no `[workspace.dependencies]` table is valid —\n    /// `inheritance()` then returns `WorkspaceInheritance::default()`, meaning no member can\n    /// legally use `.workspace = true` (a member that does anyway is a Cargo-level error, not\n    /// this resolver's to catch — `cargo metadata`/`cargo check` will refuse it before\n    /// callisto ever runs).\n    pub fn load(root_manifest_path: &Path) -> Result<Self, ManifestError>;\n\n    /// Cheap: extracts and parses the current `[workspace.package].version`/\n    /// `[workspace.dependencies]` into an owned snapshot. Called once per invocation, then\n    /// wrapped in `Arc` for `OpenContext` (§CM.2).\n    pub fn inheritance(&self) -> Result<WorkspaceInheritance, ManifestError>;\n\n    /// Writes `[workspace.package].version`. *Intended* as the single write that satisfies\n    /// every member inheriting `version.workspace = true` at once (§18 Q2) — but as of this\n    /// writing, a member's own `CargoToml::write_version` never delegates here; it pins an\n    /// explicit version directly into the member instead (see the prose below the method\n    /// list). This method is reachable only through `apply_version_plan`'s\n    /// `VersionWriteTarget::CargoWorkspacePackage` dispatch arm, and that write target is\n    /// itself never constructed by the real planner today (§G.10.2 step 3's note) — so this\n    /// method has no live production caller.\n    pub fn write_version(&mut self, v: &Version) -> Result<(), ManifestError>;\n\n    /// Writes one `[workspace.dependencies]` entry. Two real, independent callers reach this:\n    /// (1) the apply-phase target for every `SpecRewrite` whose `DepWriteTarget` is\n    /// `CargoWorkspaceDependency` (§G.7.3, §G.10.2 step 6) — `cascade.rs`'s real rewrite\n    /// planning does construct this target for a genuinely inherited dependency edge, unlike","numLines":45,"startLine":3905,"totalLines":11449}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0ee683d4-5a19-4145-a0bb-a7dfc0bb7d68","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
