{"parentUuid":"0e4b58c6-10f3-42ac-98c6-4ac50d373d9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGJ1dzuy7C5BGr3fjEyu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HxFysq8Dm3Qh33F5RvxGK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","offset":3950,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":677464,"output_tokens":2736,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2591},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1787,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2736,"cache_read_input_tokens":677464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1787},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGJ1bcnre4jFk1CAgLtv","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a1f1c6e-8351-456f-8e68-3f6dfd94bbdd","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:33:27.368Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"5a1f1c6e-8351-456f-8e68-3f6dfd94bbdd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a254f192-f991-43d4-85e4-802bb6fad84e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HxFysq8Dm3Qh33F5RvxGK","type":"tool_result","content":"3950\t    /// `CargoWorkspacePackage` above; and (2) a member's own `update_dependency_spec`, called\n3951\t    /// directly on an inherited dependency, which transparently delegates here itself rather\n3952\t    /// than returning an error the caller must redirect on (see the prose below). Rewriting\n3953\t    /// it here is correct Cargo semantics (§18 Q2: *\"Bumping a member's dep means editing the\n3954\t    /// root, not the member\"*), and affects every member that inherits `name`, which is the\n3955\t    /// intended effect, not a side effect to guard against.\n3956\t    ///\n3957\t    /// **Takes no `DepKind`**, for the same reason `WorkspaceInheritance::inherited` returns\n3958\t    /// none: the root's table has no sections. One call updates the entry every inheriting\n3959\t    /// member sees, whatever section each of them declared it under.\n3960\t    pub fn write_dependency(&mut self, name: &str, new: DepSpec) -> Result<(), ManifestError>;\n3961\t}\n3962\t```\n3963\t\n3964\t**Reads are transparent; the two write methods handle inheritance differently, and neither\n3965\tsurfaces `WorkspaceInherited`.** A member `CargoToml` opened with `ctx.cargo_workspace =\n3966\tSome(inheritance)` answers `current_version()` and `iter_dependencies()` with the *real,\n3967\tresolved* values — a caller reading a member's version or dependency list never needs to know\n3968\tinheritance was involved. Grep of `callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs` confirms\n3969\t`ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited` is constructed in exactly one place, and it's not a write\n3970\tpath at all: `current_version()`, when `self.inherited_version` is set but no\n3971\t`WorkspaceCargoResolver` context was ever supplied to `open()` — a caller-contract violation\n3972\tcaught the first time anyone tries to read the version, not a \"which file gets edited\" signal.\n3973\t\n3974\t`write_version` on an inherited member never touches the root and never errors: it writes an\n3975\texplicit pinned version string directly into the member's own `[package]` section, replacing\n3976\tthe inheritance declaration (tested by\n3977\t`write_version_pins_explicitly_on_workspace_inheriting_member`). `update_dependency_spec` on\n3978\tan inherited dependency instead delegates transparently — it loads a\n3979\t`WorkspaceCargoResolver` for the root and calls `write_dependency` itself, with no error\n3980\tsurfaced to its own caller — *unless* the manifest being edited **is** the workspace root\n3981\titself, in which case it refuses with `ManifestError::InvariantViolation` (not\n3982\t`WorkspaceInherited`) to avoid overwriting the just-written root with a stale in-memory\n3983\tdocument.\n3984\t\n3985\tIf `open()` is called for a decl that uses `.workspace = true` but `ctx.cargo_workspace` is\n3986\t`None` (no resolver context was ever built for this invocation), `open()` itself fails with\n3987\t`ManifestError::Read { path, message: \"declares .workspace = true but no\n3988\tWorkspaceCargoResolver context was supplied\" }` — a caller-contract violation caught at\n3989\tconstruction rather than deferred to the first read. `callisto-graph` always builds a\n3990\t`WorkspaceCargoResolver` once per invocation whenever any `Cargo.toml` is present in the\n3991\tworkspace (§G.4.1), matching §18 Q2's *\"must be handled correctly from v0.1.\"*\n3992\t\n3993\t### CM.5 The `npm` feature — `PackageJson`\n3994\t\n3995\t#### CM.5.1 The format-preserving editor — what \"custom\" has to preserve\n3996\t\n3997\tJSON has no `toml_edit` equivalent to reach for, because JSON (unlike TOML) has no comments\n3998\tand no whitespace attached to a specific node a library could hang a round-trip guarantee on\n3999\t— there is nothing *in* a parsed JSON tree that remembers how it was indented. What\n4000\t\"format-preserving\" can mean for JSON is therefore narrower and fully enumerable, and npm's\n4001\town tooling (`detect-indent` + `write-file-atomic`) solves it the same way callisto does here:\n4002\t**detect a small, fixed set of format degrees of freedom once, on read, and reproduce them\n4003\texactly on write.** There is nothing else to preserve — `package.json` has no multi-line\n4004\tstrings, no significant blank lines, no trailing commas.\n4005\t\n4006\t```rust\n4007\tpub struct PackageJson {\n4008\t    path: PathBuf,\n4009\t    absolute: PathBuf,"}]},"uuid":"47cdc0ae-c70c-4942-b6cf-645c9de0838a","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:33:27.426Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"    /// `CargoWorkspacePackage` above; and (2) a member's own `update_dependency_spec`, called\n    /// directly on an inherited dependency, which transparently delegates here itself rather\n    /// than returning an error the caller must redirect on (see the prose below). Rewriting\n    /// it here is correct Cargo semantics (§18 Q2: *\"Bumping a member's dep means editing the\n    /// root, not the member\"*), and affects every member that inherits `name`, which is the\n    /// intended effect, not a side effect to guard against.\n    ///\n    /// **Takes no `DepKind`**, for the same reason `WorkspaceInheritance::inherited` returns\n    /// none: the root's table has no sections. One call updates the entry every inheriting\n    /// member sees, whatever section each of them declared it under.\n    pub fn write_dependency(&mut self, name: &str, new: DepSpec) -> Result<(), ManifestError>;\n}\n```\n\n**Reads are transparent; the two write methods handle inheritance differently, and neither\nsurfaces `WorkspaceInherited`.** A member `CargoToml` opened with `ctx.cargo_workspace =\nSome(inheritance)` answers `current_version()` and `iter_dependencies()` with the *real,\nresolved* values — a caller reading a member's version or dependency list never needs to know\ninheritance was involved. Grep of `callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs` confirms\n`ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited` is constructed in exactly one place, and it's not a write\npath at all: `current_version()`, when `self.inherited_version` is set but no\n`WorkspaceCargoResolver` context was ever supplied to `open()` — a caller-contract violation\ncaught the first time anyone tries to read the version, not a \"which file gets edited\" signal.\n\n`write_version` on an inherited member never touches the root and never errors: it writes an\nexplicit pinned version string directly into the member's own `[package]` section, replacing\nthe inheritance declaration (tested by\n`write_version_pins_explicitly_on_workspace_inheriting_member`). `update_dependency_spec` on\nan inherited dependency instead delegates transparently — it loads a\n`WorkspaceCargoResolver` for the root and calls `write_dependency` itself, with no error\nsurfaced to its own caller — *unless* the manifest being edited **is** the workspace root\nitself, in which case it refuses with `ManifestError::InvariantViolation` (not\n`WorkspaceInherited`) to avoid overwriting the just-written root with a stale in-memory\ndocument.\n\nIf `open()` is called for a decl that uses `.workspace = true` but `ctx.cargo_workspace` is\n`None` (no resolver context was ever built for this invocation), `open()` itself fails with\n`ManifestError::Read { path, message: \"declares .workspace = true but no\nWorkspaceCargoResolver context was supplied\" }` — a caller-contract violation caught at\nconstruction rather than deferred to the first read. `callisto-graph` always builds a\n`WorkspaceCargoResolver` once per invocation whenever any `Cargo.toml` is present in the\nworkspace (§G.4.1), matching §18 Q2's *\"must be handled correctly from v0.1.\"*\n\n### CM.5 The `npm` feature — `PackageJson`\n\n#### CM.5.1 The format-preserving editor — what \"custom\" has to preserve\n\nJSON has no `toml_edit` equivalent to reach for, because JSON (unlike TOML) has no comments\nand no whitespace attached to a specific node a library could hang a round-trip guarantee on\n— there is nothing *in* a parsed JSON tree that remembers how it was indented. What\n\"format-preserving\" can mean for JSON is therefore narrower and fully enumerable, and npm's\nown tooling (`detect-indent` + `write-file-atomic`) solves it the same way callisto does here:\n**detect a small, fixed set of format degrees of freedom once, on read, and reproduce them\nexactly on write.** There is nothing else to preserve — `package.json` has no multi-line\nstrings, no significant blank lines, no trailing commas.\n\n```rust\npub struct PackageJson {\n    path: PathBuf,\n    absolute: PathBuf,","numLines":60,"startLine":3950,"totalLines":11449}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5a1f1c6e-8351-456f-8e68-3f6dfd94bbdd","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
