{"parentUuid":"82080659-f22d-423f-95f5-4d4049db21ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGJ7GDQ7wS2zSgMAoNRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L5VH8wateo6HCkd5hiBgfr","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","offset":1681,"limit":40},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":690406,"output_tokens":116,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":116,"cache_read_input_tokens":690406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGJ7CasKxzYQi1ZBAkT5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd565b55-85d1-438e-a31a-145a3137590d","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:34:14.903Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"fd565b55-85d1-438e-a31a-145a3137590d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a254f192-f991-43d4-85e4-802bb6fad84e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L5VH8wateo6HCkd5hiBgfr","type":"tool_result","content":"1681\t**Q2 (resolved, committed to v0.1) — `Cargo [workspace.dependencies]` inheritance.** Modern\n1682\tCargo workspaces define versions once at the root; members inherit via `foo.workspace =\n1683\ttrue`. Bumping a member's dep means editing the root, not the member. `WorkspaceCargoResolver`\n1684\tin `callisto-manifests`, §17 v0.1 — this used to say \"must be handled correctly from v0.1\"\n1685\twhile sitting in this open-questions list and absent from the actual v0.1 milestone bullet;\n1686\tit's committed there now, not just asserted here.\n1687\t\n1688\t**Q3 (resolved) — `validate` as a subcommand or a flag on other commands?** Dedicated\n1689\tsubcommand (`callisto validate --staged`, `--since <ref>`) — §11 and §12.2 already assumed\n1690\tthis shape before the question was formally closed; §17 v0.2 now ships it explicitly.\n1691\t\n1692\t**Q4 (resolved) — Migration from `.changeset/config.json`**\n1693\t\n1694\t**Shape: `callisto init` detecting an existing `.changeset` directory, not a standalone\n1695\t`callisto migrate` subcommand.** A dedicated subcommand would have exactly one legitimate\n1696\tinvocation per repo, ever — once at adoption, then dead weight in the CLI's surface for the\n1697\trest of the project's life. `callisto init` already owns this class of decision: §5.3\n1698\tspecifies the identical UX pattern for napi group derivation (\"`callisto init` offers to\n1699\twrite the derived group into `callisto.toml` as explicit config on first run\"), and §10 gives\n1700\t`init` a host-side prompt surface via `initialize_extension` that a new subcommand would have\n1701\tto duplicate or route around. Folding migration into `init` also keeps it on the WASM surface\n1702\tfor free (§11: `init` is already WASM-compatible because `initialize_extension` supplies the\n1703\tprompt seam) rather than forcing a fresh CLI-vs-WASM classification for a new command. Against\n1704\t§4's principles: P5 (structural fixes, not a README step a user has to remember to run) favors\n1705\tdetection over a command a migrating user has to know exists and invoke correctly; P1 (byte-\n1706\tcompat as the adoption gate) is served either way, since neither shape touches the files P1\n1707\tguarantees compatibility for — but folding into `init` means the byte-compat promise and the\n1708\tconfig-translation offer are presented to the user in the same breath, at the one moment\n1709\tthey're evaluating whether to adopt at all. Concretely: `callisto init`, on finding\n1710\t`.changeset/config.json`, reads it, produces the translated `callisto.toml` block described\n1711\tbelow as a diff for review (never a silent write — same reviewability contract as §5.3's\n1712\tgroup-derivation offer and §13 invariant 21's \"membership changes are only ever written via\n1713\tan explicit, reviewable flow\"), and proceeds with normal scaffolding if the user declines.\n1714\t\n1715\t**Confirmed: migration touches `config.json` only, never `.changeset/*.md` or `pre.json`.**\n1716\tThis is the reason the surface is small at all. Per P1, the changeset Markdown files and\n1717\t`pre.json` are already byte-compatible with what callisto reads and writes (§6, §6.4) — there\n1718\tis nothing to translate in either, and `callisto init`'s migration step does not open, parse,\n1719\tor rewrite a single one of them. The only artifact requiring translation is `config.json`,\n1720\tbecause it's the one part of `@changesets/cli`'s on-disk footprint that encodes *settings*"}]},"uuid":"1b5e04d6-9ad7-488e-be6f-e67cd030f9e1","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:34:14.965Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","content":"**Q2 (resolved, committed to v0.1) — `Cargo [workspace.dependencies]` inheritance.** Modern\nCargo workspaces define versions once at the root; members inherit via `foo.workspace =\ntrue`. Bumping a member's dep means editing the root, not the member. `WorkspaceCargoResolver`\nin `callisto-manifests`, §17 v0.1 — this used to say \"must be handled correctly from v0.1\"\nwhile sitting in this open-questions list and absent from the actual v0.1 milestone bullet;\nit's committed there now, not just asserted here.\n\n**Q3 (resolved) — `validate` as a subcommand or a flag on other commands?** Dedicated\nsubcommand (`callisto validate --staged`, `--since <ref>`) — §11 and §12.2 already assumed\nthis shape before the question was formally closed; §17 v0.2 now ships it explicitly.\n\n**Q4 (resolved) — Migration from `.changeset/config.json`**\n\n**Shape: `callisto init` detecting an existing `.changeset` directory, not a standalone\n`callisto migrate` subcommand.** A dedicated subcommand would have exactly one legitimate\ninvocation per repo, ever — once at adoption, then dead weight in the CLI's surface for the\nrest of the project's life. `callisto init` already owns this class of decision: §5.3\nspecifies the identical UX pattern for napi group derivation (\"`callisto init` offers to\nwrite the derived group into `callisto.toml` as explicit config on first run\"), and §10 gives\n`init` a host-side prompt surface via `initialize_extension` that a new subcommand would have\nto duplicate or route around. Folding migration into `init` also keeps it on the WASM surface\nfor free (§11: `init` is already WASM-compatible because `initialize_extension` supplies the\nprompt seam) rather than forcing a fresh CLI-vs-WASM classification for a new command. Against\n§4's principles: P5 (structural fixes, not a README step a user has to remember to run) favors\ndetection over a command a migrating user has to know exists and invoke correctly; P1 (byte-\ncompat as the adoption gate) is served either way, since neither shape touches the files P1\nguarantees compatibility for — but folding into `init` means the byte-compat promise and the\nconfig-translation offer are presented to the user in the same breath, at the one moment\nthey're evaluating whether to adopt at all. Concretely: `callisto init`, on finding\n`.changeset/config.json`, reads it, produces the translated `callisto.toml` block described\nbelow as a diff for review (never a silent write — same reviewability contract as §5.3's\ngroup-derivation offer and §13 invariant 21's \"membership changes are only ever written via\nan explicit, reviewable flow\"), and proceeds with normal scaffolding if the user declines.\n\n**Confirmed: migration touches `config.json` only, never `.changeset/*.md` or `pre.json`.**\nThis is the reason the surface is small at all. Per P1, the changeset Markdown files and\n`pre.json` are already byte-compatible with what callisto reads and writes (§6, §6.4) — there\nis nothing to translate in either, and `callisto init`'s migration step does not open, parse,\nor rewrite a single one of them. The only artifact requiring translation is `config.json`,\nbecause it's the one part of `@changesets/cli`'s on-disk footprint that encodes *settings*","numLines":40,"startLine":1681,"totalLines":2198}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd565b55-85d1-438e-a31a-145a3137590d","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
