{"parentUuid":"d4ea2cef-b622-44ee-bf14-3a0032b54439","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a254f192-f991-43d4-85e4-802bb6fad84e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AhBVrDq94MhJ6EHJAwHWxU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"knope release tool cargo workspace shared version highest bump wins changesets\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cargo-workspaces 0.4.2 - Docs.rs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/crate/cargo-workspaces/latest\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pksunkara/cargo-workspaces: A tool for managing cargo workspaces and their crates, inspired by lerna · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pksunkara/cargo-workspaces\"},{\"title\":\"Updating dependencies | Knope\",\"url\":\"https://knope.tech/recipes/updating-dependencies/\"},{\"title\":\"cargo-workspaces - crates.io: Rust Package Registry\",\"url\":\"https://crates.io/crates/cargo-workspaces\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ava-labs/cargo-workspace-version: Cargo plugin to check and/or update all local package versions in a workspace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ava-labs/cargo-workspace-version\"},{\"title\":\"Knope — command-line utility in Rust // Lib.rs\",\"url\":\"https://lib.rs/crates/knope\"},{\"title\":\"cargo-workspaces — Cargo add-on // Lib.rs\",\"url\":\"https://lib.rs/crates/cargo-workspaces\"},{\"title\":\"cargo-release - crates.io: Rust Package Registry\",\"url\":\"https://crates.io/crates/cargo-release\"},{\"title\":\"Packages | Knope\",\"url\":\"https://knope.tech/reference/concepts/package/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - knope-dev/knope: A command line tool to handle all the tasks most developers find tedious. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/knope-dev/knope\"}]\n\nNow let me search specifically for information about Knope's handling of changesets and version bumping in workspaces:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - knope-dev/changesets: A Rust crate for parsing and creating changesets—Markdown files describing releases\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/knope-dev/changesets\"},{\"title\":\"changesets - crates.io: Rust Package Registry\",\"url\":\"https://crates.io/crates/changesets/0.1.1\"},{\"title\":\"Changesets — Rust dev tool // Lib.rs\",\"url\":\"https://lib.rs/crates/changesets\"},{\"title\":\"BumpVersion | Knope\",\"url\":\"https://knope.tech/reference/config-file/steps/bump-version/\"},{\"title\":\"knope/CHANGELOG.md at main · knope-dev/knope\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/knope-dev/knope/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\"},{\"title\":\"Is it possible to bump major version based on latest published version? · changesets/changesets · Discussion #974\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/changesets/changesets/discussions/974\"},{\"title\":\"PrepareRelease | Knope\",\"url\":\"https://knope.tech/reference/config-file/steps/prepare-release/\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - Knope\",\"url\":\"https://knope-dev.github.io/knope/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - knope-dev/knope: A command line tool to handle all the tasks most developers find tedious. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/knope-dev/knope\"},{\"title\":\"ChangeSet | Knope\",\"url\":\"https://knope.tech/reference/concepts/changeset/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about Knope's release tool and how it handles changesets with cargo workspaces:\n\n## Knope Release Tool Overview\n\nKnope is a command line tool that happily completes the tasks which most developers find tedious. Knope is a CLI/CI tool which automates common tasks for developers.\n\n## Changesets and Version Bumping\n\nA changeset is a set of change files in the .changeset directory. When creating a release, Knope combines every change file in the changeset (along with any conventional commits) to generate the changelog and decide the next version for each package.\n\nRegarding the \"highest bump wins\" approach you mentioned: When you release, if a package has multiple changes, the package would bump the version based on the highest change type. If a package has multiple changesets affecting it (for example, one with minor and one with patch), the version would be bumped based on the highest change type (in this case, minor).\n\n## Cargo Workspace Support\n\nYou get a GitHub release and a changelog, picking the semantic version based on the combination of conventional commits and changesets. Knope can work with Cargo workspaces, allowing it to manage versioning across multiple packages in a workspace by coordinating version bumps based on the changesets and conventional commits found in the repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dede24a6-22d1-48df-a312-b5c3589805aa","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:35:02.883Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"knope release tool cargo workspace shared version highest bump wins changesets","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0167cwSB4gaT5hzAarFYWn4A","content":[{"title":"cargo-workspaces 0.4.2 - Docs.rs","url":"https://docs.rs/crate/cargo-workspaces/latest"},{"title":"GitHub - pksunkara/cargo-workspaces: A tool for managing cargo workspaces and their crates, inspired by lerna · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/pksunkara/cargo-workspaces"},{"title":"Updating dependencies | Knope","url":"https://knope.tech/recipes/updating-dependencies/"},{"title":"cargo-workspaces - crates.io: Rust Package Registry","url":"https://crates.io/crates/cargo-workspaces"},{"title":"GitHub - ava-labs/cargo-workspace-version: Cargo plugin to check and/or update all local package versions in a workspace · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/ava-labs/cargo-workspace-version"},{"title":"Knope — command-line utility in Rust // Lib.rs","url":"https://lib.rs/crates/knope"},{"title":"cargo-workspaces — Cargo add-on // Lib.rs","url":"https://lib.rs/crates/cargo-workspaces"},{"title":"cargo-release - crates.io: Rust Package Registry","url":"https://crates.io/crates/cargo-release"},{"title":"Packages | Knope","url":"https://knope.tech/reference/concepts/package/"},{"title":"GitHub - knope-dev/knope: A command line tool to handle all the tasks most developers find tedious. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/knope-dev/knope"}]},"Now let me search specifically for information about Knope's handling of changesets and version bumping in workspaces:",{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XUiiM2mDfKcVEjACJDvXdp","content":[{"title":"GitHub - knope-dev/changesets: A Rust crate for parsing and creating changesets—Markdown files describing releases","url":"https://github.com/knope-dev/changesets"},{"title":"changesets - crates.io: Rust Package Registry","url":"https://crates.io/crates/changesets/0.1.1"},{"title":"Changesets — Rust dev tool // Lib.rs","url":"https://lib.rs/crates/changesets"},{"title":"BumpVersion | Knope","url":"https://knope.tech/reference/config-file/steps/bump-version/"},{"title":"knope/CHANGELOG.md at main · knope-dev/knope","url":"https://github.com/knope-dev/knope/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md"},{"title":"Is it possible to bump major version based on latest published version? · changesets/changesets · Discussion #974","url":"https://github.com/changesets/changesets/discussions/974"},{"title":"PrepareRelease | Knope","url":"https://knope.tech/reference/config-file/steps/prepare-release/"},{"title":"Introduction - Knope","url":"https://knope-dev.github.io/knope/"},{"title":"GitHub - knope-dev/knope: A command line tool to handle all the tasks most developers find tedious. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/knope-dev/knope"},{"title":"ChangeSet | Knope","url":"https://knope.tech/reference/concepts/changeset/"}]},"Based on the search results, I can provide you with information about Knope's release tool and how it handles changesets with cargo workspaces:\n\n## Knope Release Tool Overview\n\nKnope is a command line tool that happily completes the tasks which most developers find tedious. Knope is a CLI/CI tool which automates common tasks for developers.\n\n## Changesets and Version Bumping\n\nA changeset is a set of change files in the .changeset directory. When creating a release, Knope combines every change file in the changeset (along with any conventional commits) to generate the changelog and decide the next version for each package.\n\nRegarding the \"highest bump wins\" approach you mentioned: When you release, if a package has multiple changes, the package would bump the version based on the highest change type. If a package has multiple changesets affecting it (for example, one with minor and one with patch), the version would be bumped based on the highest change type (in this case, minor).\n\n## Cargo Workspace Support\n\nYou get a GitHub release and a changelog, picking the semantic version based on the combination of conventional commits and changesets. Knope can work with Cargo workspaces, allowing it to manage versioning across multiple packages in a workspace by coordinating version bumps based on the changesets and conventional commits found in the repository."],"durationSeconds":8.451898541003466,"searchCount":2},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4ea2cef-b622-44ee-bf14-3a0032b54439","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
