{"parentUuid":"88563c7e-810a-4d79-8ea5-808fbf84ae1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGQ9yQ9Am9zH4Xx86kZU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checked the GH Action thoroughly — **no changes needed**. Concretely verified:\n\n- `callisto-action/action.yml`: `status --check` only reads the exit code (not JSON), `compose-pr-body` uses `--format text` (never touches the `pr_body`→`body` rename), `callisto tag`'s output is discarded (`|| true`, never parses the `created_tags`→`tags` rename), `callisto matrix`'s `jq` path (`.platformTargets[].targets[]`) already matches the real schema.\n- `callisto-validate/action.yml`: everything defaults to text output, no JSON parsing at all.\n- The action's own test script (`test_status_check_branching.sh`) still passes.\n- CI's OS matrix (`ubuntu-latest`/`macos-latest`) is unrelated to `callisto matrix` (that's napi/maturin platform targets, a different concern) — no wiring needed there.\n\n**Other things checked, nothing outstanding:**\n- No hardcoded version numbers anywhere in workflows/actions.\n- `docs/06-publishing.md`/`release-paradigms.md` are generic tool docs (for any callisto consumer), not this repo's own config notes — didn't need a fixed-group mention.\n- No stray `.valid`/`.pr_body`/`created_tags` references anywhere in `.github/`.\n\nI don't see anything else forgotten. PR #5 is in good shape: https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/5"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":763648,"output_tokens":906,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":409},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":76364