{"parentUuid":"ee94a049-7bf8-43b9-8e20-83680f09f175","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGQcM2d82E2mexLx2Ded","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017oSZLkYUbj5Gq4BnfcsRXe","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/changesets/changesets/blob/main/docs/prereleases.md","prompt":"How does changesets (@changesets/cli) represent or detect whether a specific release/tag is a pre-release vs a stable release? What field or terminology do they use?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3314,"cache_read_input_tokens":787716,"output_tokens":428,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":278},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3314,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":787716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3314},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGQcHZX9cNwDY9jp6dCF","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c48a50c-cc0c-48ca-bbe7-f560e185250e","timestamp":"2026-08-21T18:59:35.457Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"2c48a50c-cc0c-48ca-bbe7-f560e185250e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bda760ce-6576-45ed-9527-0e82452684f1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017oSZLkYUbj5Gq4BnfcsRXe","type":"tool_result","content":"# Changesets Prerelease Identification\n\nBased on the documentation, Changesets distinguishes prerelease from stable releases using **version tags and npm dist tags**.\n\n## Version Format\n\nPrerelease versions append a tag identifier to the version number. The documentation illustrates this with: `\"1.0.0-beta.0\"` format, where the tag (like \"beta\" or \"next\") follows a hyphen.\n\n## NPM Dist Tag\n\nThe critical mechanism is the **npm dist tag**. When entering prerelease mode with `pre enter <tag>`, that tag becomes the npm distribution marker. As stated in the guide: \"it will set the dist tag to the tag you specified when running the prerelease command.\"\n\nStable releases are published to the `latest` dist tag, while prerelease versions use custom tags (e.g., `next`, `beta`) that you designate during `pre enter`.\n\n## State Tracking\n\nChangesets maintains a `pre.json` file in the `.changeset` directory that \"stores information about the state the prerelease is in\" during prerelease mode.\n\nThis combination of version suffixes, custom dist tags, and the `pre.json` state file allows Changesets to clearly distinguish and manage prerelease versus stable releases."}]},"uuid":"9ff9319b-0ed4-40f5-8582-f9246690eef6","timestamp":"2026-08-21T18:59:42.503Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":265778,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Changesets Prerelease Identification\n\nBased on the documentation, Changesets distinguishes prerelease from stable releases using **version tags and npm dist tags**.\n\n## Version Format\n\nPrerelease versions append a tag identifier to the version number. The documentation illustrates this with: `\"1.0.0-beta.0\"` format, where the tag (like \"beta\" or \"next\") follows a hyphen.\n\n## NPM Dist Tag\n\nThe critical mechanism is the **npm dist tag**. When entering prerelease mode with `pre enter <tag>`, that tag becomes the npm distribution marker. As stated in the guide: \"it will set the dist tag to the tag you specified when running the prerelease command.\"\n\nStable releases are published to the `latest` dist tag, while prerelease versions use custom tags (e.g., `next`, `beta`) that you designate during `pre enter`.\n\n## State Tracking\n\nChangesets maintains a `pre.json` file in the `.changeset` directory that \"stores information about the state the prerelease is in\" during prerelease mode.\n\nThis combination of version suffixes, custom dist tags, and the `pre.json` state file allows Changesets to clearly distinguish and manage prerelease versus stable releases.","durationMs":5497,"url":"https://github.com/changesets/changesets/blob/main/docs/prereleases.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2c48a50c-cc0c-48ca-bbe7-f560e185250e","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
