{"parentUuid":"13c42489-2380-4119-acd5-69605c751491","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGQdRGeGTF8XhJF2PVQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — confirms my diagnosis. Changesets itself relies on parsing the SemVer string (no separate boolean either), but the GH Actions ecosystem's own `semver-tag` action *does* expose a proper `is-prerelease` boolean output — validating that a structured boolean field (rather than fragile regex) is the established, correct pattern once you have real version-parsing available, which callisto already does internally. Now running the full spec pipeline."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":925,"cache_read_input_tokens":791030,"output_tokens":3685,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":561},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":925,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3685,"cache_read_input_tokens":791030,"cache_creation_input_tokens":925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":925},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGQdMm4G9bJaTm14chdF","type":"assistant","uuid":"52e90126-13da-48ae-8db7-93b16a4d2177","timestamp":"2026-08-21T18:59:52.741Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"52e90126-13da-48ae-8db7-93b16a4d2177","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGQdRGeGTF8XhJF2PVQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ThAY8XvHnQj7S58yC3nL8A","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Draft spec for ReleaseEntry pre_release field","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"Draft a spec@1 for the following requirement. This is for \"callisto\", a Rust release/versioning CLI tool (AGPL-3.0 for callisto-graph/callisto-model's report types, MIT/Apache-2.0 for pure domain types). The workspace is at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto.\n\n## Requirement\n\n**Problem**: The shipped GitHub Action (`.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`, lines 200-216) creates a GitHub Release entry per tag in a publish plan, and needs to know whether each release is a pre-release (to pass `--prerelease` to `gh release create`). Today it guesses this via a fragile bash regex on the TAG STRING itself:\n\n```bash\nfor TAG in $(echo \"$PLAN_JSON\" | jq -r '.releases[]?.tagName // empty'); do\n  EXTRA_FLAGS=\"\"\n  if [[ \"$TAG\" =~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next) ]]; then\n    EXTRA_FLAGS=\"--prerelease\"\n  fi\n  gh release create \"$TAG\" --title \"$TAG\" --generate-notes $EXTRA_FLAGS || true\ndone\n```\n\nThis is wrong whenever a workspace uses a custom `tag_template` that doesn't literally embed one of those substrings (e.g. a tag template like `\"v{version}\"` where the version itself is `2.0.0-alpha.1` — the tag string would be `v2.0.0-alpha.1`, which DOES still match here, but a template omitting the raw version's prerelease suffix, or using a different prerelease naming scheme entirely, would silently misclassify). It's a workaround for missing data, not a deliberate design choice.\n\n**Root cause**: `ReleaseEntry` (defined in `crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs`, around line 111) has fields `package: PackageId`, `tag_name: TagName`, `sha: CommitSha`, and an optional `changelog_section: Option<String>` — but NO field indicating whether the release is a pre-release. Meanwhile, callisto's own `Version` type (in `callisto-format`/`callisto-model`, exact location TBD by your own research — grep for `is_prerelease` in the codebase, there is definitely an existing method with this or an equivalent name, already used internally for both SemVer and PEP 440 grammars, and a PEP 440 `is_prerelease` bug was just fixed this session) already knows how to correctly determine pre-release status from a real parsed `Version`, for both SemVer and PEP 440 grammars.\n\n**External precedent researched this session** (the user explicitly asked to check this before drafting): `@changesets/cli` doesn't expose a separate prerelease boolean either — it relies on parsing the SemVer string directly (same category of approach the current bash regex crudely imitates). However, the GitHub Actions ecosystem's own \"semver-tag\" action DOES expose a real `is-prerelease` boolean output as an established, working convention for exactly this need — validating that once real version-parsing is available (which callisto has), exposing a structured boolean is the correct, idiomatic fix rather than re-deriving it downstream via string matching.\n\n**Desired outcome**: `ReleaseEntry` should carry a new field (name TBD by you, but `is_prerelease` or `pre_release` matching Rust `bool` field naming conventions, and camelCase `isPrerelease`/`preRelease` in the `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]` JSON output that this crate's other types already use) that is TRUE if and only if the release's real, parsed `Version` reports itself as a pre-release, computed at the same place `plan_publish` (in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` — confirm the exact function/file by reading it) already constructs each `ReleaseEntry`, using the version that's ALREADY resolved and available at that construction site (do not re-derive it from the tag string; the real `Version` object is already in scope there — read the file to confirm).\n\nThe shipped GitHub Action script must then be updated to read this field via `jq` instead of regexing the tag string, e.g. something like:\n```bash\nIS_PRE=$(echo \"$PLAN_JSON\" | jq -r --arg tag \"$TAG\" '.releases[] | select(.tagName == $tag) | .isPrerelease')\n```\n(exact jq shape is an implementation detail — the acceptance criteria should specify the OBSERVABLE behavior: the Action correctly passes `--prerelease` to `gh release create` when and only when the release's actual parsed version is a pre-release, for BOTH SemVer and PEP 440 grammars, verified by a real fixture where the tag string itself does NOT contain any of the old regex's substrings but the version genuinely is a pre-release under whatever grammar).\n\n## Constraints and context you must incorporate\n\n1. **This is an additive JSON schema change** (new field on an already-public, already-serialized report type in a real AGPL-published-for-real crate). This project's own established policy this session: NO `schemaVersion` bump for additive report-field changes (confirmed: this project has never completed a real registry publish, so there's no external consumer depending on schema stability yet — see this session's Track 6-mechanical precedent, e.g. `StatusReport` gaining `hasChangesets`/`lastReleasedVersion`/`releaseTrigger` with no schema bump). Do NOT propose a schemaVersion bump.\n2. **Layer isolation invariant** (from this project's CLAUDE.md): `callisto-model` must remain MIT OR Apache-2.0 licensed and must never depend on AGPL crates. `ReleaseEntry` lives in `callisto-model`; whatever \"is this a prerelease\" logic gets reused must already be available in a Layer-1-safe way (it should be — `Version`/`is_prerelease` is domain-primitive logic, already in callisto-model or callisto-format, both permissively licensed. Confirm this via your own research, don't assume).\n3. **The GitHub Action script change is in scope** for this spec — `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`'s GitHub Release creation loop must be updated as part of this work, with a real test proving the new behavior (there's an existing test harness at `.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh` for this action — follow its established pattern/style for any new test script, or add to it, your call).\n4. **Docs**: `docs/01-spec.md` documents `ReleaseEntry`'s exact field list (search for it — I found references around line ~111-118 area conceptually, but the docs file has its own copy of this struct definition with doc comments; find and update it). Also check the README/ARCHITECTURE.md for any place that documents the GitHub Action's `--prerelease` behavior or `ReleaseEntry`'s shape, and update those too if found.\n5. **Tests**: must cover both SemVer (e.g. `1.2.3-alpha.1`) and PEP 440 (e.g. `1.2.3a1` or similar, matching whatever pattern existing PEP 440 prerelease tests in this codebase already use — grep for existing PEP 440 prerelease test fixtures to match the established format) grammars, proving `is_prerelease`/`pre_release` is computed correctly for each, via the real `plan_publish` pipeline (not just a unit test on the `Version` type in isolation, which likely already exists — this spec is specifically about `ReleaseEntry` carrying the RIGHT value end-to-end).\n6. **A regression test for the OLD bug** should exist: a fixture where the tag string does NOT match the old regex's alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substrings but the version genuinely is a pre-release (proving the NEW field-based approach doesn't have the same blind spot the regex did).\n\n## Process notes\n\nThis project follows a full canon → vector → lambda pipeline for schema/architecture-significant changes (this qualifies: new field on a public report type, cross-cutting into the shipped Action script). Draft the spec@1 now. Do not implement anything — spec only. Read the actual current code (`crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs`, wherever `is_prerelease` currently lives, `docs/01-spec.md`'s ReleaseEntry section, `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`) before finalizing acceptance criteria — do not guess at exact current field names, function signatures, or line numbers; verify them."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":925,"cache_read_input_tokens":791030,"output_tokens":3685,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":561},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":925,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3685,"cache_read_input_tokens":791030,"cache_creation_input_tokens":925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":925},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGQdMm4G9bJaTm14chdF","type":"assistant","uuid":"35e140b1-66af-444e-964a-0b20c89ffb2d","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:00:24.910Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
