{"parentUuid":"a52e5b82-659b-4b0f-912f-f4ed4120d265","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGRNozpyN3dYna87EQU5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5334,"cache_read_input_tokens":814453,"output_tokens":5335,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":114},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5334,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5335,"cache_read_input_tokens":814453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5334},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGRNm5i8dRduLwnBf9WZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"9cf48b0f-332f-4412-8489-bd433b45adc7","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:09:34.892Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"9cf48b0f-332f-4412-8489-bd433b45adc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGRNozpyN3dYna87EQU5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ax4jCW54HeB1Kt2PsxNvek","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-005\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Replace the GitHub Action's regex-on-tag-string guess for GitHub Release pre-release status with a real, parsed boolean carried on ReleaseEntry, so `--prerelease` is passed to `gh release create` based on the actual SemVer/PEP 440 pre-release status of the release's resolved Version, not on whether the rendered tag string happens to contain one of a fixed set of substrings.\",\n  \"scope\": \"1. Add a new required boolean field to `ReleaseEntry` in crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs. 2. Populate that field at the one construction site of ReleaseEntry in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (plan_publish, inside the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block, currently lines 505-510), computed from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope at that call site via its existing `is_prerelease()` method. 3. Update .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (currently lines 200-216) to read the new field via `jq` instead of regex-matching `$TAG`, hard-failing if the field is absent rather than defaulting to false. 4. Add a new test to .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ following the extraction-and-stub pattern established in test_status_check_branching.sh, proving the new loop's behavior for both a SemVer and a PEP 440 fixture, including the regression fixture for the original bug and the missing-field hard-fail case. 5. Update docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry field documentation (struct doc block at lines 1740-1763 and the decision-table row referencing §M.12.2 at line 2667) to list the new field.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"No `schemaVersion` bump on PublishPlan/ReleaseEntry's JSON schema -- this is an additive field, consistent with this session's established precedent (StatusReport's hasChangesets/lastReleasedVersion/releaseTrigger additions shipped with no schemaVersion bump).\",\n    \"No change to plan_publish's function signature or parameters. `ver: &Version` is already in scope at the ReleaseEntry construction site (publish.rs line 75 parameter, used at line 507-509); no new parameter or return type is introduced.\",\n    \"No change to Version::is_prerelease()'s SemVer/PEP 440 parsing logic itself (crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:126-131) -- it is reused as-is, not modified or re-implemented.\",\n    \"No fallback regex path retained in action.yml for any reason (e.g. absent field, older plan JSON) -- the regex-based `[[ \\\"$TAG\\\" =~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next) ]]` branch is removed entirely, not kept as a secondary check, since the Action always invokes a freshly-built `callisto plan-publish --format json` in the same run and there is no cross-version JSON compatibility boundary to bridge. A missing `isPrerelease` key is a hard error (AC-015), never a silent false.\",\n    \"No changes to NpmMainPublish, NpmPublish, PypiPublish, or any other PublishPlan entry type -- only ReleaseEntry gains this field.\",\n    \"No reconciliation of the pre-existing, unrelated drift where docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry doc block (lines 1740-1763) omits the `package`/`PackageId` field that the live struct (crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs:111-118) already has -- that gap predates this change and is out of scope here; only the new field is added to the doc.\",\n    \"No update to README.md or ARCHITECTURE.md -- neither file documents ReleaseEntry's field shape or the Action's --prerelease behavior today (confirmed by grep), so neither requires a change under this spec.\",\n    \"No change to how `gh release create`'s other flags (`--title`, `--generate-notes`) are derived -- only the `--prerelease` flag's derivation changes.\",\n    \"This spec's edit to the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (lines 505-510) touches the same struct literal that SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS's AC-10/AC-10b/AC-11/AC-12 already modified (populating `changelog_section`) earlier in this session -- that spec is already implemented and committed, so this spec's diff is against the post-TRACK4 state of that block (which already includes `changelog_section`), not the pre-TRACK4 hardcoded-`None` state. No field ordering within the literal is prescribed beyond `is_prerelease` being present as a keyed field.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub is_prerelease: bool  // in crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs, struct ReleaseEntry (currently lines 111-118), under #[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, JsonSchema)] and #[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")] -> JSON key \\\"isPrerelease\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"New required (non-Option, no skip_serializing_if) boolean field on ReleaseEntry. Always present in every serialized ReleaseEntry, including PublishPlan.releases[] JSON emitted by `callisto plan-publish --format json`.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Version::is_prerelease\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub fn is_prerelease(&self) -> bool  // crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:126-131 (unchanged; reused, not modified)\",\n      \"description\": \"Existing method on callisto_model::Version, already correct for both grammars: for SemVer, true iff `!v.pre.is_empty()`; for PEP 440, true iff `!v.is_post() && (v.is_pre() || v.is_dev())`. This is the single source of truth ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease must be derived from at construction time -- never re-derived from a tag string.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-001\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs's ReleaseEntry struct has a new field `is_prerelease: bool` with no `Option` wrapper and no `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = ...)]` attribute, so the field appears in every serialized ReleaseEntry's JSON output as the key \\\"isPrerelease\\\" (per the struct's existing `#[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")]`), never omitted.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-002\", \"criterion\": \"Running `callisto plan-publish --format json` in a workspace with at least one publishable package produces a PublishPlan JSON whose `releases[]` entries each contain an `isPrerelease` boolean key (in addition to the existing `tagName`, `sha`, and optional `changelogSection` keys).\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-003\", \"criterion\": \"For a package P whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.2.3` (no pre-release component), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId -- there is exactly one such entry per package per invocation -- has `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-004\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (SemVer): for a package P whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.0.0-1` (a valid SemVer pre-release with a purely numeric identifier, containing none of the substrings \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-005\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (PEP 440, the original bug this spec exists to fix): for a package P whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.2.3a1` (a canonical PEP 440 pre-release with no dash and no substring match against \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string, e.g. tag `v1.2.3a1`), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-006\", \"criterion\": \"For a package P whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.0.0.dev1` (a dev-release, which the codebase's existing `Version::is_prerelease()` test `pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease` at crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:365 already asserts must be treated as pre-release), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`, proving the field is computed via `Version::is_prerelease()` end-to-end through plan_publish rather than a narrower ad hoc check that only recognizes alpha/beta/rc.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-007\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease is computed at its one construction site in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block) directly from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope there, by calling `ver.is_prerelease()` -- confirmable by inspecting that no new call to `Version::parse`, no string parsing of `tag_name`, and no regex against the tag string appears anywhere in that construction path.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-008\", \"criterion\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block) no longer contains the pattern `=~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)` anywhere in its script body.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-009\", \"criterion\": \"For each tag processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop, `gh release create \\\"$TAG\\\" --title \\\"$TAG\\\" --generate-notes` is invoked with the additional flag `--prerelease` if and only if that tag's matching entry in `$PLAN_JSON`'s `releases[]` array has `isPrerelease: true`; when `isPrerelease` is `false`, the same `gh release create` invocation runs with no `--prerelease` flag.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-010\", \"criterion\": \"A new test file under .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ (either a new script or an extension of test_status_check_branching.sh) follows the same established harness pattern -- it extracts the exact current run-body text of the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block directly out of action.yml via a `sed` range between its `::group::` and matching `::endgroup::` markers, stubs `gh` (and `jq` remains real) to capture invocation arguments, feeds it a fixture `$PLAN_JSON` value, and asserts on the captured `gh release create` argument list -- so the test cannot drift from action.yml's actual current logic. This test includes at minimum: one case with `isPrerelease: true` where the tag string contains no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring (the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture), one case with `isPrerelease: false`, and one case covering AC-015 (missing `isPrerelease` key).\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-011\", \"criterion\": \"docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry struct documentation block (the section spanning the struct doc comments immediately preceding `pub struct ReleaseEntry` at line 1742, and the decision-table row at line 2667 referencing §M.12.2) is updated to list the new `is_prerelease` / `isPrerelease` field alongside the existing documented fields (`tag_name`, `sha`, `changelog_section`), stating that it is a required (non-optional) boolean.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-012a\", \"criterion\": \"Every existing golden-file or snapshot test in callisto-graph or callisto-fixtures asserting the JSON shape of a ReleaseEntry is updated to include the `isPrerelease` key at its expected value.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-012b\", \"criterion\": \"`just test` / `moon run :test` exits 0 after this change, with no remaining test asserting a ReleaseEntry JSON shape that omits `isPrerelease`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-013\", \"criterion\": \"A grep of crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's plan_publish function shows no default-false fallback, no `Result`/`Option` wrapping, and no new conditional branch introduced around the `ver.is_prerelease()` call added for ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease -- consistent with `ver: &Version` at that call site already being a successfully-parsed, non-optional value, so no malformed-version error path is reachable or needed at this construction site.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-014\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry's `is_prerelease` field computation introduces no new dependency edge from callisto-model to any AGPL-licensed crate: `Version::is_prerelease()` is defined and remains defined in crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs, a crate whose Cargo.toml declares `license = \\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\"` and whose `[dependencies]` list (semver, pep440_rs, serde, serde_json, thiserror, miette, camino, path-slash, schemars, tempfile) contains no AGPL crate; `cargo metadata`'s resolve graph for callisto-model shows no edge to any crate licensed AGPL after this change.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-015\", \"criterion\": \"For a tag processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop whose matching `releases[]` entry in `$PLAN_JSON` has no `isPrerelease` key at all (e.g. a stale cached plan, a hand-edited fixture, or a plan produced by a pre-this-change callisto binary), the step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error message naming the offending tag, before any `gh release create` call is made for that tag -- the missing key is never silently treated as `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": true }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-008\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5334,"cache_read_input_tokens":814453,"output_tokens":5335,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":114},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5334,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5335,"cache_read_input_tokens":814453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5334},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGRNm5i8dRduLwnBf9WZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf88a588-49d2-4e4c-b3db-b740d1f75bfd","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:10:12.241Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"bf88a588-49d2-4e4c-b3db-b740d1f75bfd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6ed687cd-73ac-42da-8a69-13f26f4fa10b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ax4jCW54HeB1Kt2PsxNvek","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"950b306d-559d-4fc9-b4c3-b56833c2fef6","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:10:14.362Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-005\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Replace the GitHub Action's regex-on-tag-string guess for GitHub Release pre-release status with a real, parsed boolean carried on ReleaseEntry, so `--prerelease` is passed to `gh release create` based on the actual SemVer/PEP 440 pre-release status of the release's resolved Version, not on whether the rendered tag string happens to contain one of a fixed set of substrings.\",\n  \"scope\": \"1. Add a new required boolean field to `ReleaseEntry` in crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs. 2. Populate that field at the one construction site of ReleaseEntry in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (plan_publish, inside the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block, currently lines 505-510), computed from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope at that call site via its existing `is_prerelease()` method. 3. Update .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (currently lines 200-216) to read the new field via `jq` instead of regex-matching `$TAG`, hard-failing if the field is absent rather than defaulting to false. 4. Add a new test to .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ following the extraction-and-stub pattern established in test_status_check_branching.sh, proving the new loop's behavior for both a SemVer and a PEP 440 fixture, including the regression fixture for the original bug and the missing-field hard-fail case. 5. Update docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry field documentation (struct doc block at lines 1740-1763 and the decision-table row referencing §M.12.2 at line 2667) to list the new field.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"No `schemaVersion` bump on PublishPlan/ReleaseEntry's JSON schema -- this is an additive field, consistent with this session's established precedent (StatusReport's hasChangesets/lastReleasedVersion/releaseTrigger additions shipped with no schemaVersion bump).\",\n    \"No change to plan_publish's function signature or parameters. `ver: &Version` is already in scope at the ReleaseEntry construction site (publish.rs line 75 parameter, used at line 507-509); no new parameter or return type is introduced.\",\n    \"No change to Version::is_prerelease()'s SemVer/PEP 440 parsing logic itself (crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:126-131) -- it is reused as-is, not modified or re-implemented.\",\n    \"No fallback regex path retained in action.yml for any reason (e.g. absent field, older plan JSON) -- the regex-based `[[ \\\"$TAG\\\" =~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next) ]]` branch is removed entirely, not kept as a secondary check, since the Action always invokes a freshly-built `callisto plan-publish --format json` in the same run and there is no cross-version JSON compatibility boundary to bridge. A missing `isPrerelease` key is a hard error (AC-015), never a silent false.\",\n    \"No changes to NpmMainPublish, NpmPublish, PypiPublish, or any other PublishPlan entry type -- only ReleaseEntry gains this field.\",\n    \"No reconciliation of the pre-existing, unrelated drift where docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry doc block (lines 1740-1763) omits the `package`/`PackageId` field that the live struct (crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs:111-118) already has -- that gap predates this change and is out of scope here; only the new field is added to the doc.\",\n    \"No update to README.md or ARCHITECTURE.md -- neither file documents ReleaseEntry's field shape or the Action's --prerelease behavior today (confirmed by grep), so neither requires a change under this spec.\",\n    \"No change to how `gh release create`'s other flags (`--title`, `--generate-notes`) are derived -- only the `--prerelease` flag's derivation changes.\",\n    \"This spec's edit to the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (lines 505-510) touches the same struct literal that SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS's AC-10/AC-10b/AC-11/AC-12 already modified (populating `changelog_section`) earlier in this session -- that spec is already implemented and committed, so this spec's diff is against the post-TRACK4 state of that block (which already includes `changelog_section`), not the pre-TRACK4 hardcoded-`None` state. No field ordering within the literal is prescribed beyond `is_prerelease` being present as a keyed field.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub is_prerelease: bool  // in crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs, struct ReleaseEntry (currently lines 111-118), under #[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, JsonSchema)] and #[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")] -> JSON key \\\"isPrerelease\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"New required (non-Option, no skip_serializing_if) boolean field on ReleaseEntry. Always present in every serialized ReleaseEntry, including PublishPlan.releases[] JSON emitted by `callisto plan-publish --format json`.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Version::is_prerelease\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub fn is_prerelease(&self) -> bool  // crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:126-131 (unchanged; reused, not modified)\",\n      \"description\": \"Existing method on callisto_model::Version, already correct for both grammars: for SemVer, true iff `!v.pre.is_empty()`; for PEP 440, true iff `!v.is_post() && (v.is_pre() || v.is_dev())`. This is the single source of truth ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease must be derived from at construction time -- never re-derived from a tag string.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-001\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs's ReleaseEntry struct has a new field `is_prerelease: bool` with no `Option` wrapper and no `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = ...)]` attribute, so the field appears in every serialized ReleaseEntry's JSON output as the key \\\"isPrerelease\\\" (per the struct's existing `#[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")]`), never omitted.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-002\", \"criterion\": \"Running `callisto plan-publish --format json` in a workspace with at least one publishable package produces a PublishPlan JSON whose `releases[]` entries each contain an `isPrerelease` boolean key (in addition to the existing `tagName`, `sha`, and optional `changelogSection` keys).\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-003\", \"criterion\": \"For a package P whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.2.3` (no pre-release component), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId -- there is exactly one such entry per package per invocation -- has `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-004\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (SemVer): for a package P whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.0.0-1` (a valid SemVer pre-release with a purely numeric identifier, containing none of the substrings \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-005\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (PEP 440, the original bug this spec exists to fix): for a package P whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.2.3a1` (a canonical PEP 440 pre-release with no dash and no substring match against \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string, e.g. tag `v1.2.3a1`), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-006\", \"criterion\": \"For a package P whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.0.0.dev1` (a dev-release, which the codebase's existing `Version::is_prerelease()` test `pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease` at crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:365 already asserts must be treated as pre-release), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`, proving the field is computed via `Version::is_prerelease()` end-to-end through plan_publish rather than a narrower ad hoc check that only recognizes alpha/beta/rc.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-007\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease is computed at its one construction site in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block) directly from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope there, by calling `ver.is_prerelease()` -- confirmable by inspecting that no new call to `Version::parse`, no string parsing of `tag_name`, and no regex against the tag string appears anywhere in that construction path.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-008\", \"criterion\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block) no longer contains the pattern `=~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)` anywhere in its script body.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-009\", \"criterion\": \"For each tag processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop, `gh release create \\\"$TAG\\\" --title \\\"$TAG\\\" --generate-notes` is invoked with the additional flag `--prerelease` if and only if that tag's matching entry in `$PLAN_JSON`'s `releases[]` array has `isPrerelease: true`; when `isPrerelease` is `false`, the same `gh release create` invocation runs with no `--prerelease` flag.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-010\", \"criterion\": \"A new test file under .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ (either a new script or an extension of test_status_check_branching.sh) follows the same established harness pattern -- it extracts the exact current run-body text of the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block directly out of action.yml via a `sed` range between its `::group::` and matching `::endgroup::` markers, stubs `gh` (and `jq` remains real) to capture invocation arguments, feeds it a fixture `$PLAN_JSON` value, and asserts on the captured `gh release create` argument list -- so the test cannot drift from action.yml's actual current logic. This test includes at minimum: one case with `isPrerelease: true` where the tag string contains no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring (the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture), one case with `isPrerelease: false`, and one case covering AC-015 (missing `isPrerelease` key).\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-011\", \"criterion\": \"docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry struct documentation block (the section spanning the struct doc comments immediately preceding `pub struct ReleaseEntry` at line 1742, and the decision-table row at line 2667 referencing §M.12.2) is updated to list the new `is_prerelease` / `isPrerelease` field alongside the existing documented fields (`tag_name`, `sha`, `changelog_section`), stating that it is a required (non-optional) boolean.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-012a\", \"criterion\": \"Every existing golden-file or snapshot test in callisto-graph or callisto-fixtures asserting the JSON shape of a ReleaseEntry is updated to include the `isPrerelease` key at its expected value.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-012b\", \"criterion\": \"`just test` / `moon run :test` exits 0 after this change, with no remaining test asserting a ReleaseEntry JSON shape that omits `isPrerelease`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-013\", \"criterion\": \"A grep of crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's plan_publish function shows no default-false fallback, no `Result`/`Option` wrapping, and no new conditional branch introduced around the `ver.is_prerelease()` call added for ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease -- consistent with `ver: &Version` at that call site already being a successfully-parsed, non-optional value, so no malformed-version error path is reachable or needed at this construction site.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-014\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry's `is_prerelease` field computation introduces no new dependency edge from callisto-model to any AGPL-licensed crate: `Version::is_prerelease()` is defined and remains defined in crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs, a crate whose Cargo.toml declares `license = \\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\"` and whose `[dependencies]` list (semver, pep440_rs, serde, serde_json, thiserror, miette, camino, path-slash, schemars, tempfile) contains no AGPL crate; `cargo metadata`'s resolve graph for callisto-model shows no edge to any crate licensed AGPL after this change.\", \"is_error_case\": false },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-015\", \"criterion\": \"For a tag processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop whose matching `releases[]` entry in `$PLAN_JSON` has no `isPrerelease` key at all (e.g. a stale cached plan, a hand-edited fixture, or a plan produced by a pre-this-change callisto binary), the step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error message naming the offending tag, before any `gh release create` call is made for that tag -- the missing key is never silently treated as `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": true }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-008\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":16,"newStart":1,"newLines":17,"lines":[" {","   \"id\": \"SPEC-005\",","   \"purpose\": \"Replace the GitHub Action's regex-on-tag-string guess for GitHub Release pre-release status with a real, parsed boolean carried on ReleaseEntry, so `--prerelease` is passed to `gh release create` based on the actual SemVer/PEP 440 pre-release status of the release's resolved Version, not on whether the rendered tag string happens to contain one of a fixed set of substrings.\",","-  \"scope\": \"1. Add a new required boolean field to `ReleaseEntry` in crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs. 2. Populate that field at the one construction site of ReleaseEntry in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (plan_publish, inside the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block, currently lines 505-510), computed from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope at that call site via its existing `is_prerelease()` method. 3. Update .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (currently lines 200-216) to read the new field via `jq` instead of regex-matching `$TAG`. 4. Add a new test to .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ following the extraction-and-stub pattern established in test_status_check_branching.sh, proving the new loop's behavior for both a SemVer and a PEP 440 fixture, including the regression fixture for the original bug. 5. Update docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry field documentation (struct doc block at lines 1740-1763 and the decision-table row referencing §M.12.2 at line 2667) to list the new field.\",","+  \"scope\": \"1. Add a new required boolean field to `ReleaseEntry` in crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs. 2. Populate that field at the one construction site of ReleaseEntry in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (plan_publish, inside the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block, currently lines 505-510), computed from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope at that call site via its existing `is_prerelease()` method. 3. Update .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (currently lines 200-216) to read the new field via `jq` instead of regex-matching `$TAG`, hard-failing if the field is absent rather than defaulting to false. 4. Add a new test to .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ following the extraction-and-stub pattern established in test_status_check_branching.sh, proving the new loop's behavior for both a SemVer and a PEP 440 fixture, including the regression fixture for the original bug and the missing-field hard-fail case. 5. Update docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry field documentation (struct doc block at lines 1740-1763 and the decision-table row referencing §M.12.2 at line 2667) to list the new field.\",","   \"non_goals\": [","     \"No `schemaVersion` bump on PublishPlan/ReleaseEntry's JSON schema -- this is an additive field, consistent with this session's established precedent (StatusReport's hasChangesets/lastReleasedVersion/releaseTrigger additions shipped with no schemaVersion bump).\",","     \"No change to plan_publish's function signature or parameters. `ver: &Version` is already in scope at the ReleaseEntry construction site (publish.rs line 75 parameter, used at line 507-509); no new parameter or return type is introduced.\",","     \"No change to Version::is_prerelease()'s SemVer/PEP 440 parsing logic itself (crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:126-131) -- it is reused as-is, not modified or re-implemented.\",","-    \"No fallback regex path retained in action.yml for any reason (e.g. absent field, older plan JSON) -- the regex-based `[[ \\\"$TAG\\\" =~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next) ]]` branch is removed entirely, not kept as a secondary check, since the Action always invokes a freshly-built `callisto plan-publish --format json` in the same run and there is no cross-version JSON compatibility boundary to bridge.\",","+    \"No fallback regex path retained in action.yml for any reason (e.g. absent field, older plan JSON) -- the regex-based `[[ \\\"$TAG\\\" =~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next) ]]` branch is removed entirely, not kept as a secondary check, since the Action always invokes a freshly-built `callisto plan-publish --format json` in the same run and there is no cross-version JSON compatibility boundary to bridge. A missing `isPrerelease` key is a hard error (AC-015), never a silent false.\",","     \"No changes to NpmMainPublish, NpmPublish, PypiPublish, or any other PublishPlan entry type -- only ReleaseEntry gains this field.\",","     \"No reconciliation of the pre-existing, unrelated drift where docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry doc block (lines 1740-1763) omits the `package`/`PackageId` field that the live struct (crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs:111-118) already has -- that gap predates this change and is out of scope here; only the new field is added to the doc.\",","     \"No update to README.md or ARCHITECTURE.md -- neither file documents ReleaseEntry's field shape or the Action's --prerelease behavior today (confirmed by grep), so neither requires a change under this spec.\",","-    \"No change to how `gh release create`'s other flags (`--title`, `--generate-notes`) are derived -- only the `--prerelease` flag's derivation changes.\"","+    \"No change to how `gh release create`'s other flags (`--title`, `--generate-notes`) are derived -- only the `--prerelease` flag's derivation changes.\",","+    \"This spec's edit to the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (lines 505-510) touches the same struct literal that SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS's AC-10/AC-10b/AC-11/AC-12 already modified (populating `changelog_section`) earlier in this session -- that spec is already implemented and committed, so this spec's diff is against the post-TRACK4 state of that block (which already includes `changelog_section`), not the pre-TRACK4 hardcoded-`None` state. No field ordering within the literal is prescribed beyond `is_prerelease` being present as a keyed field.\"","   ],","   \"api_surface\": [","     {"]},{"oldStart":27,"oldLines":18,"newStart":28,"newLines":20,"lines":["   \"acceptance_criteria\": [","     { \"id\": \"AC-001\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs's ReleaseEntry struct has a new field `is_prerelease: bool` with no `Option` wrapper and no `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = ...)]` attribute, so the field appears in every serialized ReleaseEntry's JSON output as the key \\\"isPrerelease\\\" (per the struct's existing `#[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")]`), never omitted.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","     { \"id\": \"AC-002\", \"criterion\": \"Running `callisto plan-publish --format json` in a workspace with at least one publishable package produces a PublishPlan JSON whose `releases[]` entries each contain an `isPrerelease` boolean key (in addition to the existing `tagName`, `sha`, and optional `changelogSection` keys).\", \"is_error_case\": false },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-003\", \"criterion\": \"For a package whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.2.3` (no pre-release component), the corresponding entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array has `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-004\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (SemVer): for a package whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.0.0-1` (a valid SemVer pre-release with a purely numeric identifier, containing none of the substrings \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string), the corresponding entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-005\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (PEP 440, the original bug this spec exists to fix): for a package whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.2.3a1` (a canonical PEP 440 pre-release with no dash and no substring match against \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string, e.g. tag `v1.2.3a1`), the corresponding entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-006\", \"criterion\": \"For a package whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.0.0.dev1` (a dev-release, which the codebase's existing `Version::is_prerelease()` test `pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease` at crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:365 already asserts must be treated as pre-release), the corresponding `releases[]` entry has `isPrerelease: true`, proving the field is computed via `Version::is_prerelease()` end-to-end through plan_publish rather than a narrower ad hoc check that only recognizes alpha/beta/rc.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-003\", \"criterion\": \"For a package P whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.2.3` (no pre-release component), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId -- there is exactly one such entry per package per invocation -- has `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-004\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (SemVer): for a package P whose resolved release version is the SemVer value `1.0.0-1` (a valid SemVer pre-release with a purely numeric identifier, containing none of the substrings \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-005\", \"criterion\": \"Regression fixture (PEP 440, the original bug this spec exists to fix): for a package P whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.2.3a1` (a canonical PEP 440 pre-release with no dash and no substring match against \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"rc\\\", \\\"pre\\\", or \\\"next\\\" anywhere in its rendered tag string, e.g. tag `v1.2.3a1`), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-006\", \"criterion\": \"For a package P whose resolved release version is the PEP 440 value `1.0.0.dev1` (a dev-release, which the codebase's existing `Version::is_prerelease()` test `pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease` at crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:365 already asserts must be treated as pre-release), the entry in `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s `releases[]` array whose `package` field equals P's PackageId has `isPrerelease: true`, proving the field is computed via `Version::is_prerelease()` end-to-end through plan_publish rather than a narrower ad hoc check that only recognizes alpha/beta/rc.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","     { \"id\": \"AC-007\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease is computed at its one construction site in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block) directly from the `ver: &Version` value already resolved and in scope there, by calling `ver.is_prerelease()` -- confirmable by inspecting that no new call to `Version::parse`, no string parsing of `tag_name`, and no regex against the tag string appears anywhere in that construction path.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","     { \"id\": \"AC-008\", \"criterion\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block) no longer contains the pattern `=~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)` anywhere in its script body.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","     { \"id\": \"AC-009\", \"criterion\": \"For each tag processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop, `gh release create \\\"$TAG\\\" --title \\\"$TAG\\\" --generate-notes` is invoked with the additional flag `--prerelease` if and only if that tag's matching entry in `$PLAN_JSON`'s `releases[]` array has `isPrerelease: true`; when `isPrerelease` is `false`, the same `gh release create` invocation runs with no `--prerelease` flag.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-010\", \"criterion\": \"A new test file under .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ (either a new script or an extension of test_status_check_branching.sh) follows the same established harness pattern -- it extracts the exact current run-body text of the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block directly out of action.yml via a `sed` range between its `::group::` and matching `::endgroup::` markers, stubs `gh` (and `jq` remains real) to capture invocation arguments, feeds it a fixture `$PLAN_JSON` value, and asserts on the captured `gh release create` argument list -- so the test cannot drift from action.yml's actual current logic. This test includes at minimum: one case with `isPrerelease: true` where the tag string contains no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring (the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture), and one case with `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-010\", \"criterion\": \"A new test file under .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ (either a new script or an extension of test_status_check_branching.sh) follows the same established harness pattern -- it extracts the exact current run-body text of the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block directly out of action.yml via a `sed` range between its `::group::` and matching `::endgroup::` markers, stubs `gh` (and `jq` remains real) to capture invocation arguments, feeds it a fixture `$PLAN_JSON` value, and asserts on the captured `gh release create` argument list -- so the test cannot drift from action.yml's actual current logic. This test includes at minimum: one case with `isPrerelease: true` where the tag string contains no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring (the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture), one case with `isPrerelease: false`, and one case covering AC-015 (missing `isPrerelease` key).\", \"is_error_case\": false },","     { \"id\": \"AC-011\", \"criterion\": \"docs/01-spec.md's ReleaseEntry struct documentation block (the section spanning the struct doc comments immediately preceding `pub struct ReleaseEntry` at line 1742, and the decision-table row at line 2667 referencing §M.12.2) is updated to list the new `is_prerelease` / `isPrerelease` field alongside the existing documented fields (`tag_name`, `sha`, `changelog_section`), stating that it is a required (non-optional) boolean.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-012\", \"criterion\": \"No existing test asserting the JSON shape of a ReleaseEntry (e.g. golden-file or snapshot tests in callisto-graph or callisto-fixtures covering PublishPlan/ReleaseEntry serialization) is left asserting the pre-change shape without `isPrerelease` -- every such test is updated to expect the new field, and the full workspace test suite (`just test` / `moon run :test`) passes with the field present.\", \"is_error_case\": true },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-013\", \"criterion\": \"Because `ver` at ReleaseEntry's construction site in publish.rs is already typed as `&callisto_model::Version` (a value that can only exist as the result of a prior successful `Version::parse` earlier in the pipeline, before plan_publish's package-processing loop runs), there is no code path at the ReleaseEntry construction site where `is_prerelease` is computed from an unparseable or malformed version string -- Rust's type system rules out that error case at this call site, so no error-handling branch (e.g. a default-false fallback) needs to exist there, and none should be added.\", \"is_error_case\": true },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-014\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry's `is_prerelease` field computation introduces no new dependency edge from callisto-model to any AGPL-licensed crate: `Version::is_prerelease()` is defined and remains defined in crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs, a crate whose Cargo.toml declares `license = \\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\"` and whose `[dependencies]` list (semver, pep440_rs, serde, serde_json, thiserror, miette, camino, path-slash, schemars, tempfile) contains no AGPL crate; `cargo metadata`'s resolve graph for callisto-model shows no edge to any crate licensed AGPL after this change.\", \"is_error_case\": false }","+    { \"id\": \"AC-012a\", \"criterion\": \"Every existing golden-file or snapshot test in callisto-graph or callisto-fixtures asserting the JSON shape of a ReleaseEntry is updated to include the `isPrerelease` key at its expected value.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-012b\", \"criterion\": \"`just test` / `moon run :test` exits 0 after this change, with no remaining test asserting a ReleaseEntry JSON shape that omits `isPrerelease`.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-013\", \"criterion\": \"A grep of crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's plan_publish function shows no default-false fallback, no `Result`/`Option` wrapping, and no new conditional branch introduced around the `ver.is_prerelease()` call added for ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease -- consistent with `ver: &Version` at that call site already being a successfully-parsed, non-optional value, so no malformed-version error path is reachable or needed at this construction site.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-014\", \"criterion\": \"ReleaseEntry's `is_prerelease` field computation introduces no new dependency edge from callisto-model to any AGPL-licensed crate: `Version::is_prerelease()` is defined and remains defined in crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs, a crate whose Cargo.toml declares `license = \\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\"` and whose `[dependencies]` list (semver, pep440_rs, serde, serde_json, thiserror, miette, camino, path-slash, schemars, tempfile) contains no AGPL crate; `cargo metadata`'s resolve graph for callisto-model shows no edge to any crate licensed AGPL after this change.\", \"is_error_case\": false },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-015\", \"criterion\": \"For a tag processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop whose matching `releases[]` entry in `$PLAN_JSON` has no `isPrerelease` key at all (e.g. a stale cached plan, a hand-edited fixture, or a plan produced by a pre-this-change callisto binary), the step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error message naming the offending tag, before any `gh release create` call is made for that tag -- the missing key is never silently treated as `isPrerelease: false`.\", \"is_error_case\": true }","   ],","   \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-008\""," }"]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf88a588-49d2-4e4c-b3db-b740d1f75bfd","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
