{"parentUuid":"4c34e9df-5f8f-4d48-9ae2-3768cec9bb27","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7ed5957d-108e-4fd8-acb1-51f673edf70f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5bce6bf3adfef360</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01XzZBJcBENJ1BRA8RBbcGZe</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a5bce6bf3adfef360.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate SPEC-005\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I read the spec and verified every factual claim it makes against the live codebase. Here is the binding verdict.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"retry_count\": 1,\n  \"verdict_summary\": \"FAIL (retry 1). No TBDs, and most criteria are testable, but AC-012a names the wrong crates and artifact class and misses the tests that actually break; AC-009/AC-015 omit the tag-to-entry correlation key; AC-007/AC-013 misstate `ver`. Five blockers; fix and resubmit before planning.\",\n  \"blockers\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-012a\",\n      \"location\": \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs:1-6, :92, :95; crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs:357; crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs:98; crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs:23,111,273,404,410\",\n      \"finding\": \"AC-012a is scoped to 'golden-file or snapshot test in callisto-graph or callisto-fixtures asserting the JSON shape of a ReleaseEntry'. Both halves of that scoping are wrong. (1) Wrong crate: callisto-fixtures contains no reference to `releases` at all (grep: zero hits), while the test that actually breaks lives in callisto-cli — schema_guard_test.rs:92 asserts `req == set([\\\"package\\\",\\\"sha\\\",\\\"tagName\\\"])` and :95 asserts `props == set([\\\"changelogSection\\\",\\\"package\\\",\\\"sha\\\",\\\"tagName\\\"])` against `callisto schema --type` output. A required `isPrerelease` breaks both. (2) Wrong artifact class: adding a non-Option field breaks eight Rust *struct literals*, not JSON assertions — callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs:357, callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs:98, and callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs at 23, 111, 273, 404, 410. These are compile errors, and none is a 'golden-file or snapshot test asserting the JSON shape'. (3) Unauthorized contract decision: schema_guard_test.rs's module doc (lines 1-6) states 'none of this track's fixes may change any report struct's field shape, except where a task's explicit scope is the shape change itself' and carries an explicit allowlist of permitted schema deltas. No criterion in SPEC-005 authorizes amending that allowlist, so an implementer hitting the failure must decide unilaterally whether this spec permits it — a follow-up question. Required change: replace AC-012a with three criteria. (a) 'crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs's ReleaseEntry assertions are updated to req == {isPrerelease, package, sha, tagName} and props == {changelogSection, isPrerelease, package, sha, tagName}, and its module-doc permitted-schema-delta list (lines 1-6) gains an entry naming ReleaseEntry.isPrerelease as an intentional additive required field.' (b) 'Every ReleaseEntry struct literal in the workspace — callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs:357, callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs:98, callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs:23,111,273,404,410 — sets is_prerelease explicitly; no Default impl is added to ReleaseEntry to avoid touching them.' (c) keep the existing AC-012b `just test` exit-0 criterion. Also add a non_goal stating that growing ReleaseEntry's required-key set does not bump schemaVersion, so the schema-guard edit is expected rather than a contract violation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-009 and AC-015\",\n      \"location\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml:202 (`for TAG in $(echo \\\"$PLAN_JSON\\\" | jq -r '.releases[]?.tagName // empty')`)\",\n      \"finding\": \"Both criteria say 'that tag's matching entry in `$PLAN_JSON`'s `releases[]` array' without naming the correlation key — the exact ambiguity the prior audit round removed from AC-003/004/005/006 by specifying the `package` field, left unfixed on the two Action-side criteria where it is load-bearing. The current loop iterates bare tag *strings*, so the implementer must invent the correlation: either restructure to iterate entry objects, or keep the string loop and add a `select(.tagName == $TAG)` lookup. These diverge observably when two packages render the same tag (a global `v{version}` tag template at equal versions), where the select-form yields multiple matches with no specified resolution, and they make AC-015's 'no matching entry' vs 'entry missing the key' distinct failures under one form and identical under the other. Required change: rewrite AC-009's opening to 'The loop iterates release *entries*, not tag strings — e.g. `jq -c '.releases[]?'` — and for each entry reads `tagName` and `isPrerelease` off that same entry object, so no cross-entry lookup by tag is performed. `gh release create \\\"$TAG\\\" --title \\\"$TAG\\\" --generate-notes` is invoked with `--prerelease` iff that entry's `isPrerelease` is `true`...'. Apply the same 'that same entry object' phrasing to AC-015, and add one clause: 'Two entries rendering an identical tag are processed independently, each on its own `isPrerelease`.'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-015\",\n      \"location\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml:200-216 (group 5 body)\",\n      \"finding\": \"AC-015 covers only the case where the entry 'has no `isPrerelease` key at all', but its own rationale names hand-edited fixtures as a source — and a hand-edited or stale plan just as easily yields `\\\"isPrerelease\\\": null` or `\\\"isPrerelease\\\": \\\"true\\\"`. The spec does not say whether a present-but-non-boolean value is a hard error or a silent false, so the implementer must decide what 'correct' means on the exact failure path this criterion exists to close. Compounding it, the natural jq idiom is a trap the spec does not warn against: `.isPrerelease // empty` returns empty for a legitimate `false` as well as for a missing key, making the two indistinguishable and re-introducing the silent-false behavior AC-015 forbids. Required change: extend AC-015 to 'an entry whose `isPrerelease` key is absent, `null`, or of any JSON type other than boolean causes the step to exit non-zero with an error message naming the offending tag, before any `gh release create` call for that entry', and add a clause: 'presence and type are tested explicitly (e.g. `jq -e 'has(\\\"isPrerelease\\\") and (.isPrerelease|type==\\\"boolean\\\")'`); the `//` alternative operator must not be used to read this field, since `false // empty` yields empty and would make a legitimate `false` indistinguishable from a missing key.' Extend AC-010's enumerated test cases to include one non-boolean-value case alongside the missing-key case.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"non_goals[1], AC-007, AC-013\",\n      \"location\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:75, :237, :390, :505\",\n      \"finding\": \"The spec's grounding claim for its central computation is factually wrong in two ways, and it is repeated in a non_goal and in two acceptance criteria. (1) non_goals[1] states '`ver: &amp;Version` is already in scope at the ReleaseEntry construction site (publish.rs line 75 parameter)'. Line 75 is the `ver: &amp;callisto_model::Version` parameter of `resolve_changelog_section`, a *different function*. Inside `plan_publish`, `ver` is an owned `callisto_model::Version` bound at line 237: `let (is_release, ver) = if let Some(bump) = bump_info { (true, bump.to.clone()) } else { ... (!tag_match, cur_ver) };`. AC-007 and AC-013 both inherit the wrong `&amp;Version` type from this claim. (2) The spec never mentions that `ver.is_prerelease()` is *already called* at publish.rs:390 (`let tag = if ver.is_prerelease() {`) for the npm dist-tag, inside a conditional branch — so AC-013's flat prohibition on 'no new conditional branch introduced around the `ver.is_prerelease()` call' reads, on a literal grep, as already violated by pre-existing code. Required change: rewrite non_goals[1] to '`ver` is an owned `callisto_model::Version`, bound at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:237 from either `bump.to` or the current manifest version, and already in scope at the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block at line 505; no new parameter or return type is introduced.' Change AC-007's phrase '`ver: &amp;Version` value' to 'the owned `ver: Version` value bound at line 237'. Scope AC-013's prohibition explicitly: '...no new conditional branch introduced *around the `ver.is_prerelease()` call added at the ReleaseEntry construction site (line 505)*; the pre-existing `if ver.is_prerelease()` npm dist-tag branch at line 390 is unrelated and unchanged.'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-011\",\n      \"location\": \"docs/01-spec.md:2667 (decision-table row 23)\",\n      \"finding\": \"AC-011 requires that 'the decision-table row at line 2667 referencing §M.12.2 is updated to list the new `is_prerelease` / `isPrerelease` field'. Line 2667 is row 23, whose entire content is a distinct decision record: '§M.12.2 | `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` is `Option&lt;String&gt;`, produced by reading the written `CHANGELOG.md` back (§CL.7.1).' Editing that row to also carry the new field overwrites a historical decision record with an unrelated one; appending a new row 24 leaves it intact. Both readings satisfy the criterion's text, and they produce materially different documents, so the implementer must guess which the spec means. Required change: replace that clause with 'a new decision-table row is appended after row 23 (currently line 2667), numbered 24, referencing §M.12.2 and reading: `ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease` is a required `bool`, computed at plan time from the resolved `Version::is_prerelease()`, never re-derived from the rendered tag string. Row 23 is left unmodified.'\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified against disk rather than the spec's self-description. Confirmed accurate: plan.rs ReleaseEntry at 111-118 with package/tag_name/sha/changelog_section under camelCase; version.rs is_prerelease at 126-131 with the exact SemVer/PEP 440 arms quoted; the pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease test at 365; the releases.push block at 505-510 post-TRACK4 including changelog_section; action.yml's `[[ \\\"$TAG\\\" =~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next) ]]` at 208 inside group 5 (200-216); the sed-range/stub harness pattern in test_status_check_branching.sh exactly as AC-010 describes; docs/01-spec.md struct block 1740-1763 with `pub struct ReleaseEntry` at 1742 and row 23 at 2667; callisto-model's Cargo.toml license and the ten dependencies AC-014 enumerates, verbatim. Condition 2 (no TBDs) passes — grep for TBD/TODO/to-be-determined/??? returns nothing. Condition 4 (single planning cycle) passes — one boolean field end-to-end, roughly five files plus test fixups, even with the eight struct literals added back in. Condition 3 is nominally satisfied by AC-015 carrying is_error_case: true, but the covered error surface is incomplete (blocker 3). Condition 1 is where the spec fails: AC-012a is testable but points at the wrong crates and the wrong artifact class, hiding a contract decision the implementer would have to make alone; AC-009/AC-015 leave the tag-to-entry correlation to the implementer; AC-011's docs instruction admits two materially different documents. Blocker 4 is factual accuracy rather than untestability, but it is the grounding cited by two criteria and a non_goal, so it is corrected here rather than waved through. retry_count is 1, below the escalation threshold of 3, so this is a fail, not an escalate.\"\n}\n```\n\nRelevant absolute paths for the drafter: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md`.\n\nTwo exact texts are load-bearing for blocker 1. The guard assertions that break:\n\n```rust\nassert_eq!(req, set(&amp;[\"package\", \"sha\", \"tagName\"]));\nassert_eq!(props, set(&amp;[\"changelogSection\", \"package\", \"sha\", \"tagName\"]));\n```\n\nand the guard's own prohibition, which the spec never authorizes overriding: \"none of this track's fixes may change any report struct's field shape, except where a task's explicit scope is the shape change itself.\"</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70328</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>14</tool_uses><duration_ms>365436</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"306e52a3-97a0-4e29-be86-552a2c26f6a5","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:16:34.185Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
