200-216, and the existing test harness pattern in `.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh`\n- Docs: `docs/01-spec.md` struct doc block (line 1742) and decision-table row 23 (line 2667)\n- Confirmed `Version::is_prerelease()` at `crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs:126-131` and its PEP440/dev-release test fixture\n\n**Key sequencing decision (per the critical constraint):** AC-001 (field), AC-007 (production site), and AC-012b (7 sibling literals) are combined into a single task (T1) — splitting them into separate commits would leave the workspace non-compiling in git history, since Rust's whole-crate model means an unfixed required field breaks every dependent crate. The schema-guard fix (AC-012a, T3) is safely separate since it's a runtime assertion, not a compile blocker. AC-013/AC-014 got a dedicated grep/`cargo metadata`-based structural verification task (T4) rather than a unit test, per the spec's own framing. The GitHub Action script change and its test (AC-008/009/010/015) are combined into one genuinely TDD task (T5): the new test is written first against the *unedited* action.yml, where it legitimately fails (old regex misses the PEP 440 fixture, and the old loop never validates `isPrerelease` presence/type before calling `gh`).\n\nPlan written to: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json`\n\nAll 17 acceptance criteria (AC-001–AC-015, AC-012a/b/c) are each covered by exactly one task's `covers_criteria`, verified programmatically against the source spec and against `plan@1.json`'s schema (no extra keys, all required fields present).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>134382</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>76</tool_uses><duration_ms>716123</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
