ec's changes, proving no new `[dependencies]` entry was added to callisto-model.\",\n    \"CHECK (AC-014, part 2 -- Version::is_prerelease() itself unmodified): run `git diff -- crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs`. Expected output: empty (no output at all) -- version.rs is reused as-is per this spec's non_goals; this task's earlier tasks never touch it.\",\n    \"CHECK (AC-014, part 3 -- resolve graph has no AGPL edge): run `cargo metadata --format-version 1 | jq -r --arg pkg callisto-model '.resolve.nodes[] | select(.id | startswith($pkg + \\\" \\\")) | .deps[].name' | sort -u`. Expected output: exactly the crate names `camino`, `miette`, `path-slash`, `pep440_rs`, `schemars`, `semver`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `tempfile`, `thiserror` (callisto-model's declared [dependencies], per its Cargo.toml) plus each crate's own transitive non-workspace deps already present before this spec (this list does not change as a result of this spec, since Cargo.toml was untouched per the prior check) -- confirm by inspection that none of the printed names is a crate known to be AGPL-licensed; there is no AGPL-licensed crate in callisto-model's dependency tree today and this spec adds none.\",\n    \"CHECK (AC-012c -- full suite green): run `cargo nextest run --workspace` (equivalently `just test` / `moon run :test`). Expected output: the run completes with exit code 0 and a summary line of the form `Summary [ ... ] <N> tests run: <N> passed, 0 skipped` with zero failures -- including every test touched by T1, T2, and T3, and no remaining test anywhere in the workspace asserting a ReleaseEntry JSON shape or struct literal that omits `is_prerelease`/`isPrerelease`.\",\n    \"No commit is required for this task if all checks pass as expected -- it verifies work already committed in T1-T3. If any check fails, fix the offending file in the task that introduced it (T1, T2, or T3) and re-run that task's own GREEN command before re-running this task's checks.\"\n  ],\n  \"commit_message\": 