{"parentUuid":"88227f0b-ce00-4f8d-ab8e-f076713b75f3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fd36fa10-03fb-40ad-8e82-adafebf39683","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019TmeWHiUFb2cU65K2H5int","type":"tool_result","content":"CHECK (AC-014, part 3 -- resolve graph has no AGPL edge): run `cargo metadata --format-version 1 | jq -r --arg pkg callisto-model '.packages[] | select(.name == $pkg) | .dependencies[].name' | sort -u`. Expected output: exactly callisto-model's direct [dependencies] list per its Cargo.toml -- `camino`, `miette`, `path-slash`, `pep440_rs`, `schemars`, `semver`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `tempfile`, `thiserror` -- with no other names; confirm by inspection that none of these is AGPL-licensed. (The older `.resolve.nodes[] | select(.id | startswith($pkg + \" \"))` form does not work on modern cargo, whose resolve-node id format is `path+file://.../crates/callisto-model#0.3.3`, not `callisto-model 0.3.3 (...)` -- use the `.packages[]` form above instead.)\n---\nRUN (expect failure, confirming these are meaningful tests, not tautologies): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`. Because T1's production-site code already exists, run this BEFORE writing it by temporarily reverting the `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` line to `is_prerelease: false,` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs to observe genuine red: expected output is 3 of the 4 tests failing (`plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true` each report `assertion failed` on their `assert!(release.is_prerelease, ...)` line), with only `plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json` passing. Then revert the temporary change back to `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` before proceeding. After reverting publish.rs back to its T1-committed form, run `git diff --stat crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` and confirm it shows NO output before proceeding to GREEN -- this mechanically catches a forgotten or incomplete revert rather than relying on memory.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f3fde785-9e55-44de-ac3c-7a123b8c0c6a","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:39:32.858Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"CHECK (AC-014, part 3 -- resolve graph has no AGPL edge): run `cargo metadata --format-version 1 | jq -r --arg pkg callisto-model '.packages[] | select(.name == $pkg) | .dependencies[].name' | sort -u`. Expected output: exactly callisto-model's direct [dependencies] list per its Cargo.toml -- `camino`, `miette`, `path-slash`, `pep440_rs`, `schemars`, `semver`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `tempfile`, `thiserror` -- with no other names; confirm by inspection that none of these is AGPL-licensed. (The older `.resolve.nodes[] | select(.id | startswith($pkg + \" \"))` form does not work on modern cargo, whose resolve-node id format is `path+file://.../crates/callisto-model#0.3.3`, not `callisto-model 0.3.3 (...)` -- use the `.packages[]` form above instead.)\n---\nRUN (expect failure, confirming these are meaningful tests, not tautologies): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`. Because T1's production-site code already exists, run this BEFORE writing it by temporarily reverting the `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` line to `is_prerelease: false,` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs to observe genuine red: expected output is 3 of the 4 tests failing (`plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true` each report `assertion failed` on their `assert!(release.is_prerelease, ...)` line), with only `plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json` passing. Then revert the temporary change back to `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` before proceeding. After reverting publish.rs back to its T1-committed form, run `git diff --stat crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` and confirm it shows NO output before proceeding to GREEN -- this mechanically catches a forgotten or incomplete revert rather than relying on memory.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"88227f0b-ce00-4f8d-ab8e-f076713b75f3","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
