6 all depend on T1 only (correct — none reference anything T2/T3/T5/T6 produce). T4 depends on T1, T2, T3 (correct, since it verifies the full suite including T2/T3's tests). No task references a symbol before its producing task.\n- **poor-batching**: T1 correctly bundles the required-field addition with every construction-site fix in one commit, per the reasoning about whole-workspace compilation — no task leaves the workspace non-compiling.\n- **over-specified**: T4's `sed -n '495,515p'` hardcoded line range is a minor fragility (line numbers may drift slightly depending on exact diff shape) but this is a verification/inspection step, not dictating a private variable — round-2 policy is to demote this, not block.\n- **under-specified**: none found — every step has exact file paths, exact find/replace text, exact commands, and exact expected output.\n- **missing-error-handling**: AC-015 (missing/null/non-boolean `isPrerelease`) is fully covered by T5 with explicit test cases (missing-key, null-value, non-boolean-value) and a hard-fail implementation via `jq -e 'has(...) and (...|type==\"boolean\")'`, correctly avoiding the `//` operator pitfall the spec calls out.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T4\",\n      \"type\": \"over-specified\",\n      \"description\": \"The `sed -n '495,515p' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` line range in T4's AC-013 check is hardcoded and may drift by a few lines depending on exact diff shape from T1, making the visual-confirm step slightly fragile.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Non-blocking per round-2 policy. If desired, replace with a `grep -n -A3 'releases.push(ReleaseEntry'` anchor-based extraction instead of a fixed line range, so it's robust to minor line drift.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"pass\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Round 2. The single blocking issue from round 1 (T4's stale .resolve.nodes[] jq form) is verifiably fixed: I ran the corrected `.packages[] | select(.name==$pkg) | .dependencies[].name` command live against this repo's cargo 1.96.0 and got exactly the plan's expected 11-name output, matching crates/callisto-model/Cargo.toml's actual dependency lists. T3's schema_guard_test.rs find/replace text was also cross-checked against the live file and matches verbatim. All 17 acceptance criteria (AC-001..AC-015 with 012a/b/c) are covered by exactly one task each, no orphaned criteria. Task dependency order is correct throughout. T2's added git diff --stat mechanical safeguard for the manual revert is present and sound. Only a minor, non-blocking fragility remains in T4's hardcoded sed line range, correctly demoted per round-2 policy since all criteria are covered and no blocking-class issue remains.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70828</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>34290</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
