{"parentUuid":"ccb795eb-fef2-4084-bbc1-4d71c3d8ab7d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0f4234f2-3701-40e9-b93b-319b6369ef79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHatb3f55cY33yArQnYhiE","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"T1\",\n  \"title\": \"Add ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease field, populate it at the production construction site, and fix every sibling struct literal\",\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-001\",\n    \"AC-007\",\n    \"AC-012b\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"RED: Append this new test to the end of crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs (it uses `write_release_candidate_pkg`, `init_git_repo`, and `DummyRunner`, all already defined earlier in this same file):\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_release_entry_is_prerelease_matches_version() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.0.0-1\\\");\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"SemVer 1.0.0-1 must be reported as a pre-release via Version::is_prerelease()\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n```\",\n    \"RUN (expect failure): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_release_entry_is_prerelease_matches_version`. Expected output: a compile error, e.g. `error[E0609]: no field \\\\`is_prerelease\\\\` on type \\\\`&ReleaseEntry\\\\`` (exact rustc wording may vary by toolchain version; the required signal is a compile failure naming the missing `is_prerelease` field, not a runtime assertion failure -- the field does not exist yet).\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT (1/4 -- the field): In crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs, find:\\n```rust\\npub struct ReleaseEntry {\\n    pub package: PackageId,\\n    pub tag_name: TagName,\\n    pub sha: CommitSha,\\n\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub changelog_section: Option<String>,\\n}\\n```\\nReplace with:\\n```rust\\npub struct ReleaseEntry {\\n    pub package: PackageId,\\n    pub tag_name: TagName,\\n    pub sha: CommitSha,\\n\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub changelog_section: Option<String>,\\n\\n    pub is_prerelease: bool,\\n}\\n```\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT (2/4 -- the production construction site, AC-007): In crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs, find:\\n```rust\\n                    releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\\n                        package: pkg.id.clone(),\\n                        tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\\n                        sha: sha.clone(),\\n                        changelog_section,\\n                    });\\n```\\nReplace with:\\n```rust\\n                    releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\\n                        package: pkg.id.clone(),\\n                        tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\\n                        sha: sha.clone(),\\n                        changelog_section,\\n                        is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),\\n                    });\\n```\\nThis is the only edit at this call site: `ver` is the owned `Version` already bound earlier in the same function (from `bump.to.clone()` or `cur_ver`), and `Version::is_prerelease()` is called directly with no wrapping `if`/`match`/`unwrap_or`.\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT (3/4 -- the CLI's sibling literal, 1 of 7): In crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs, find:\\n```rust\\n            releases: vec![ReleaseEntry {\\n                package: PackageId::Bare(\\\"my-lib\\\".to_string()),\\n                tag_name: TagName(\\\"my-lib@1.0.0\\\".to_string()),\\n                sha,\\n                changelog_section: None,\\n            }],\\n```\\nReplace with:\\n```rust\\n            releases: vec![ReleaseEntry {\\n                package: PackageId::Bare(\\\"my-lib\\\".to_string()),\\n                tag_name: TagName(\\\"my-lib@1.0.0\\\".to_string()),\\n                sha,\\n                changelog_section: None,\\n                is_prerelease: false,\\n            }],\\n```\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT (4/4 -- the remaining 6 sibling literals in tests): In crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs, find:\\n```rust\\nfn release_entry(tag_name: &str, sha: &str) -> ReleaseEntry {\\n    ReleaseEntry {\\n        package: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap(),\\n        tag_name: TagName(tag_name.to_string()),\\n        sha: CommitSha::parse(sha).unwrap(),\\n        changelog_section: None,\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\nReplace with:\\n```rust\\nfn release_entry(tag_name: &str, sha: &str) -> ReleaseEntry {\\n    ReleaseEntry {\\n        package: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap(),\\n        tag_name: TagName(tag_name.to_string()),\\n        sha: CommitSha::parse(sha).unwrap(),\\n        changelog_section: None,\\n        is_prerelease: false,\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\nIn crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs, there are 5 remaining `ReleaseEntry { ... }` literals (at approximately lines 23, 111, 273, 404, 410 as of this plan's writing -- locate each with `grep -n \\\"ReleaseEntry {\\\" crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs`). Each one ends with a `changelog_section: <expr>,` field immediately before the literal's closing `}`. For every one of the 5, insert `is_prerelease: false,` as a new line immediately after that literal's `changelog_section: ...,` line and before the literal's closing `}`. Concretely, each of these 5 blocks:\\n```rust\\n            ReleaseEntry {\\n                ...\\n                changelog_section: <expr>,\\n            }\\n```\\nbecomes:\\n```rust\\n            ReleaseEntry {\\n                ...\\n                changelog_section: <expr>,\\n                is_prerelease: false,\\n            }\\n```\\nwith `<expr>` and every other field left byte-for-byte unchanged. Do this for all 5 remaining sites so no `ReleaseEntry` literal anywhere in the workspace omits `is_prerelease`.\",\n    \"GREEN (compile check across the whole workspace): `cargo build --workspace`. Expected output: exit code 0, ending in `Finished` with no errors (warnings, if any, are pre-existing and unrelated to this change).\",\n    \"GREEN (the new test): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_release_entry_is_prerelease_matches_version`. Expected output: `test plan_publish_release_entry_is_prerelease_matches_version ... ok` and a final `test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed`.\",\n    \"COMMIT: `git add crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs`\"\n  ],\n  \"commit_message\": \"feat(model): add required ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease computed from Version::is_prerelease()\\n\\nReleaseEntry gains a new required `is_prerelease: bool` field (JSON key\\n`isPrerelease`), populated at its one construction site in plan_publish\\nfrom the already-parsed `ver.is_prerelease()` -- never re-derived from\\nthe rendered tag string. Every other ReleaseEntry struct literal in the\\nworkspace is updated in the same commit so the crate keeps compiling.\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2094a0cc-ae13-4737-8390-acd2ecc016e1","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:41:29.655Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"T1\",\n  \"title\": \"Add ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease field, populate it at the production construction site, and fix every sibling struct literal\",\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-001\",\n    \"AC-007\",\n    \"AC-012b\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"RED: Append this new test to the end of crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs (it uses `write_release_candidate_pkg`, `init_git_repo`, and `DummyRunner`, all already defined earlier in this same file):\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_release_entry_is_prerelease_matches_version() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.0.0-1\\\");\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let re