{"parentUuid":"fe41eac9-5d88-415f-b7ce-e475994d7092","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca7edced-0c12-4b7d-b059-5aebe9446790","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ETxZL4MTL2ypgeC5baE59L","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"T2\",\n  \"title\": \"Prove is_prerelease is computed correctly for SemVer and PEP 440 pre-release and non-pre-release fixtures, and appears in JSON output\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"T1\"\n  ],\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-002\",\n    \"AC-003\",\n    \"AC-004\",\n    \"AC-005\",\n    \"AC-006\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"test\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"RED: Append these 3 tests to the end of crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs (after the T1 test). They must fail before this task's fixtures exist to prove the assertions are meaningful -- since T1 already landed the field, these will fail on their `assert!`/`assert_eq!` calls (wrong boolean value or missing find), not on a compile error:\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(!release.is_prerelease, \\\"SemVer 1.2.3 must not be a prerelease\\\");\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1, \\\"expected exactly one release entry\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"],\\n        serde_json::json!(false),\\n        \\\"isPrerelease key must be present in serialized JSON and equal false\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.0.0-1\\\");\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"SemVer 1.0.0-1 (numeric pre-release identifier, no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring) must be a prerelease\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1);\\n    assert_eq!(entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"], serde_json::json!(true));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n    use callisto_model::{ManifestDecl, ManifestFormat, ManifestRole, PublishTarget};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[project]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0.dev1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let pyproject_decl = ManifestDecl::new(\\n        PathBuf::from(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        ManifestRole::Canonical,\\n        ManifestFormat::PyprojectToml,\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    let graph = GraphBuilder::new()\\n        .package(pkg_id.clone(), |p: PackageBuilder| {\\n            p.manifests(vec![pyproject_decl])\\n                .publish_to(vec![PublishTarget::Pypi { index: None }])\\n        })\\n        .build()\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n    let cfg = callisto_graph::config::load(&root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\")).unwrap();\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace {\\n        root: root.to_path_buf(),\\n        config: cfg,\\n        graph,\\n        tags: OnceCell::new(),\\n        git: OnceCell::new(),\\n        runner: &runner,\\n        manifest_cache: Default::default(),\\n        identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default(),\\n    };\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"PEP 440 1.0.0.dev1 (dev-release) must be a prerelease per pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1);\\n    assert_eq!(entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"], serde_json::json!(true));\\n}\\n```\\nAlso append this 4th test, the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture (identical structure to the dev-release test above, different version and function name):\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n    use callisto_model::{ManifestDecl, ManifestFormat, ManifestRole, PublishTarget};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[project]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.2.3a1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let pyproject_decl = ManifestDecl::new(\\n        PathBuf::from(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        ManifestRole::Canonical,\\n        ManifestFormat::PyprojectToml,\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    let graph = GraphBuilder::new()\\n        .package(pkg_id.clone(), |p: PackageBuilder| {\\n            p.manifests(vec![pyproject_decl])\\n                .publish_to(vec![PublishTarget::Pypi { index: None }])\\n        })\\n        .build()\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n    let cfg = callisto_graph::config::load(&root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\")).unwrap();\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace {\\n        root: root.to_path_buf(),\\n        config: cfg,\\n        graph,\\n        tags: OnceCell::new(),\\n        git: OnceCell::new(),\\n        runner: &runner,\\n        manifest_cache: Default::default(),\\n        identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default(),\\n    };\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"PEP 440 1.2.3a1 (no dash, no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring) must be a prerelease -- the original bug\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1);\\n    assert_eq!(entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"], serde_json::json!(true));\\n}\\n```\",\n    \"RUN (expect failure, confirming these are meaningful tests, not tautologies): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`. Because T1's production-site code already exists, run this BEFORE writing it by temporarily reverting the `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` line to `is_prerelease: false,` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs to observe genuine red: expected output is 3 of the 4 tests failing (`plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true` each report `assertion failed` on their `assert!(release.is_prerelease, ...)` line), with only `plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json` passing. Then revert the temporary change back to `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` before proceeding. After reverting publish.rs back to its T1-committed form, run `git diff --stat crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` and confirm it shows NO output before proceeding to GREEN -- this mechanically catches a forgotten or incomplete revert rather than relying on memory.\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT: No production code changes in this task -- T1 already wired the correct computation. This task only adds the fixture tests above, which exercise T1's implementation.\",\n    \"GREEN: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`. Expected output: all 4 tests report `... ok` and the summary line reads `test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed`.\",\n    \"COMMIT: `git add crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs`\"\n  ],\n  \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease across SemVer and PEP 440 fixtures\\n\\nRegression-pins the AC-004 SemVer numeric-prerelease fixture (1.0.0-1)\\nand the AC-005 PEP 440 fixture (1.2.3a1, the original bug this field\\nexists to fix) alongside a non-prerelease SemVer control and the\\nexisting PEP 440 dev-release contract, proving is_prerelease is read\\nfrom the serialized JSON's isPrerelease key end-to-end.\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"21042e4b-5c42-4fc4-ad6a-c00912407d9f","timestamp":"2026-08-21T19:53:24.461Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"T2\",\n  \"title\": \"Prove is_prerelease is computed correctly for SemVer and PEP 440 pre-release and non-pre-release fixtures, and appears in JSON output\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"T1\"\n  ],\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-002\",\n    \"AC-003\",\n    \"AC-004\",\n    \"AC-005\",\n    \"AC-006\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"test\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"RED: Append these 3 tests to the end of crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs (after the T1 test). They must fail before this task's fixtures exist to prove the assertions are meaningful -- since T1 already landed the field, these will fail on their `assert!`/`assert_eq!` calls (wrong boolean value or missing find), not on a compile error:\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(!release.is_prerelease, \\\"SemVer 1.2.3 must not be a prerelease\\\");\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1, \\\"expected exactly one release entry\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"],\\n        serde_json::json!(false),\\n        \\\"isPrerelease key must be present in serialized JSON and equal false\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.0.0-1\\\");\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"SemVer 1.0.0-1 (numeric pre-release identifier, no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring) must be a prerelease\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1);\\n    assert_eq!(entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"], serde_json::json!(true));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n    use callisto_model::{ManifestDecl, ManifestFormat, ManifestRole, PublishTarget};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[project]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0.dev1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let pyproject_decl = ManifestDecl::new(\\n        PathBuf::from(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        ManifestRole::Canonical,\\n        ManifestFormat::PyprojectToml,\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    let graph = GraphBuilder::new()\\n        .package(pkg_id.clone(), |p: PackageBuilder| {\\n            p.manifests(vec![pyproject_decl])\\n                .publish_to(vec![PublishTarget::Pypi { index: None }])\\n        })\\n        .build()\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n    let cfg = callisto_graph::config::load(&root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\")).unwrap();\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace {\\n        root: root.to_path_buf(),\\n        config: cfg,\\n        graph,\\n        tags: OnceCell::new(),\\n        git: OnceCell::new(),\\n        runner: &runner,\\n        manifest_cache: Default::default(),\\n        identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default(),\\n    };\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"PEP 440 1.0.0.dev1 (dev-release) must be a prerelease per pep440_dev_release_is_prerelease\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1);\\n    assert_eq!(entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"], serde_json::json!(true));\\n}\\n```\\nAlso append this 4th test, the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture (identical structure to the dev-release test above, different version and function name):\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n    use callisto_model::{ManifestDecl, ManifestFormat, ManifestRole, PublishTarget};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[project]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.2.3a1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let pyproject_decl = ManifestDecl::new(\\n        PathBuf::from(\\\"pyproject.toml\\\"),\\n        ManifestRole::Canonical,\\n        ManifestFormat::PyprojectToml,\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    let graph = GraphBuilder::new()\\n        .package(pkg_id.clone(), |p: PackageBuilder| {\\n            p.manifests(vec![pyproject_decl])\\n                .publish_to(vec![PublishTarget::Pypi { index: None }])\\n        })\\n        .build()\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n    let cfg = callisto_graph::config::load(&root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\")).unwrap();\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace {\\n        root: root.to_path_buf(),\\n        config: cfg,\\n        graph,\\n        tags: OnceCell::new(),\\n        git: OnceCell::new(),\\n        runner: &runner,\\n        manifest_cache: Default::default(),\\n        identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default(),\\n    };\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n    assert!(\\n        release.is_prerelease,\\n        \\\"PEP 440 1.2.3a1 (no dash, no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring) must be a prerelease -- the original bug\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    let json = serde_json::to_value(&plan).unwrap();\\n    let entries = json[\\\"releases\\\"].as_array().unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(entries.len(), 1);\\n    assert_eq!(entries[0][\\\"isPrerelease\\\"], serde_json::json!(true));\\n}\\n```\",\n    \"RUN (expect failure, confirming these are meaningful tests, not tautologies): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`. Because T1's production-site code already exists, run this BEFORE writing it by temporarily reverting the `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` line to `is_prerelease: false,` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs to observe genuine red: expected output is 3 of the 4 tests failing (`plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true`, `plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true` each report `assertion failed` on their `assert!(release.is_prerelease, ...)` line), with only `plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json` passing. Then revert the temporary change back to `is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),` before proceeding. After reverting publish.rs back to its T1-committed form, run `git diff --stat crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` and confirm it shows NO output before proceeding to GREEN -- this mechanically catches a forgotten or incomplete revert rather than relying on memory.\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT: No production code changes in this task -- T1 already wired the correct computation. This task only adds the fixture tests above, which exercise T1's implementation.\",\n    \"GREEN: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true`. Expected output: all 4 tests report `... ok` and the summary line reads `test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed`.\",\n    \"COMMIT: `git add crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs`\"\n  ],\n  \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease across SemVer and PEP 440 fixtures\\n\\nRegression-pins the AC-004 SemVer numeric-prerelease fixture (1.0.0-1)\\nand the AC-005 PEP 440 fixture (1.2.3a1, the original bug this field\\nexists to fix) alongside a non-prerelease SemVer control and the\\nexisting PEP 440 dev-release contract, proving is_prerelease is read\\nfrom the serialized JSON's isPrerelease key end-to-end.\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fe41eac9-5d88-415f-b7ce-e475994d7092","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"extern