{"parentUuid":"a2268876-564f-4571-bbc2-a218044c4bad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f5c3712b-9d58-46b9-ad02-83bddc7fe7dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   This is a continuation of a very long release-remediation session on \"callisto\" (a Rust monorepo release/versioning CLI tool at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto`). This window's explicit user directives, in chronological order:\n   - Continue PR #5 preparation/verification (already in flight from prior context): a changeset had been written and refined for readability, CI failures fixed.\n   - \"Are we confident this will result in a proper release? Also packages that have a diffent bump should be in a separate changeset...\" — led to discovering the workspace uses shared `version.workspace = true`.\n   - **Critical correction from user**: \"The first part, your assumption is incorrect. The way callisto should work is the highest bump should win-out when there are multiple changesets that are in a fixed group. Isn't that right? Isn't that in the spec? Check changelogs and knope to be sure.\" — required retracting my incorrect \"apply_version_plan bug\" claim and instead adding a `[[fixed-group]]` config.\n   - \"Let's shipped them together right? We should make sure that we don't bump versions multiple times across a group of changesets in one release PR (two changesets with minor should not bump 0.2 -> 0.3 -> 0.4, it should be 0.2 -> 0.3). Do we have that speced out properly? Tested properly?\" — required tracing the aggregation/bump architecture and adding a dedicated regression test.\n   - \"Anything else we forgot to do??? Did we need to make any changes to the GH action???\" — full read of `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`.\n   - \"/reload-plugins... Think critically about ALL of the changes we made since the last version and triple check that we don't need any changes to the actions. Anything that can be simplified by support from callisto now?\" — deeper audit, found the `ReleaseEntry` missing-prerelease-field issue.\n   - **\"Yes, please add it now with a comprehensive spec, implementation, docs, tests, etc. Check changesets and knope of input\"** — this is the standing directive currently being executed: full canon→vector→lambda pipeline for adding `ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease`.\n   - Mid-implementation pushback (process-related, not scope-related): \"Keep an eye on the running tasks, you lose track of them easily\", \"Been waiting for a while\", \"seems like we've been waiting for a while\", \"What's running that's taking hours??\" — established/reinforced the pattern of checking actual process state directly (ps/log tail) rather than assuming, and recognizing `callisto-moon`'s WASM sandbox tests as a known-slow (60+ sec/test) test suite not worth waiting on when unrelated crates are already individually verified green.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Cargo workspace-shared version** (`version.workspace = true`) vs. **callisto's own `[[fixed-group]]` config concept** — two distinct mechanisms; the former is a pure Cargo.toml convenience, the latter is what actually triggers callisto's max-severity convergence logic (`groups.rs`'s `fixed_group_target`, confirmed using real `max_sev` computation and a single `.bump(&aligned_base, max_sev)` call).\n   - **`WorkspaceCargoResolver::write_version`'s `CargoWorkspacePackage` write target has \"no live production caller\"** (confirmed via `docs/01-spec.md` line ~3936-3943) — this was the source of my incorrect \"bug\" diagnosis; the REAL production path for a workspace-inherited-version member is `CargoToml::write_version` pinning an explicit version into the member's own `[package]` section (never touching the shared root field), tested via `write_version_pins_explicitly_on_workspace_inheriting_member`.\n   - **Severity aggregation architecture**: `aggregate.rs`'s changeset loop uses `if entry.severity > cur_sev { insert }` (proper max-union across multiple changesets for one package, not sequential compounding); `groups.rs`'s `fixed_group_target` computes `max_sev` across all group members' already-aggregated severities and calls `.bump()` exactly once from `aligned_base` (always the pristine on-disk snapshot, never an intermediate/already-bumped value) — this structurally guarantees no compounding.\n   - **Canon→vector→lambda full pipeline discipline** (established project convention): canon:drafter → canon:auditor → canon:exit-gate (retry loop) → vector:planner → vector:challenger (retry loop) → lambda implementation (TDD per task: RED confirmed, implement, GREEN confirmed, fmt/clippy/full-suite, commit).\n   - **Premature-completion pattern recurrence**: the FIRST `canon:auditor` dispatch returned only a meta-description (\"I've launched the audit agent...\") not real findings — required an explicit re-dispatch with \"Complete the ENTIRE audit... do not just describe what you are about to do.\"\n   - **`cargo metadata`'s resolve-node id format changed** across cargo versions — the old `.resolve.nodes[] | select(.id | startswith($pkg + \" \"))` jq pattern silently produces empty output on cargo 1.96.0 (modern format is `path+file://.../crates/pkg#version`), a real bug caught by `vector:challenger` by actually running the command against the live repo, not just trusting the plan's text.\n   - **`.packages[].dependencies` doesn't distinguish dependency kind** — includes both `[dependencies]` and `[dev-dependencies]` entries (confirmed `proptest` from callisto-model's `[dev-dependencies]` appears in the \"direct dependencies\" jq query), a real discrepancy I found myself beyond what the challenger caught, requiring the plan's expected-output text to be corrected.\n   - **Cargo incremental-compile stale-cache false-negative**: after `sed -i.bak` + `mv .bak` revert-restore dance during T2's manual red-phase verification, `cargo test` initially showed stale FAILED results even though the source was correctly restored (confirmed via `grep`/`git diff --stat` showing clean state) — required a `touch` on the file to force recompilation before tests passed correctly. This is a process/tooling gotcha to remember, distinct from a real bug.\n   - **`callisto-moon`'s WASM sandbox test suite is inherently slow** (60+ seconds per test, confirmed multiple times this session) — not a hang, but not worth waiting on for a `cargo test --workspace` run when the change under test doesn't touch that crate at all.\n   - **No schemaVersion bump policy** (established earlier this session, reaffirmed for SPEC-005): additive report fields (like `ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease`) never trigger a schemaVersion bump, since no external registry consumer has ever depended on this JSON wire format.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/callisto.toml` — added:\n     ```toml\n     [[fixed-group]]\n     name = \"workspace\"\n     members = [\n         \"callisto-model\",\n         \"callisto-format\",\n         \"callisto-conventional\",\n         \"callisto-changelog\",\n         \"callisto-manifests\",\n         \"callisto-vcs\",\n         \"callisto-graph\",\n         \"callisto-cli\",\n         \"callisto-moon\",\n         \"callisto-fixtures\",\n     ]\n     ```\n     Committed together with the new test (below) as `feat(config): declare workspace as a fixed group; pin no-compounding guarantee` (commit `8bb8eee`).\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs` — added `tag()` and `commit_all()` helper functions (mirroring `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`'s own test-module helpers), plus new test `test_fixed_group_two_changesets_converge_on_single_bump_not_compounded`: two packages `pkg-a`/`pkg-b` in a `[[fixed-group]]`, each with its OWN separate minor-severity changeset, both tagged at `1.0.0`, asserting both converge to `to.render() == \"1.1.0\"` (not a compounded `1.2.0`). Same commit `8bb8eee`.\n   - `.claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json` — final gated spec (passed exit-gate on 2nd attempt). Key content: 15 acceptance criteria (AC-001 through AC-015, no AC-012 alone — split into AC-012a/b/c), `linked_requirement: \"REQ-008\"`. Final corrected `ver` grounding: \"`ver` is an owned `callisto_model::Version`, bound at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:237... already in scope at the `releases.push(ReleaseEntry { ... })` block at line 505.\" AC-015 (is_error_case: true): \"For a release entry... whose `isPrerelease` key is absent, `null`, or of any JSON type other than boolean... the step fails with a non-zero exit code... Presence and type are tested explicitly (e.g. `jq -e 'has(\"isPrerelease\") and (.isPrerelease|type==\"boolean\")'`); the `//` alternative operator must not be used.\" Committed as `docs(specs): add gated spec for ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease field` (commit `28aff95`).\n   - `.claude/plans/PLAN-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json` — final gated plan (passed vector-challenger on 2nd attempt), `spec_file_path: \".claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json\"`, `spec_hash: \"sha256:5217011e...\"` (verified matches live spec file). 6 tasks T1-T6. T4's corrected AC-014 verification step: `cargo metadata --format-version 1 | jq -r --arg pkg callisto-model '.packages[] | select(.name == $pkg) | .dependencies[].name' | sort -u` with expected output including `proptest`. Committed as `docs(plans): add plan for ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease field` (commit `5ae003e`).\n   - `crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs` — `ReleaseEntry` struct (lines ~111-119) now:\n     ```rust\n     pub struct ReleaseEntry {\n         pub package: PackageId,\n         pub tag_name: TagName,\n         pub sha: CommitSha,\n\n         #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n         pub changelog_section: Option<String>,\n\n         pub is_prerelease: bool,\n     }\n     ```\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` — line 505-511, the real construction site:\n     ```rust\n     releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\n         package: pkg.id.clone(),\n         tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\n         sha: sha.clone(),\n         changelog_section,\n         is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),\n     });\n     ```\n     Pre-existing unrelated `if ver.is_prerelease()` branch at line 390 (npm dist-tag logic) confirmed unchanged.\n   - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs` line 357-362 — sibling literal, added `is_prerelease: false,`.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs` line 97-104 — `release_entry()` helper fn, added `is_prerelease: false,`.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs` — 5 sites updated (all previously verified against live file before editing): lines ~23-28, ~111-116, ~273-278, ~404-409, ~410-415 (last two are two `ReleaseEntry` literals in one `vec![...]` for `pkg_a`/`pkg_b`), each got `is_prerelease: false,` appended.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs` — appended 5 new tests total this session:\n     - `plan_publish_release_entry_is_prerelease_matches_version` (T1's RED/GREEN test, SemVer `1.0.0-1` fixture via `write_release_candidate_pkg`).\n     - `plan_publish_semver_non_prerelease_has_is_prerelease_false_in_json` (SemVer `1.2.3`, false, asserts JSON `isPrerelease` key).\n     - `plan_publish_semver_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true` (SemVer `1.0.0-1`, true).\n     - `plan_publish_pep440_dev_release_has_is_prerelease_true` (PEP440 `1.0.0.dev1` via manual `pyproject.toml` write + `GraphBuilder`/`PackageBuilder` + manual `Workspace { root, config, graph, tags: OnceCell::new(), git: OnceCell::new(), runner: &runner, manifest_cache: Default::default(), identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default() }` struct literal construction, matching an existing precedent pattern at line ~977 in this same file).\n     - `plan_publish_pep440_regression_fixture_has_is_prerelease_true` (PEP440 `1.2.3a1`, true — the original bug fixture, no dash, no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring).\n     All 5 tests pass; verified genuinely meaningful via a manual temporary revert (`sed -i.bak 's/is_prerelease: ver.is_prerelease(),/is_prerelease: false,/'` then `mv .bak` back) proving 3 of the 4 T2 tests fail when the bug is reintroduced.\n   - `crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs` — module doc (lines 1-8) updated to mention `ReleaseEntry.isPrerelease` as a permitted additive delta; assertions (lines ~92-99) updated:\n     ```rust\n     let release_entry = &plan_schema[\"definitions\"][\"ReleaseEntry\"];\n     let (req, props) = required_and_props(release_entry);\n     assert_eq!(req, set(&[\"isPrerelease\", \"package\", \"sha\", \"tagName\"]));\n     assert_eq!(\n         props,\n         set(&[\n             \"changelogSection\",\n             \"isPrerelease\",\n             \"package\",\n             \"sha\",\n             \"tagName\"\n         ])\n     );\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Incorrect \"apply_version_plan last-write-wins bug\" claim** — I initially misdiagnosed the diverging per-package dry-run target versions as a real bug in `apply.rs`'s `CargoWorkspacePackage` write branch. **User directly corrected this**: \"your assumption is incorrect... Isn't that in the spec? Check changelogs and knope to be sure.\" I researched and found the flagged code path has \"no live production caller\" per the spec's own docs, and the real fix was a missing `[[fixed-group]]` config declaration, not a code bug. I explicitly acknowledged the error to the user.\n   - **First `canon:auditor` dispatch returned only a meta-description**, not real findings (matches the session's recurring \"premature completion\" pattern) — fixed by re-dispatching with explicit \"Complete the ENTIRE audit... do not just describe what you are about to do.\"\n   - **SPEC-005 exit-gate round 1 failed with 5 blockers** (all fixed directly by rewriting the spec JSON): wrong crate/artifact-class citation in AC-012a (callisto-fixtures/JSON-golden-tests instead of callisto-cli's schema_guard_test.rs + 8 Rust struct literals); missing tag-to-entry correlation key in AC-009/AC-015; incomplete null/non-boolean coverage in AC-015 plus the `//` jq-operator trap; factually wrong `ver: &Version` claim (actually an owned `Version` bound at publish.rs:237, not the `&Version` parameter of the unrelated `resolve_changelog_section` function at line 75); ambiguous AC-011 docs-edit instruction (two \"row 23\"s exist in docs/01-spec.md).\n   - **`vector:challenger` round 1 failed**: T4's AC-014 verification command (`.resolve.nodes[] | select(.id | startswith($pkg + \" \"))`) produces empty output on cargo 1.96.0 due to a resolve-node id format change — the challenger actually RAN the command to confirm this. Fixed by switching to `.packages[] | select(.name == $pkg) | .dependencies[].name`. **I then personally discovered a second issue** in my own fix: the corrected command also surfaces `proptest` (a `[dev-dependencies]` entry), which the expected-output text didn't mention — fixed by adding it to the expected list with an explanatory note.\n   - **Stale build-cache false test failure during T2**: after reverting a temporary `sed` change back via `mv .bak`, `cargo test` still showed 3 tests failing even though `grep`/`git diff --stat` confirmed the source was correctly restored — resolved by running `touch` on the file to force cargo to recompile, after which all 4 tests passed cleanly.\n   - **Repeated external process kills** on long-running `cargo test --workspace`/`cargo build --workspace` background commands throughout this session (not caused by my own commands — confirmed via checking `ps aux`/log tails showing zero test failures and genuine ongoing compilation/test progress each time) — established practice: re-run cleanly, don't treat \"killed\" status as a real failure signal, always check the log content first.\n   - **Most recent, still-unresolved issue**: I issued `pkill -f \"cargo test --workspace\"` to stop a 54-minute-running `cargo test --workspace` (PID 24174, confirmed via `ps -o pid,etime,%cpu,command` showing `ELAPSED 54:02`) after the user asked \"What's running that's taking hours??\" — **this Bash tool call was REJECTED by the system** with the exact error: *\"claude-sonnet-5[1m] is temporarily unavailable (rate-limited), so auto mode cannot determine the safety of Bash right now. Wait a moment and then try this action again. If it keeps failing, continue with other tasks that don't require this action and come back to it later. Note: reading files, searching code, and other read-only operations do not require the classifier and can still be used.\"* This is the last event before the summary request arrived — the kill has NOT yet succeeded.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: correctly identifying that `[[fixed-group]]` (not a code fix) was the right solution to \"shouldn't versions be lined up,\" verified end-to-end via real `callisto version --dry-run --format json` output showing all 10 packages converging on `0.3.3 → 0.4.0` uniformly.\n   - Solved: proving the no-compounding guarantee both by code trace (aggregate.rs's max-union logic, groups.rs's single-bump-from-pristine-base logic) and by a new, real, passing regression test.\n   - Solved: navigating SPEC-005/PLAN-005 through their respective adversarial gate rounds, incorporating every blocker's exact suggested fix, and in two cases (the `proptest` omission, and re-verifying jq commands live against the actual repo) catching additional issues myself beyond what the automated gates found.\n   - Solved: T1 through T4 of PLAN-005 implemented directly (bypassing lambda:implementer agent dispatch entirely, per \"the established pattern of agent dispatches stalling on background test runs, I'll implement these 6 tasks directly myself\") — all with real RED-then-GREEN verification, fmt/clippy/full-crate-suite runs, and commits.\n   - **Ongoing/unresolved**: AC-012c (full workspace `cargo test --workspace` green) — three attempts all showed zero real test failures but were killed by external process interruption before completing (most recently at 54 minutes elapsed, stuck compiling/running through `callisto-moon`'s inherently slow WASM sandbox test suite). My own most recent kill attempt (`pkill -f \"cargo test --workspace\"`) was itself rejected by a temporary rate-limit on the safety classifier, not yet retried.\n\n6. All user messages (this window, non-tool-result, verbatim or near-verbatim):\n   - \"Are we confident this will result in a proper release? Also packages that have a diffent bump should be in a separate changeset. A changeset should have related things right? Are all the patch bumps related? If so they can go in one changeset but they are not related to the minor bumps if they are not the same bump level, right? Does that make sense?\"\n   - \"The first part, your assumption is incorrect. The way callisto should work is the highest bump should win-out when there are multiple changesets that are in a fixed group. Isn't that right? Isn't that in the spec? Check changelogs and knope to be sure.\"\n   - \"Yes, please add it now with a comprehensive spec, implementation, docs, tests, etc. Check changesets and knope of input\" *(referring to the previously-proposed `ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease` field fix)*\n   - \"Anything else we forgot to do??? Did we need to make any changes to the GH action???\"\n   - (via `/reload-plugins` local command, followed by a genuine user message) \"Think critically about ALL of the changes we made since the last version and triple check that we don't need any changes to the actions. Anything that can be simplified by support from callisto now?\"\n   - \"Yes, let's shipped them together right? We should make sure that we don't bump versions multiple times across a group of changesets in one release PR (two changesets with minor should not bump 0.2 -> 0.3 -> 0.4, it should be 0.2 -> 0.3). Do we have that speced out properly? Tested properly?\"\n   - \"Keep an eye on the running tasks, you lose track of them easily\"\n   - \"Been waiting for a while\"\n   - \"seems like we've been waiting for a while\"\n   - \"What's running that's taking hours??\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish AC-012c verification (full workspace test suite green) for PLAN-005's T4 — currently blocked on a killed/rate-limited process; needs the `pkill` retried (once the Bash rate-limit clears) or a decision to accept already-collected per-crate evidence (callisto-model, callisto-graph, callisto-cli all independently verified green; full `cargo build --workspace` already confirmed clean earlier) as sufficient, matching established session precedent of not re-running redundant/slow full-workspace checks.\n   - T5: Rewrite `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`'s GitHub Release creation loop (lines 200-216) to iterate release *entries* (not tag strings), read `isPrerelease` per-entry, drop the old `=~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)` regex entirely, hard-fail on missing/null/non-boolean `isPrerelease` (per AC-015's exact jq-based approach, forbidding the `//` operator). Covers AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-015. Also requires a new test under `.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/` following the `test_status_check_branching.sh` extraction-and-stub pattern (sed-range extraction of the exact script block, stub `gh`, assert on captured `gh release create` arguments), covering at minimum: SemVer/PEP440 prerelease-true case, prerelease-false case, missing-key case, non-boolean-value case.\n   - T6: Update `docs/01-spec.md`'s `ReleaseEntry` struct doc block (lines ~1740-1763, before `pub struct ReleaseEntry` at line 1742) to document the new field, AND append a new decision-table row 24 after row 23 (currently at line 2667) — explicitly NOT modifying row 23 itself (which documents an unrelated `changelog_section` decision). Covers AC-011.\n   - After T1-T6 all complete and verified: run fmt/clippy/full-suite one final time across all touched crates, commit any remaining pieces, then push all of PLAN-005's commits (spec `28aff95`, plan `5ae003e`, T1 `be00e08`, T2 `52365d0`, T3 `62d264b`, plus T4/T5/T6 once committed) to the `release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening` branch, and confirm CI goes green on PR #5 (https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/5) — this branch has NOT been pushed since before this SPEC-005 work began, so all of T1-T4's commits are currently local-only.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary was requested, I was executing PLAN-005's T4 (structural verification task, no code changes — covers AC-013, AC-014, AC-012c). I had already directly confirmed:\n   - AC-013 (no fallback branch): `grep -n \"is_prerelease\" crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs` → exactly 2 matches, confirmed the new one at line 510 is a bare field assignment with no wrapping conditional, and the pre-existing one at line 390 is unrelated/unchanged.\n   - AC-014 parts 1-2 (no new dependency, version.rs untouched): both `git diff --stat`/`git diff --` calls returned empty output as expected.\n   - AC-014 part 3 (no AGPL dependency edge): ran the corrected `cargo metadata --format-version 1 | jq -r --arg pkg callisto-model '.packages[] | select(.name == $pkg) | .dependencies[].name' | sort -u`, got exactly `camino, miette, path-slash, pep440_rs, proptest, schemars, semver, serde, serde_json, tempfile, thiserror` — matches the plan's (my own corrected) expected output.\n\n   I was in the middle of AC-012c (full workspace test suite green) when interrupted repeatedly:\n   - First `cargo test --workspace` attempt (task `bavthu3gy`) — killed externally while still compiling wasmtime/callisto-moon's dependency tree, zero failures logged.\n   - Second attempt (task `bbv1jflov`) — killed externally again while compiling, zero failures logged.\n   - Third attempt (task `bjh6uzzzw`, PID 24174, log at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/scratchpad/t4_workspace_full3.log`) — this one actually got INTO the test-running phase (unlike the first two which only got through compilation), reaching `callisto-cli`'s `schema_guard_test.rs`, then further into `callisto-moon`'s `moon_wasm_sandbox.rs` integration tests, which are known from earlier in this session to take 60+ seconds PER TEST due to real subprocess/WASM sandbox spawning. At the moment the user asked \"What's running that's taking hours??\", I checked `ps -o pid,etime,%cpu,command -p 24174` and found **54 minutes elapsed** with genuine ongoing progress (tests streaming \"ok\" results, zero FAILED anywhere in the log). I explained this clearly to the user and decided to kill this run, reasoning that `callisto-moon` is completely untouched by PLAN-005's T1-T3 diff (only `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli` were modified, and all three already passed their own full test suites individually earlier in T1/T2/T3's own verification steps), and that the workspace already built cleanly via `cargo build --workspace` earlier in the session.\n\n   I issued: `pkill -f \"cargo test --workspace\" 2>/dev/null; sleep 1; ps aux | grep \"cargo test\" | grep -v grep; echo done` — **this call was rejected** with the error: *\"claude-sonnet-5[1m] is temporarily unavailable (rate-limited), so auto mode cannot determine the safety of Bash right now. Wait a moment and then try this action again. If it keeps failing, continue with other tasks that don't require this action and come back to it later.\"* This is the exact last event before the summary/compaction request arrived. The `cargo test --workspace` process (PID 24174) may still be running at this moment — its actual current state is unknown until I check again.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Retry the exact same kill command once the Bash rate-limit clears (it should resolve shortly per the error message: \"Wait a moment and then try this action again\"): `pkill -f \"cargo test --workspace\" 2>/dev/null; sleep 1; ps aux | grep \"cargo test\" | grep -v grep; echo done` — or, if Bash remains unavailable, use only read-only verification (checking the log file directly via Read, which the error message explicitly says remains available: \"reading files, searching code, and other read-only operations do not require the classifier and can still be used\") to confirm whether the process already finished or is still stuck, before deciding whether to force-kill it again. Once resolved, proceed with the plan exactly as stated to the user immediately prior to this interruption: treat AC-012c as satisfied via the already-collected per-crate evidence (callisto-model/callisto-graph/callisto-cli all independently green, full workspace build already clean) rather than waiting further on the slow `callisto-moon` WASM sandbox suite, then move on to implementing PLAN-005's T5 (action.yml rewrite + new bash test) and T6 (docs update), following the exact same direct-implementation-with-TDD-verification approach used for T1-T4.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"36cca492-47d4-473f-bdc8-de6e46ffe47b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T21:39:48.315Z","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"36cca492-47d4-473f-bdc8-de6e46ffe47b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs","content":"//! AC-13 guard: none of this track's fixes may change any report struct's field shape,\n//! except where a task's explicit scope is the shape change itself. Permitted schema\n//! deltas: the additive DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant, TagReport/\n//! CreatedTag's field-shape fix (docs/01-spec.md §M.12.6: `tags` not `createdTags`,\n//! plus `CreatedTag::already_existed`), and the additive required field\n//! `ReleaseEntry.isPrerelease` (SPEC-005: computed from `Version::is_prerelease()`,\n//! never re-derived from the tag string). Expected sets below were captured from\n//! `callisto schema` against the live repository after those intentional changes.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\nuse std::process::Command;\n\nfn run_schema(target: &str) -> serde_json::Value {\n    let bin = env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_callisto\");\n    let out = Command::new(bin)\n        .args([\"schema\", \"--type\", target])\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"callisto schema must run\");\n    assert!(\n        out.status.success(),\n        \"callisto schema --type {target} failed: {}\",\n        String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\n    );\n    serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).expect(\"schema output must be valid JSON\")\n}\n\nfn required_and_props(schema: &serde_json::Value) -> (BTreeSet<String>, BTreeSet<String>) {\n    let required: BTreeSet<String> = schema[\"required\"]\n        .as_array()\n        .unwrap()\n        .iter()\n        .map(|v| v.as_str().unwrap().to_string())\n        .collect();\n    let props: BTreeSet<String> = schema[\"properties\"]\n        .as_object()\n        .unwrap()\n        .keys()\n        .cloned()\n        .collect();\n    (required, props)\n}\n\nfn set(items: &[&str]) -> BTreeSet<String> {\n    items.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect()\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged() {\n    let tag_schema = run_schema(\"tag\");\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&tag_schema);\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\"tags\", \"schemaVersion\"]));\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\"tags\", \"diagnostics\", \"schemaVersion\"]));\n\n    let created_tag = &tag_schema[\"definitions\"][\"CreatedTag\"];\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(created_tag);\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\"alreadyExisted\", \"package\", \"sha\", \"tagName\"]));\n    assert_eq!(props, req);\n\n    let status_schema = run_schema(\"status\");\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&status_schema);\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\"hasChangesets\", \"packages\", \"schemaVersion\"]));\n    assert_eq!(\n        props,\n        set(&[\"diagnostics\", \"hasChangesets\", \"packages\", \"schemaVersion\"])\n    );\n\n    let plan_schema = run_schema(\"plan-publish\");\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&plan_schema);\n    assert_eq!(\n        req,\n        set(&[\n            \"npmMainPackages\",\n            \"npmPlatformPackages\",\n            \"releases\",\n            \"rustCrates\",\n            \"schemaVersion\"\n        ])\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        props,\n        set(&[\n            \"diagnostics\",\n            \"npmMainPackages\",\n            \"npmPlatformPackages\",\n            \"pypiPackages\",\n            \"releases\",\n            \"rustCrates\",\n            \"schemaVersion\"\n        ])\n    );\n\n    let release_entry = &plan_schema[\"definitions\"][\"ReleaseEntry\"];\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(release_entry);\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\"isPrerelease\", \"package\", \"sha\", \"tagName\"]));\n    assert_eq!(\n        props,\n        set(&[\n            \"changelogSection\",\n            \"isPrerelease\",\n            \"package\",\n            \"sha\",\n            \"tagName\"\n        ])\n    );\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error() {\n    let tag_schema = run_schema(\"tag\");\n    let variants: BTreeSet<String> = tag_schema[\"definitions\"][\"DiagnosticCode\"][\"oneOf\"]\n        .as_array()\n        .unwrap()\n        .iter()\n        .map(|v| v[\"enum\"][0].as_str().unwrap().to_string())\n        .collect();\n\n    let expected = set(&[\n        \"empty-changeset\",\n        \"empty-summary\",\n        \"unknown-package\",\n        \"invalid-package-name\",\n        \"napi-target-added-not-in-members\",\n        \"napi-target-removed-still-on-disk\",\n        \"napi-coordination-not-yet-supported\",\n        \"graph-edge-disagreement\",\n        \"range-not-round-trippable\",\n        \"catalog-spec-not-rewritten\",\n        \"tag-glob-non-version-match\",\n        \"changesets-config-key-dropped\",\n        \"pre-major-inference-inert\",\n        \"changelog-section-not-found\",\n        \"changeset-read-error\",\n        \"git-discovery-failed\",\n        \"bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems\",\n        \"unrecognised-platform-triple\",\n        \"publish-target-not-implemented\",\n        \"package-set-matched-nothing\",\n        \"duplicate-platform-triple\",\n        \"changelog-read-error\",\n        \"ambiguous-package-name\",\n    ]);\n\n    assert_eq!(\n        variants, expected,\n        \"DiagnosticCode schema must gain exactly one new variant: ambiguous-package-name\"\n    );\n}\n","numLines":148,"startLine":1,"totalLines":148}},"displayPath":"crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"297cc491-b954-47ca-a702-3d8bcdf59699","timestamp":"2026-08-21T21:39:48.322Z","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
