{"parentUuid":"2bf46d80-593e-4c49-b26b-5b051096c8eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGcsbb3SsNYEC19Fx9Kk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012oukcbHr4R67sqoNZG6C1q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nspec = json.load(open('.claude/specs/SPEC-005-release-entry-is-prerelease.json'))\nfor ac in spec['acceptance_criteria']:\n    if ac['id'] in ('AC-008','AC-009','AC-010','AC-015'):\n        print(json.dumps(ac, indent=2))\n\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_read_input_tokens":87293,"output_tokens":256,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":71},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":87293,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGcsaoAisek5PtLAuE4H","type":"assistant","uuid":"657f3b3e-a6eb-4b37-81a3-2a3c4d4c88d8","timestamp":"2026-08-21T21:40:20.328Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"657f3b3e-a6eb-4b37-81a3-2a3c4d4c88d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f5c3712b-9d58-46b9-ad02-83bddc7fe7dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012oukcbHr4R67sqoNZG6C1q","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AC-008\",\n  \"criterion\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block) no longer contains the pattern `=~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)` anywhere in its script body.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": false\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"AC-009\",\n  \"criterion\": \"The loop iterates release *entries*, not tag strings -- e.g. `jq -c '.releases[]?'` -- and for each entry reads `tagName` and `isPrerelease` off that same entry object, so no cross-entry lookup by tag is performed. `gh release create \\\"$TAG\\\" --title \\\"$TAG\\\" --generate-notes` is invoked with the additional flag `--prerelease` if and only if that same entry's `isPrerelease` is `true`; when it is `false`, the same invocation runs with no `--prerelease` flag. Two entries rendering an identical tag string are processed independently, each on its own entry's `isPrerelease` value.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": false\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"AC-010\",\n  \"criterion\": \"A new test file under .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ (either a new script or an extension of test_status_check_branching.sh) follows the same established harness pattern -- it extracts the exact current run-body text of the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block directly out of action.yml via a `sed` range between its `::group::` and matching `::endgroup::` markers, stubs `gh` (and `jq` remains real) to capture invocation arguments, feeds it a fixture `$PLAN_JSON` value, and asserts on the captured `gh release create` argument list -- so the test cannot drift from action.yml's actual current logic. This test includes at minimum: one case with `isPrerelease: true` where the tag string contains no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring (the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture), one case with `isPrerelease: false`, one case covering AC-015's missing-key path, and one case covering AC-015's non-boolean-value path.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": false\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"AC-015\",\n  \"criterion\": \"For a release entry processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop whose `isPrerelease` key is absent, `null`, or of any JSON type other than boolean (e.g. a stale cached plan, a hand-edited fixture, or a plan produced by a pre-this-change callisto binary), the step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error message naming the offending tag, before any `gh release create` call is made for that entry -- it is never silently treated as `isPrerelease: false`. Presence and type are tested explicitly (e.g. `jq -e 'has(\\\"isPrerelease\\\") and (.isPrerelease|type==\\\"boolean\\\")'`); the `//` alternative operator must not be used to read this field, since `false // empty` yields empty and would make a legitimate `false` indistinguishable from a missing key.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": true\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d0b101b1-6e85-4ee0-8bda-56730ee7cdba","timestamp":"2026-08-21T21:40:21.862Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"AC-008\",\n  \"criterion\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop (the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block) no longer contains the pattern `=~ -(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)` anywhere in its script body.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": false\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"AC-009\",\n  \"criterion\": \"The loop iterates release *entries*, not tag strings -- e.g. `jq -c '.releases[]?'` -- and for each entry reads `tagName` and `isPrerelease` off that same entry object, so no cross-entry lookup by tag is performed. `gh release create \\\"$TAG\\\" --title \\\"$TAG\\\" --generate-notes` is invoked with the additional flag `--prerelease` if and only if that same entry's `isPrerelease` is `true`; when it is `false`, the same invocation runs with no `--prerelease` flag. Two entries rendering an identical tag string are processed independently, each on its own entry's `isPrerelease` value.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": false\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"AC-010\",\n  \"criterion\": \"A new test file under .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/ (either a new script or an extension of test_status_check_branching.sh) follows the same established harness pattern -- it extracts the exact current run-body text of the `::group::5. Creating GitHub Release Entries` block directly out of action.yml via a `sed` range between its `::group::` and matching `::endgroup::` markers, stubs `gh` (and `jq` remains real) to capture invocation arguments, feeds it a fixture `$PLAN_JSON` value, and asserts on the captured `gh release create` argument list -- so the test cannot drift from action.yml's actual current logic. This test includes at minimum: one case with `isPrerelease: true` where the tag string contains no alpha/beta/rc/pre/next substring (the AC-005 PEP 440 regression fixture), one case with `isPrerelease: false`, one case covering AC-015's missing-key path, and one case covering AC-015's non-boolean-value path.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": false\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"AC-015\",\n  \"criterion\": \"For a release entry processed by .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's GitHub Release creation loop whose `isPrerelease` key is absent, `null`, or of any JSON type other than boolean (e.g. a stale cached plan, a hand-edited fixture, or a plan produced by a pre-this-change callisto binary), the step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error message naming the offending tag, before any `gh release create` call is made for that entry -- it is never silently treated as `isPrerelease: false`. Presence and type are tested explicitly (e.g. `jq -e 'has(\\\"isPrerelease\\\") and (.isPrerelease|type==\\\"boolean\\\")'`); the `//` alternative operator must not be used to read this field, since `false // empty` yields empty and would make a legitimate `false` indistinguishable from a missing key.\",\n  \"is_error_case\": true\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"657f3b3e-a6eb-4b37-81a3-2a3c4d4c88d8","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
