{"parentUuid":"79d1b68f-9d1c-4c11-af03-2ea9c31daa53","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGeU6mXyyNfgkT2This3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_read_input_tokens":119702,"output_tokens":1852,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":541},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1852,"cache_read_input_tokens":119702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGeU5vSYRt8AaVbeZnPf","type":"assistant","uuid":"4a39cee8-ff96-46c7-a87c-e300e9fab612","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:01:20.049Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"4a39cee8-ff96-46c7-a87c-e300e9fab612","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGeU6mXyyNfgkT2This3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017egogvSiBE2VhxyXGQLwT4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/project_pr5_release_pipeline_hardening.md","content":"---\nname: project-pr5-release-pipeline-hardening\ndescription: \"PR #5 (release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening) shipped fixed-group max-severity-wins config, no-compounding regression test, and SPEC-005 (ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease) end to end; all CI checks green as of 2026-08-21.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118\n  modified: 2026-08-21\n---\n\n**Fixed-group semantics**: callisto's `[[fixed-group]]` config makes the *highest severity bump\namong the group's changesets win* (max-union aggregation, then a single bump from the pristine\non-disk base) — this is canonical per the spec/changesets/knope precedent, not a bug. A prior\ndiagnosis in this same session incorrectly called the diverging-versions symptom an\n`apply_version_plan` code bug; the real fix was declaring `callisto.toml`'s own workspace members\nunder `[[fixed-group]]`, which had simply never been added. Verified end-to-end via real\n`callisto version --dry-run --format json` output (all 10 workspace packages converging uniformly)\nand a new regression test (`test_fixed_group_two_changesets_converge_on_single_bump_not_compounded`\nin `crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs`) proving two independent changesets in one group\nconverge to one bump, not a compounded double-bump. Shipped in commit `8bb8eee`.\n\n**SPEC-005 / PLAN-005 (`ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease`)**: full canon→vector→lambda pipeline, shipped\n2026-08-20/21. `ReleaseEntry` gained a required `is_prerelease: bool` field\n(`crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs`), computed at construction from `Version::is_prerelease()`\n(`crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:510`) — covers both SemVer's `-` prerelease\ncomponent and PEP 440's dev/pre segments, neither of which the old tag-string regex\n(`-(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)`) could detect (e.g. `1.2.3a1` matched nothing). No schemaVersion bump\n— additive report fields never trigger one here, since no external registry consumer depends on\nthis JSON wire format.\n\n`.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`'s GitHub Release creation loop (T5, commit `1eb16b7`)\nwas rewritten to iterate `.releases[]` entries directly and read each entry's `isPrerelease` field,\nhard-failing (non-zero exit, before any `gh release create` call) if that field is missing, null,\nor non-boolean — never silently treated as `false`. New test:\n`.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_github_release_creation.sh`, following the existing\n`test_status_check_branching.sh` sed-extraction-of-the-real-script-block pattern. `docs/01-spec.md`\ngot the new field's doc block plus decision-table row 24 (T6, commit `90476d1`).\n\nAll of PR #5's CI checks (Formatting, Security, Clippy, Test Suite/WASM on both Ubuntu and macOS,\nCode Coverage) are green as of this shipment. See [[feedback_iterate_reviews_in_foreground]] for\nhow the spec/plan gates were run, and [[feedback_hardcoded_values]] for the general audit-rigor\nprecedent this track followed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_read_input_tokens":119702,"output_tokens":1852,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":541},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1852,"cache_read_input_tokens":119702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGeU5vSYRt8AaVbeZnPf","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1374526-a498-4018-8214-6abceeb2704d","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:01:33.822Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"f1374526-a498-4018-8214-6abceeb2704d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"86e1894d-c35b-4df9-97ec-885c9b60f730","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017egogvSiBE2VhxyXGQLwT4","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/project_pr5_release_pipeline_hardening.md"}]},"uuid":"69e0d82a-0808-4c7a-80dc-7cb6b185ef15","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:01:33.900Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/project_pr5_release_pipeline_hardening.md","content":"---\nname: project-pr5-release-pipeline-hardening\ndescription: \"PR #5 (release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening) shipped fixed-group max-severity-wins config, no-compounding regression test, and SPEC-005 (ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease) end to end; all CI checks green as of 2026-08-21.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118\n  modified: 2026-08-21T22:01:33.847Z\n---\n\n**Fixed-group semantics**: callisto's `[[fixed-group]]` config makes the *highest severity bump\namong the group's changesets win* (max-union aggregation, then a single bump from the pristine\non-disk base) — this is canonical per the spec/changesets/knope precedent, not a bug. A prior\ndiagnosis in this same session incorrectly called the diverging-versions symptom an\n`apply_version_plan` code bug; the real fix was declaring `callisto.toml`'s own workspace members\nunder `[[fixed-group]]`, which had simply never been added. Verified end-to-end via real\n`callisto version --dry-run --format json` output (all 10 workspace packages converging uniformly)\nand a new regression test (`test_fixed_group_two_changesets_converge_on_single_bump_not_compounded`\nin `crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs`) proving two independent changesets in one group\nconverge to one bump, not a compounded double-bump. Shipped in commit `8bb8eee`.\n\n**SPEC-005 / PLAN-005 (`ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease`)**: full canon→vector→lambda pipeline, shipped\n2026-08-20/21. `ReleaseEntry` gained a required `is_prerelease: bool` field\n(`crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs`), computed at construction from `Version::is_prerelease()`\n(`crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:510`) — covers both SemVer's `-` prerelease\ncomponent and PEP 440's dev/pre segments, neither of which the old tag-string regex\n(`-(alpha|beta|rc|pre|next)`) could detect (e.g. `1.2.3a1` matched nothing). No schemaVersion bump\n— additive report fields never trigger one here, since no external registry consumer depends on\nthis JSON wire format.\n\n`.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`'s GitHub Release creation loop (T5, commit `1eb16b7`)\nwas rewritten to iterate `.releases[]` entries directly and read each entry's `isPrerelease` field,\nhard-failing (non-zero exit, before any `gh release create` call) if that field is missing, null,\nor non-boolean — never silently treated as `false`. New test:\n`.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_github_release_creation.sh`, following the existing\n`test_status_check_branching.sh` sed-extraction-of-the-real-script-block pattern. `docs/01-spec.md`\ngot the new field's doc block plus decision-table row 24 (T6, commit `90476d1`).\n\nAll of PR #5's CI checks (Formatting, Security, Clippy, Test Suite/WASM on both Ubuntu and macOS,\nCode Coverage) are green as of this shipment. See [[feedback_iterate_reviews_in_foreground]] for\nhow the spec/plan gates were run, and [[feedback_hardcoded_values]] for the general audit-rigor\nprecedent this track followed.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1374526-a498-4018-8214-6abceeb2704d","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
