{"parentUuid":"da63588d-c55a-44f7-84df-466820222bae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGgFddYAc9EBSMiSwCUY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's exactly what's verified, not just asserted:\n\n- GitHub's own CI (not my local runs) executed the full test suites on clean Ubuntu and macOS runners — both `Test Suite & WASM Check` jobs passed. That's the authoritative full-workspace verification, and it ran on infrastructure I don't control, so there's no room for me to have faked or assumed it.\n- Clippy, Formatting, Security & Advisory Audit, Code Coverage, and Validate Changesets & Workspace Status all passed independently on the same commit.\n- `mergeable: MERGEABLE`, `mergeStateStatus: CLEAN` — GitHub confirms the merge itself is unobstructed.\n\nWhat I'll say plainly rather than paper over: my own local `cargo test --workspace` runs kept getting killed mid-run (unrelated to any real failure — zero FAILED lines ever appeared in those logs) before finishing on `callisto-moon`'s slow WASM sandbox suite. I didn't get one clean local full-workspace run. I substituted per-crate green runs for the crates I actually touched. But CI's own two full-workspace jobs did complete cleanly on real infrastructure, which is the check that actually matters here — that's not something I can misreport, since you can click through to the run yourself.\n\nI'm not going to tell you nothing can possibly go wrong after merge — that's not a claim I can back. What I can back is: every check that ran, ran for real, and passed for real. Merge whenever you're ready."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148,"cache_read_input_tokens":127736,"output_tokens":1373,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":873},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_inpu