{"parentUuid":"b36622ec-afc8-4efd-9b37-19aa284019ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGgP7kuu1fuSrceDkd49","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjciKVfET8kbMpjHtnFgTg","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"fork","name":"changeset-render-check","description":"Verify changeset-to-changelog rendering scope","prompt":"Read-only investigation, do not edit anything.\n\nContext: `.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md` is a single changeset file whose frontmatter lists 9 packages each with their own severity (e.g. `callisto-model: minor`, `callisto-moon: patch`), and whose body is one long markdown document with sections like \"Breaking Changes\", \"Features\", \"Security\", \"Fixes\", \"Performance\", \"Housekeeping\" — most bullet points only apply to 1-2 of the 9 packages (e.g. the `callisto matrix` command bullet only concerns callisto-graph, not callisto-format).\n\nI need to know EXACTLY how callisto turns this one changeset file into each package's CHANGELOG.md entry when `callisto version` runs. Specifically:\n\n1. Find the changeset parsing code (likely in `callisto-conventional` or wherever `.changeset/*.md` files are read) — find where the frontmatter (package: severity pairs) and the markdown body are extracted.\n2. Find where a changeset's body gets attached to a specific package's changelog entry (likely something in `callisto-changelog` or `callisto-graph`'s version/changelog assembly code, look for `ChangeSource::Changeset` or similar, and wherever `ChangelogInput.entries` gets built from changeset data).\n3. Determine: does EVERY package listed in one changeset's frontmatter get the changeset's ENTIRE body text as its changelog entry (i.e. callisto-format's CHANGELOG.md would show the full \"Breaking Changes / Features / Security / ...\" document even though most of it doesn't concern callisto-format)? Or is there some mechanism (e.g. a per-package `##` heading convention, or manual body-splitting) that scopes only the relevant portion to each package?\n4. If it's \"whole body to every listed package\" — is that documented/intended behavior in `docs/01-spec.md` or `docs/00-design.md`'s changeset section, or does the spec actually describe/expect per-package-scoped content within one changeset file?\n\nReport back concisely (under 400 words): the exact file:line where this attachment happens, whether the \"whole body to every package\" behavior is real, and whether it's spec-documented/intended or a gap. Do not propose a fix — just report the facts with citations."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1720,"cache_read_input_tokens":139292,"output_tokens":1914,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":953},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1720,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1914,"cache_read_input_tokens":139292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1720},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGgP6ta1UYEscA8cGWcx","type":"assistant","uuid":"8dbbcbe7-a87a-4fdf-b6ee-e3723fb55995","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:26:40.658Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
