{"parentUuid":"8342171c-27db-4e76-8979-7b3b8be0eff9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGgQwNt498M7Z15Q3FoZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On plans/specs cleanup: the established convention in this repo is to **keep them permanently** as an audit trail, not delete after shipping — `ACTIVE.md` still lists every past track (B, E, F, G, Spec A/Spec B, Track1/2/3B1/4/5/9) with a \"DONE\" marker rather than removing the entry, and their spec/plan JSON files are all still sitting in `.claude/specs/`/`.claude/plans/` going back to the start of this effort. So \"clean up\" would mean breaking an established pattern, not following one — if you want that changed, tell me what you actually want (delete the JSONs, archive them to a subfolder, just trim `ACTIVE.md` to a summary), because I don't want to guess and delete something you're treating as a record.\n\nOn the changeset: confirmed, not split — there's exactly one file, `.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md`, with all 9 packages and a single combined body. I'm checking something more important than the missed split right now: whether that one file's *entire* body (Breaking Changes, Features, Security, everything) gets written into every one of the 9 packages' `CHANGELOG.md`, including packages the bullet has nothing to do with — that would make this a real correctness bug, not just a hygiene preference. Verifying against the actual rendering code now, will report back with facts before proposing anything."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":141012,"output_tokens":1009,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":555},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_availa