{"parentUuid":"dab01407-dc8d-4023-8f03-3aecaba328a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGgVqW47vd1hneg7Wy6p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — and it's a real miss, not just a hygiene nitpick. The investigation found:\n\n- One changeset file's `summary` text is written **verbatim into every listed package's CHANGELOG.md**, unfiltered — this is deliberate, spec-documented behavior (`docs/00-design.md` §6.1, matching upstream `@changesets/cli`'s own model: one summary block per file, applied to every named package).\n- The spec's own stated remedy for \"a package showing irrelevant content\" is exactly what you asked for and I never did: **write multiple smaller, single-purpose changeset files**, each naming only the packages it actually concerns.\n- Concretely: `callisto-format`'s CHANGELOG.md is about to get the entire \"Breaking Changes / Features / Security / Fixes / Performance / Housekeeping\" essay, even though only ~2 of its ~30 bullets touch `callisto-format` at all.\n\nThat's a real gap I should have closed and didn't. The changeset hasn't been consumed yet (still sitting unrun in `.changeset/`), so it's fixable before you merge — I can split it into per-topic files (each scoped to the packages/severities it actually concerns) right now if you want that done before release.\n\nOn licensing — I don't have any context on \"lumen\" in this session (different project, nothing I've touched here), so I don't know what license you're moving it to or why. Callisto's current split, for reference: Layer 1 (`callisto-model`, `callisto-format`, `callisto-vcs`) is `MIT OR Apache-2.0`; everything else (`callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, `callisto-conventional`, `callisto-changelog`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-moon`, `callisto-fixtures`) is `AGPL-3.0-only`, deliberately isolating permissive data types from copyleft execution logic (`ARCHITECTURE.md`). What license is lumen moving to, and why — is this about relicensing the whole thing, or something narrower like just the CLI binary?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4062,"cache_read_input_tokens":144525,"output_tokens":1141,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":462},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4062,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":144525,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4062},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGgVpFQCK3q94QnFmNq8","type":"assistant","uuid":"0400238d-c521-4bcf-8bc9-4df8355de2e6","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:28:02.606Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
