{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"9a025078-c6cd-46a1-a9b1-2610ec490c6a","snapshotMessageId":"04394f46-f661-4838-b82b-85739f41259a","trackingPath":".changeset/security-hardening.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-08-21T22:37:34.877Z","realParentDir":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset"},"timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:37:34.892Z"}
{"parentUuid":"49e0eb80-bdc6-4c37-b72e-2c082057748c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGhEcLyxqBdigsypz2xp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sp5naeTxX2DbAGAkaXdf15","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n# Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant**, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_read_input_tokens":221388,"output_tokens":529,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":221388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":467},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGhEaqCgjPT4efLeNBZR","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a025078-c6cd-46a1-a9b1-2610ec490c6a","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:37:34.873Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"9a025078-c6cd-46a1-a9b1-2610ec490c6a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dc0d202e-5626-4519-a868-de7dad954fe3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sp5naeTxX2DbAGAkaXdf15","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b8325f25-3f97-47d5-a239-cf465442811b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T22:37:34.938Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n# Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant**, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9a025078-c6cd-46a1-a9b1-2610ec490c6a","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d11