{"parentUuid":"bf979b4d-9cea-441e-b240-3f752cc51dd3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e877a5a9-a850-4545-ae4f-100d7e4ceb26","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EMbNL1ePMpaoocJkvojGs5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tcallisto-model: minor\n3\tcallisto-graph: patch\n4\tcallisto-vcs: patch\n5\tcallisto-cli: patch\n6\tcallisto-conventional: patch\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling\n10\t\n11\t## Breaking Changes\n12\t\n13\t- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant**, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n14\t\n15\t## Security\n16\t\n17\t- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n18\t- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n19\t- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n20\t- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n21\t- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n22\t- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n23\t"}]},"uuid":"01805081-9d62-4bcd-b3f4-ebccdb888f05","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:06:27.226Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n# Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant**, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n","numLines":23,"startLine":1,"totalLines":23}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf979b4d-9cea-441e-b240-3f752cc51dd3","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
