{"parentUuid":"8d6877bd-062d-4f6a-9bba-dae38bdace72","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGjSi2cLmtsfvxnkCYXE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012CmNc9PhMJa4mHiny4RHqj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n**Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**\n\n- **Breaking:** new `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":257203,"output_tokens":522,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":522,"cache_read_input_tokens":257203,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGjSgutfMbbxmR8QyRuf","type":"assistant","uuid":"674f56c3-779b-4e33-b2a1-1f7d75f5ad49","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:06:31.440Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"674f56c3-779b-4e33-b2a1-1f7d75f5ad49","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e877a5a9-a850-4545-ae4f-100d7e4ceb26","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012CmNc9PhMJa4mHiny4RHqj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b39d68b1-d92c-44ca-885d-b08e615e98c5","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:06:31.515Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n**Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**\n\n- **Breaking:** new `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":14,"newStart":6,"newLines":9,"lines":[" callisto-conventional: patch"," ---"," ","-# Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling","+**Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**"," ","-## Breaking Changes","-","-- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant**, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).","-","-## Security","-","+- **Breaking:** new `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all)."," - Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole."," - `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL."," - The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole."]}],"originalFile":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n# Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant**, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"674f56c3-779b-4e33-b2a1-1f7d75f5ad49","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
