{"parentUuid":"a922e7a5-3f06-4f1e-9207-abc151ce870b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGjaLS4gJKKcurQh9fMb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the security-hardening and git-layer files, rewritten for consumer perspective and brevity."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":268911,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1319,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":486,"cache_read_input_tokens":268911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1319},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGjaKBQib3Xzi4M3KFKm","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc30e8fa-33b9-40b1-8c8b-906ecefc5f6a","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:08:12.826Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"bc30e8fa-33b9-40b1-8c8b-906ecefc5f6a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGjaLS4gJKKcurQh9fMb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BWzRtjtVKsWBuzEXHKNYiD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n**Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**\n\n- **Breaking:** a package name starting with `-` is now reported as its own error, instead of being misreported as a path-traversal error.\n- A malicious package name can no longer inject extra flags into the underlying `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish` command.\n- A malicious `publishConfig.registry` URL can no longer redirect an npm publish to an unapproved registry.\n- An absolute or `..`-containing `changesets.dir`/changelog path in `callisto.toml` is now rejected instead of allowing writes outside the workspace.\n- Credentials no longer leak into error messages from failed git or registry-CLI commands.\n- A runaway subprocess can no longer exhaust memory via unbounded output capture, or hang a command indefinitely.\n- A tag name starting with `-` is now rejected, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":268911,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1319,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":486,"cache_read_input_tokens":268911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1319},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGjaKBQib3Xzi4M3KFKm","type":"assistant","uuid":"9130cfa2-6bb9-415c-9edb-9b3d990246f1","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:08:15.927Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"9130cfa2-6bb9-415c-9edb-9b3d990246f1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e877a5a9-a850-4545-ae4f-100d7e4ceb26","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BWzRtjtVKsWBuzEXHKNYiD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b01cf196-c1c7-44f1-9fe8-8127a5ff9027","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:08:15.992Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/security-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n**Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**\n\n- **Breaking:** a package name starting with `-` is now reported as its own error, instead of being misreported as a path-traversal error.\n- A malicious package name can no longer inject extra flags into the underlying `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish` command.\n- A malicious `publishConfig.registry` URL can no longer redirect an npm publish to an unapproved registry.\n- An absolute or `..`-containing `changesets.dir`/changelog path in `callisto.toml` is now rejected instead of allowing writes outside the workspace.\n- Credentials no longer leak into error messages from failed git or registry-CLI commands.\n- A runaway subprocess can no longer exhaust memory via unbounded output capture, or hang a command indefinitely.\n- A tag name starting with `-` is now rejected, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":10,"newStart":8,"newLines":10,"lines":[" "," **Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**"," ","-- **Breaking:** new `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).","-- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.","-- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.","-- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.","-- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.","-- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.","-- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.","+- **Breaking:** a package name starting with `-` is now reported as its own error, instead of being misreported as a path-traversal error.","+- A malicious package name can no longer inject extra flags into the underlying `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish` command.","+- A malicious `publishConfig.registry` URL can no longer redirect an npm publish to an unapproved registry.","+- An absolute or `..`-containing `changesets.dir`/changelog path in `callisto.toml` is now rejected instead of allowing writes outside the workspace.","+- Credentials no longer leak into error messages from failed git or registry-CLI commands.","+- A runaway subprocess can no longer exhaust memory via unbounded output capture, or hang a command indefinitely.","+- A tag name starting with `-` is now rejected, closing a git argument-injection hole."]}],"originalFile":"---\ncallisto-model: minor\ncallisto-graph: patch\ncallisto-vcs: patch\ncallisto-cli: patch\ncallisto-conventional: patch\n---\n\n**Security hardening across publish, git, and subprocess handling**\n\n- **Breaking:** new `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant, split out from `PathTraversal` (which was wrongly reported for inputs with no `..` at all).\n- Package names are now validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole.\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL.\n- The `changesets.dir`/changelog path config value is now rejected if absolute or containing `..`, closing a path-traversal hole.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git and registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages.\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (DoS); reader-thread wait is also bounded so a hung descendant can't block `run_with_timeout`.\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected, and shelled git refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9130cfa2-6bb9-415c-9edb-9b3d990246f1","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
