{"parentUuid":"97eba0d1-bad7-40b3-98a4-f1237016cdee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGjdjpKntDhmMtrk317o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018zgzJnEm1jChgJ8kSB8StZ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/changelog-preview/crates/callisto-graph/CHANGELOG.md","limit":45},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":273605,"output_tokens":154,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":699,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":154,"cache_read_input_tokens":273605,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":699},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGjdiPk1VM8LxiPYmEvo","type":"assistant","uuid":"8c5ad6dc-aaaa-470b-942e-4d5ab22cada2","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:08:58.951Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"8c5ad6dc-aaaa-470b-942e-4d5ab22cada2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e877a5a9-a850-4545-ae4f-100d7e4ceb26","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018zgzJnEm1jChgJ8kSB8StZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# callisto-graph\n2\t\n3\t## 0.4.0\n4\t\n5\t### Minor Changes\n6\t\n7\t- **New `callisto matrix` command**\n8\t  \n9\t  - Discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`.\n10\t  - Builds a per-triple CI table: host runner, cross-compile flag, artifact name.\n11\t  - Reports `engines.node`/`requires-python` versions.\n12\t- **One changelog renderer, everywhere**\n13\t  \n14\t  - PR descriptions and `CHANGELOG.md` entries are now generated by the same logic, so they no longer disagree.\n15\t  - Bumps inferred from commit messages, and packages newly added to a group, now get a real changelog entry instead of a placeholder.\n16\t  - If several changes caused one package's bump, the changelog now lists all of them, not just one.\n17\t- **Fixed groups converge on a single, shared target version**\n18\t  \n19\t  - Packages in a `[[fixed-group]]` now bump to the same version together, instead of drifting apart when they carry changesets of different severity.\n20\t  - A group that would end up in an inconsistent state now aborts with a clear error instead of silently shipping a broken version.\n21\t  - Two differently-spelled group-member entries that actually point to the same package are now caught as a config error instead of silently accepted.\n22\t- **Better cross-ecosystem package discovery**\n23\t  \n24\t  - Packages excluded from your Cargo/npm/pnpm workspace (fuzz targets, scratch examples) no longer show up as release-managed.\n25\t  - A Rust crate and its same-named Python binding in one workspace no longer trigger a duplicate-package error.\n26\t  - `cargo:name`/`npm:name` prefixes in group config now work as documented.\n27\t  - A package name is no longer silently matched to the wrong ecosystem when the intended match is missing.\n28\t- **Manifest writes are batched and more reliable**\n29\t  \n30\t  - **Breaking (custom manifest integrations only):** implementing callisto's `Manifest` trait now requires a `persist()` method to actually write your changes.\n31\t  - Re-running a version bump is now safe and won't risk losing a write.\n32\t  - Multiple changes to the same manifest file in one run are now applied together instead of risking one overwriting another.\n33\t- **Platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` write planning**\n34\t  \n35\t  - Fixed groups with platform-specific packages (napi/maturin) now get their platform manifests and `optionalDependencies` updated automatically during a version bump — previously nothing happened.\n36\t- **npm publish access modeled as a 3-state enum**\n37\t  \n38\t  - **Breaking:** `plan-publish`'s npm target now reports `access` (`\"public\"`/`\"restricted\"`/unset) instead of a `restricted: bool` — update anything parsing that JSON field.\n39\t  - An unscoped npm package with `publishConfig.access: \"public\"` in its `package.json` is no longer silently dropped during publish planning.\n40\t- **Release-pipeline / CI Action contract correctness**\n41\t  \n42\t  - **Breaking:** several `--format json` field names changed or were added (`validate`, `compose-pr-body`, `tag`, `status`, `plan-publish`) — update any scripts parsing this output.\n43\t  - Re-tagging a release that already exists no longer reports the wrong commit sha.\n44\t  - The official GitHub Action now actually opens a release PR when changesets are pending — a bug made this step unreachable before.\n45\t  - GitHub Releases are now correctly marked prerelease for PEP 440 versions too (e.g. `1.2.3a1`), not just SemVer's `-` syntax."}]},"uuid":"3894717a-a426-4b6f-8bd9-c5d4aebc651d","timestamp":"2026-08-21T23:08:59.016Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/changelog-preview/crates/callisto-graph/CHANGELOG.md","content":"# callisto-graph\n\n## 0.4.0\n\n### Minor Changes\n\n- **New `callisto matrix` command**\n  \n  - Discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`.\n  - Builds a per-triple CI table: host runner, cross-compile flag, artifact name.\n  - Reports `engines.node`/`requires-python` versions.\n- **One changelog renderer, everywhere**\n  \n  - PR descriptions and `CHANGELOG.md` entries are now generated by the same logic, so they no longer disagree.\n  - Bumps inferred from commit messages, and packages newly added to a group, now get a real changelog entry instead of a placeholder.\n  - If several changes caused one package's bump, the changelog now lists all of them, not just one.\n- **Fixed groups converge on a single, shared target version**\n  \n  - Packages in a `[[fixed-group]]` now bump to the same version together, instead of drifting apart when they carry changesets of different severity.\n  - A group that would end up in an inconsistent state now aborts with a clear error instead of silently shipping a broken version.\n  - Two differently-spelled group-member entries that actually point to the same package are now caught as a config error instead of silently accepted.\n- **Better cross-ecosystem package discovery**\n  \n  - Packages excluded from your Cargo/npm/pnpm workspace (fuzz targets, scratch examples) no longer show up as release-managed.\n  - A Rust crate and its same-named Python binding in one workspace no longer trigger a duplicate-package error.\n  - `cargo:name`/`npm:name` prefixes in group config now work as documented.\n  - A package name is no longer silently matched to the wrong ecosystem when the intended match is missing.\n- **Manifest writes are batched and more reliable**\n  \n  - **Breaking (custom manifest integrations only):** implementing callisto's `Manifest` trait now requires a `persist()` method to actually write your changes.\n  - Re-running a version bump is now safe and won't risk losing a write.\n  - Multiple changes to the same manifest file in one run are now applied together instead of risking one overwriting another.\n- **Platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` write planning**\n  \n  - Fixed groups with platform-specific packages (napi/maturin) now get their platform manifests and `optionalDependencies` updated automatically during a version bump — previously nothing happened.\n- **npm publish access modeled as a 3-state enum**\n  \n  - **Breaking:** `plan-publish`'s npm target now reports `access` (`\"public\"`/`\"restricted\"`/unset) instead of a `restricted: bool` — update anything parsing that JSON field.\n  - An unscoped npm package with `publishConfig.access: \"public\"` in its `package.json` is no longer silently dropped during publish planning.\n- **Release-pipeline / CI Action contract correctness**\n  \n  - **Breaking:** several `--format json` field names changed or were added (`validate`, `compose-pr-body`, `tag`, `status`, `plan-publish`) — update any scripts parsing this output.\n  - Re-tagging a release that already exists no longer reports the wrong commit sha.\n  - The official GitHub Action now actually opens a release PR when changesets are pending — a bug made this step unreachable before.\n  - GitHub Releases are now correctly marked prerelease for PEP 440 versions too (e.g. `1.2.3a1`), not just SemVer's `-` syntax.","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c5ad6dc-aaaa-470b-942e-4d5ab22cada2","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
