{"parentUuid":"cfb7f3ee-eb3c-4d9f-82c1-3592d007d431","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGqTCxN1cWE64uytfpEa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That failed test — `execute_extension_git_binary_absent_reports_notfound_via_real_exec_seam` — traps on `FailedPluginCall` instead of catching a clean \"not found\" error. Importantly:\n\n- **This run and the PR's own passing runs share the identical tree** (zero diff between `8becde04` and the merge commit `4f1cafff`) — so this isn't a regression from anything I shipped; the same code passed CI twice already.\n- The test's own inline comment documents a known, previously-investigated fragility: the real WASM host's `exec_command` can trap instead of returning a catchable error when a binary is \"already known to be missing,\" and this file's git history shows 5 separate prior fixes for exactly this class of environment/PATH-race flakiness in this test suite.\n\nThis looks like a pre-existing flaky test, not something PR #5 introduced. Let me re-run the failed job to confirm it's transient rather than asserting that from reasoning alone."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1940,"cache_read_input_tokens":306481,"output_tokens":1740,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1359},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1940,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1740,"cache_read_input_tokens":306481,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1940},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGqTBpeGBeXLMb9ChNtx","type":"assistant","uuid":"a80152d0-1262-4e85-9676-06e7fd693e55","timestamp":"2026-08-2