{"parentUuid":"78a3eaab-db68-4eb9-a467-c1ef5fd21aab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGqfETyU31bVJcUrFGD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2069,"cache_read_input_tokens":317677,"output_tokens":1775,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1044},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2069,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1775,"cache_read_input_tokens":317677,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2069},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGqfD6NjKFYmxJ2EfFPr","type":"assistant","uuid":"654fe47b-f70c-4ca0-bb3c-bc7a0769afad","timestamp":"2026-08-22T00:28:13.190Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"654fe47b-f70c-4ca0-bb3c-bc7a0769afad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGqfETyU31bVJcUrFGD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good question — let me give you what I actually found, with appropriate confidence levels, rather than a hand-wave.\n\n**What's already been tried:** this exact test file has a `PATH_MUTEX` (a real `tokio::sync::Mutex` serializing every PATH-mutating test in the binary) added specifically after \"running this suite without `--test-threads=1` produced spurious failures\" — so cross-test PATH races within one process are already supposed to be closed. This file's git history shows 5 prior fixes for exactly this class of environment flakiness.\n\n**What's different about this failure:** it's not a wrong-PATH-value symptom — it's the WASM host trapping (`FailedPluginCall`) instead of returning a catchable error. The test's own comment documents that this specific trap is a known Extism/host-boundary behavior when `git` is invoked while genuinely absent, and says the code is supposed to avoid ever reaching that trap-prone path by checking `command_exists(\"git\")` first. If we saw the trap, that check either raced or didn't see what the test set up in time — and the actual plugin-creation/caching internals live in an external crate (`moon_pdk_test_utils`), not this repo, so I can't fully confirm the mechanism by reading our own source alone.\n\nGiven that, here's what I'd actually do, in order of cost:\n\n1. **Cheapest, lowest-risk:** wrap just this test's plugin call in a small bounded retry (2-3 attempts) — standard practice for a host-environment-sensitive sandbox test, and doesn't touch production code at all.\n2. **Slightly more isolation:** verify whether `sandbox.create_extension` reuses any cached plugin/module state across tests in this file, and if so, force fresh creation after the PATH guard is set (right now I can't confirm this from static reading — would need to actually trace into that dependency).\n3. **Root-cause properly:** this predates PR #5 and isn't something I introduced — I'd treat it as its own follow-up investigation rather than patch it blind right now.\n\nWant me to just add the retry wrapper (fast, pragmatic), or actually dig into `moon_pdk_test_utils`'s plugin-creation internals to confirm the real mechanism first?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2069,"cache_read_input_tokens":317677,"output_tokens":1775,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1044},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2069,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1775,"cache_read_input_tokens":317677,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2069},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGqfD6NjKFYmxJ2EfFPr","type":"assistant","uuid":"8fc48085-b7d3-4eb5-bf35-5f69d519a7be","timestamp":"2026-08-22T00:28:21.084Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
