{"parentUuid":"cca07a1c-0631-4701-b7f9-cc91c8be7e0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGsReTxGPU5yxX5juK7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2290,"cache_read_input_tokens":349357,"output_tokens":2462,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1908},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2290,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2462,"cache_read_input_tokens":349357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2290},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGsRcQBUkBoFGATQGtAH","type":"assistant","uuid":"2772f379-9f37-4148-9f0e-bd7dcbf49c59","timestamp":"2026-08-22T00:51:31.149Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"2772f379-9f37-4148-9f0e-bd7dcbf49c59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGsReTxGPU5yxX5juK7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checked the real diff for both packages. The version number itself is correct (`callisto-graph` and `callisto-vcs` both bump to `0.4.0`, confirmed in their `Cargo.toml` diffs), and the changelog splitting *isn't* a bug — it's working as designed.\n\nFor `callisto-graph`, the split is legitimate: it has real minor-severity changes (new `callisto matrix` command, breaking changes) *and* real patch-only fixes, bundled into one release. Showing both sections under one version is normal — that's how `@changesets/cli`-style tools always render a release that bundles a minor change with some patches.\n\nFor `callisto-vcs`, there's already a mechanism for exactly your concern: it has zero minor-severity changesets of its own, but a synthetic entry — *\"Released together with the `workspace` fixed group.\"* — gets inserted under \"Minor Changes\" specifically to explain why a package with only patch-level fixes still got a minor bump. That's the `ChangeSource::GroupUnion` variant, already built for this.\n\nThe actual UX problem, I think, is this: that one-line explanation is dwarfed by a 15-bullet \"Patch Changes\" list right below it, so a reader skims past the real reason (fixed-group convergence) and comes away thinking \"this looks like a patch release with something odd tacked on.\" The version number and the categorization are both correct — the presentation just undersells *why*.\n\nI don't think this needs a code fix so much as a judgment call: do you want the `GroupUnion` explanation made more prominent (e.g., a bolder note, or listed differently when it's the *only* reason for the version bump), or is this fine as-is once you know what to look for?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2290,"cache_read_input_tokens":349357,"output_tokens":2462,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1908},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2290,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2462,"cache_read_input_tokens":349357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2290},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeGsRcQBUkBoFGATQGtAH","type":"assistant","uuid":"28bc8e01-45e1-4590-8c8b-2655bac39e64","timestamp":"2026-08-22T00:51:37.123Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
