{"parentUuid":"bec349a9-b265-4a58-912a-c17bd1d7e044","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeH4yagRKzqVx6d9cr7QP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qbm2Es7rJWKq1eAASJqTzZ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","offset":4880,"limit":45},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":377179,"output_tokens":335,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":217},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":377179,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeH4yYceZrcusCZ5x6744","type":"assistant","uuid":"d06b8f55-749b-4276-90ea-42b478dc326b","timestamp":"2026-08-22T03:22:40.492Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"d06b8f55-749b-4276-90ea-42b478dc326b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f33ed927-5970-4ad9-b678-041679a8cd99","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qbm2Es7rJWKq1eAASJqTzZ","type":"tool_result","content":"4880\t  > multiply-authored bump, which contradicts §6.1's \"summary paragraph\" being the whole point\n4881\t  > of a changeset. This is the smallest fix consistent with P1's byte-compat spirit — the\n4882\t  > changeset text itself must survive into the changelog, verbatim, or the crate has failed\n4883\t  > at its one job.\n4884\t\n4885\t- *Commit/PR linking.* `@changesets/cli`'s `changelog` config key selects a pluggable\n4886\t  generator, most commonly `@changesets/changelog-github`, which prefixes each bullet with a\n4887\t  commit hash and links a PR number via the GitHub API. §18 Q4's migration table already\n4888\t  resolves this: that key has **no equivalent** in `callisto.toml` and is dropped with a\n4889\t  warning, because `callisto-changelog` is a single built-in generator, not a plugin host\n4890\t  (§14 has no changelog-selection key for the same reason), and §9.5 removed all\n4891\t  HTTP/GitHub-API dependencies from callisto's tree entirely. This crate's default output\n4892\t  matches `@changesets/cli`'s own **built-in, non-GitHub** default generator shape — plain\n4893\t  summary text, no link — which is the one part of changesets' changelog behaviour that has\n4894\t  no external-service dependency and is therefore the only one worth being consistent with.\n4895\t  (The short commit sha in §CL.5's `Commit` bullet is read off `CommitSha::short`, not\n4896\t  fetched.)\n4897\t- *Byte-compatibility.* P1's guarantee is scoped to `.changeset/*.md` and `pre.json` only\n4898\t  (§4's scope note) — `CHANGELOG.md` is not part of it. This crate borrows changesets'\n4899\t  heading conventions (`## <version>`, `### Major Changes` / `### Minor Changes` /\n4900\t  `### Patch Changes`) because they are familiar to every migrating user and there is no\n4901\t  reason to invent new vocabulary for the same concept, not because anything requires it.\n4902\t- *Rendering `.bumps[].governedBy` attribution lines.* That is `callisto-cli`'s (§CLI.5.3) —\n4903\t  a CLI-output concern, not a changelog-content concern. This crate never reads `ConfigKey`\n4904\t  and has no dependency on it.\n4905\t\n4906\t### CL.2 Where this sits in the pipeline\n4907\t\n4908\t§7.6's mutation phase, with this crate's role made explicit:\n4909\t\n4910\t```text\n4911\t3. Write canonical manifests\n4912\t4. Write platform manifests\n4913\t5. Update optionalDependencies\n4914\t6. Rewrite dependency specs (cascade)\n4915\t7. Prepend changelog entries      ← callisto-changelog, this crate\n4916\t8. Delete consumed changeset files\n4917\t```\n4918\t\n4919\tStep 7 runs after every version-bearing write (3–6) and before changeset deletion (8) — by the\n4920\ttime this crate runs, every package's `to` version is final and every cascade decision has\n4921\talready fired, but the changeset files this crate's *input* was built from still exist on disk.\n4922\t\n4923\t**Called from two places, not one**, both driving the same pure `render_section` (§CL.5):\n4924\t"}]},"uuid":"2948e83b-54be-48c4-ba37-b3f77d66f373","timestamp":"2026-08-22T03:22:40.555Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"  > multiply-authored bump, which contradicts §6.1's \"summary paragraph\" being the whole point\n  > of a changeset. This is the smallest fix consistent with P1's byte-compat spirit — the\n  > changeset text itself must survive into the changelog, verbatim, or the crate has failed\n  > at its one job.\n\n- *Commit/PR linking.* `@changesets/cli`'s `changelog` config key selects a pluggable\n  generator, most commonly `@changesets/changelog-github`, which prefixes each bullet with a\n  commit hash and links a PR number via the GitHub API. §18 Q4's migration table already\n  resolves this: that key has **no equivalent** in `callisto.toml` and is dropped with a\n  warning, because `callisto-changelog` is a single built-in generator, not a plugin host\n  (§14 has no changelog-selection key for the same reason), and §9.5 removed all\n  HTTP/GitHub-API dependencies from callisto's tree entirely. This crate's default output\n  matches `@changesets/cli`'s own **built-in, non-GitHub** default generator shape — plain\n  summary text, no link — which is the one part of changesets' changelog behaviour that has\n  no external-service dependency and is therefore the only one worth being consistent with.\n  (The short commit sha in §CL.5's `Commit` bullet is read off `CommitSha::short`, not\n  fetched.)\n- *Byte-compatibility.* P1's guarantee is scoped to `.changeset/*.md` and `pre.json` only\n  (§4's scope note) — `CHANGELOG.md` is not part of it. This crate borrows changesets'\n  heading conventions (`## <version>`, `### Major Changes` / `### Minor Changes` /\n  `### Patch Changes`) because they are familiar to every migrating user and there is no\n  reason to invent new vocabulary for the same concept, not because anything requires it.\n- *Rendering `.bumps[].governedBy` attribution lines.* That is `callisto-cli`'s (§CLI.5.3) —\n  a CLI-output concern, not a changelog-content concern. This crate never reads `ConfigKey`\n  and has no dependency on it.\n\n### CL.2 Where this sits in the pipeline\n\n§7.6's mutation phase, with this crate's role made explicit:\n\n```text\n3. Write canonical manifests\n4. Write platform manifests\n5. Update optionalDependencies\n6. Rewrite dependency specs (cascade)\n7. Prepend changelog entries      ← callisto-changelog, this crate\n8. Delete consumed changeset files\n```\n\nStep 7 runs after every version-bearing write (3–6) and before changeset deletion (8) — by the\ntime this crate runs, every package's `to` version is final and every cascade decision has\nalready fired, but the changeset files this crate's *input* was built from still exist on disk.\n\n**Called from two places, not one**, both driving the same pure `render_section` (§CL.5):\n","numLines":45,"startLine":4880,"totalLines":11457}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d06b8f55-749b-4276-90ea-42b478dc326b","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
