{"parentUuid":"8c6b180b-5633-4395-91e5-0ee361da88cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeH4yx5HKm14KZi7gfFr4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NCgbCZ7U2Zjof2ZGsYDUX5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","offset":5040,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1565,"cache_read_input_tokens":378550,"output_tokens":497,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":379},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":378550,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeH4yv8Cy7afQK9HEMvhk","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b1d35d2-6aea-4733-91c3-0a7c7ab7d79e","timestamp":"2026-08-22T03:22:47.013Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3b1d35d2-6aea-4733-91c3-0a7c7ab7d79e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f33ed927-5970-4ad9-b678-041679a8cd99","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NCgbCZ7U2Zjof2ZGsYDUX5","type":"tool_result","content":"5040\t> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: `ChangeSource` has exactly these six variants, a\n5041\t> subset of `BumpReason`'s eight.]` `BumpReason::PreRelease { tag }` (§8's pre-mode counter) is\n5042\t> deliberately **not** a `ChangeSource` — pre-mode never fires in isolation; the real cause is\n5043\t> always one of the six variants above, and pre-mode only changes which *version number* that\n5044\t> cause produces (`pre.0` vs. a real release), not *what content* the changelog should show.\n5045\t> `render_section` takes the already-resolved `to: Option<Version>` — including a prerelease\n5046\t> version string when relevant — so it needs no separate pre-mode branch.\n5047\t\n5048\t### CL.4 Severity grouping — the rule, made structural\n5049\t\n5050\t```rust\n5051\t/// Groups a `ChangelogInput`'s entries into the three renderable buckets, in render order.\n5052\t/// Buckets with zero entries are simply absent from the result — `render_section` (§CL.5)\n5053\t/// never emits an empty `### <X> Changes` heading.\n5054\t///\n5055\t/// `Severity::None` entries are rejected here, not silently dropped: constructing a\n5056\t/// `ChangelogEntry` with `severity: Severity::None` is a caller bug (§CL.3's doc comment says\n5057\t/// why one should never exist), and returning an error rather than quietly discarding it means\n5058\t/// that bug surfaces as a test failure in `callisto-graph`'s aggregation code, not as a\n5059\t/// silently-thinner changelog nobody notices.\n5060\tpub fn group_entries(entries: &[ChangelogEntry]) -> Result<GroupedEntries<'_>, ChangelogError>;\n5061\t\n5062\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n5063\tpub struct GroupedEntries<'a> {\n5064\t    pub major: Vec<&'a ChangelogEntry>,\n5065\t    pub minor: Vec<&'a ChangelogEntry>,\n5066\t    pub patch: Vec<&'a ChangelogEntry>,\n5067\t}\n5068\t```\n5069\t\n5070\t### CL.5 Rendering — `render.rs`\n5071\t\n5072\t```rust\n5073\t/// Pure. No file I/O, no `CommandRunner` — the WASM-safety property this crate leans on is\n5074\t/// simply \"this function touches no external state at all.\" Called identically by `version`'s\n5075\t/// mutation phase and by `compose-pr-body`'s preview (§CL.2).\n5076\t///\n5077\t/// Output shape (heading levels chosen to nest under a package's `# <name>` file header,\n5078\t/// §CL.6):\n5079\t///\n5080\t/// ```markdown\n5081\t/// ## 1.3.0\n5082\t///\n5083\t/// ### Major Changes\n5084\t///\n5085\t/// - Widen the public `Foo` trait to accept async closures.\n5086\t///\n5087\t/// ### Patch Changes\n5088\t///\n5089\t/// - Fix a panic when `bar()` is called with an empty slice.\n5090\t/// - Dependency updates\n5091\t///   - `@myorg/sdk` → `2.0.0`\n5092\t///   - `@myorg/utils` → `1.4.1`\n5093\t/// ```\n5094\t///\n5095\t/// When `input.to` is `None` — a package with contributing entries but no computable target\n5096\t/// version (§CL.3) — the heading renders as `## Unreleased` instead of a version number,\n5097\t/// matching the one case where changesets' own convention already has a name for \"a version\n5098\t/// that does not exist yet.\" This is **not** the normal `compose-pr-body` path: that call\n5099\t/// site supplies a real prospective version (§G.11's `compose_pr_body`, §CL.7.2).\n5100\tpub fn render_section(input: &ChangelogInput) -> Result<String, ChangelogError>;\n5101\t```\n5102\t\n5103\tBullet text per `ChangeSource` variant (all rendered as `- <text>`, at 2-space nested indent\n5104\tfor the `DependencyUpdate` sub-list):\n5105\t\n5106\t| Variant | Rendered text |\n5107\t|---|---|\n5108\t| `Changeset { summary, .. }` | `summary`, verbatim |\n5109\t| `Commit { subject, sha }` | `` `subject` (`{sha.short()}`) `` — 7 characters, matching `git`'s own default abbreviation length |\n5110\t| `DependencyUpdate { .. }` (≥1 in a section) | one parent bullet `Dependency updates`, followed by one nested `` `{dependency}` → `{to}` `` line per entry, all `DependencyUpdate`s in that section collapsed under the single parent bullet |\n5111\t| `PeerEscalation { dependency, to }` | `` Peer dependency `{dependency}` requires `{to}` `` — rendered standalone, not nested under `DependencyUpdate`'s parent bullet, per §CL.3's rationale for keeping the variant distinct |\n5112\t| `GroupUnion { group, kind }` | ``Released together with the `{group}` {fixed \\| linked} group.`` |\n5113\t| `NewGroupMember { group }` | ``Joined the `{group}` group at this version.`` |\n5114\t\n5115\t> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: the exact bullet-text templates above.]` Neither the\n5116\t> design doc nor P1 constrains changelog prose. These are kept close to `@changesets/cli`'s own\n5117\t> wording (`Dependency updates` mirrors its `Updated dependencies`) specifically so a migrating\n5118\t> user's muscle memory for reading a changesets-generated `CHANGELOG.md` transfers with minimal\n5119\t> friction — the same adoption-friction reasoning P1 applies to the file formats it does"}]},"uuid":"45d04073-1c10-496a-b957-72b9d2263c97","timestamp":"2026-08-22T03:22:47.081Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: `ChangeSource` has exactly these six variants, a\n> subset of `BumpReason`'s eight.]` `BumpReason::PreRelease { tag }` (§8's pre-mode counter) is\n> deliberately **not** a `ChangeSource` — pre-mode never fires in isolation; the real cause is\n> always one of the six variants above, and pre-mode only changes which *version number* that\n> cause produces (`pre.0` vs. a real release), not *what content* the changelog should show.\n> `render_section` takes the already-resolved `to: Option<Version>` — including a prerelease\n> version string when relevant — so it needs no separate pre-mode branch.\n\n### CL.4 Severity grouping — the rule, made structural\n\n```rust\n/// Groups a `ChangelogInput`'s entries into the three renderable buckets, in render order.\n/// Buckets with zero entries are simply absent from the result — `render_section` (§CL.5)\n/// never emits an empty `### <X> Changes` heading.\n///\n/// `Severity::None` entries are rejected here, not silently dropped: constructing a\n/// `ChangelogEntry` with `severity: Severity::None` is a caller bug (§CL.3's doc comment says\n/// why one should never exist), and returning an error rather than quietly discarding it means\n/// that bug surfaces as a test failure in `callisto-graph`'s aggregation code, not as a\n/// silently-thinner changelog nobody notices.\npub fn group_entries(entries: &[ChangelogEntry]) -> Result<GroupedEntries<'_>, ChangelogError>;\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct GroupedEntries<'a> {\n    pub major: Vec<&'a ChangelogEntry>,\n    pub minor: Vec<&'a ChangelogEntry>,\n    pub patch: Vec<&'a ChangelogEntry>,\n}\n```\n\n### CL.5 Rendering — `render.rs`\n\n```rust\n/// Pure. No file I/O, no `CommandRunner` — the WASM-safety property this crate leans on is\n/// simply \"this function touches no external state at all.\" Called identically by `version`'s\n/// mutation phase and by `compose-pr-body`'s preview (§CL.2).\n///\n/// Output shape (heading levels chosen to nest under a package's `# <name>` file header,\n/// §CL.6):\n///\n/// ```markdown\n/// ## 1.3.0\n///\n/// ### Major Changes\n///\n/// - Widen the public `Foo` trait to accept async closures.\n///\n/// ### Patch Changes\n///\n/// - Fix a panic when `bar()` is called with an empty slice.\n/// - Dependency updates\n///   - `@myorg/sdk` → `2.0.0`\n///   - `@myorg/utils` → `1.4.1`\n/// ```\n///\n/// When `input.to` is `None` — a package with contributing entries but no computable target\n/// version (§CL.3) — the heading renders as `## Unreleased` instead of a version number,\n/// matching the one case where changesets' own convention already has a name for \"a version\n/// that does not exist yet.\" This is **not** the normal `compose-pr-body` path: that call\n/// site supplies a real prospective version (§G.11's `compose_pr_body`, §CL.7.2).\npub fn render_section(input: &ChangelogInput) -> Result<String, ChangelogError>;\n```\n\nBullet text per `ChangeSource` variant (all rendered as `- <text>`, at 2-space nested indent\nfor the `DependencyUpdate` sub-list):\n\n| Variant | Rendered text |\n|---|---|\n| `Changeset { summary, .. }` | `summary`, verbatim |\n| `Commit { subject, sha }` | `` `subject` (`{sha.short()}`) `` — 7 characters, matching `git`'s own default abbreviation length |\n| `DependencyUpdate { .. }` (≥1 in a section) | one parent bullet `Dependency updates`, followed by one nested `` `{dependency}` → `{to}` `` line per entry, all `DependencyUpdate`s in that section collapsed under the single parent bullet |\n| `PeerEscalation { dependency, to }` | `` Peer dependency `{dependency}` requires `{to}` `` — rendered standalone, not nested under `DependencyUpdate`'s parent bullet, per §CL.3's rationale for keeping the variant distinct |\n| `GroupUnion { group, kind }` | ``Released together with the `{group}` {fixed \\| linked} group.`` |\n| `NewGroupMember { group }` | ``Joined the `{group}` group at this version.`` |\n\n> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: the exact bullet-text templates above.]` Neither the\n> design doc nor P1 constrains changelog prose. These are kept close to `@changesets/cli`'s own\n> wording (`Dependency updates` mirrors its `Updated dependencies`) specifically so a migrating\n> user's muscle memory for reading a changesets-generated `CHANGELOG.md` transfers with minimal\n> friction — the same adoption-friction reasoning P1 applies to the file formats it does","numLines":80,"startLine":5040,"totalLines":11457}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b1d35d2-6aea-4733-91c3-0a7c7ab7d79e","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
