{"parentUuid":"151ffdf1-cf7e-4e71-97a9-94f15e21c0dd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f33ed927-5970-4ad9-b678-041679a8cd99","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SqeTk8fuFs4wYpbgKFMRvp","type":"tool_result","content":"5119\t> friction — the same adoption-friction reasoning P1 applies to the file formats it does\n5120\t> guarantee, applied here as a *design preference*, not a *compatibility requirement*.\n5121\t\n5122\t### CL.6 Writing — `write.rs`\n5123\t\n5124\t```rust\n5125\t/// Prepends `rendered` (the output of `render_section`) to the package's `CHANGELOG.md`,\n5126\t/// creating the file with a `# <display_name>` header if it does not exist yet. Never touches\n5127\t/// any earlier section — this is a pure prepend, matching every other changelog-generating\n5128\t/// tool's newest-first convention.\n5129\t///\n5130\t/// `root` is the workspace root (an already-resolved absolute path supplied by the caller —\n5131\t/// this crate does not resolve it); `changelog_path` is `Package.changelog`'s value (§5.1,\n5132\t/// §M.6.1), workspace-root-relative per §M.1.3.\n5133\t///\n5134\t/// Plain `std::fs` read/write — no format-preserving-editor machinery is needed the way\n5135\t/// `callisto-manifests`' TOML/JSON writers need one (§CM.5.1), because there is no existing\n5136\t/// structure to preserve: a prepend to a Markdown file is byte-identical whether or not\n5137\t/// anything already understands the file's contents.\n5138\tpub fn prepend("}]},"uuid":"4d58d6ca-4974-48d5-b05f-77f63627e2f8","timestamp":"2026-08-22T03:22:50.882Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"> friction — the same adoption-friction reasoning P1 applies to the file formats it does\n> guarantee, applied here as a *design preference*, not a *compatibility requirement*.\n\n### CL.6 Writing — `write.rs`\n\n```rust\n/// Prepends `rendered` (the output of `render_section`) to the package's `CHANGELOG.md`,\n/// creating the file with a `# <display_name>` header if it does not exist yet. Never touches\n/// any earlier section — this is a pure prepend, matching every other changelog-generating\n/// tool's newest-first convention.\n///\n/// `root` is the workspace root (an already-resolved absolute path supplied by the caller —\n/// this crate does not resolve it); `changelog_path` is `Package.changelog`'s value (§5.1,\n/// §M.6.1), workspace-root-relative per §M.1.3.\n///\n/// Plain `std::fs` read/write — no format-preserving-editor machinery is needed the way\n/// `callisto-manifests`' TOML/JSON writers need one (§CM.5.1), because there is no existing\n/// structure to preserve: a prepend to a Markdown file is byte-identical whether or not\n/// anything already understands the file's contents.\npub fn prepend(","numLines":20,"startLine":5119,"totalLines":11457}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"151ffdf1-cf7e-4e71-97a9-94f15e21c0dd","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
