{"parentUuid":"5f9ee1d5-f333-4082-a175-9225aeff6730","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeH7YuMENy3JkrkfnAtK4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017fuDbh3d4kFim7fyQVAGHS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(changelog): render one flat bullet list per version, drop severity split\n\nrender_section previously grouped a version's entries into ### Major/\nMinor/Patch Changes sub-headings, mirroring @changesets/cli. Once a\nversion's own heading already states the one real applied bump (which\na fixed group's convergence, not any single entry's originally-authored\nseverity, decides), resurfacing each entry's individual severity added\na reader-facing distinction with no reader-facing meaning -- and for a\npackage bumped solely by group convergence, produced a one-line \"Minor\nChanges\" section dwarfed by an unrelated \"Patch Changes\" list below it,\nvisually implying a patch release under a heading that had just bumped\nminor.\n\ndocs/01-spec.md §CL.4/§CL.5 already scoped CHANGELOG.md's heading style\nout of P1's byte-compatibility guarantee (a borrowed convention, not a\nrequirement), so this doesn't touch that guarantee -- only a stylistic\nchoice this crate had made on top of it. group_entries/GroupedEntries\nhad no other caller and is removed rather than left dead.\nEOF\n)\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":401603,"output_tokens":459,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":340,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":401603,"cache_cr