{"parentUuid":"aa7be784-876a-4430-a442-7ca2de2ed557","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeH7bax2YD1xs32BJAR5T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MS2xTSiHJ6vADWvVWdhUt2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngh pr create --title \"fix(changelog): flatten severity grouping in rendered CHANGELOG.md\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- `render_section` previously split one version's entries into `### Major/Minor/Patch Changes` sub-headings, mirroring `@changesets/cli`. That's now a single flat bullet list per version.\n- Removed `group_entries`/`GroupedEntries` (no other caller).\n- `docs/01-spec.md` §CL.4/§CL.5 updated — this was always a borrowed stylistic convention, not part of P1's byte-compatibility guarantee (which is scoped to `.changeset/*.md`/`pre.json`, not `CHANGELOG.md`).\n\n## Why\nOnce a version's own heading states the one real applied bump (a fixed group's convergence decides that, not any single entry's originally-authored severity), re-splitting entries underneath by their own severity adds a distinction with no reader-facing meaning. For a package bumped solely by fixed-group convergence, this previously rendered a one-line \"Minor Changes\" section dwarfed by an unrelated \"Patch Changes\" list — visually implying a patch release under a heading that had just bumped minor. See the currently-open `chore(release): version packages` PR for a live example.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-changelog` — 13/13 pass, including a new test pinning the flattened, mixed-severity case\n- [x] `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` — clean\n- [x] `cargo fmt` / `cargo clippy -p callisto-changelog --all-targets -- -D warnings` — clean\n- [x] Confirmed no other crate references the removed `group_entries`/`GroupedEntries` or asserts on the old heading text\nEOF\n)\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":nul