{"parentUuid":"a7e8f1c4-11bd-4b29-ae09-ddf0cd39d7bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJ7RRcBQjf6bmTRdy3bh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1914,"cache_read_input_tokens":435035,"output_tokens":2937,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2150},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1914,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":435035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1914},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJ7RPoXiJmsjeuXryCju","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbe391b0-45bb-4171-8a55-7024ab77fd89","timestamp":"2026-08-22T16:35:41.776Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"flatten-changelog-severity-grouping","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"fbe391b0-45bb-4171-8a55-7024ab77fd89","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJ7RRcBQjf6bmTRdy3bh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed the exact mechanism, and it's a real bug — one I introduced earlier in this session, not something transient.\n\n**Root cause:** `callisto-vcs` is a *dev-dependency* of `callisto-conventional` (from this session's own earlier \"decouple `callisto-conventional` from `callisto-vcs`\" fix, which correctly moved production code onto a `CommitWalker` trait but left `callisto-vcs` as a test-only dependency). `plan_publish`'s topological sort (`ws.graph.toposort`) reuses the *same* dependency graph as cascade/version-bump propagation — which correctly excludes dev-dependency edges for versioning purposes, but that same graph also decides **publish order**, where dev-dependencies still matter: `cargo publish` (run without `--no-verify`, confirmed in `publish_client.rs`) does a local verification build that needs to compile the crate's test suite, which needs dev-dependencies resolvable from the registry.\n\nSince there's no ordering edge between `callisto-conventional` and `callisto-vcs` anymore, the toposort had no reason to sequence `callisto-vcs` first — it just happened to attempt `callisto-conventional` before `callisto-vcs` had gotten uploaded, so `cargo publish`'s own verification build failed to resolve it. This is a real design gap: cascade ordering and publish ordering have different edge-inclusion requirements, and today they're conflated into one graph.\n\n**Current live state (crates.io):** `callisto-model`, `callisto-changelog`, `callisto-format`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-vcs` are live at `0.4.0`. `callisto-conventional`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, `callisto-moon` are still stuck at `0.3.3` — the release is genuinely half-published right now.\n\n**Good news on recovery:** `callisto-vcs 0.4.0` is now confirmed live and indexed, so the specific thing that caused the failure is no longer missing — retrying the remaining 4 crates should succeed now. But re-triggering a real publish against crates.io is exactly the kind of external, irreversible action I won't take without your explicit go-ahead.\n\nHow do you want to handle it — should I re-run the GitHub Action's publish step now, and separately fix the topo-sort gap so this can't recur?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1914,"cache_read_input_tokens":435035,"output_tokens":2937,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2150},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1914,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":435035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1914},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJ7RPoXiJmsjeuXryCju","type":"assistant","uuid":"b15f46da-8615-44f8-afec-5b3d9fa7549c","timestamp":"2026-08-22T16:35:49.106Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"flatten-changelog-severity-grouping","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
