{"parentUuid":"9fbedd62-279f-41ce-a87b-c2afcf9e0222","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJ7rZgJSvWDiaBWSZceN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Narrowly, yes — one real extraction is justified here; a broader system-wide reorg isn't, based on what I've actually found.\n\nThe concrete issue: `toposort()` lives as a generically-named method on the general-purpose `DependencyResolverExt` trait (`resolver.rs`), but its edge-kind filter (`Runtime | Build | Optional`, excluding `Dev`) is a decision tuned specifically for its one and only caller, `plan_publish`. Nothing in its name or location signals \"this is publish-order-specific, don't reuse it elsewhere without checking what edge kinds you need\" — which is exactly how we got here silently. I'd rename/move it to something like `publish_order()` living next to `plan_publish` itself, with the edge-kind choice and its cargo-verification rationale documented inline, rather than a neutral-sounding `toposort()` on a shared trait implying it's the one true topological sort for any purpose.\n\nBeyond that specific spot, I don't see evidence of a broader pattern needing extraction — cascade's own edge-kind filtering (in `cascade.rs`) is already separately and deliberately scoped, so this isn't a system-wide \"graph purposes are tangled everywhere\" problem, just this one under-labeled leaky abstraction with a single caller. I wouldn't go further than that without a reason grounded in an actual second instance of the same conflation — do you want me to also sweep for other single-caller \"generic-sounding but actually purpose-specific\" methods while I'm in here, or keep this scoped to just the publish-order fix?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3349,"cache_read_input_tokens":467023,"output_tokens":2764,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2248},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2764,"cache_read_input_tokens":467023,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJ7rXHS2dQEs8J8GGiQo","type":"assistant","uuid":"f36e53d1-3b50-4fac-9201-ba4a531f8afd","timestamp":"2026-08-22T16:41:29.534Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"flatten-changelog-severity-grouping","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
