{"parentUuid":"f9f366a8-966c-4077-9e81-2376b9333812","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJC3vdeR6F9tHPbjXN6J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129,"cache_read_input_tokens":506282,"output_tokens":6491,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5767},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6491,"cache_read_input_tokens":506282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJC3tas9CxiUCNspKjwJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"c476b39b-be6e-4358-bc49-7bd01fa28ec8","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:37:07.337Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"flatten-changelog-severity-grouping","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"c476b39b-be6e-4358-bc49-7bd01fa28ec8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJC3vdeR6F9tHPbjXN6J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good pushback — and you're right, that was the wrong call. Let me redo this honestly rather than engineer around the process.\n\nReconsidering it straight: the fix is a real, user-relevant bug fix (any consumer doing a coordinated multi-crate Cargo release with a dev-dependency between packages in the same batch could hit this exact failure) — it deserves a real changeset, not an omission dressed up as \"internal enough not to need one.\" Omitting it specifically to dodge the release workflow's own changeset detection is exactly what \"sneaking it in\" means, and I shouldn't have proposed it.\n\nHere's what actually happens if I just do it normally, and it turns out to be fine:\n\n1. Merge the fix with a real changeset.\n2. The next push to `main` sees a pending changeset again, so the Action creates/updates a version-packages PR — bumping **all nine** packages again (fixed-group convergence, same as always), to whatever the next version is (0.4.1, 0.5.0, depending on what else has landed by then).\n3. When that version-PR is reviewed and merged, the Action publishes all nine at that new version. The five already at `0.4.0` bump forward normally. The four currently stuck at `0.3.3` go straight to that new version too — skipping `0.4.0` entirely, permanently.\n\nIs skipping a version number for four crates actually a problem? Semver-wise, no — there's no rule that every crate must publish every version number. The only real cost is cosmetic: those four crates' `CHANGELOG.md` will show their first post-`0.3.3` entry at the *later* version instead of `0.4.0`, with the content that would've been in `0.4.0` folded in alongside whatever else accumulated by then — which is still fully honest, just consolidated differently. No manipulated merge order, no unmerged-branch publishing, no credential workarounds.\n\nSo: normal changeset, normal review, and I'd drop the whole \"complete 0.4.0 exactly\" goal — the real goal is \"all nine packages consistent again,\" which this achieves cleanly. Does that sit right with you, or do you actually want them to land on `0.4.0` specifically, which would mean one of the more manual paths we already ruled out as risky?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129,"cache_read_input_tokens":506282,"output_tokens":6491,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5767},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6491,"cache_read_input_tokens":506282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJC3tas9CxiUCNspKjwJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"474a2561-e943-4205-94f4-1c39e40254d1","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:37:15.544Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"flatten-changelog-severity-grouping","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
