{"parentUuid":"61b82490-06a1-4480-88c6-e2370a586aea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81b6ef85-239d-4fc4-b9b1-676f32937f03","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CvuG9wotk42nXKfn8hRpGU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tuse std::collections::HashSet;\n2\t\n3\tuse callisto_model::{\n4\t    CommandRunner, CratePublish, NpmMainPublish, PackageId, PublishPlan, PublishTarget,\n5\t    PypiPublish, RegistryKey, ReleaseEntry, SCHEMA_VERSION,\n6\t};\n7\tuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\n8\t\n9\tuse crate::error::GraphError;\n10\tuse crate::resolver::DependencyResolver;\n11\tuse crate::toposort::toposort_impl;\n12\tuse crate::Workspace;\n13\t\n14\t/// Computes the order packages must be published in.\n15\t///\n16\t/// This is a thin, purpose-named wrapper around [`toposort_impl`] (the\n17\t/// generic algorithm, reused as-is) rather than a generic\n18\t/// `DependencyResolverExt::toposort()` on a shared trait — it exists\n19\t/// specifically for `plan_publish` below, its only caller, and its\n20\t/// semantics are publish-specific, not \"the one true topological sort.\"\n21\t///\n22\t/// `toposort_impl` currently only treats `Runtime`/`Build`/`Optional`\n23\t/// edges as ordering constraints, which matches cascade/version-bump\n24\t/// propagation's own scope (a `Dev`-only dependency change correctly\n25\t/// doesn't force a consumer's version to bump). For *publish* ordering\n26\t/// specifically that scope is too narrow: `cargo publish` (run without\n27\t/// `--no-verify`, see `publish_client.rs`) re-extracts the packaged\n28\t/// tarball and does a real local build to verify it, which needs *every*\n29\t/// dependency in the crate's `Cargo.toml` — `[dev-dependencies]` included\n30\t/// — resolvable from the registry. A dev-dependency on a workspace sibling\n31\t/// published in the same batch therefore still needs that sibling to\n32\t/// publish first, or the verification build can fail with an unresolvable\n33\t/// version requirement even though the two crates have no real ordering\n34\t/// constraint between them otherwise. This function does not yet account\n35\t/// for that (tracked separately) — it currently reuses the same\n36\t/// cascade-scoped edge filter `toposort_impl` already applies.\n37\tfn publish_order<D: DependencyResolver + ?Sized>(\n38\t    resolver: &D,\n39\t    subset: &HashSet<PackageId>,\n40\t) -> Result<Vec<PackageId>, GraphError> {\n41\t    let all_pkg_ids: Vec<PackageId> = resolver.packages().map(|p| p.id.clone()).collect();\n42\t    toposort_impl(subset, &all_pkg_ids, |id| {\n43\t        resolver\n44\t            .dependencies_of(id)\n45\t            .map(|e| (e.to.clone(), e.kind))"}]},"uuid":"790383c0-dcc2-4dfe-b15c-e724c92eb34f","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:44:44.942Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs","content":"use std::collections::HashSet;\n\nuse callisto_model::{\n    CommandRunner, CratePublish, NpmMainPublish, PackageId, PublishPlan, PublishTarget,\n    PypiPublish, RegistryKey, ReleaseEntry, SCHEMA_VERSION,\n};\nuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\n\nuse crate::error::GraphError;\nuse crate::resolver::DependencyResolver;\nuse crate::toposort::toposort_impl;\nuse crate::Workspace;\n\n/// Computes the order packages must be published in.\n///\n/// This is a thin, purpose-named wrapper around [`toposort_impl`] (the\n/// generic algorithm, reused as-is) rather than a generic\n/// `DependencyResolverExt::toposort()` on a shared trait — it exists\n/// specifically for `plan_publish` below, its only caller, and its\n/// semantics are publish-specific, not \"the one true topological sort.\"\n///\n/// `toposort_impl` currently only treats `Runtime`/`Build`/`Optional`\n/// edges as ordering constraints, which matches cascade/version-bump\n/// propagation's own scope (a `Dev`-only dependency change correctly\n/// doesn't force a consumer's version to bump). For *publish* ordering\n/// specifically that scope is too narrow: `cargo publish` (run without\n/// `--no-verify`, see `publish_client.rs`) re-extracts the packaged\n/// tarball and does a real local build to verify it, which needs *every*\n/// dependency in the crate's `Cargo.toml` — `[dev-dependencies]` included\n/// — resolvable from the registry. A dev-dependency on a workspace sibling\n/// published in the same batch therefore still needs that sibling to\n/// publish first, or the verification build can fail with an unresolvable\n/// version requirement even though the two crates have no real ordering\n/// constraint between them otherwise. This function does not yet account\n/// for that (tracked separately) — it currently reuses the same\n/// cascade-scoped edge filter `toposort_impl` already applies.\nfn publish_order<D: DependencyResolver + ?Sized>(\n    resolver: &D,\n    subset: &HashSet<PackageId>,\n) -> Result<Vec<PackageId>, GraphError> {\n    let all_pkg_ids: Vec<PackageId> = resolver.packages().map(|p| p.id.clone()).collect();\n    toposort_impl(subset, &all_pkg_ids, |id| {\n        resolver\n            .dependencies_of(id)\n            .map(|e| (e.to.clone(), e.kind))","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1467}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61b82490-06a1-4480-88c6-e2370a586aea","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
