{"parentUuid":"aa686b34-02d8-4b39-8220-88a1ee12f9d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJCkB8eZgTUjawBLJ4XJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":532991,"output_tokens":1429,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1054},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":532991,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJCk96N95uDQkUnJNHB6","type":"assistant","uuid":"41723f53-f2ec-4466-864a-7190be15bcfd","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:45:17.269Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"41723f53-f2ec-4466-864a-7190be15bcfd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJCkB8eZgTUjawBLJ4XJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — and that part's already done. To recap where things stand:\n\n- **`DependencyResolverExt::toposort()`** (the generic-sounding trait method that was secretly publish-specific) — removed. Replaced with `publish_order()` in `commands/publish.rs`, next to its only caller (`plan_publish`), with the rationale documented inline. That was the actual rename we agreed on.\n- **`toposort_impl`** (in `toposort.rs`) — I kept this name. It's the underlying Kahn's-algorithm utility, and I just made it *genuinely* generic: it now takes an explicit `ordering_kinds: &[DepKind]` parameter instead of a hardcoded filter, so it no longer bakes in any one caller's assumptions. Since it's no longer secretly purpose-specific, \"topological sort\" is now an accurate, honest name for it — the leaky part was the trait method wrapping it, not the algorithm itself.\n\nSo: the misleading name is gone, and the actually-generic piece keeps a generic name. Did you have something else in mind for `toposort_impl` specifically, or does that distinction match what you meant?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":532991,"output_tokens":1429,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1054},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":532991,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJCk9