{"parentUuid":"d06eae8b-27e3-4498-b37c-b67711c19894","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJDQ2peDzwm33p55Rym9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689,"cache_read_input_tokens":543957,"output_tokens":1843,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1313},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1843,"cache_read_input_tokens":543957,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJDPzn7GYhCTZv9kvALv","type":"assistant","uuid":"d68ae758-5de0-49ad-8f8c-68dfbf23f7dd","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:53:56.059Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"d68ae758-5de0-49ad-8f8c-68dfbf23f7dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJDQ2peDzwm33p55Rym9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Neither is \"bad practice\" exactly, but they're different kinds of tradeoffs:\n\n**`max_width = 120`**: legitimate, not a red flag. rustfmt's default is 100 and that's the overwhelming Rust-ecosystem convention (rust-lang/rust itself, most crates.io crates), so 120 is a real deviation from what most Rust devs expect — PRs/diffs will look different from typical Rust code, and side-by-side diff review (GitHub PR view, split-pane editors) starts needing horizontal scroll past ~100-110 on a normal laptop screen. If your team mostly reviews full-width on wide monitors, that's a non-issue. If you do split-screen review often, 100 stays more practical.\n\n**`wrap_comments = true`**: this is the one I'd actually push back on. rustfmt's comment-wrapping reflows the *entire* paragraph on every `cargo fmt` run — so editing one word in a multi-line doc comment can rewrap the whole paragraph, turning a one-word semantic change into a large, noisy diff that muddies `git blame` and code review. This is a well-known, deliberate reason a lot of experienced Rust teams leave it off and just hand-wrap comments instead (imperfectly, as I've been doing). It's not wrong to enable it, but it's a real cost, not just a formatting nicety.\n\nMy honest take: `max_width = 120` alone is fine if you want it. I'd leave `wrap_comments` off and just have me hand-wrap comments to 120 consistently, rather than take on the reflow-diff-noise tradeoff."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689,"cache_read_input_tokens":543957,"output_tokens":1843,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1313},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1843,"cache_read_input_tokens":543957,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJDPzn7GYhCTZv9kvALv","type":"assistant","uuid":"c03564c0-f81b-4e47-a1b0-6b3fdb25d351","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:54:01.277Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
