{"parentUuid":"6c53f995-6b5c-4060-9258-6162e6e13923","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJFh3s6u8TX49ukTc56u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HjazEUTpL3Li8j7bNNzT9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/AGENTS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":570560,"output_tokens":143,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":143,"cache_read_input_tokens":570560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJFh2TWyCw441c3RvdB4","type":"assistant","uuid":"911ea557-fcd6-4ef8-bbb9-5685dee51336","timestamp":"2026-08-22T18:23:44.965Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"rustfmt-max-width-120","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"911ea557-fcd6-4ef8-bbb9-5685dee51336","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"929bd648-a34a-47c5-8b79-b7b40b1e1cd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HjazEUTpL3Li8j7bNNzT9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Callisto AI Agent Guidelines (`AGENTS.md`)\n2\t\n3\tThis guide provides instructions, architectural rules, engineering invariants, and task runner workflows for AI coding agents (Antigravity, Claude, Cursor, Copilot, Codex) working on the Callisto codebase.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## 1. Repository Architecture & Crate Layers\n8\t\n9\tCallisto is a fast, polyglot monorepo versioning and release management engine written in Rust. It is divided into 10 workspace crates structured in strict architectural layers:\n10\t\n11\t```text\n12\t┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n13\t│                        CALLISTO CRATE LAYERS                           │\n14\t├───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┤\n15\t│ LAYER & CRATE                     │ LICENSE & PURPOSE                  │\n16\t├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n17\t│ Layer 1: callisto-model           │ MIT / Apache-2.0                   │\n18\t│          callisto-format          │ Domain primitives, SemVer grammars │\n19\t├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n20\t│ Layer 1.5: callisto-vcs           │ MIT / Apache-2.0                   │\n21\t│                                    │ Native Git integration             │\n22\t├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n23\t│ Layer 2: callisto-manifests       │ AGPL-3.0-only                      │\n24\t│          callisto-conventional    │ AST manifest editors, changeset    │\n25\t│          callisto-changelog       │ markdown parser/writer             │\n26\t├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n27\t│ Layer 3: callisto-graph           │ AGPL-3.0-only                      │\n28\t│                                   │ Dependency DAG solver & cascades   │\n29\t├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n30\t│ Layer 4: callisto-cli             │ AGPL-3.0-only                      │\n31\t│          callisto-moon            │ Standalone CLI & Moon WASM plugin  │\n32\t├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n33\t│ Dev:     callisto-fixtures        │ AGPL-3.0-only — dev-only byte-compat│\n34\t│                                    │ test corpus                        │\n35\t└───────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘\n36\t```\n37\t\n38\t> **CRITICAL RULE (Layer Licensing Boundaries)**: Layer 1 crates (`callisto-model`, `callisto-format`) and Layer 1.5 (`callisto-vcs`) MUST NOT depend on Layer 2, 3, or 4 crates (`callisto-manifests`, `callisto-conventional`, `callisto-changelog`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, `callisto-moon`). Layer 1/1.5 crates must remain permissive (`MIT OR Apache-2.0`) and standalone. This table reflects each crate's actual `Cargo.toml` `license` field — verify with `grep -H \"^license\" crates/*/Cargo.toml` before trusting it if crates are added/moved.\n39\t\n40\t---\n41\t\n42\t## 2. Primary Task Runners & Verification Pipelines\n43\t\n44\tAlways use `just` or `moon` task runners for building, testing, linting, and formatting. Do not invent manual cargo command combinations when task runners exist.\n45\t\n46\t### Primary Command Reference\n47\t\n48\t| Action | Primary Task Runner Command | Moon Engine Command |\n49\t| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n50\t| **Run Full Verification CI** | `just ci` | `moon run :format-check && moon run :lint && moon run :test` |\n51\t| **Run Test Suite** | `just test` | `moon run :test` |\n52\t| **Check Clippy Lints** | `just lint` | `moon run :lint` |\n53\t| **Check Formatting** | `just fmt-check` | `moon run :format-check` |\n54\t| **Format Code** | `just fmt` | `moon run :format` |\n55\t| **Verify WASM Cross-Compilation** | `just wasm-check` | `cargo check -p callisto-moon --target wasm32-wasip1 --features pdk` |\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## 3. Strict Engineering Invariants\n60\t\n61\tAgents modifying Callisto code MUST enforce the following 5 engineering invariants:\n62\t\n63\t### 1. Safe Rust Only (`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`)\n64\t- `unsafe` code blocks are strictly forbidden across all 10 workspace crates.\n65\t- Memory and thread safety must be guaranteed by safe Rust abstractions.\n66\t\n67\t### 2. Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Format Preservation\n68\t- NEVER use regular expressions or line-based string replace for manifest editing (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`).\n69\t- **TOML Editing**: Must use `toml_edit` to manipulate CST elements, preserving user comments, key order, and whitespace.\n70\t- **JSON Editing**: Must fingerprint indentation style (`IndentStyle::Tabs` vs `IndentStyle::Spaces(N)`) and preserve key insertion order using `serde_json`.\n71\t\n72\t### 3. Crash-Safe Atomic Disk Writes\n73\t- All manifest and configuration edits MUST go through `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write`. (`callisto_manifests::atomic::atomic_write` remains a backward-compatible re-export of the same function.)\n74\t- Writes create a `NamedTempFile` in the target file's parent directory, flush data to disk, and atomically replace the target file via `fs::rename`.\n75\t\n76\t### 4. Rich Diagnostic Cards (`miette`)\n77\t- User-facing CLI errors MUST derive `miette::Diagnostic` with explicit error codes, clear error cards, and actionable remediation suggestions.\n78\t\n79\t### 5. No Emoji Directive in Documentation & Code\n80\t- Documentation (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`) and code comments MUST remain clean, technical, scannable, and devoid of emojis or AI bot filler phrases.\n81\t\n82\t---\n83\t\n84\t## 4. Changeset CLI Execution Modes\n85\t\n86\tWhen generating changesets using Callisto CLI (`callisto add`):\n87\t\n88\t- **Interactive Human Mode (Terminal TTY)**: Launches the 5-step interactive `dialoguer` wizard (Package Selection -> Major Bump Selection -> Minor Bump Selection -> Summary Input -> Confirmation Preview).\n89\t- **Non-Interactive Agent/CI Mode**: Bypasses the wizard completely using explicit CLI flags:\n90\t  ```bash\n91\t  callisto add --package callisto-cli:minor --summary \"Add feature description\"\n92\t  ```\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## 5. Preferred Modern CLI Tools Directive\n97\t\n98\tAgents executing shell operations or terminal commands MUST prioritize modern CLI tools over legacy POSIX/Unix shell builtins:\n99\t\n100\t- **Code & Pattern Search**: `ripgrep` (`rg`) over `grep`\n101\t- **File Discovery**: `fd` over `find`\n102\t- **Interactive Filtering**: `fzf` for selection menus\n103\t- **File & Code Viewing**: `bat` over `cat`\n104\t- **Directory Navigation**: `zoxide` (`z`) over `cd`\n105\t- **Diff Inspection**: `delta` over `diff` / `git diff`\n106\t- **Directory Formatting**: `eza` over `ls`\n107\t- **JSON Processing**: `jq` for stream & file transformations\n108\t- **GitHub Workflow & API**: `gh` CLI for GitHub release, PR, and repo management\n109\t"}]},"uuid":"270eee78-19d2-4d1e-a247-f87b21f5dec1","timestamp":"2026-08-22T18:23:45.076Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/AGENTS.md","content":"# Callisto AI Agent Guidelines (`AGENTS.md`)\n\nThis guide provides instructions, architectural rules, engineering invariants, and task runner workflows for AI coding agents (Antigravity, Claude, Cursor, Copilot, Codex) working on the Callisto codebase.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Repository Architecture & Crate Layers\n\nCallisto is a fast, polyglot monorepo versioning and release management engine written in Rust. It is divided into 10 workspace crates structured in strict architectural layers:\n\n```text\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        CALLISTO CRATE LAYERS                           │\n├───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ LAYER & CRATE                     │ LICENSE & PURPOSE                  │\n├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Layer 1: callisto-model           │ MIT / Apache-2.0                   │\n│          callisto-format          │ Domain primitives, SemVer grammars │\n├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Layer 1.5: callisto-vcs           │ MIT / Apache-2.0                   │\n│                                    │ Native Git integration             │\n├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Layer 2: callisto-manifests       │ AGPL-3.0-only                      │\n│          callisto-conventional    │ AST manifest editors, changeset    │\n│          callisto-changelog       │ markdown parser/writer             │\n├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Layer 3: callisto-graph           │ AGPL-3.0-only                      │\n│                                   │ Dependency DAG solver & cascades   │\n├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Layer 4: callisto-cli             │ AGPL-3.0-only                      │\n│          callisto-moon            │ Standalone CLI & Moon WASM plugin  │\n├───────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Dev:     callisto-fixtures        │ AGPL-3.0-only — dev-only byte-compat│\n│                                    │ test corpus                        │\n└───────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n> **CRITICAL RULE (Layer Licensing Boundaries)**: Layer 1 crates (`callisto-model`, `callisto-format`) and Layer 1.5 (`callisto-vcs`) MUST NOT depend on Layer 2, 3, or 4 crates (`callisto-manifests`, `callisto-conventional`, `callisto-changelog`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, `callisto-moon`). Layer 1/1.5 crates must remain permissive (`MIT OR Apache-2.0`) and standalone. This table reflects each crate's actual `Cargo.toml` `license` field — verify with `grep -H \"^license\" crates/*/Cargo.toml` before trusting it if crates are added/moved.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Primary Task Runners & Verification Pipelines\n\nAlways use `just` or `moon` task runners for building, testing, linting, and formatting. Do not invent manual cargo command combinations when task runners exist.\n\n### Primary Command Reference\n\n| Action | Primary Task Runner Command | Moon Engine Command |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Run Full Verification CI** | `just ci` | `moon run :format-check && moon run :lint && moon run :test` |\n| **Run Test Suite** | `just test` | `moon run :test` |\n| **Check Clippy Lints** | `just lint` | `moon run :lint` |\n| **Check Formatting** | `just fmt-check` | `moon run :format-check` |\n| **Format Code** | `just fmt` | `moon run :format` |\n| **Verify WASM Cross-Compilation** | `just wasm-check` | `cargo check -p callisto-moon --target wasm32-wasip1 --features pdk` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Strict Engineering Invariants\n\nAgents modifying Callisto code MUST enforce the following 5 engineering invariants:\n\n### 1. Safe Rust Only (`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`)\n- `unsafe` code blocks are strictly forbidden across all 10 workspace crates.\n- Memory and thread safety must be guaranteed by safe Rust abstractions.\n\n### 2. Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Format Preservation\n- NEVER use regular expressions or line-based string replace for manifest editing (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`).\n- **TOML Editing**: Must use `toml_edit` to manipulate CST elements, preserving user comments, key order, and whitespace.\n- **JSON Editing**: Must fingerprint indentation style (`IndentStyle::Tabs` vs `IndentStyle::Spaces(N)`) and preserve key insertion order using `serde_json`.\n\n### 3. Crash-Safe Atomic Disk Writes\n- All manifest and configuration edits MUST go through `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write`. (`callisto_manifests::atomic::atomic_write` remains a backward-compatible re-export of the same function.)\n- Writes create a `NamedTempFile` in the target file's parent directory, flush data to disk, and atomically replace the target file via `fs::rename`.\n\n### 4. Rich Diagnostic Cards (`miette`)\n- User-facing CLI errors MUST derive `miette::Diagnostic` with explicit error codes, clear error cards, and actionable remediation suggestions.\n\n### 5. No Emoji Directive in Documentation & Code\n- Documentation (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`) and code comments MUST remain clean, technical, scannable, and devoid of emojis or AI bot filler phrases.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Changeset CLI Execution Modes\n\nWhen generating changesets using Callisto CLI (`callisto add`):\n\n- **Interactive Human Mode (Terminal TTY)**: Launches the 5-step interactive `dialoguer` wizard (Package Selection -> Major Bump Selection -> Minor Bump Selection -> Summary Input -> Confirmation Preview).\n- **Non-Interactive Agent/CI Mode**: Bypasses the wizard completely using explicit CLI flags:\n  ```bash\n  callisto add --package callisto-cli:minor --summary \"Add feature description\"\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Preferred Modern CLI Tools Directive\n\nAgents executing shell operations or terminal commands MUST prioritize modern CLI tools over legacy POSIX/Unix shell builtins:\n\n- **Code & Pattern Search**: `ripgrep` (`rg`) over `grep`\n- **File Discovery**: `fd` over `find`\n- **Interactive Filtering**: `fzf` for selection menus\n- **File & Code Viewing**: `bat` over `cat`\n- **Directory Navigation**: `zoxide` (`z`) over `cd`\n- **Diff Inspection**: `delta` over `diff` / `git diff`\n- **Directory Formatting**: `eza` over `ls`\n- **JSON Processing**: `jq` for stream & file transformations\n- **GitHub Workflow & API**: `gh` CLI for GitHub release, PR, and repo management\n","numLines":109,"startLine":1,"totalLines":109}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"911ea557-fcd6-4ef8-bbb9-5685dee51336","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"rustfmt-max-width-120","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
