{"parentUuid":"85b69aa1-558a-43b1-91e8-ca5fbb53d683","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeJFjEfYLFKkHXawc6F2C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013pFg8eGX75uRZdP5gNqbou","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":576925,"output_tokens":75,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":434,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":75,"cache_read_input_tokens":576925,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":434},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJFjCgjAoebsMrW79w2Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"97d0a98d-7e5d-4032-96c9-8659742d8109","timestamp":"2026-08-22T18:24:13.696Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"rustfmt-max-width-120","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"97d0a98d-7e5d-4032-96c9-8659742d8109","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"929bd648-a34a-47c5-8b79-b7b40b1e1cd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013pFg8eGX75uRZdP5gNqbou","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<p align=\"center\">\n2\t  <img src=\"assets/callisto-logo.png\" width=\"180\" alt=\"Callisto Release Engine Logo\" />\n3\t</p>\n4\t\n5\t<p align=\"center\">\n6\t  <b>The fast, crash-safe, polyglot monorepo release engine.</b><br />\n7\t  <i>Replaces Node.js runtimes, fragile regular expression edits, and duplicate CI matrix YAML with a single native Rust binary.</i>\n8\t</p>\n9\t\n10\t<p align=\"center\">\n11\t  <a href=\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/workflows/callisto-ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n12\t  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT%20OR%20Apache--2.0-blue.svg\" alt=\"License\" /></a>\n13\t  <a href=\"crates/callisto-model\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/unsafe_code-forbid-success.svg\" alt=\"Safety\" /></a>\n14\t</p>\n15\t\n16\t---\n17\t\n18\t## Key Capabilities\n19\t\n20\t> **Sub-10ms Native Speed**  \n21\t> Native Rust binary executes workspace discovery and version planning in under 10ms — 30x to 50x faster than `@changesets/cli` or `release-please`.\n22\t\n23\t> **Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Format Preservation**  \n24\t> Edits `Cargo.toml` and `package.json` using `toml_edit` and `serde_json` indentation fingerprinting, preserving user comments, table ordering, and whitespace.\n25\t\n26\t> **Crash-Safe Atomic Disk Writes**  \n27\t> Writes updates to `NamedTempFile` temporary buffers before atomic POSIX `fs::rename` swaps, preventing corrupt or partial manifest writes during process interruption.\n28\t\n29\t> **Topological Directed Graph Solver**  \n30\t> Models workspace package dependencies using `petgraph`'s Kahn topological solver and Tarjan's SCC algorithm to compute cascading version bumps and catch circular dependency cycles.\n31\t\n32\t> **Zero-Config Native Matrix Auto-Discovery**  \n33\t> `callisto matrix` auto-discovers napi-rs and maturin build targets (`napi.targets`, `[tool.maturin].targets`) plus npm/PyPI runtime constraints (`engines.node`, `requires-python`) straight from manifests — no duplicate CI YAML to keep in sync.  \n34\t> Java (`java.version`) and .NET native-AOT discovery are planned for a future release.\n35\t\n36\t> **Hermetic & Build-System Agnostic**  \n37\t> Pure Rust CLI engine runs seamlessly in Bazel sandboxes (`rules_callisto`), Buck2, Nix flakes, Moon WASM (`callisto-moon`), GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and local VCS hooks (`just hooks`).\n38\t\n39\t---\n40\t\n41\t## Quick Start (4 Steps)\n42\t\n43\t```text\n44\t$ callisto status\n45\tStatus (schema v1):\n46\t  callisto-cli 0.1.0 (pending: minor)\n47\t  callisto-graph 0.1.0 (pending: patch)\n48\t\n49\t$ callisto version\n50\tVersion Plan (schema v1):\n51\t  callisto-cli 0.1.0 → 0.2.0\n52\t  callisto-graph 0.1.0 → 0.1.1\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t### Step 1: Initialize Callisto in Your Workspace\n56\t\n57\tRun `init` in your repository root to create `callisto.toml` and `.changeset/`:\n58\t\n59\t```bash\n60\tcallisto init --yes\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t### Step 2: Create a Changeset\n64\t\n65\tWhen adding a feature, fix, or breaking change to a package:\n66\t\n67\t```bash\n68\tcallisto add --package my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\tThis generates a `.changeset/<random-id>.md` file in your repository.\n72\t\n73\t### Step 3: Inspect Workspace Status\n74\t\n75\tView pending changesets and calculated version bumps across your monorepo DAG:\n76\t\n77\t```bash\n78\tcallisto status\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\t### Step 4: Preview & Apply Version Bumps\n82\t\n83\tPreview calculated manifest modifications with unified colored diffs:\n84\t\n85\t```bash\n86\t# Preview diffs without modifying files\n87\tcallisto version --dry-run\n88\t\n89\t# Apply version bumps, update changelogs, and consume changesets\n90\tcallisto version\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\t> [!TIP]\n94\t> Run `callisto version --dry-run` locally anytime to inspect calculated version bumps and changelog updates with colored diffs before committing.\n95\t\n96\t---\n97\t\n98\t## Release Workflow & Branch Configuration\n99\t\n100\tCallisto integrates natively with GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and custom release pipelines.\n101\t\n102\t### 1. Release PR Branch Naming & Configuration\n103\t\n104\tWhen Callisto generates automated release pull requests, it targets the default release branch **`changeset-release/main`** (matching `@changesets/action` standards).\n105\t\n106\tYou can override the release branch name per invocation using the `--branch` flag:\n107\t\n108\t```bash\n109\t# Generate PR body targeting a custom release branch\n110\tcallisto compose-pr-body --branch release-packages\n111\t```\n112\t\n113\t### 2. Production GitHub Actions Workflow (`release.yml`)\n114\t\n115\tCreate `.github/workflows/release.yml` to automate version bumps and registry publishing on `push` to `main`:\n116\t\n117\t```yaml\n118\tname: Release\n119\t\n120\ton:\n121\t  push:\n122\t    branches: [main]\n123\t\n124\tconcurrency:\n125\t  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n126\t  cancel-in-progress: true\n127\t\n128\tjobs:\n129\t  release:\n130\t    name: Release / Version Packages\n131\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n132\t    permissions:\n133\t      contents: write\n134\t      pull-requests: write\n135\t      id-token: write  # OIDC registry publishing\n136\t\n137\t    steps:\n138\t      - name: Checkout Repository\n139\t        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n140\t        with:\n141\t          fetch-depth: 0\n142\t\n143\t      - name: Install Rust Toolchain\n144\t        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n145\t\n146\t      - name: Run Callisto Release Action\n147\t        uses: orin-dx/callisto-action@v1\n148\t        with:\n149\t          branch: changeset-release/main\n150\t          publish: just publish\n151\t        env:\n152\t          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n153\t          CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN }}\n154\t          NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n155\t```\n156\t\n157\t### 3. Bypassing Heavy CI Workflows on Release PRs\n158\t\n159\tRelease PRs contain automated version bumps and changelog updates. To prevent running expensive CI build matrices on release PRs, ignore `changeset-release/**` branches in your main `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:\n160\t\n161\t```yaml\n162\tname: CI Pipeline\n163\t\n164\ton:\n165\t  push:\n166\t    branches: [main]\n167\t  pull_request:\n168\t    branches-ignore:\n169\t      - 'changeset-release/**'\n170\t```\n171\t\n172\t---\n173\t\n174\t## Why Callisto?\n175\t\n176\tCallisto combines ideas from `@changesets/cli`, `release-please`, and `nx release` into one native Rust engine built for polyglot monorepos:\n177\t\n178\t| | Callisto | Alternatives |\n179\t| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n180\t| **Speed** | Workspace discovery + graph solving in <10ms | `@changesets/cli`, `release-please`, `nx release` pay a 300-500ms Node.js startup cost |\n181\t| **Manifest edits** | CST-based (`toml_edit`, `serde_json`), preserves comments/order/whitespace | `release-please` uses regex; `@changesets/cli` re-serializes JSON with default formatting |\n182\t| **Cycle detection** | Kahn + Tarjan SCC with `miette` diagnostic cards | `release-please` is single-repo only; `nx release` is tied to Nx JS trees |\n183\t| **Matrix discovery** | Auto-discovers napi-rs/maturin targets and npm/PyPI runtime constraints from manifests (Java/.NET planned) | Manual 50-line matrix arrays in CI YAML |\n184\t| **Portability** | Runs in Bazel, Buck2, Nix, Moon WASM, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and local Git hooks | Locked to GitHub REST APIs or JS workspace tooling |\n185\t\n186\t---\n187\t\n188\t## Installation\n189\t\n190\t> [!IMPORTANT]\n191\t> Callisto enforces safe Rust (`#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`) and POSIX atomic disk writes (`NamedTempFile` + `fs::rename`) across all workspace manifest edits.\n192\t\n193\t### 1. Standalone Native Binary (Cargo)\n194\t\n195\t```bash\n196\tcargo install callisto-cli\n197\t```\n198\t\n199\t### 2. Pre-Built Release Binary (GitHub Releases)\n200\t\n201\tDownload pre-compiled binaries for Linux (x86_64) or macOS from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases):\n202\t\n203\t```bash\n204\tcurl -sL https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases/latest/download/callisto-linux-amd64.tar.gz | tar -xz -C /usr/local/bin\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t### 3. Moon Extension Plugin (WebAssembly)\n208\t\n209\tAdd Callisto as a WASM plugin in your repository's `.moon/workspace.yml`:\n210\t\n211\t```yaml\n212\textensions:\n213\t  callisto:\n214\t    plugin: 'https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases/download/v0.1.0/callisto-moon.wasm'\n215\t```\n216\t\n217\t---\n218\t\n219\t## Workspace Crate Architecture\n220\t\n221\tCallisto is structured into 10 workspace crates divided across permissive (`MIT OR Apache-2.0`) and copyleft (`AGPL-3.0-only`) licenses:\n222\t\n223\t| Layer | Crate | License | Purpose |\n224\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n225\t| **Layer 1** | [`callisto-model`](crates/callisto-model) | MIT/Apache-2.0 | Domain primitives, version grammars, JSON report contracts |\n226\t| | [`callisto-format`](crates/callisto-format) | MIT/Apache-2.0 | Changeset `.md` and `pre.json` parsers and writers |\n227\t| | [`callisto-conventional`](crates/callisto-conventional) | AGPL-3.0 | Conventional commit parsing and bump severity classification |\n228\t| | [`callisto-changelog`](crates/callisto-changelog) | AGPL-3.0 | Markdown changelog renderer |\n229\t| **Layer 2** | [`callisto-manifests`](crates/callisto-manifests) | AGPL-3.0 | Format-preserving manifest AST editors and atomic file writes |\n230\t| | [`callisto-vcs`](crates/callisto-vcs) | MIT/Apache-2.0 | Native in-process Git operations powered by `gix` (gitoxide) |\n231\t| **Layer 3** | [`callisto-graph`](crates/callisto-graph) | AGPL-3.0 | Dependency DAG solver and Tarjan SCC cycle diagnostics |\n232\t| **Layer 4** | [`callisto-cli`](crates/callisto-cli) | AGPL-3.0 | Standalone CLI binary, colored diff previews, `miette` diagnostic cards |\n233\t| | [`callisto-moon`](crates/callisto-moon) | AGPL-3.0 | Moon extension protocol implementation (`extism-pdk`) |\n234\t| **Dev** | [`callisto-fixtures`](crates/callisto-fixtures) | AGPL-3.0 | Multi-ecosystem corpus and in-memory test doubles |\n235\t\n236\t---\n237\t\n238\t## Development & Task Runners\n239\t\n240\tCallisto uses `just` as its primary developer command runner, delegating workspace tasks to `moon`:\n241\t\n242\t```bash\n243\t# Run full local CI suite (formatting, clippy lints, test suite, security audit, WASM check)\n244\tjust ci\n245\t\n246\t# Run test suite\n247\tjust test\n248\t\n249\t# Check clippy lints\n250\tjust lint\n251\t\n252\t# Check code formatting compliance\n253\tjust fmt-check\n254\t\n255\t# Format code automatically\n256\tjust fmt\n257\t\n258\t# Check security advisories\n259\tjust audit\n260\t```\n261\t"}]},"uuid":"d2226544-e7e2-409c-b7ab-7d0dfae3d37a","timestamp":"2026-08-22T18:24:13.766Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/README.md","content":"<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/callisto-logo.png\" width=\"180\" alt=\"Callisto Release Engine Logo\" />\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>The fast, crash-safe, polyglot monorepo release engine.</b><br />\n  <i>Replaces Node.js runtimes, fragile regular expression edits, and duplicate CI matrix YAML with a single native Rust binary.</i>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/workflows/callisto-ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT%20OR%20Apache--2.0-blue.svg\" alt=\"License\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"crates/callisto-model\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/unsafe_code-forbid-success.svg\" alt=\"Safety\" /></a>\n</p>\n\n---\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\n> **Sub-10ms Native Speed**  \n> Native Rust binary executes workspace discovery and version planning in under 10ms — 30x to 50x faster than `@changesets/cli` or `release-please`.\n\n> **Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Format Preservation**  \n> Edits `Cargo.toml` and `package.json` using `toml_edit` and `serde_json` indentation fingerprinting, preserving user comments, table ordering, and whitespace.\n\n> **Crash-Safe Atomic Disk Writes**  \n> Writes updates to `NamedTempFile` temporary buffers before atomic POSIX `fs::rename` swaps, preventing corrupt or partial manifest writes during process interruption.\n\n> **Topological Directed Graph Solver**  \n> Models workspace package dependencies using `petgraph`'s Kahn topological solver and Tarjan's SCC algorithm to compute cascading version bumps and catch circular dependency cycles.\n\n> **Zero-Config Native Matrix Auto-Discovery**  \n> `callisto matrix` auto-discovers napi-rs and maturin build targets (`napi.targets`, `[tool.maturin].targets`) plus npm/PyPI runtime constraints (`engines.node`, `requires-python`) straight from manifests — no duplicate CI YAML to keep in sync.  \n> Java (`java.version`) and .NET native-AOT discovery are planned for a future release.\n\n> **Hermetic & Build-System Agnostic**  \n> Pure Rust CLI engine runs seamlessly in Bazel sandboxes (`rules_callisto`), Buck2, Nix flakes, Moon WASM (`callisto-moon`), GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and local VCS hooks (`just hooks`).\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (4 Steps)\n\n```text\n$ callisto status\nStatus (schema v1):\n  callisto-cli 0.1.0 (pending: minor)\n  callisto-graph 0.1.0 (pending: patch)\n\n$ callisto version\nVersion Plan (schema v1):\n  callisto-cli 0.1.0 → 0.2.0\n  callisto-graph 0.1.0 → 0.1.1\n```\n\n### Step 1: Initialize Callisto in Your Workspace\n\nRun `init` in your repository root to create `callisto.toml` and `.changeset/`:\n\n```bash\ncallisto init --yes\n```\n\n### Step 2: Create a Changeset\n\nWhen adding a feature, fix, or breaking change to a package:\n\n```bash\ncallisto add --package my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n```\n\nThis generates a `.changeset/<random-id>.md` file in your repository.\n\n### Step 3: Inspect Workspace Status\n\nView pending changesets and calculated version bumps across your monorepo DAG:\n\n```bash\ncallisto status\n```\n\n### Step 4: Preview & Apply Version Bumps\n\nPreview calculated manifest modifications with unified colored diffs:\n\n```bash\n# Preview diffs without modifying files\ncallisto version --dry-run\n\n# Apply version bumps, update changelogs, and consume changesets\ncallisto version\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Run `callisto version --dry-run` locally anytime to inspect calculated version bumps and changelog updates with colored diffs before committing.\n\n---\n\n## Release Workflow & Branch Configuration\n\nCallisto integrates natively with GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and custom release pipelines.\n\n### 1. Release PR Branch Naming & Configuration\n\nWhen Callisto generates automated release pull requests, it targets the default release branch **`changeset-release/main`** (matching `@changesets/action` standards).\n\nYou can override the release branch name per invocation using the `--branch` flag:\n\n```bash\n# Generate PR body targeting a custom release branch\ncallisto compose-pr-body --branch release-packages\n```\n\n### 2. Production GitHub Actions Workflow (`release.yml`)\n\nCreate `.github/workflows/release.yml` to automate version bumps and registry publishing on `push` to `main`:\n\n```yaml\nname: Release\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\njobs:\n  release:\n    name: Release / Version Packages\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      pull-requests: write\n      id-token: write  # OIDC registry publishing\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout Repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - name: Install Rust Toolchain\n        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n\n      - name: Run Callisto Release Action\n        uses: orin-dx/callisto-action@v1\n        with:\n          branch: changeset-release/main\n          publish: just publish\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN }}\n          NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n```\n\n### 3. Bypassing Heavy CI Workflows on Release PRs\n\nRelease PRs contain automated version bumps and changelog updates. To prevent running expensive CI build matrices on release PRs, ignore `changeset-release/**` branches in your main `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nname: CI Pipeline\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n    branches-ignore:\n      - 'changeset-release/**'\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why Callisto?\n\nCallisto combines ideas from `@changesets/cli`, `release-please`, and `nx release` into one native Rust engine built for polyglot monorepos:\n\n| | Callisto | Alternatives |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Speed** | Workspace discovery + graph solving in <10ms | `@changesets/cli`, `release-please`, `nx release` pay a 300-500ms Node.js startup cost |\n| **Manifest edits** | CST-based (`toml_edit`, `serde_json`), preserves comments/order/whitespace | `release-please` uses regex; `@changesets/cli` re-serializes JSON with default formatting |\n| **Cycle detection** | Kahn + Tarjan SCC with `miette` diagnostic cards | `release-please` is single-repo only; `nx release` is tied to Nx JS trees |\n| **Matrix discovery** | Auto-discovers napi-rs/maturin targets and npm/PyPI runtime constraints from manifests (Java/.NET planned) | Manual 50-line matrix arrays in CI YAML |\n| **Portability** | Runs in Bazel, Buck2, Nix, Moon WASM, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and local Git hooks | Locked to GitHub REST APIs or JS workspace tooling |\n\n---\n\n## Installation\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Callisto enforces safe Rust (`#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`) and POSIX atomic disk writes (`NamedTempFile` + `fs::rename`) across all workspace manifest edits.\n\n### 1. Standalone Native Binary (Cargo)\n\n```bash\ncargo install callisto-cli\n```\n\n### 2. Pre-Built Release Binary (GitHub Releases)\n\nDownload pre-compiled binaries for Linux (x86_64) or macOS from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases):\n\n```bash\ncurl -sL https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases/latest/download/callisto-linux-amd64.tar.gz | tar -xz -C /usr/local/bin\n```\n\n### 3. Moon Extension Plugin (WebAssembly)\n\nAdd Callisto as a WASM plugin in your repository's `.moon/workspace.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nextensions:\n  callisto:\n    plugin: 'https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases/download/v0.1.0/callisto-moon.wasm'\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workspace Crate Architecture\n\nCallisto is structured into 10 workspace crates divided across permissive (`MIT OR Apache-2.0`) and copyleft (`AGPL-3.0-only`) licenses:\n\n| Layer | Crate | License | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Layer 1** | [`callisto-model`](crates/callisto-model) | MIT/Apache-2.0 | Domain primitives, version grammars, JSON report contracts |\n| | [`callisto-format`](crates/callisto-format) | MIT/Apache-2.0 | Changeset `.md` and `pre.json` parsers and writers |\n| | [`callisto-conventional`](crates/callisto-conventional) | AGPL-3.0 | Conventional commit parsing and bump severity classification |\n| | [`callisto-changelog`](crates/callisto-changelog) | AGPL-3.0 | Markdown changelog renderer |\n| **Layer 2** | [`callisto-manifests`](crates/callisto-manifests) | AGPL-3.0 | Format-preserving manifest AST editors and atomic file writes |\n| | [`callisto-vcs`](crates/callisto-vcs) | MIT/Apache-2.0 | Native in-process Git operations powered by `gix` (gitoxide) |\n| **Layer 3** | [`callisto-graph`](crates/callisto-graph) | AGPL-3.0 | Dependency DAG solver and Tarjan SCC cycle diagnostics |\n| **Layer 4** | [`callisto-cli`](crates/callisto-cli) | AGPL-3.0 | Standalone CLI binary, colored diff previews, `miette` diagnostic cards |\n| | [`callisto-moon`](crates/callisto-moon) | AGPL-3.0 | Moon extension protocol implementation (`extism-pdk`) |\n| **Dev** | [`callisto-fixtures`](crates/callisto-fixtures) | AGPL-3.0 | Multi-ecosystem corpus and in-memory test doubles |\n\n---\n\n## Development & Task Runners\n\nCallisto uses `just` as its primary developer command runner, delegating workspace tasks to `moon`:\n\n```bash\n# Run full local CI suite (formatting, clippy lints, test suite, security audit, WASM check)\njust ci\n\n# Run test suite\njust test\n\n# Check clippy lints\njust lint\n\n# Check code formatting compliance\njust fmt-check\n\n# Format code automatically\njust fmt\n\n# Check security advisories\njust audit\n```\n","numLines":261,"startLine":1,"totalLines":261}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"97d0a98d-7e5d-4032-96c9-8659742d8109","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"rustfmt-max-width-120","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
