{"parentUuid":"e550ac64-c8ce-4065-86f2-12c3817b5ad1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7e639fa-bb3f-487c-a2d1-83df6e40753d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CY6v9Lfc6Lw6BAww2ySRoY","type":"tool_result","content":"17\t}\n18\t\n19\t/// Validates a `publishConfig.registry` URL read from a package's own\n20\t/// `package.json` before it is threaded into the publish plan (and\n21\t/// eventually into `npm publish --registry <url>` / `npm view --registry\n22\t/// <url>`, both run with `NPM_TOKEN` live in the process environment in CI).\n23\t///\n24\t/// `publishConfig.registry` is manifest-controlled data -- something a PR\n25\t/// author can set in their own package.json -- not operator-controlled\n26\t/// config, so it must never be trusted verbatim as a publish destination.\n27\t/// Two checks are enforced, mirroring the leading-`-` flag-injection guard\n28\t/// already applied to package names before they reach these same CLI\n29\t/// invocations (see `SubprocessRegistryClient::npm_publish`):\n30\t///\n31\t/// 1. The URL must use the `https` scheme. A scheme downgrade (e.g. `http`)\n32\t///    is rejected even if the host would otherwise be approved, since scheme\n33\t///    downgrade is itself part of the attack this guard defends against.\n34\t/// 2. The URL must exactly match a `url` configured on an `npm`-kind entry\n35\t///    in the operator's `[registries]` table in `callisto.toml`.\n36\t///\n37\t/// If the operator has configured no custom npm registries at all (no\n38\t/// `[registries.*]` block with `kind = \"npm\"` and a `url`), any override is\n39\t/// rejected. This is the conservative choice: `callisto.toml`, not an\n40\t/// attacker-influenced `package.json`, must always be the source of truth\n41\t/// for where credentials-bearing publish requests are allowed to go, so\n42\t/// operators who need a private npm registry must opt in explicitly by\n43\t/// declaring it in `[registries]`.\n44\tfn validate_npm_registry_url(\n45\t    url: &str,\n46\t    package: &PackageId,\n47\t    registries: &std::collections::BTreeMap<RegistryKey, crate::config::RegistryConfig>,\n48\t) -> Result<(), GraphError> {\n49\t    let is_approved = url.starts_with(\"https://\")\n50\t        && registries\n51\t            .values()\n52\t            .any(|cfg| cfg.kind == Ecosystem::Npm && cfg.url.as_deref() == Some(url));\n53\t\n54\t    if is_approved {\n55\t        Ok(())\n56\t    } else {\n57\t        Err(GraphError::UntrustedNpmRegistry {\n58\t            package: package.clone(),\n59\t            url: url.to_string(),\n60\t        })\n61\t    }\n62\t}"}]},"uuid":"21ef6637-050f-4dff-ab0a-18d4a9394ef8","timestamp":"2026-08-22T19:19:08.186Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs","content":"}\n\n/// Validates a `publishConfig.registry` URL read from a package's own\n/// `package.json` before it is threaded into the publish plan (and\n/// eventually into `npm publish --registry <url>` / `npm view --registry\n/// <url>`, both run with `NPM_TOKEN` live in the process environment in CI).\n///\n/// `publishConfig.registry` is manifest-controlled data -- something a PR\n/// author can set in their own package.json -- not operator-controlled\n/// config, so it must never be trusted verbatim as a publish destination.\n/// Two checks are enforced, mirroring the leading-`-` flag-injection guard\n/// already applied to package names before they reach these same CLI\n/// invocations (see `SubprocessRegistryClient::npm_publish`):\n///\n/// 1. The URL must use the `https` scheme. A scheme downgrade (e.g. `http`)\n///    is rejected even if the host would otherwise be approved, since scheme\n///    downgrade is itself part of the attack this guard defends against.\n/// 2. The URL must exactly match a `url` configured on an `npm`-kind entry\n///    in the operator's `[registries]` table in `callisto.toml`.\n///\n/// If the operator has configured no custom npm registries at all (no\n/// `[registries.*]` block with `kind = \"npm\"` and a `url`), any override is\n/// rejected. This is the conservative choice: `callisto.toml`, not an\n/// attacker-influenced `package.json`, must always be the source of truth\n/// for where credentials-bearing publish requests are allowed to go, so\n/// operators who need a private npm registry must opt in explicitly by\n/// declaring it in `[registries]`.\nfn validate_npm_registry_url(\n    url: &str,\n    package: &PackageId,\n    registries: &std::collections::BTreeMap<RegistryKey, crate::config::RegistryConfig>,\n) -> Result<(), GraphError> {\n    let is_approved = url.starts_with(\"https://\")\n        && registries\n            .values()\n            .any(|cfg| cfg.kind == Ecosystem::Npm && cfg.url.as_deref() == Some(url));\n\n    if is_approved {\n        Ok(())\n    } else {\n        Err(GraphError::UntrustedNpmRegistry {\n            package: package.clone(),\n            url: url.to_string(),\n        })\n    }\n}","numLines":46,"startLine":17,"totalLines":1428}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e550ac64-c8ce-4065-86f2-12c3817b5ad1","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
