{"parentUuid":"49759777-7d65-4282-aaed-2cfc1428a0a9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7e639fa-bb3f-487c-a2d1-83df6e40753d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pd2PcPYtwz8vmrqKt6CPeN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Central native-`gix`-first, `CommandRunner`-shell-fallback selection\n2\t//! logic for [`GitDataSource`], replacing the `if let Ok(repo) = ... { if\n3\t//! let Ok(x) = repo.op(...) { return x } } /* fall through */` boilerplate\n4\t//! that used to be hand-rolled independently at five call sites across\n5\t//! `callisto-graph` and `callisto-conventional`.\n6\t\n7\tuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n8\t\n9\tuse callisto_model::{ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, CommitSha, TagName};\n10\t\n11\tuse crate::{GitCommit, GitDataSource, GitRepository, ShellGit, VcsError};\n12\t\n13\t/// Selects between native `gix` ([`GitRepository`]) and a `CommandRunner`\n14\t/// shell-out ([`ShellGit`]) per operation, so callers never have to.\n15\t///\n16\t/// Construct via [`GitAccess::discover`], then call [`GitDataSource`]\n17\t/// methods directly -- there is no branching visible at the call site.\n18\t///\n19\t/// **Fallback policy differs by operation category, deliberately:**\n20\t///\n21\t/// - **Read operations** ([`GitDataSource::list_tags`],\n22\t///   [`GitDataSource::resolve_commit`], [`GitDataSource::commits_since`]):\n23\t///   fall back to the shell backend whenever native `gix` errors for *any*\n24\t///   reason -- failed discovery (`wasm32`, or the root simply isn't a repo)\n25\t///   as well as a discovered repo's operation itself failing. Retrying a\n26\t///   read through the shell can only help: at worst it fails too and the\n27\t///   error propagates from there instead.\n28\t/// - **Write operations** ([`GitDataSource::create_tag`],\n29\t///   [`GitDataSource::create_floating_major`]): fall back to the shell\n30\t///   *only* when native `gix` was never available to begin with (discovery\n31\t///   failed). If a repo *was* discovered, its result -- success or failure\n32\t///   -- is authoritative and returned as-is. Retrying a failed mutation\n33\t///   through a second, different code path risks masking a genuine\n34\t///   failure (or double-applying a mutation the first attempt partially\n35\t///   completed), which read-only retries don't risk.\n36\tpub struct GitAccess<'r> {\n37\t    native: Option<GitRepository>,\n38\t    shell: ShellGit<'r>,\n39\t}\n40\t"}]},"uuid":"b1e398d9-d95d-40ad-8415-546adc6d15c0","timestamp":"2026-08-22T19:19:41.446Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs","content":"//! Central native-`gix`-first, `CommandRunner`-shell-fallback selection\n//! logic for [`GitDataSource`], replacing the `if let Ok(repo) = ... { if\n//! let Ok(x) = repo.op(...) { return x } } /* fall through */` boilerplate\n//! that used to be hand-rolled independently at five call sites across\n//! `callisto-graph` and `callisto-conventional`.\n\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n\nuse callisto_model::{ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, CommitSha, TagName};\n\nuse crate::{GitCommit, GitDataSource, GitRepository, ShellGit, VcsError};\n\n/// Selects between native `gix` ([`GitRepository`]) and a `CommandRunner`\n/// shell-out ([`ShellGit`]) per operation, so callers never have to.\n///\n/// Construct via [`GitAccess::discover`], then call [`GitDataSource`]\n/// methods directly -- there is no branching visible at the call site.\n///\n/// **Fallback policy differs by operation category, deliberately:**\n///\n/// - **Read operations** ([`GitDataSource::list_tags`],\n///   [`GitDataSource::resolve_commit`], [`GitDataSource::commits_since`]):\n///   fall back to the shell backend whenever native `gix` errors for *any*\n///   reason -- failed discovery (`wasm32`, or the root simply isn't a repo)\n///   as well as a discovered repo's operation itself failing. Retrying a\n///   read through the shell can only help: at worst it fails too and the\n///   error propagates from there instead.\n/// - **Write operations** ([`GitDataSource::create_tag`],\n///   [`GitDataSource::create_floating_major`]): fall back to the shell\n///   *only* when native `gix` was never available to begin with (discovery\n///   failed). If a repo *was* discovered, its result -- success or failure\n///   -- is authoritative and returned as-is. Retrying a failed mutation\n///   through a second, different code path risks masking a genuine\n///   failure (or double-applying a mutation the first attempt partially\n///   completed), which read-only retries don't risk.\npub struct GitAccess<'r> {\n    native: Option<GitRepository>,\n    shell: ShellGit<'r>,\n}\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":393}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"49759777-7d65-4282-aaed-2cfc1428a0a9","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
