{"parentUuid":"727ee16f-c0ea-458a-a040-4c0b589d20ba","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7aa590e2-63aa-4f6f-9e48-42c3a3be0a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TBdJT7mrSRbPawx64MSRcn","type":"tool_result","content":"778:/// Classifies combined `twine upload` output into a [`PublishOutcome`] or\n779:/// [`RegistryError`].\n780:///\n781:/// Priority order (highest wins):\n782:/// 1. `\"already exist\"` substring (from `--skip-existing`) without any\n783:///    `\"uploading\"` line → [`PublishOutcome::AlreadyPublished`] (all artifacts\n784:///    were skipped; none were freshly uploaded).\n785:///    When both phrases appear, at least one artifact was newly uploaded\n786:///    alongside the skipped stale artifact, so the result is `Published`.\n787:///    This handles the common case where `dist/` accumulates stale pre-release\n788:///    artifacts: glob `dist/my_pkg-1.0.0*` matches both `my_pkg-1.0.0a0.whl`\n789:///    (skipped) and `my_pkg-1.0.0.whl` (uploaded), producing mixed output.\n790:/// 2. Zero exit code with no skip-only mention → [`PublishOutcome::Published`].\n791:/// 3. Rate-limit signal (`429`, `too many requests`, `rate limit`) →\n792:///    [`RegistryError::RateLimited`] with a parsed or default 60-second\n793:///    retry-after duration.\n794:/// 4. Auth-failure signal (`401`, `403`, `authentication`, etc.) →\n795:///    [`RegistryError::AuthFailed`].\n796:/// 5. Anything else → [`RegistryError::Other`].\n797:fn classify_twine_output(output: &CommandOutput) -> Result<PublishOutcome, RegistryError> {\n798:    let combined = combined_lower(output);\n799:\n800:    let has_skip = combined.contains(\"already exist\");\n801:    let has_upload = combined.contains(\"uploading\");\n802:    if has_skip && !has_upload {\n803:        return Ok(PublishOutcome::AlreadyPublished);\n804:    }\n805:    if output.success() {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5a69a445-d7ca-4f5a-b73a-a5ddbae1e468","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:11:10.254Z","t