{"parentUuid":"63189dd5-6ac6-4533-8164-c311bfd435cc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7aa590e2-63aa-4f6f-9e48-42c3a3be0a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KX2LB7Ee5MwUG8tTDZqB5P","type":"tool_result","content":"96\t    doc[\"init\"][\"ecosystems\"] = toml_edit::value(array);\n97\t\n98\t    Ok(doc.to_string())\n99\t}\n100\t\n101\t/// Scaffolds `callisto.toml` and `.changeset/`, or reconciles an existing\n102\t/// config against the workspace's currently-discovered ecosystems.\n103\t///\n104\t/// `permit` and [`InitOptions::yes`] are independent gates and neither\n105\t/// subsumes the other. `yes` answers \"should detected drift be applied?\";\n106\t/// `permit` answers \"may anything be written at all?\". `--yes --dry-run`\n107\t/// therefore takes the apply *branch* while performing no write -- the\n108\t/// returned [`InitReport`] describes what would happen, exactly as\n109\t/// `version --dry-run` reports the plan it did not apply.\n110\t///\n111\t/// Every computation still runs under a dry run, including the TOML re-render\n112\t/// in `set_recorded_ecosystems`, so a config that would fail to parse on a\n113\t/// real run fails the dry run too rather than reporting a false preview.\n114\t///\n115\t/// # Errors\n116\t///\n117\t/// Returns `Err(GraphError::Config(...))` if `callisto.toml` cannot be read or parsed,\n118\t/// or if the TOML edit for the reconciled ecosystem list fails.\n119\t/// Returns `Err` wrapping an I/O error on filesystem write failures.\n120\tpub fn init<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\n121\t    ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>,\n122\t    opts: &InitOptions,\n123\t    permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>,"}]},"uuid":"79acac3c-a674-45ca-97bc-2e6484d8dd5a","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:11:22.424Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/init.rs","content":"    doc[\"init\"][\"ecosystems\"] = toml_edit::value(array);\n\n    Ok(doc.to_string())\n}\n\n/// Scaffolds `callisto.toml` and `.changeset/`, or reconciles an existing\n/// config against the workspace's currently-discovered ecosystems.\n///\n/// `permit` and [`InitOptions::yes`] are independent gates and neither\n/// subsumes the other. `yes` answers \"should detected drift be applied?\";\n/// `permit` answers \"may anything be written at all?\". `--yes --dry-run`\n/// therefore takes the apply *branch* while performing no write -- the\n/// returned [`InitReport`] describes what would happen, exactly as\n/// `version --dry-run` reports the plan it did not apply.\n///\n/// Every computation still runs under a dry run, including the TOML re-render\n/// in `set_recorded_ecosystems`, so a config that would fail to parse on a\n/// real run fails the dry run too rather than reporting a false preview.\n///\n/// # Errors\n///\n/// Returns `Err(GraphError::Config(...))` if `callisto.toml` cannot be read or parsed,\n/// or if the TOML edit for the reconciled ecosystem list fails.\n/// Returns `Err` wrapping an I/O error on filesystem write failures.\npub fn init<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\n    ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>,\n    opts: &InitOptions,\n    permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>,","numLines":28,"startLine":96,"totalLines":198}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"63189dd5-6ac6-4533-8164-c311bfd435cc","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
