{"parentUuid":"063f1211-c401-4d98-b7f6-5c9f9af9d9c6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7aa590e2-63aa-4f6f-9e48-42c3a3be0a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Chi173aLxkWB4EBrbjGJbX","type":"tool_result","content":"80\t/// Trait for Git VCS operations.\n81\tpub trait GitVcsProvider {\n82\t    fn head_sha(&self) -> Result<CommitSha, VcsError>;\n83\t    fn list_tags(&self, glob_pattern: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<TagName>, VcsError>;\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t/// Unified git-data access surface covering every operation callisto's\n87\t/// release-graph logic needs, independent of *how* the data is sourced.\n88\t///\n89\t/// Two backends implement this trait:\n90\t///\n91\t/// - [`GitRepository`] -- native, backed by `gix`. Fast and side-effect-free\n92\t///   for reads, but entirely unavailable on `wasm32` (gix is excluded from\n93\t///   that target's dependency set, so [`GitRepository::discover`] always\n94\t///   returns `Err` there).\n95\t/// - [`ShellGit`] -- shells out to the real `git` binary via a\n96\t///   [`callisto_model::CommandRunner`], so it works everywhere a `git`\n97\t///   binary is reachable, including through the `wasm32`/Extism host\n98\t///   bridge.\n99\t///\n100\t/// Callers should not implement or select between these directly; use\n101\t/// [`GitAccess::discover`], which tries native `gix` first and transparently\n102\t/// falls back to the `CommandRunner` shell-out, applying the correct\n103\t/// per-operation fallback policy (see [`GitAccess`]'s docs).\n104\tpub trait GitDataSource {\n105\t    /// Returns the commit SHA that `HEAD` currently resolves to.\n106\t    fn head_sha(&self) -> Result<CommitSha, VcsError>;\n107\t\n108\t    /// Lists tag names, optionally filtered by `glob` (a [`globset::Glob`]\n109\t    /// pattern). Both backends filter with the exact same `globset`"}]},"uuid":"6be451fe-e0af-4d5c-aa15-f475f2ab771f","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:11:35.141Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs","content":"/// Trait for Git VCS operations.\npub trait GitVcsProvider {\n    fn head_sha(&self) -> Result<CommitSha, VcsError>;\n    fn list_tags(&self, glob_pattern: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<TagName>, VcsError>;\n}\n\n/// Unified git-data access surface covering every operation callisto's\n/// release-graph logic needs, independent of *how* the data is sourced.\n///\n/// Two backends implement this trait:\n///\n/// - [`GitRepository`] -- native, backed by `gix`. Fast and side-effect-free\n///   for reads, but entirely unavailable on `wasm32` (gix is excluded from\n///   that target's dependency set, so [`GitRepository::discover`] always\n///   returns `Err` there).\n/// - [`ShellGit`] -- shells out to the real `git` binary via a\n///   [`callisto_model::CommandRunner`], so it works everywhere a `git`\n///   binary is reachable, including through the `wasm32`/Extism host\n///   bridge.\n///\n/// Callers should not implement or select between these directly; use\n/// [`GitAccess::discover`], which tries native `gix` first and transparently\n/// falls back to the `CommandRunner` shell-out, applying the correct\n/// per-operation fallback policy (see [`GitAccess`]'s docs).\npub trait GitDataSource {\n    /// Returns the commit SHA that `HEAD` currently resolves to.\n    fn head_sha(&self) -> Result<CommitSha, VcsError>;\n\n    /// Lists tag names, optionally filtered by `glob` (a [`globset::Glob`]\n    /// pattern). Both backends filter with the exact same `globset`","numLines":30,"startLine":80,"totalLines":1256}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"063f1211-c401-4d98-b7f6-5c9f9af9d9c6","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
