{"parentUuid":"f13f1fe5-aee8-42fe-ac01-941443d17c06","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7aa590e2-63aa-4f6f-9e48-42c3a3be0a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Aj5oPef3qjQgrDRwFMdeJM","type":"tool_result","content":"162\t    {\n163\t        serializer.serialize_str(self.render())\n164\t    }\n165\t}\n166\t\n167\timpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Version {\n168\t    /// Generic (grammar-unaware) deserialization. The serialized form of a\n169\t    /// `Version` is just its raw string (see `Serialize`), which does not\n170\t    /// carry the grammar it was parsed under, so this impl cannot *know*\n171\t    /// which grammar to use — it can only guess by trying grammars in turn,\n172\t    /// exactly as `VersionReq::deserialize` already does for Cargo/Npm/Pypi.\n173\t    ///\n174\t    /// SemVer is tried first because it is the strictest, most unambiguous\n175\t    /// grammar; PEP 440 is tried only if SemVer parsing fails. This means a\n176\t    /// string that happens to be valid under *both* grammars (e.g. plain\n177\t    /// `1.2.3`) always resolves to `VersionGrammar::SemVer`, never\n178\t    /// `VersionGrammar::Pep440` — the same residual-ambiguity tradeoff\n179\t    /// `VersionReq::deserialize` accepts for its Cargo/Npm/Pypi chain.\n180\t    ///\n181\t    /// Callers that know the intended ecosystem/grammar ahead of time (e.g.\n182\t    /// because a sibling field names it, or the value came from a\n183\t    /// known-SemVer-only source such as a git tag) should prefer\n184\t    /// [`Version::parse`] with an explicit [`VersionGrammar`] instead of\n185\t    /// going through this generic `serde` impl.\n186\t    fn deserialize<D>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error>\n187\t    where\n188\t        D: Deserializer<'de>,\n189\t    {"}]},"uuid":"9366d03f-42f3-4e89-8199-0a219ce427db","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:11:46.786Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs","content":"    {\n        serializer.serialize_str(self.render())\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Version {\n    /// Generic (grammar-unaware) deserialization. The serialized form of a\n    /// `Version` is just its raw string (see `Serialize`), which does not\n    /// carry the grammar it was parsed under, so this impl cannot *know*\n    /// which grammar to use — it can only guess by trying grammars in turn,\n    /// exactly as `VersionReq::deserialize` already does for Cargo/Npm/Pypi.\n    ///\n    /// SemVer is tried first because it is the strictest, most unambiguous\n    /// grammar; PEP 440 is tried only if SemVer parsing fails. This means a\n    /// string that happens to be valid under *both* grammars (e.g. plain\n    /// `1.2.3`) always resolves to `VersionGrammar::SemVer`, never\n    /// `VersionGrammar::Pep440` — the same residual-ambiguity tradeoff\n    /// `VersionReq::deserialize` accepts for its Cargo/Npm/Pypi chain.\n    ///\n    /// Callers that know the intended ecosystem/grammar ahead of time (e.g.\n    /// because a sibling field names it, or the value came from a\n    /// known-SemVer-only source such as a git tag) should prefer\n    /// [`Version::parse`] with an explicit [`VersionGrammar`] instead of\n    /// going through this generic `serde` impl.\n    fn deserialize<D>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error>\n    where\n        D: Deserializer<'de>,\n    {","numLines":28,"startLine":162,"totalLines":513}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f13f1fe5-aee8-42fe-ac01-941443d17c06","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
