{"parentUuid":"d695d3eb-628e-49f0-8ea8-3cfc76ef1d63","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7aa590e2-63aa-4f6f-9e48-42c3a3be0a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Un5kdRnShX2drrbxAzCqc","type":"tool_result","content":"118\t            }\n119\t        }\n120\t    }\n121\t}\n122\t\n123\t/// Resolves the subcommand `execute_extension` should dispatch to from the\n124\t/// raw `args` moon passes on the command line: the first argument if\n125\t/// present, otherwise `\"status\"`.\n126\t///\n127\t/// Pulled out as its own pure function (no `CommandRunner`/workspace I/O) so\n128\t/// this fallback can be unit-tested directly, natively, without requiring a\n129\t/// real Extism guest -- unlike `execute_extension` itself, which unavoidably\n130\t/// references `crate::runner::MoonCommandRunner` and therefore only links\n131\t/// against a real wasm32 Extism host (see `runner.rs`'s `pdk`-feature impl).\n132\t///\n133\t/// NOTE: this only resolves *which* subcommand name to dispatch on; it does\n134\t/// not validate that name. The `match` in `execute_extension` treats any\n135\t/// name it doesn't specifically recognize (`\"plan-publish\"`/`\"plan_publish\"`,\n136\t/// `\"validate\"`) the same as no subcommand at all -- i.e. it silently falls\n137\t/// back to running `status`, exactly like an empty `args` list. There is\n138\t/// currently no distinct \"unrecognized subcommand\" error path.\n139\t#[cfg(feature = \"pdk\")]\n140\tfn resolve_subcommand(args: &[String]) -> &str {\n141\t    args.first().map(|s| s.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"status\")\n142\t}\n143\t\n144\t#[cfg(feature = \"pdk\")]\n145\tpub fn execute_extension(input: ExecuteExtensionInput) -> ExecuteExtensionOutput {"}]},"uuid":"8aab2b42-cb7f-4f0a-be44-79ef76c18b7c","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:16:44.063Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-moon/src/extension.rs","content":"            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Resolves the subcommand `execute_extension` should dispatch to from the\n/// raw `args` moon passes on the command line: the first argument if\n/// present, otherwise `\"status\"`.\n///\n/// Pulled out as its own pure function (no `CommandRunner`/workspace I/O) so\n/// this fallback can be unit-tested directly, natively, without requiring a\n/// real Extism guest -- unlike `execute_extension` itself, which unavoidably\n/// references `crate::runner::MoonCommandRunner` and therefore only links\n/// against a real wasm32 Extism host (see `runner.rs`'s `pdk`-feature impl).\n///\n/// NOTE: this only resolves *which* subcommand name to dispatch on; it does\n/// not validate that name. The `match` in `execute_extension` treats any\n/// name it doesn't specifically recognize (`\"plan-publish\"`/`\"plan_publish\"`,\n/// `\"validate\"`) the same as no subcommand at all -- i.e. it silently falls\n/// back to running `status`, exactly like an empty `args` list. There is\n/// currently no distinct \"unrecognized subcommand\" error path.\n#[cfg(feature = \"pdk\")]\nfn resolve_subcommand(args: &[String]) -> &str {\n    args.first().map(|s| s.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"status\")\n}\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"pdk\")]\npub fn execute_extension(input: ExecuteExtensionInput) -> ExecuteExtensionOutput {","numLines":28,"startLine":118,"totalLines":474}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d695d3eb-628e-49f0-8ea8-3cfc76ef1d63","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
