{"parentUuid":"f528597c-83eb-4c7c-875b-b9d7ab61dbf6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7aa590e2-63aa-4f6f-9e48-42c3a3be0a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CGQP7GAj5uwrQfAGpm3YFj","type":"tool_result","content":"1245:            \"1.0.0\",\n1246:            \"bump_target with Exit mode, base=1.0.0-alpha.2, sev=Minor must finalize to 1.0.0\"\n1247:        );\n1248:    }\n1249:\n1250:    /// A pre-release cycle must bump from the PINNED baseline captured in\n1251:    /// `PreState.initial_versions` at `pre enter` time, not from whatever the\n1252:    /// latest on-disk prerelease happens to be. Otherwise the release segment\n1253:    /// re-derives from a moving target instead of the pinned one.\n1254:    /// Diamond dependency: A→B, A→C, B→D, C→D.\n1255:    ///\n1256:    /// Bumping D (seeded with a Major severity) causes both B and C to\n1257:    /// cascade. A depends on BOTH B and C, so the cascade solver visits A\n1258:    /// from two different paths. The worklist algorithm must process A only\n1259:    /// ONCE -- it must not be duplicated in the outcome's severity map or\n1260:    /// target map even though two separate edges arrive at A.\n1261:    ///\n1262:    /// Without proper deduplication (e.g. if `raise` were called twice for A\n1263:    /// at the same severity) the idempotency check `sev <= cur_sev` in `raise`\n1264:    /// prevents double-insertion into the maps, but this test makes the\n1265:    /// constraint explicit and guards against regressions where dedup breaks.\n1266:    #[test]\n1267:    fn test_diamond_dependency_a_appears_exactly_once_in_cascade_result() {\n1268:        let pkg_a = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-a\").unwrap();\n1269:        let pkg_b = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-b\").unwrap();\n1270:        let pkg_c = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-c\").unwrap();\n1271:        let pkg_d = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-d\").unwrap();\n1272:\n1273:        // Edges: B→D, C→D, A→B, A→C\n1274:        // B and C use \"^1.0.0\" for D; A uses exact \"=1.0.0\" for B and C.\n1275:        // With CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch, when D is seeded Major (→ 2.0.0):","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"13d94124-6f07-4148-b72f-543e1ecdc221","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:17:35.214Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1245:            \"1.0.0\",\n1246:            \"bump_target with Exit mode, base=1.0.0-alpha.2, sev=Minor must finalize to 1.0.0\"\n1247:        );\n1248:    }\n1249:\n1250:    /// A pre-release cycle must bump from the PINNED baseline captured in\n1251:    /// `PreState.initial_versions` at `pre enter` time, not from whatever the\n1252:    /// latest on-disk prerelease happens to be. Otherwise the release segment\n1253:    /// re-derives from a moving target instead of the pinned one.\n1254:    /// Diamond dependency: A→B, A→C, B→D, C→D.\n1255:    ///\n1256:    /// Bumping D (seeded with a Major severity) causes both B and C to\n1257:    /// cascade. A depends on BOTH B and C, so the cascade solver visits A\n1258:    /// from two different paths. The worklist algorithm must process A only\n1259:    /// ONCE -- it must not be duplicated in the outcome's severity map or\n1260:    /// target map even though two separate edges arrive at A.\n1261:    ///\n1262:    /// Without proper deduplication (e.g. if `raise` were called twice for A\n1263:    /// at the same severity) the idempotency check `sev <= cur_sev` in `raise`\n1264:    /// prevents double-insertion into the maps, but this test makes the\n1265:    /// constraint explicit and guards against regressions where dedup breaks.\n1266:    #[test]\n1267:    fn test_diamond_dependency_a_appears_exactly_once_in_cascade_result() {\n1268:        let pkg_a = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-a\").unwrap();\n1269:        let pkg_b = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-b\").unwrap();\n1270:        let pkg_c = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-c\").unwrap();\n1271:        let pkg_d = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-d\").unwrap();\n1272:\n1273:        // Edges: B→D, C→D, A→B, A→C\n1274:        // B and C use \"^1.0.0\" for D; A uses exact \"=1.0.0\" for B and C.\n1275:        // With CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch, when D is seeded Major (→ 2.0.0):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f528597c-83eb-4c7c-875b-b9d7ab61dbf6","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
