{"parentUuid":"7bcc400c-4c87-4662-a22c-08a1de6bce72","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a8e1128a-4f2b-4a95-9cad-c568b2d24138","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BxaPgfiZtuRfXPTwGW5y8o","type":"tool_result","content":"85\t        } else {\n86\t            batched.insert(path, group);\n87\t        }\n88\t    }\n89\t\n90\t    ManifestWriteClassification { batched, excluded }\n91\t}\n92\t\n93\t/// Writes `plan` to disk and stages the touched paths in git.\n94\t///\n95\t/// Every side effect this performs is unconditional -- the decision of whether\n96\t/// to apply at all belongs to the caller, which is why an [`ApplyPermit`] is\n97\t/// required rather than a `dry_run` flag being passed in. The previous\n98\t/// `ApplyOptions::transient` field was that flag, and being a plain bool it\n99\t/// carried no guarantee that any caller consulted it before constructing the\n100\t/// options. A dry-run caller now cannot obtain a permit and simply does not\n101\t/// call this function; it reports `plan` instead.\n102\t///\n103\t/// # Errors\n104\t///\n105\t/// - Manifest parse or write failures (malformed TOML/JSON, unsupported format).\n106\t/// - Git subprocess failures (`git add` or `git rm --cached` returns a non-zero exit code).\n107\t/// - I/O errors writing changelog sections or `pre.json`.\n108\tpub fn apply_version_plan<R: CommandRunner>(\n109\t    root: &Path,\n110\t    plan: &VersionPlan,\n111\t    runner: &R,\n112\t    opts: &ApplyOptions,\n113\t    permit: &ApplyPermit,\n114\t) -> Result<ApplyOutcome, GraphError> {"}]},"uuid":"edfaafbb-899a-4ecd-8005-25c3a8d3189f","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:48:41.591Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs","content":"        } else {\n            batched.insert(path, group);\n        }\n    }\n\n    ManifestWriteClassification { batched, excluded }\n}\n\n/// Writes `plan` to disk and stages the touched paths in git.\n///\n/// Every side effect this performs is unconditional -- the decision of whether\n/// to apply at all belongs to the caller, which is why an [`ApplyPermit`] is\n/// required rather than a `dry_run` flag being passed in. The previous\n/// `ApplyOptions::transient` field was that flag, and being a plain bool it\n/// carried no guarantee that any caller consulted it before constructing the\n/// options. A dry-run caller now cannot obtain a permit and simply does not\n/// call this function; it reports `plan` instead.\n///\n/// # Errors\n///\n/// - Manifest parse or write failures (malformed TOML/JSON, unsupported format).\n/// - Git subprocess failures (`git add` or `git rm --cached` returns a non-zero exit code).\n/// - I/O errors writing changelog sections or `pre.json`.\npub fn apply_version_plan<R: CommandRunner>(\n    root: &Path,\n    plan: &VersionPlan,\n    runner: &R,\n    opts: &ApplyOptions,\n    permit: &ApplyPermit,\n) -> Result<ApplyOutcome, GraphError> {","numLines":30,"startLine":85,"totalLines":2541}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7bcc400c-4c87-4662-a22c-08a1de6bce72","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
