{"parentUuid":"74fb483a-438d-4170-ac00-a9df2c893d91","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17f8931c-2c00-4d04-b776-0d3ff9f043f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MujRUfLTrE6usnHm4PsGrh","type":"tool_result","content":"28\t    InvalidSeverity {\n29\t        name: String,\n30\t        source: SeverityParseError,\n31\t    },\n32\t}\n33\t\n34\t/// Splits one frontmatter line into its name token and the unparsed remainder (starting at\n35\t/// the separator `:`). This is the function §13 invariant 1 names: \"unquotes before\n36\t/// splitting on `:`, not after.\"\n37\t///\n38\t/// For a **quoted** name, the closing `\"` is located by scanning forward for the matching\n39\t/// delimiter — never by searching for `:` — before anything about the remainder of the line\n40\t/// is inspected. A name that itself contains a `:` (Maven's `groupId:artifactId` form) is\n41\t/// never mis-split, because the colon search for the *separator* only ever runs on the\n42\t/// remainder *after* the name's own boundary has already been resolved by quote-matching.\n43\t///\n44\t/// For a **bare** (unquoted) name, there is nothing to unquote, so `rsplit_once(':')` over\n45\t/// the whole line is applied directly.\n46\tpub(crate) fn split_name_and_rest(line: &str) -> Result<(NameToken<'_>, &str), LineError> {\n47\t    let trimmed = line.trim_start();"}]},"uuid":"6aff8c24-64d1-4f00-ba7d-82c8118a3ace","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:47:41.652Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-format/src/changeset/frontmatter.rs","content":"    InvalidSeverity {\n        name: String,\n        source: SeverityParseError,\n    },\n}\n\n/// Splits one frontmatter line into its name token and the unparsed remainder (starting at\n/// the separator `:`). This is the function §13 invariant 1 names: \"unquotes before\n/// splitting on `:`, not after.\"\n///\n/// For a **quoted** name, the closing `\"` is located by scanning forward for the matching\n/// delimiter — never by searching for `:` — before anything about the remainder of the line\n/// is inspected. A name that itself contains a `:` (Maven's `groupId:artifactId` form) is\n/// never mis-split, because the colon search for the *separator* only ever runs on the\n/// remainder *after* the name's own boundary has already been resolved by quote-matching.\n///\n/// For a **bare** (unquoted) name, there is nothing to unquote, so `rsplit_once(':')` over\n/// the whole line is applied directly.\npub(crate) fn split_name_and_rest(line: &str) -> Result<(NameToken<'_>, &str), LineError> {\n    let trimmed = line.trim_start();","numLines":20,"startLine":28,"totalLines":237}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"74fb483a-438d-4170-ac00-a9df2c893d91","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
