{"parentUuid":"49556bc4-c50d-48b2-82e1-454b4e854140","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17f8931c-2c00-4d04-b776-0d3ff9f043f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N24fydvh71ECUs5kEML7e8","type":"tool_result","content":"1370:        assert_eq!(\n1371:            outcome.severities[&pkg_a],\n1372:            Severity::Patch,\n1373:            \"A's cascaded severity must be Patch (Patch cascade config)\"\n1374:        );\n1375:    }\n1376:\n1377:    /// Pre-release cascade: when D bumps to a pre-release version (via\n1378:    /// `PreMode::Pre`) and a dependent B has a stable-only spec that does NOT\n1379:    /// cover the pre-release version, B is cascaded and its target is also a\n1380:    /// pre-release (because `bump_target` in `PreMode::Pre` calls\n1381:    /// `bump_prerelease`). This test documents and pins that behavior.\n1382:    ///\n1383:    /// The concrete scenario:\n1384:    ///   - D is at 1.0.0, seeded with Major severity in pre-release mode\n1385:    ///   - D bumps to 2.0.0-alpha.0\n1386:    ///   - B depends on D with \"^1.0.0\" (stable-only)\n1387:    ///   - \"^1.0.0\" does NOT cover 2.0.0-alpha.0 (different major, and cargo\n1388:    ///     semver excludes pre-releases from stable ranges)\n1389:    ///   - B IS cascaded (DoesNotCover → cascade) and also bumps to a\n1390:    ///     pre-release version\n1391:    #[test]\n1392:    fn test_prerelease_cascade_stable_spec_out_of_range_triggers_cascade() {\n1393:        let pkg_b = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-b\").unwrap();\n1394:        let pkg_d = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-d\").unwrap();\n1395:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"be86adcf-e094-41e8-924c-cfaa11d65576","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:52:39.440Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1370:        assert_eq!(\n1371:            outcome.severities[&pkg_a],\n1372:            Severity::Patch,\n1373:            \"A's cascaded severity must be Patch (Patch cascade config)\"\n1374:        );\n1375:    }\n1376:\n1377:    /// Pre-release cascade: when D bumps to a pre-release version (via\n1378:    /// `PreMode::Pre`) and a dependent B has a stable-only spec that does NOT\n1379:    /// cover the pre-release version, B is cascaded and its target is also a\n1380:    /// pre-release (because `bump_target` in `PreMode::Pre` calls\n1381:    /// `bump_prerelease`). This test documents and pins that behavior.\n1382:    ///\n1383:    /// The concrete scenario:\n1384:    ///   - D is at 1.0.0, seeded with Major severity in pre-release mode\n1385:    ///   - D bumps to 2.0.0-alpha.0\n1386:    ///   - B depends on D with \"^1.0.0\" (stable-only)\n1387:    ///   - \"^1.0.0\" does NOT cover 2.0.0-alpha.0 (different major, and cargo\n1388:    ///     semver excludes pre-releases from stable ranges)\n1389:    ///   - B IS cascaded (DoesNotCover → cascade) and also bumps to a\n1390:    ///     pre-release version\n1391:    #[test]\n1392:    fn test_prerelease_cascade_stable_spec_out_of_range_triggers_cascade() {\n1393:        let pkg_b = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-b\").unwrap();\n1394:        let pkg_d = PackageId::parse(\"pkg-d\").unwrap();\n1395:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"49556bc4-c50d-48b2-82e1-454b4e854140","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
