{"parentUuid":"180c637f-110d-4134-9f42-40d1de76ac13","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17f8931c-2c00-4d04-b776-0d3ff9f043f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0199EaeyPCmWNHxKtsxjwoyR","type":"tool_result","content":"95:    }\n96:    doc[\"init\"][\"ecosystems\"] = toml_edit::value(array);\n97:\n98:    Ok(doc.to_string())\n99:}\n100:\n101:/// Scaffolds `callisto.toml` and `.changeset/`, or reconciles an existing\n102:/// config against the workspace's currently-discovered ecosystems.\n103:///\n104:/// `permit` and [`InitOptions::yes`] are independent gates: `yes` answers\n105:/// \"should detected drift be applied?\"; `permit` answers \"may anything be\n106:/// written at all?\". `--yes --dry-run` takes the apply *branch* while\n107:/// writing nothing -- the returned [`InitReport`] describes what would\n108:/// happen, exactly as `version --dry-run` reports its unapplied plan.\n109:///\n110:/// Every computation runs under a dry run too, including the TOML\n111:/// re-render in `set_recorded_ecosystems`, so a config that would fail to\n112:/// parse on a real run fails the dry run instead of reporting a false\n113:/// preview.\n114:///\n115:/// # Errors\n116:///\n117:/// `Err(GraphError::Config(...))` if `callisto.toml` can't be read/parsed,\n118:/// or the ecosystem-list TOML edit fails. `Err` wrapping an I/O error on\n119:/// write failures.\n120:pub fn init<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\n121:    ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>,\n122:    opts: &InitOptions,","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"64675acd-56c6-475d-a401-ff24887c73be","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:54:27.571Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"95:    }\n96:    doc[\"init\"][\"ecosystems\"] = toml_edit::value(array);\n97:\n98:    Ok(doc.to_string())\n99:}\n100:\n101:/// Scaffolds `callisto.toml` and `.changeset/`, or reconciles an existing\n102:/// config against the workspace's currently-discovered ecosystems.\n103:///\n104:/// `permit` and [`InitOptions::yes`] are independent gates: `yes` answers\n105:/// \"should detected drift be applied?\"; `permit` answers \"may anything be\n106:/// written at all?\". `--yes --dry-run` takes the apply *branch* while\n107:/// writing nothing -- the returned [`InitReport`] describes what would\n108:/// happen, exactly as `version --dry-run` reports its unapplied plan.\n109:///\n110:/// Every computation runs under a dry run too, including the TOML\n111:/// re-render in `set_recorded_ecosystems`, so a config that would fail to\n112:/// parse on a real run fails the dry run instead of reporting a false\n113:/// preview.\n114:///\n115:/// # Errors\n116:///\n117:/// `Err(GraphError::Config(...))` if `callisto.toml` can't be read/parsed,\n118:/// or the ecosystem-list TOML edit fails. `Err` wrapping an I/O error on\n119:/// write failures.\n120:pub fn init<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\n121:    ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>,\n122:    opts: &InitOptions,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"180c637f-110d-4134-9f42-40d1de76ac13","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
