{"parentUuid":"c571449b-14cc-4def-b8f7-da7c9668d234","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"174e3405-9e1f-4d45-afa2-c6ee797de729","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018v97KnSxgJZ4KaTFq46TLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tuse std::collections::HashSet;\n2\t\n3\tuse callisto_model::{\n4\t    CommandRunner, CratePublish, DepKind, NpmMainPublish, PackageId, PublishPlan, PublishTarget,\n5\t    PypiPublish, RegistryKey, ReleaseEntry, SCHEMA_VERSION,\n6\t};\n7\tuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\n8\t\n9\tuse crate::error::GraphError;\n10\tuse crate::resolver::DependencyResolver;\n11\tuse crate::toposort::toposort_impl;\n12\tuse crate::Workspace;\n13\t\n14\t/// Edge kinds cascade/version-bump propagation cares about: a `Dev`-only\n15\t/// dependency change correctly never forces a consumer's version to bump.\n16\tconst CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[DepKind::Runtime, DepKind::Build, DepKind::Optional];\n17\t\n18\t/// Edge kinds publish ordering cares about: cascade's kinds, plus `Dev`.\n19\t/// `cargo publish` (run without `--no-verify`, see `publish_client.rs`)\n20\t/// re-extracts the packaged tarball and does a real local build to verify\n21\t/// it, which needs *every* dependency in the crate's `Cargo.toml` —\n22\t/// `[dev-dependencies]` included — resolvable from the registry. A\n23\t/// dev-dependency on a workspace sibling published in the same batch\n24\t/// therefore still needs that sibling to publish first, even though the\n25\t/// two crates have no cascade-relevant ordering constraint between them.\n26\tconst PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[\n27\t    DepKind::Runtime,\n28\t    DepKind::Build,\n29\t    DepKind::Optional,\n30\t    DepKind::Dev,\n31\t];\n32\t\n33\t/// Computes the order packages must be published in.\n34\t///\n35\t/// This is a thin, purpose-named wrapper around [`toposort_impl`] (the\n36\t/// generic algorithm, reused as-is) rather than a generic\n37\t/// `DependencyResolverExt::toposort()` on a shared trait — it exists\n38\t/// specifically for `plan_publish` below, its only caller, and its\n39\t/// semantics are publish-specific, not \"the one true topological sort.\"\n40\t///\n41\t/// Tries [`PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS`] first (including `Dev`, unlike cascade's\n42\t/// own [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`]) so a dev-dependency on a same-batch\n43\t/// sibling publishes in the right order. `Dev` edges are best-effort, not a\n44\t/// hard requirement, precisely because mutual dev-only dependencies between\n45\t/// two otherwise-unrelated packages are a legitimate pattern (e.g. two\n46\t/// crates each dev-depending on the other for cross-integration tests) —\n47\t/// unlike `Runtime`/`Build`/`Optional`, which must never cycle, a `Dev`\n48\t/// cycle must not hard-fail the whole publish plan. If including `Dev`\n49\t/// edges would produce a cycle, this falls back to\n50\t/// [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`] alone, which is guaranteed not to introduce a\n51\t/// *new* cycle here since it is a strict subset of the edges just proven\n52\t/// cyclic — accepting the original race this function exists to close for\n53\t/// that one pair, rather than failing the entire plan over it.\n54\tfn publish_order<D: DependencyResolver + ?Sized>(\n55\t    resolver: &D,\n56\t    subset: &HashSet<PackageId>,\n57\t) -> Result<Vec<PackageId>, GraphError> {\n58\t    let all_pkg_ids: Vec<PackageId> = resolver.packages().map(|p| p.id.clone()).collect();\n59\t    let edges_of = |id: &PackageId| -> Vec<(PackageId, DepKind)> {\n60\t        resolver\n61\t            .dependencies_of(id)\n62\t            .map(|e| (e.to.clone(), e.kind))\n63\t            .collect()\n64\t    };\n65\t"}]},"uuid":"d777cacb-fab1-4a0a-aa42-8960d0d659cb","timestamp":"2026-08-23T03:34:39.303Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs","content":"use std::collections::HashSet;\n\nuse callisto_model::{\n    CommandRunner, CratePublish, DepKind, NpmMainPublish, PackageId, PublishPlan, PublishTarget,\n    PypiPublish, RegistryKey, ReleaseEntry, SCHEMA_VERSION,\n};\nuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\n\nuse crate::error::GraphError;\nuse crate::resolver::DependencyResolver;\nuse crate::toposort::toposort_impl;\nuse crate::Workspace;\n\n/// Edge kinds cascade/version-bump propagation cares about: a `Dev`-only\n/// dependency change correctly never forces a consumer's version to bump.\nconst CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[DepKind::Runtime, DepKind::Build, DepKind::Optional];\n\n/// Edge kinds publish ordering cares about: cascade's kinds, plus `Dev`.\n/// `cargo publish` (run without `--no-verify`, see `publish_client.rs`)\n/// re-extracts the packaged tarball and does a real local build to verify\n/// it, which needs *every* dependency in the crate's `Cargo.toml` —\n/// `[dev-dependencies]` included — resolvable from the registry. A\n/// dev-dependency on a workspace sibling published in the same batch\n/// therefore still needs that sibling to publish first, even though the\n/// two crates have no cascade-relevant ordering constraint between them.\nconst PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[\n    DepKind::Runtime,\n    DepKind::Build,\n    DepKind::Optional,\n    DepKind::Dev,\n];\n\n/// Computes the order packages must be published in.\n///\n/// This is a thin, purpose-named wrapper around [`toposort_impl`] (the\n/// generic algorithm, reused as-is) rather than a generic\n/// `DependencyResolverExt::toposort()` on a shared trait — it exists\n/// specifically for `plan_publish` below, its only caller, and its\n/// semantics are publish-specific, not \"the one true topological sort.\"\n///\n/// Tries [`PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS`] first (including `Dev`, unlike cascade's\n/// own [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`]) so a dev-dependency on a same-batch\n/// sibling publishes in the right order. `Dev` edges are best-effort, not a\n/// hard requirement, precisely because mutual dev-only dependencies between\n/// two otherwise-unrelated packages are a legitimate pattern (e.g. two\n/// crates each dev-depending on the other for cross-integration tests) —\n/// unlike `Runtime`/`Build`/`Optional`, which must never cycle, a `Dev`\n/// cycle must not hard-fail the whole publish plan. If including `Dev`\n/// edges would produce a cycle, this falls back to\n/// [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`] alone, which is guaranteed not to introduce a\n/// *new* cycle here since it is a strict subset of the edges just proven\n/// cyclic — accepting the original race this function exists to close for\n/// that one pair, rather than failing the entire plan over it.\nfn publish_order<D: DependencyResolver + ?Sized>(\n    resolver: &D,\n    subset: &HashSet<PackageId>,\n) -> Result<Vec<PackageId>, GraphError> {\n    let all_pkg_ids: Vec<PackageId> = resolver.packages().map(|p| p.id.clone()).collect();\n    let edges_of = |id: &PackageId| -> Vec<(PackageId, DepKind)> {\n        resolver\n            .dependencies_of(id)\n            .map(|e| (e.to.clone(), e.kind))\n            .collect()\n    };\n","numLines":65,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1492}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c571449b-14cc-4def-b8f7-da7c9668d234","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
