{"parentUuid":"f1822c02-0b82-4d3d-a619-a7e64e01c4a8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs","snippet":"1\tuse std::collections::HashSet;\n2\t\n3\tuse callisto_model::{\n4\t    CommandRunner, CratePublish, DepKind, NpmMainPublish, PackageId, PublishPlan, PublishTarget,\n5\t    PypiPublish, RegistryKey, ReleaseEntry, SCHEMA_VERSION,\n6\t};\n7\tuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\n8\t\n9\tuse crate::error::GraphError;\n10\tuse crate::resolver::DependencyResolver;\n11\tuse crate::toposort::toposort_impl;\n12\tuse crate::Workspace;\n13\t\n14\t/// Edge kinds cascade/version-bump propagation cares about: a `Dev`-only\n15\t/// dependency change correctly never forces a consumer's version to bump.\n16\tconst CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[DepKind::Runtime, DepKind::Build, DepKind::Optional];\n17\t\n18\t/// Edge kinds publish ordering cares about: cascade's kinds, plus `Dev`.\n19\t/// `cargo publish` (run without `--no-verify`, see `publish_client.rs`)\n20\t/// re-extracts the packaged tarball and does a real local build to verify\n21\t/// it, which needs *every* dependency in the crate's `Cargo.toml` —\n22\t/// `[dev-dependencies]` included — resolvable from the registry. A\n23\t/// dev-dependency on a workspace sibling published in the same batch\n24\t/// therefore still needs that sibling to publish first, even though the\n25\t/// two crates have no cascade-relevant ordering constraint between them.\n26\tconst PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[\n27\t    DepKind::Runtime,\n28\t    DepKind::Build,\n29\t    DepKind::Optional,\n30\t    DepKind::Dev,\n31\t];\n32\t\n33\t/// Computes the order packages must be published in.\n34\t///\n35\t/// This is a thin, purpose-named wrapper around [`toposort_impl`] (the\n36\t/// generic algorithm, reused as-is) rather than a generic\n37\t/// `DependencyResolverExt::toposort()` on a shared trait — it exists\n38\t/// specifically for `plan_publish` below, its only caller, and its\n39\t/// semantics are publish-specific, not \"the one true topological sort.\"\n40\t///\n41\t/// Tries [`PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS`] first (including `Dev`, unlike cascade's\n42\t/// own [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`]) so a dev-dependency on a same-batch\n43\t/// sibling publishes in the right order. `Dev` edges are best-effort, not a\n44\t/// hard requirement, precisely because mutual dev-only dependencies between\n45\t/// two otherwise-unrelated packages are a legitimate pattern (e.g. two\n46\t/// crates each dev-depending on the other for cross-integration tests) —\n47\t/// unlike `Runtime`/`Build`/`Optional`, which must never cycle, a `Dev`\n48\t/// cycle must not hard-fail the whole publish plan. If including `Dev`\n49\t/// edges would produce a cycle, this falls back to\n50\t/// [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`] alone, which is guaranteed not to introduce a\n51\t/// *new* cycle here since it is a strict subset of the edges just proven\n52\t/// cyclic — accepting the original race this function exists to close for\n53\t/// that one pair, rather than failing the entire plan over it.\n54\tfn publish_order<D: DependencyResolver + ?Sized>(\n55\t    resolver: &D,\n56\t    subset: &HashSet<PackageId>,\n57\t) -> Result<Vec<PackageId>, GraphError> {\n58\t    let all_pkg_ids: Vec<PackageId> = resolver.packages().map(|p| p.id.clone()).collect();\n59\t    let edges_of = |id: &PackageId| -> Vec<(PackageId, DepKind)> {\n60\t        resolver\n61\t            .dependencies_of(id)\n62\t            .map(|e| (e.to.clone(), e.kind))\n63\t            .collect()\n64\t    };\n65\t\n66\t    toposort_impl(subset, &all_pkg_ids, CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS, edges_of)\n67\t}\n68\t\n69\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]\n70\tpub struct PublishOptions {\n71\t    /// When non-empty, only packages whose bare name (without ecosystem prefix)\n72\t    /// appears in this list are included in the plan. An empty `only` list\n73\t    /// means \"include all packages\" (the default).\n74\t    pub only: Vec<String>,\n75\t}\n76\t\n77\t/// Validates a `publishConfig.registry` URL read from a package's own\n78\t/// `package.json` before it is threaded into the publish plan (and\n79\t/// eventually into `npm publish --registry <url>` / `npm view --registry\n80\t/// <url>`, both run with `NPM_TOKEN` live in the process environment in CI).\n81\t///\n82\t/// `publishConfig.registry` is manifest-controlled data -- something a PR\n83\t/// author can set in their own package.json -- not operator-controlled\n84\t/// config, so it must never be trusted verbatim as a publish destination.\n85\t/// Two checks are enforced, mirroring the leading-`-` flag-injection guard\n86\t/// already applied to package names before they reach these same CLI\n87\t/// invocations (see `SubprocessRegistryClient::npm_publish`):\n88\t///\n89\t/// 1. The URL must use the `https` scheme. A scheme downgrade (e.g. `http`)\n90\t///    is rejected even if the host would otherwise be approved, since scheme\n91\t///    downgrade is itself part of the attack this guard defends against.\n92\t/// 2. The URL must exactly match a `url` configured on an `npm`-kind entry\n93\t///    in the operator's `[registries]` table in `callisto.toml`.\n94\t///\n95\t/// If the operator has configured no custom npm registries at all (no\n96\t/// `[registries.*]` block with `kind = \"npm\"` and a `url`), any override is\n97\t/// rejected. This is the conservative choice: `callisto.toml`, not an\n98\t/// attacker-influenced `package.json`, must always be the source of truth\n99\t/// for where credentials-bearing publish requests are allowed to go, so\n100\t/// operators who need a private npm registry must opt in explicitly by\n101\t/// declaring it in `[registries]`.\n102\tfn validate_npm_registry_url(\n103\t    url: &str,\n104\t    package: &PackageId,\n105\t    registries: &std::collections::BTreeMap<RegistryKey, crate::config::RegistryConfig>,\n106\t) -> Result<(), GraphError> {\n107\t    let is_approved = url.starts_with(\"https://\")\n108\t        && registries\n109\t            .values()\n110\t            .any(|cfg| cfg.kind == Ecosystem::Npm && cfg.url.as_deref() == Some(url));\n111\t\n112\t    if is_approved {\n113\t        Ok(())\n114\t    } else {\n115\t        Err(GraphError::UntrustedNpmRegistry {\n116\t            package: package.clone(),\n117\t            url: url.to_string(),\n118\t        })\n119\t    }\n120\t}\n121\t\n122\t/// Resolves a package's `changelog_section` for `plan_publish`: reads the file at\n123\t/// `ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path)` and extracts the `## {ver}` section via\n124\t/// `callisto_changelog::extract_section`. Every non-fatal outcome (file not found, no\n125\t/// matching heading, empty matched section, or an unreadable file) leaves the return value\n126\t/// `None` and pushes exactly one Warning diagnostic into `diagnostics` rather than aborting\n127\t/// the plan -- `ChangelogSectionNotFound` for the first three (AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12),\n128\t/// `ChangelogReadError` for a read failure that is not \"file does not exist\" (AC-12c).\n129\tfn resolve_changelog_section(\n130\t    ws_root: &std::path::Path,\n131\t    changelog_rel_path: &std::path::Path,\n132\t    pkg_id: &callisto_model::PackageId,\n133\t    ver: &callisto_model::Version,\n134\t    diagnostics: &mut Vec<callisto_model::Diagnostic>,\n135\t) -> Option<String> {\n136\t    let full_path = ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path);\n137\t    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n138\t        Ok(c) => c,\n139\t        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {\n140\t            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n141\t                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound,\n142\t                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n143\t                message: format!(\n144\t                    \"no changelog file found at `{}` for package `{}`\",\n145\t                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\n146\t                    pkg_id.display_name()\n147\t                ),\n148\t                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\n149\t                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\n150\t                escalated_by: None,\n151\t                governed_by: None,\n152\t            });\n153\t            return None;\n154\t        }\n155\t        Err(e) => {\n156\t            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n157\t                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError,\n158\t                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n159\t                message: format!(\n\n... [1442 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a34fdc04-299a-4676-a34b-3dbb8b936d7a","timestamp":"2026-08-23T03:40:12.762Z","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
