{"parentUuid":"04c9b81e-1b91-4e06-ba6f-29a95a7819d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKtNoQm85HQLGgcEajea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Trivial rustc compiles fine (0.35s) — so it's not systemic OS/rustc breakage. This is specific to `callisto-moon`'s test target, which links `extism_convert_macros`/`prost_derive` (proc-macro dylibs). The actual hang, per the stack trace I captured earlier, is inside rustc's own Ctrl-C handler installation (`ctrlc::set_handler_inner` → a GCD semaphore wait) — that's an unusual place to deadlock, and it's now reproduced 3 times today specifically on this one compilation target.\n\nMy best-supported theory: repeated `kill -9`s on rustc processes throughout this long session may have left the `target/` build state or some OS-level resource in a condition that reliably trips this one proc-macro-heavy link step, though I can't fully confirm the exact mechanism from here.\n\nGiven that:\n- This is a **pre-push hook** (local tooling) issue, not a code issue.\n- The actual 3 conflict-resolved files are already independently verified: `cargo check -p callisto-graph -p callisto-vcs` clean, 14 cascade tests + 12 tags tests + 38 vcs tests all pass.\n\nHow do you want to handle it — keep retrying the push (it may clear on its own like `callisto-model` did earlier), or should I try a full `cargo clean` on just the `callisto-moon` build artifacts to force a truly fresh link attempt?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1897,"cache_read_input_tokens":905735,"output_tokens":1877,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1403},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1897,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1877,"c