{"parentUuid":"aaf6354b-c8cb-40ad-a479-24489d367cca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKu3vYy3pu2UBa1vaTmG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now ruled out every likely cause methodically:\n- **Not systemic** — a trivial `rustc` compile runs in 0.35s.\n- **Not incremental-compilation corruption** — disabled it entirely (`CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`), still hangs identically.\n- **Not moon's own locking** — `.moon/cache/locks/` is empty, no lock held anywhere.\n- **Not disk space** — 194GB free.\n- **Not file descriptor exhaustion** — 196 open for this process, limit is over 1M.\n- **Not a child-process deadlock** — no children exist; it's stuck single-threaded before parallel codegen even starts.\n\nWhat's left, honestly: this compile links a genuinely unusual native-code chain for a *metadata-only* check (`wasmtime`'s JIT/internal-jit-debug output, `aws-lc-sys`, `ring`, `zstd-sys`, `liblzma-sys` — several of these have their own `build.rs` scripts that probe the toolchain/CPU). I can't pin the exact single mechanism further without attaching a debugger, which risks disrupting things more than it clarifies. My best-supported remaining guess is a build-script-level hang specific to one of those native deps in this environment, not something in the code I changed.\n\nGiven the actual PR content is independently verified (targeted `cargo check`/`cargo test` on all 3 conflict-resolved files passed cleanly earlier), do you want me to skip the pre-push hook for this one push (`--no-verify`) to get this merged, or keep digging?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":926831,"output_tokens":1251,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":728},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999,"epheme