{"parentUuid":"db2af5b4-ad35-4475-aa1b-3c06dbc367b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKvJfKDdQrJsp7oXZNbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found the actual root cause. The log shows `moon run :lint` isn't hanging — it's running each crate's `cargo clippy -p $project` as a **separate cargo invocation**, and every single one prints `Blocking waiting for file lock on package cache` / `build directory` before it can even start. All 10 crates share one workspace `target/` dir, and Cargo takes a process-level lock on it — so moon's \"parallel\" task graph is actually fully serialized by Cargo itself. Total wall time was the *sum* of each crate's build (11m + 8m + 13m + 12m + 7m + ... ≈ 60+ minutes), not any single crate hanging.\n\nThis means the user's clippy/wasm-crate hypothesis was reasonable but wrong: it's not specific to `callisto-moon` or to clippy at all — every crate serializes behind the same lock, and dropping clippy from one crate would only remove one link in a 10-deep chain, saving a few minutes out of an hour."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4502,"cache_read_input_tokens":80988,"output_tokens":3276,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2852},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4502,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3276,"cache_read_input_tokens":80988,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4502},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKvJchTFoyMGS8A4GtRQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5ba8185-3d7f-46ca-845d-3495b54eb12c","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:31:17.964Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e