{"parentUuid":"9a80e8e3-8d54-495d-b52d-6172901e3ee7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fc3a55ec-1780-48ea-b842-55f438ab4c0f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TWu1VhQjFcdCxF11bispVP","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the documentation provided, moon's toolchain configuration does **not** include Rust/Cargo-specific settings regarding target directories, build locking, or parallel invocation coordination.\n\nThe page only references a generic `rust` toolchain with a note to \"Run `moon toolchain info rust` for all available settings,\" but those specific settings are not documented in the content shown.\n\nFor detailed Rust toolchain options, you would need to run that command directly or consult additional documentation beyond what's presented here."}]},"uuid":"e352650d-e752-48a8-8ea4-bb4ee7bee32e","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:43:34.215Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":60916,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Based on the documentation provided, moon's toolchain configuration does **not** include Rust/Cargo-specific settings regarding target directories, build locking, or parallel invocation coordination.\n\nThe page only references a generic `rust` toolchain with a note to \"Run `moon toolchain info rust` for all available settings,\" but those specific settings are not documented in the content shown.\n\nFor detailed Rust toolchain options, you would need to run that command directly or consult additional documentation beyond what's presented here.","durationMs":2119,"url":"https://moonrepo.dev/docs/config/toolchain#rust"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9a80e8e3-8d54-495d-b52d-6172901e3ee7","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"attachment":{"command":"","content":"","durationMs":48,"exitCode":0,"hookEvent":"","hookName":"","stderr":"","stdout":"","toolUseID":"","type":"hook_success"},"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"e352650d-e752-48a8-8ea4-bb4ee7bee32e","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:43:34.214Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"dae722e0-d84f-4bca-b2be-da57b1078ee9","version":"2.1.238"}
{"parentUuid":"3ab2a5ed-206a-4ed8-9269-5e71c2ca2312","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fc3a55ec-1780-48ea-b842-55f438ab4c0f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011qGJ1hQQogak1R6nsags6V","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"moonrepo moon monorepo rust cargo workspace target directory lock parallel tasks 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"moon v1.5 - Rust tier 2 and 3 support | moonrepo\",\"url\":\"https://moonrepo.dev/blog/moon-v1.5\"},{\"title\":\"moon | Skills Marketplace\",\"url\":\"https://lobehub.com/skills/hyperb1iss-moonrepo-skill-moon\"},{\"title\":\"moonrepo | Skills Marketplace\",\"url\":\"https://lobehub.com/skills/terminalskills-skills-moonrepo\"},{\"title\":\"Rust handbook | moonrepo\",\"url\":\"https://moonrepo.dev/docs/guides/rust/handbook\"},{\"title\":\"moon/Cargo.lock at master · moonrepo/moon\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/moonrepo/moon/blob/master/Cargo.lock\"},{\"title\":\"moon - A task runner and monorepo management tool for the web ecosystem, written in Rust | moonrepo\",\"url\":\"https://moonrepo.dev/moon\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - moonrepo/moon: A build system and monorepo management tool for the web ecosystem, written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/moonrepo/moon\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · moonrepo/moon\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/moonrepo/moon/releases\"},{\"title\":\"internals.rust-lang.org\",\"url\":\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/c/tools-and-infrastructure/cargo/15/l/latest?page=1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about moon (moonrepo), Rust/Cargo workspaces, and parallel task execution:\n\n## Moon - Monorepo Task Runner\n\nmoonrepo is a Rust-based monorepo manager and task runner that builds an explicit dependency graph to schedule and execute tasks deterministically and in the correct order.\n\n## Key Features for Rust/Cargo Integration\n\nMoon is not a build system and does not replace Cargo. Instead, moon runs cargo commands, and efficiently orchestrates those tasks within the workspace.\n\n### Cargo Workspace Configuration\n\nRust/Cargo repositories come in two flavors: a single crate with one Cargo.toml, or multiple crates with many Cargo.tomls using Cargo workspaces. The latter is highly preferred as it enables Cargo incremental caching.\n\nIf you do per-crate configurations, Cargo itself will \"wait for build lock\" when multiple processes are running.\n\n## Parallel Task Execution\n\nMoon executes actions in parallel and in order using a thread pool and our dependency graph. Core features include dependency-aware task orchestration, fine-grained inputs/outputs for incremental builds, persistent caching, parallel execution, and CI pipeline generation.\n\n## Recent Updates\n\nThe moon docker prune command has been updated to remove the entire target directory, greatly reducing the size of the image.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ed9507a6-e939-45ee-9fac-3416773f589b","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:43:41.452Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"moonrepo moon monorepo rust cargo workspace target directory lock parallel tasks 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Ar9Y9KswUhzuVg7ZguWUCc","content":[{"title":"moon v1.5 - Rust tier 2 and 3 support | moonrepo","url":"https://moonrepo.dev/blog/moon-v1.5"},{"title":"moon | Skills Marketplace","url":"https://lobehub.com/skills/hyperb1iss-moonrepo-skill-moon"},{"title":"moonrepo | Skills Marketplace","url":"https://lobehub.com/skills/terminalskills-skills-moonrepo"},{"title":"Rust handbook | moonrepo","url":"https://moonrepo.dev/docs/guides/rust/handbook"},{"title":"moon/Cargo.lock at master · moonrepo/moon","url":"https://github.com/moonrepo/moon/blob/master/Cargo.lock"},{"title":"moon - A task runner and monorepo management tool for the web ecosystem, written in Rust | moonrepo","url":"https://moonrepo.dev/moon"},{"title":"GitHub - moonrepo/moon: A build system and monorepo management tool for the web ecosystem, written in Rust. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/moonrepo/moon"},{"title":"Releases · moonrepo/moon","url":"https://github.com/moonrepo/moon/releases"},{"title":"internals.rust-lang.org","url":"https://internals.rust-lang.org/c/tools-and-infrastructure/cargo/15/l/latest?page=1"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about moon (moonrepo), Rust/Cargo workspaces, and parallel task execution:\n\n## Moon - Monorepo Task Runner\n\nmoonrepo is a Rust-based monorepo manager and task runner that builds an explicit dependency graph to schedule and execute tasks deterministically and in the correct order.\n\n## Key Features for Rust/Cargo Integration\n\nMoon is not a build system and does not replace Cargo. Instead, moon runs cargo commands, and efficiently orchestrates those tasks within the workspace.\n\n### Cargo Workspace Configuration\n\nRust/Cargo repositories come in two flavors: a single crate with one Cargo.toml, or multiple crates with many Cargo.tomls using Cargo workspaces. The latter is highly preferred as it enables Cargo incremental caching.\n\nIf you do per-crate configurations, Cargo itself will \"wait for build lock\" when multiple processes are running.\n\n## Parallel Task Execution\n\nMoon executes actions in parallel and in order using a thread pool and our dependency graph. Core features include dependency-aware task orchestration, fine-grained inputs/outputs for incremental builds, persistent caching, parallel execution, and CI pipeline generation.\n\n## Recent Updates\n\nThe moon docker prune command has been updated to remove the entire target directory, greatly reducing the size of the image."],"durationSeconds":7.3403762910068036,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ab2a5ed-206a-4ed8-9269-5e71c2ca2312","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","ve