{"parentUuid":"e75a8b15-b926-43e9-bbda-3fdf7bd9641d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKwJFZLJCWj7kz8eCGpu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MZTPKtocJ8QqHGKrJVPWPZ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://moonrepo.dev/docs/guides/rust/handbook","prompt":"How does moonrepo recommend structuring cargo/clippy/test tasks for a Cargo workspace monorepo with many crates? Specifically: does it recommend one task per crate or a single workspace-wide task? How does it handle the Cargo build-lock/target-directory contention problem when multiple cargo processes run concurrently? What's the recommended way to get both affected-project scoping and real parallelism?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1911,"cache_read_input_tokens":162762,"output_tokens":419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":194},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1911,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":162762,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1911},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKwJEZ4es1XpmxBQq1Br","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0c4cca2-0d12-41ed-a46b-22c9e32879a0","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:43:46.230Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"a0c4cca2-0d12-41ed-a46b-22c9e32879a0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fc3a55ec-1780-48ea-b842-55f438ab4c0f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MZTPKtocJ8QqHGKrJVPWPZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# moonrepo's Cargo Workspace Task Recommendations\n\nBased on the handbook, moonrepo provides **limited specific guidance** on this architecture question. Here's what's documented:\n\n## Task Structure\nThe handbook shows example configurations using **workspace-wide tasks** (e.g., `cargo test --workspace`, `cargo clippy --workspace`), suggesting this is the recommended approach for monorepos.\n\n## Build Lock Contention\nRegarding concurrent cargo processes, moonrepo explicitly acknowledges the problem:\n\n> \"if you do per-crate, Cargo itself will 'wait for build lock' when multiple processes are running.\"\n\nHowever, the handbook **does not provide a detailed solution** beyond noting this limitation exists. It simply states you can choose between workspace-level or per-crate configuration, with this as a known tradeoff.\n\n## Parallelism Strategy\nThe documentation emphasizes that \"moon is not a build system and does _not_ replace Cargo. Instead, moon runs `cargo` commands, and efficiently orchestrates those tasks.\"\n\nThe handbook doesn't detail how moonrepo balances affected-project scoping with real parallelism when facing Cargo's build-lock constraints. It recommends using workspace-level Cargo commands but doesn't explain the orchestration mechanics that solve concurrent execution problems.\n\n**Bottom line:** moonrepo recommends workspace-wide tasks but acknowledges the contention problem without providing an explicit technical solution in this handbook."}]},"uuid":"d4fc56df-eac3-41e0-b4cf-753195aaccd8","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:43:53.373Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":79107,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# moonrepo's Cargo Workspace Task Recommendations\n\nBased on the handbook, moonrepo provides **limited specific guidance** on this architecture question. Here's what's documented:\n\n## Task Structure\nThe handbook shows example configurations using **workspace-wide tasks** (e.g., `cargo test --workspace`, `cargo clippy --workspace`), suggesting this is the recommended approach for monorepos.\n\n## Build Lock Contention\nRegarding concurrent cargo processes, moonrepo explicitly acknowledges the problem:\n\n> \"if you do per-crate, Cargo itself will 'wait for build lock' when multiple processes are running.\"\n\nHowever, the handbook **does not provide a detailed solution** beyond noting this limitation exists. It simply states you can choose between workspace-level or per-crate configuration, with this as a known tradeoff.\n\n## Parallelism Strategy\nThe documentation emphasizes that \"moon is not a build system and does _not_ replace Cargo. Instead, moon runs `cargo` commands, and efficiently orchestrates those tasks.\"\n\nThe handbook doesn't detail how moonrepo balances affected-project scoping with real parallelism when facing Cargo's build-lock constraints. It recommends using workspace-level Cargo commands but doesn't explain the orchestration mechanics that solve concurrent execution problems.\n\n**Bottom line:** moonrepo recommends workspace-wide tasks but acknowledges the contention problem without providing an explicit technical solution in this handbook.","durationMs":5279,"url":"https://moonrepo.dev/docs/guides/rust/handbook"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0c4cca2-0d12-41ed-a46b-22c9e32879a0","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
