{"parentUuid":"22d907c1-3335-48b5-9e94-f319b98cf365","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKwnTtGvL4UKcNaXrybF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_read_input_tokens":180793,"output_tokens":2872,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":760},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2872,"cache_read_input_tokens":180793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKwnT2Bp1PXFbDLcRQCj","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf8f6e60-52b3-4108-a6b7-bb0b428a8785","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:50:15.480Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"cf8f6e60-52b3-4108-a6b7-bb0b428a8785","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKwnTtGvL4UKcNaXrybF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Speed comparison (measured, not estimated):**\n\n| Path | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full-workspace lint (`just ci`) | ~63 min (sum of 10 serialized per-crate `cargo clippy` runs, each queued behind the last) | **5m 13s** (one process, Cargo's own parallel scheduler) — confirmed clean run |\n| Pre-push lint (`lint-affected`) | Same ~63 min every push, regardless of what changed | Near-instant when nothing affects a crate; when N crates are affected, one scoped `cargo clippy -p A -p B...` instead of N serialized processes |\n\nNet: full CI lint is ~12x faster, and pre-push no longer pays a fixed 60+ minute tax on every push — it scales with what actually changed.\n\nFor teaching other agents/repos, here's a portable prompt — this isn't moon-specific, it's inherent to Cargo, so it applies to any monorepo task runner (Turborepo, Nx, Makefiles, Bazel wrappers) that fans out `cargo clippy -p $crate`/`cargo test -p $crate` per-package over a shared `target/` dir:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_read_input_tokens":180793,"output_tokens":2872,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":760},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2872,"cache_read_input_tokens":180793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKwnT2Bp1PXFbDLcRQCj","type":"assistant","uuid":"3bc9cc87-c5f7-467e-8ae8-17a5d3f3e48f","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:50:20.394Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3bc9cc87-c5f7-467e-8ae8-17a5d3f3e48f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKwnTtGvL4UKcNaXrybF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PTtyRR8HX2U8eKh5ZvB8GM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/cargo-monorepo-lock-fix-prompt.md","content":"Investigate whether this repo has a Cargo-workspace build-lock serialization bug in its\nCI/lint/test task runner (moon, Turborepo, Nx, Makefile, or similar), and fix it if so.\n\n## Background\n\nCargo takes a process-level file lock on a workspace's shared `target/` directory for the\nduration of any `cargo` invocation (build, check, clippy, test) touching it. If a monorepo\ntask runner fans out one `cargo <cmd> -p $crate` invocation per crate — even when it *thinks*\nit's running them in parallel — every one of those processes contends for the same lock, so\nthey serialize behind each other. The task runner's own parallelism is real at the process-\nspawn level; Cargo silently defeats it underneath. Symptom: a lint/build/test step that \"hangs\"\nor takes 10-60+ minutes even though no single crate should take that long, with repeated\n\"Blocking waiting for file lock on build directory\" lines in verbose output — easy to\nmisdiagnose as a hung process, a bad dependency (heavy C-linked crates like aws-lc-sys/ring/\nwasmtime are common red herrings), or a caching bug, when it's actually just N processes\nqueued behind one lock.\n\nThis is a known, acknowledged Cargo/monorepo-tool interaction — moonrepo's own Rust handbook\nstates it explicitly: \"if you do per-crate, Cargo itself will 'wait for build lock' when\nmultiple processes are running,\" and recommends workspace-wide invocations instead.\n\n## Diagnose\n\n1. Find the task definition that runs clippy/build/test per-crate (e.g. a global task template\n   with `-p $project` or equivalent, applied to every package).\n2. Run the full task with verbose/streaming output and check for repeated\n   \"Blocking waiting for file lock\" lines, and whether wall-clock time is roughly the *sum* of\n   each crate's individual build time rather than the *max*.\n3. Confirm: kill everything, run one crate's task alone and time it, then run the full fan-out\n   and compare total wall time against (that time) × (crate count). If they're close, this is\n   the bug.\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo changes, not one — they serve different call sites:\n\n1. **Full-scope runs (CI, `just ci`-equivalent):** replace the per-crate fan-out with a single\n   `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` (same pattern for `build`/`test`,\n   though `cargo test --workspace` doesn't run doctests — pair with `cargo test --doc`, or use\n   `cargo nextest run --workspace` and fall back to the runner's own task for coverage it\n   doesn't handle). One process, Cargo's internal job scheduler parallelizes compilation across\n   crates on its own — no lock contention because there's only one lock-holder.\n\n2. **Affected-only runs (pre-push, incremental CI):** don't drop the task runner's affected-\n   project detection — it's real, dependency-graph-aware signal a plain Cargo invocation can't\n   compute on its own. Instead of letting it *execute* per-project (which reintroduces the same\n   lock problem at a smaller scale whenever 2+ projects are affected), use it only to *build the\n   scope*, then feed that into one Cargo invocation with multiple `-p` flags:\n   ```\n   projects=$(<task-runner query for affected project ids>)\n   if [ -z \"$projects\" ]; then exit 0; fi\n   args=(); for p in $projects; do args+=(-p \"$p\"); done\n   cargo clippy \"${args[@]}\" --all-targets -- -D warnings\n   ```\n   For moon specifically: `moon query projects --affected` returns JSON with a `.projects[].id`\n   array of exactly the changed crates (verified: touching two crates' files returns exactly\n   those two project ids, nothing else) — pipe that through `jq -r '.projects[].id'`.\n\nDo not scope lint to affected crates' *downstream dependents* — clippy warnings are about a\ncrate's own source, not its callers, so only the changed crates themselves need relinting. Test\nscoping is a separate, judgment-call question (a changed crate's behavior can break a\ndownstream crate's integration tests) — don't fold that into a lint fix without deciding it\nexplicitly.\n\n## Verify\n\n- Time the old fan-out path once for a real before/after number, not just \"it feels faster.\"\n- Test both the zero-affected case (clean tree → instant no-op) and a multi-affected case\n  (touch 2+ unrelated crates → confirm the resulting single command lints exactly those crates\n  and nothing else) before trusting the fix.\n- Re-run the repo's full CI/lint suite once after the change to confirm nothing else broke.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_read_input_tokens":180793,"output_tokens":2872,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":760},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2872,"cache_read_input_tokens":180793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKwnT2Bp1PXFbDLcRQCj","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b9c899b-0054-4147-b1ad-1eb7b2723824","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:50:38.883Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"5b9c899b-0054-4147-b1ad-1eb7b2723824","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"60ad7ca5-c166-499a-9cd0-eb95ff75a88e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PTtyRR8HX2U8eKh5ZvB8GM","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/cargo-monorepo-lock-fix-prompt.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"fc05c30e-b55b-4b77-ad94-5ccc3d2b67c3","timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:50:39.006Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/cargo-monorepo-lock-fix-prompt.md","content":"Investigate whether this repo has a Cargo-workspace build-lock serialization bug in its\nCI/lint/test task runner (moon, Turborepo, Nx, Makefile, or similar), and fix it if so.\n\n## Background\n\nCargo takes a process-level file lock on a workspace's shared `target/` directory for the\nduration of any `cargo` invocation (build, check, clippy, test) touching it. If a monorepo\ntask runner fans out one `cargo <cmd> -p $crate` invocation per crate — even when it *thinks*\nit's running them in parallel — every one of those processes contends for the same lock, so\nthey serialize behind each other. The task runner's own parallelism is real at the process-\nspawn level; Cargo silently defeats it underneath. Symptom: a lint/build/test step that \"hangs\"\nor takes 10-60+ minutes even though no single crate should take that long, with repeated\n\"Blocking waiting for file lock on build directory\" lines in verbose output — easy to\nmisdiagnose as a hung process, a bad dependency (heavy C-linked crates like aws-lc-sys/ring/\nwasmtime are common red herrings), or a caching bug, when it's actually just N processes\nqueued behind one lock.\n\nThis is a known, acknowledged Cargo/monorepo-tool interaction — moonrepo's own Rust handbook\nstates it explicitly: \"if you do per-crate, Cargo itself will 'wait for build lock' when\nmultiple processes are running,\" and recommends workspace-wide invocations instead.\n\n## Diagnose\n\n1. Find the task definition that runs clippy/build/test per-crate (e.g. a global task template\n   with `-p $project` or equivalent, applied to every package).\n2. Run the full task with verbose/streaming output and check for repeated\n   \"Blocking waiting for file lock\" lines, and whether wall-clock time is roughly the *sum* of\n   each crate's individual build time rather than the *max*.\n3. Confirm: kill everything, run one crate's task alone and time it, then run the full fan-out\n   and compare total wall time against (that time) × (crate count). If they're close, this is\n   the bug.\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo changes, not one — they serve different call sites:\n\n1. **Full-scope runs (CI, `just ci`-equivalent):** replace the per-crate fan-out with a single\n   `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` (same pattern for `build`/`test`,\n   though `cargo test --workspace` doesn't run doctests — pair with `cargo test --doc`, or use\n   `cargo nextest run --workspace` and fall back to the runner's own task for coverage it\n   doesn't handle). One process, Cargo's internal job scheduler parallelizes compilation across\n   crates on its own — no lock contention because there's only one lock-holder.\n\n2. **Affected-only runs (pre-push, incremental CI):** don't drop the task runner's affected-\n   project detection — it's real, dependency-graph-aware signal a plain Cargo invocation can't\n   compute on its own. Instead of letting it *execute* per-project (which reintroduces the same\n   lock problem at a smaller scale whenever 2+ projects are affected), use it only to *build the\n   scope*, then feed that into one Cargo invocation with multiple `-p` flags:\n   ```\n   projects=$(<task-runner query for affected project ids>)\n   if [ -z \"$projects\" ]; then exit 0; fi\n   args=(); for p in $projects; do args+=(-p \"$p\"); done\n   cargo clippy \"${args[@]}\" --all-targets -- -D warnings\n   ```\n   For moon specifically: `moon query projects --affected` returns JSON with a `.projects[].id`\n   array of exactly the changed crates (verified: touching two crates' files returns exactly\n   those two project ids, nothing else) — pipe that through `jq -r '.projects[].id'`.\n\nDo not scope lint to affected crates' *downstream dependents* — clippy warnings are about a\ncrate's own source, not its callers, so only the changed crates themselves need relinting. Test\nscoping is a separate, judgment-call question (a changed crate's behavior can break a\ndownstream crate's integration tests) — don't fold that into a lint fix without deciding it\nexplicitly.\n\n## Verify\n\n- Time the old fan-out path once for a real before/after number, not just \"it feels faster.\"\n- Test both the zero-affected case (clean tree → instant no-op) and a multi-affected case\n  (touch 2+ unrelated crates → confirm the resulting single command lints exactly those crates\n  and nothing else) before trusting the fix.\n- Re-run the repo's full CI/lint suite once after the change to confirm nothing else broke.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b9c899b-0054-4147-b1ad-1eb7b2723824","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
