{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01HxMVynBHufrDkmRHgmKgcH","lastSequenceNum":33570,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"74489285-db82-4249-a0f9-7b199be129a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2a2d3d2e-c4c3-43ec-94da-20c20fca7d57","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013eqCMgr3QKStfExHeUJ4CD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"rust cargo dev profile debug=1 line-tables-only faster clippy test compile speed 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"build: reduce Rust dev debuginfo by bolinfest · Pull Request #18844 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/18844\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing Build Performance - The Cargo Book\",\"url\":\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/build-performance.html\"},{\"title\":\"7. Release Profiles and Binary Size - Rust Engineering Practices — Beyond cargo build\",\"url\":\"https://microsoft.github.io/RustTraining/engineering-book/ch07-release-profiles-and-binary-size.html\"},{\"title\":\"Disable debuginfo to improve Rust compile times | Kobzol’s blog\",\"url\":\"https://kobzol.github.io/rust/rustc/2025/05/20/disable-debuginfo-to-improve-rust-compile-times.html\"},{\"title\":\"Build Configuration - The Rust Performance Book\",\"url\":\"https://nnethercote.github.io/perf-book/build-configuration.html\"},{\"title\":\"Profiles - The Cargo Book\",\"url\":\"https://rustwiki.org/en/cargo/reference/profiles.html\"},{\"title\":\"Profiles - The Cargo Book\",\"url\":\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Kobzol/cargo-wizard/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Keyboard shortcuts\",\"url\":\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/embedded-book/unsorted/speed-vs-size.html\"},{\"title\":\"Keyboard shortcuts\",\"url\":\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/book/ch14-01-release-profiles.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about using Rust Cargo's dev profile with `debug=1` and `line-tables-only` for faster compile speeds:\n\n## Debug Profile Settings for Faster Compilation\n\nThe Cargo Book recommends configuring the dev profile with `debug = \"line-tables-only\"`, which is a compromise between full and no debuginfo. \n\nAccording to OpenAI's Codex project, `debug = 1` is a better default dev tradeoff because it captures nearly all of the compile-time win while preserving basic debuggability. In their testing, setting a package to line-tables-only debug info brought compile times down from about 39.5s to 27.2s wall time.\n\n## Benefits of Line-Tables-Only\n\n\"line-tables-only\" generates the minimal amount of debug info for backtraces with filename/line number info, but not anything else, i.e. no variable or function parameter info. Using `debug = \"line-tables-only\"` still gives most of the compile time benefits, and disabling debuginfo entirely can improve dev build times significantly, by as much as 20-40%.\n\n## Configuration Example\n\nYou can configure this in Cargo.toml with `[profile.dev] debug = \"line-tables-only\"` for a workspace-wide setting that balances debuggability with compile speed improvements.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7561fe5c-1473-49ce-a9fb-95f2a2668f8f","timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:00:38.441Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"rust cargo dev profile debug=1 line-tables-only faster clippy test compile speed 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NDnp5PCfVsw4bF2fbfNekM","content":[{"title":"build: reduce Rust dev debuginfo by bolinfest · Pull Request #18844 · openai/codex","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/18844"},{"title":"Optimizing Build Performance - The Cargo Book","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/build-performance.html"},{"title":"7. Release Profiles and Binary Size - Rust Engineering Practices — Beyond cargo build","url":"https://microsoft.github.io/RustTraining/engineering-book/ch07-release-profiles-and-binary-size.html"},{"title":"Disable debuginfo to improve Rust compile times | Kobzol’s blog","url":"https://kobzol.github.io/rust/rustc/2025/05/20/disable-debuginfo-to-improve-rust-compile-times.html"},{"title":"Build Configuration - The Rust Performance Book","url":"https://nnethercote.github.io/perf-book/build-configuration.html"},{"title":"Profiles - The Cargo Book","url":"https://rustwiki.org/en/cargo/reference/profiles.html"},{"title":"Profiles - The Cargo Book","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html"},{"title":"github.com","url":"https://github.com/Kobzol/cargo-wizard/blob/main/README.md"},{"title":"Keyboard shortcuts","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/embedded-book/unsorted/speed-vs-size.html"},{"title":"Keyboard shortcuts","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/book/ch14-01-release-profiles.html"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about using Rust Cargo's dev profile with `debug=1` and `line-tables-only` for faster compile speeds:\n\n## Debug Profile Settings for Faster Compilation\n\nThe Cargo Book recommends configuring the dev profile with `debug = \"line-tables-only\"`, which is a compromise between full and no debuginfo. \n\nAccording to OpenAI's Codex project, `debug = 1` is a better default dev tradeoff because it captures nearly all of the compile-time win while preserving basic debuggability. In their testing, setting a package to line-tables-only debug info brought compile times down from about 39.5s to 27.2s wall time.\n\n## Benefits of Line-Tables-Only\n\n\"line-tables-only\" generates the minimal amount of debug info for backtraces with filename/line number info, but not anything else, i.e. no variable or function parameter info. Using `debug = \"line-tables-only\"` still gives most of the compile time benefits, and disabling debuginfo entirely can improve dev build times significantly, by as much as 20-40%.\n\n## Configuration Example\n\nYou can configure this in Cargo.toml with `[profile.dev] debug = \"line-tables-only\"` for a workspace-wide setting that balances debuggability with compile speed improvements."],"durationSeconds":7.877767457991839,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"74489285-db82-4249-a0f9-7b199be129a2","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
