{"parentUuid":"4d386c6b-ffaa-43a6-8f7d-13c5332050cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKxdpmFmSA5Eer383bxg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":200471,"output_tokens":3717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2623},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3717,"cache_read_input_tokens":200471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKxdnQcweZoseZQ7HxtY","type":"assistant","uuid":"3173404c-93f4-49f4-a56c-8426841591b0","timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:01:49.599Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"docs-cleanup-rust-comments","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3173404c-93f4-49f4-a56c-8426841591b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeKxdpmFmSA5Eer383bxg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pulled together concrete findings from this repo (not generic advice) — the `just ci` test run is still churning through 1055 tests (roughly on pace, nothing alarming — the ~69s-labeled tests are almost certainly nextest's elapsed-since-start clock for a 1055-test/47-binary suite bound to this machine's 12 cores, not per-test slowness; fast tests are interleaved right alongside them at 0.4-3s).\n\n**Ranked by expected impact, all verified against this repo's actual config:**\n\n1. **`[profile.dev] debug = \"line-tables-only\"`** — no `[profile.dev]` override exists in `Cargo.toml` today; every dev/test/clippy build (confirmed: `-C debuginfo=2` in the clippy invocations I captured earlier) uses full debug info. This is the single highest-leverage remaining change — it applies to *every* build we just optimized, not just lint. Documented 20-40% compile-time reduction ([Rust Perf Book](https://nnethercote.github.io/perf-book/build-configuration.html), [Kobzol's writeup](https://kobzol.github.io/rust/rustc/2025/05/20/disable-debuginfo-to-improve-rust-compile-times.html), and a [real OpenAI Codex PR](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/18844) measuring 39.5s→27.2s on one crate from this exact change). You keep file/line info for panics/backtraces, lose variable-level debug info you're unlikely to use outside an actual debugger session.\n\n2. **No linker override anywhere** — no `.cargo/config.toml` exists. With 47 separate test binaries (39 integration-test files + per-crate unit binaries) all linking against heavy deps (gix, wasmtime, aws-lc-sys), final linking is a real cost. Setting `lld` (or `mold` specifically for the Linux CI runners, where it has the biggest win — mold doesn't support macOS) via `rustflags` would help most in CI's `ubuntu-latest` job; smaller but real gains locally on macOS too.\n\n3. **CI caching is already good** — `.github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml` already uses `Swatinem/rust-cache@v2` on the clippy/test/coverage jobs. Nothing to fix there; just noting it so it's not accidentally duplicated or second-guessed.\n\n4. **nextest has no CI-side sharding** — the `test` job runs the full 1055-test suite serially per OS (ubuntu + macos matrix), no `--partition` sharding within an OS. Not needed yet at this suite size, but it's the standard next lever if wall-clock on that job becomes a pain point.\n\n5. **Worth being explicit about a tradeoff from the fix already shipped**: `lint`/`test` are now raw `cargo`/`nextest` invocations in the justfile, not moon tasks — so moon's own hash-based task caching no longer gates them. That's fine in practice (Cargo's own incremental engine already gave us a 1.00s no-op re-check), but it's a real, conscious tradeoff, not a hidden regression.\n\nWant me to implement #1 and #2 (the two concrete, low-risk config additions)? Those are the ones with measured payoff and no architectural downside."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":200471,"output_tokens":3717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2623},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3717,"cache_read_input_tokens":200471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeKxdnQcweZoseZQ7HxtY","type":"assistant","uuid":"77afc712-947a-4453-9685-59531f43505f","timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:02:01.537Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e0