{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:22:00.698Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"Check background task belfx2fxb (rerun of `callisto-moon::moon_wasm_sandbox::register_extension_matches_moon_wire_protocol` in isolation, output at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/belfx2fxb.output). It's compiling the heavy moon_wasm_sandbox test target (wasmtime/aws-lc-sys/ring deps) — confirmed genuinely progressing via ps (rustc PID 64784 had 5.81s CPU accumulated as of last check), not stalled. Also note there's a leftover `cargo clippy --workspace` process (PID 32637, started 9:05AM) from the earlier `moon run root:lint-workspace` test (task bpvlqquvi) that appears idle at 0.0% CPU — check if that task ever completed and report its result too if not already reported.\n\nContext recap: full `just ci` run had 1054/1055 tests pass, exactly one failure: callisto-moon::moon_wasm_sandbox::register_extension_matches_moon_wire_protocol. Determining now whether it's a real bug or a flake (nextest.toml already forces this test binary to run single-threaded due to shared global WasmHost state, so a failure even in isolated single-test reruns would indicate a REAL bug, not a concurrency flake). Also separately fixed a root-project moon.yml task-inheritance regression from prototyping Option B (workspace-wide moon-cached lint task) — root project's moon.yml now has `workspace: {inheritedTasks: {include: []}}` confirmed via `moon query tasks` to only have the explicit `lint-workspace` task.\n\nOnce belfx2fxb completes, report to the user: (1) exact pass/fail and assertion failure detail for the isolated rerun — is it real or flaky; (2) status of the root:lint-workspace caching prototype (task bpvlqquvi) if it finished — did a second run show `(cached, ...)`; (3) confirm `moon run :test` and `moon run :lint` no longer error on `root:test`/`root:lint` (the bug that broke just ci) by running them directly; (4) give a final recommendation on adopting Option B given all this; (5) ask whether to commit everything now, and whether the wasm sandbox test failure (if real) should be fixed first or tracked separately."}
