{"parentUuid":"47b37775-fd2b-4d62-8bd2-33d13cb6b5e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeL3ZRMZUREFKcYPsz19f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YAoL329fmyizbC5B2z9wew","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add justfile\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(build): stop moon lint from serializing per-crate cargo invocations\n\nmoon run :lint fanned out one `cargo clippy -p $project` process per crate,\nall sharing one workspace target/ dir. Cargo's own build-lock serializes any\ntwo processes touching that dir, so the \"parallel\" moon task graph was\nactually a chain of 10 sequential cargo invocations end to end (measured\n~63 minutes on this repo). A single `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets`\ninvocation lets Cargo's own job scheduler parallelize across crates instead\n(measured 5m13s clean).\n\npre-push now uses a new lint-affected recipe: query moon's project graph for\ncrates affected since the base branch, then lint just those in one cargo\ninvocation, keeping moon's dependency-aware change detection without\nreintroducing the per-crate lock contention.\nEOF\n)\"\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":274902,"output_tokens":367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":274902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeL3ZPm541ZzGHyF5C1W1","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c38e7bf-51d1-49ee-