{"parentUuid":"cea8a743-8f30-4a58-aa1d-5b8aa77c57ca","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs","snippet":"1\tuse std::collections::HashSet;\n2\t\n3\tuse callisto_model::{\n4\t    CommandRunner, CratePublish, DepKind, NpmMainPublish, PackageId, PublishPlan, PublishTarget,\n5\t    PypiPublish, RegistryKey, ReleaseEntry, SCHEMA_VERSION,\n6\t};\n7\tuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\n8\t\n9\tuse crate::error::GraphError;\n10\tuse crate::resolver::DependencyResolver;\n11\tuse crate::toposort::toposort_impl;\n12\tuse crate::Workspace;\n13\t\n14\t/// Edge kinds cascade/version-bump propagation cares about: a `Dev`-only\n15\t/// dependency change correctly never forces a consumer's version to bump.\n16\tconst CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[DepKind::Runtime, DepKind::Build, DepKind::Optional];\n17\t\n18\t/// Edge kinds publish ordering cares about: cascade's kinds, plus `Dev`.\n19\t/// `cargo publish` (run without `--no-verify`, see `publish_client.rs`)\n20\t/// re-extracts the packaged tarball and does a real local build to verify\n21\t/// it, which needs *every* dependency in the crate's `Cargo.toml` —\n22\t/// `[dev-dependencies]` included — resolvable from the registry. A\n23\t/// dev-dependency on a workspace sibling published in the same batch\n24\t/// therefore still needs that sibling to publish first, even though the\n25\t/// two crates have no cascade-relevant ordering constraint between them.\n26\tconst PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS: &[DepKind] = &[\n27\t    DepKind::Runtime,\n28\t    DepKind::Build,\n29\t    DepKind::Optional,\n30\t    DepKind::Dev,\n31\t];\n32\t\n33\t/// Computes the order packages must be published in.\n34\t///\n35\t/// This is a thin, purpose-named wrapper around [`toposort_impl`] (the\n36\t/// generic algorithm, reused as-is) rather than a generic\n37\t/// `DependencyResolverExt::toposort()` on a shared trait — it exists\n38\t/// specifically for `plan_publish` below, its only caller, and its\n39\t/// semantics are publish-specific, not \"the one true topological sort.\"\n40\t///\n41\t/// Tries [`PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS`] first (including `Dev`, unlike cascade's\n42\t/// own [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`]) so a dev-dependency on a same-batch\n43\t/// sibling publishes in the right order. `Dev` edges are best-effort, not a\n44\t/// hard requirement, precisely because mutual dev-only dependencies between\n45\t/// two otherwise-unrelated packages are a legitimate pattern (e.g. two\n46\t/// crates each dev-depending on the other for cross-integration tests) —\n47\t/// unlike `Runtime`/`Build`/`Optional`, which must never cycle, a `Dev`\n48\t/// cycle must not hard-fail the whole publish plan. If including `Dev`\n49\t/// edges would produce a cycle, this falls back to\n50\t/// [`CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`] alone, which is guaranteed not to introduce a\n51\t/// *new* cycle here since it is a strict subset of the edges just proven\n52\t/// cyclic — accepting the original race this function exists to close for\n53\t/// that one pair, rather than failing the entire plan over it.\n54\tfn publish_order<D: DependencyResolver + ?Sized>(\n55\t    resolver: &D,\n56\t    subset: &HashSet<PackageId>,\n57\t) -> Result<Vec<PackageId>, GraphError> {\n58\t    let all_pkg_ids: Vec<PackageId> = resolver.packages().map(|p| p.id.clone()).collect();\n59\t    let edges_of = |id: &PackageId| -> Vec<(PackageId, DepKind)> {\n60\t        resolver\n61\t            .dependencies_of(id)\n62\t            .map(|e| (e.to.clone(), e.kind))\n63\t            .collect()\n64\t    };\n65\t\n66\t    match toposort_impl(subset, &all_pkg_ids, PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS, edges_of) {\n67\t        Ok(order) => Ok(order),\n68\t        Err(GraphError::Cycle { .. }) => {\n69\t            toposort_impl(subset, &all_pkg_ids, CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS, edges_of)\n70\t        }\n71\t        Err(e) => Err(e),\n72\t    }\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]\n76\tpub struct PublishOptions {\n77\t    /// When non-empty, only packages whose bare name (without ecosystem prefix)\n78\t    /// appears in this list are included in the plan. An empty `only` list\n79\t    /// means \"include all packages\" (the default).\n80\t    pub only: Vec<String>,\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\t/// Validates a `publishConfig.registry` URL from a package's own\n84\t/// `package.json` before it's used as an `npm publish --registry`/`npm\n85\t/// view --registry` target (both run with `NPM_TOKEN` live in CI).\n86\t///\n87\t/// `publishConfig.registry` is attacker-controllable (a PR author sets\n88\t/// their own `package.json`) and must never be trusted verbatim. Two\n89\t/// checks, mirroring the leading-`-` flag-injection guard on package names\n90\t/// (see `SubprocessRegistryClient::npm_publish`):\n91\t///\n92\t/// 1. Must use `https` -- a scheme downgrade is rejected even if the host\n93\t///    would otherwise be approved.\n94\t/// 2. Must exactly match a `url` on an `npm`-kind entry in\n95\t///    `callisto.toml`'s `[registries]` table.\n96\t///\n97\t/// No configured npm registries means no override is ever approved --\n98\t/// `callisto.toml`, not `package.json`, is the source of truth for where\n99\t/// credentialed publish requests can go.\n100\tfn validate_npm_registry_url(\n101\t    url: &str,\n102\t    package: &PackageId,\n103\t    registries: &std::collections::BTreeMap<RegistryKey, crate::config::RegistryConfig>,\n104\t) -> Result<(), GraphError> {\n105\t    let is_approved = url.starts_with(\"https://\")\n106\t        && registries\n107\t            .values()\n108\t            .any(|cfg| cfg.kind == Ecosystem::Npm && cfg.url.as_deref() == Some(url));\n109\t\n110\t    if is_approved {\n111\t        Ok(())\n112\t    } else {\n113\t        Err(GraphError::UntrustedNpmRegistry {\n114\t            package: package.clone(),\n115\t            url: url.to_string(),\n116\t        })\n117\t    }\n118\t}\n119\t\n120\t/// Resolves a package's `changelog_section` for `plan_publish`: reads the file at\n121\t/// `ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path)` and extracts the `## {ver}` section via\n122\t/// `callisto_changelog::extract_section`. Every non-fatal outcome (file not found, no\n123\t/// matching heading, empty matched section, or an unreadable file) leaves the return value\n124\t/// `None` and pushes exactly one Warning diagnostic into `diagnostics` rather than aborting\n125\t/// the plan -- `ChangelogSectionNotFound` for the first three (AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12),\n126\t/// `ChangelogReadError` for a read failure that is not \"file does not exist\" (AC-12c).\n127\tfn resolve_changelog_section(\n128\t    ws_root: &std::path::Path,\n129\t    changelog_rel_path: &std::path::Path,\n130\t    pkg_id: &callisto_model::PackageId,\n131\t    ver: &callisto_model::Version,\n132\t    diagnostics: &mut Vec<callisto_model::Diagnostic>,\n133\t) -> Option<String> {\n134\t    let full_path = ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path);\n135\t    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n136\t        Ok(c) => c,\n137\t        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {\n138\t            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n139\t                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound,\n140\t                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n141\t                message: format!(\n142\t                    \"no changelog file found at `{}` for package `{}`\",\n143\t                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\n144\t                    pkg_id.display_name()\n145\t                ),\n146\t                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\n147\t                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\n148\t                escalated_by: None,\n149\t                governed_by: None,\n150\t            });\n151\t            return None;\n152\t        }\n153\t        Err(e) => {\n154\t            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n155\t                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError,\n156\t                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n157\t                message: format!(\n158\t                    \"could not read changelog at `{}` for package `{}`: {e}\",\n159\t                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\n160\t                    pkg_id.display_name()\n161\t                ),\n162\t                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\n163\t                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\n164\t                escalated_by: None,\n165\t                governed_by: None,\n166\t            });\n167\t            return None;\n168\t        }\n169\t    };\n170\t\n171\t    match callisto_changelog::extract_section(&content, ver) {\n\n... [1365 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"53b1bda7-9ed6-4111-8185-60c2e0a13962","timestamp":"2026-08-23T20:08:32.153Z","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"fix-publish-order-dev-deps","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
