{"parentUuid":"808ab1ab-fd29-46df-81b2-a6d22fd585c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeLMeCXd4C6vFMUu7fVMi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"With PR #10 and #11 merged, every track in **Phase 1-3** of the project's remediation plan (`.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md`) is now done — Track 3a/3b1, Track 1, Track 2, Track 9, Track 4, Track 6-mechanical, Track 5, plus the doc-only fixes. That leaves **Phase 4** as the next work, and I just confirmed its headline item is still genuinely open in the code:\n\n**Track 7 — git revwalk bounding & redundant I/O** (highest value, ready to start). `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:312`) still does two full *unbounded* `rev_walk(...).all()` calls per package — one from HEAD, one from `since` — then set-difference-excludes, exactly as the original audit measured (~2.05s vs ~13ms, >99% wasted work at 100 packages/50k commits). A correctness bug in this same function (branchy-history drop) was fixed separately, but the performance rewrite to `gix`'s actual bounded-walk API hasn't happened. Also in scope: `TagIndex::build`'s per-package glob recompile (~640ms wasted at 1000 packages/41k tags), and a few smaller redundant-manifest-reread findings.\n\nTwo smaller, parallelizable items round out Phase 4: **Track 8-mechanical** (unused `ConfigError` variants, missing Python workspace-root detection) and **Track 11/12** (diagnostic polish, stale spec citations) — both lighter-touch, no shared files with Track 7.\n\nPhase 5 (a real `moon.yml extensions.callisto` feature, and test/fixture infrastructure buildout) stays deliberately deferred — those are scoping conversations, not ready work.\n\nWant me to start Track 7?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1260,"cache_read_input_tokens":333028,"output_tokens":1053,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":436},