{"parentUuid":"c4ee6492-be09-4278-a285-f114049bb0df","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5d2ed6d4-877a-41af-bc78-85c57a8dc786","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C533t4AxiXjfR4yTXHEJUt","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/track7-prompt.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"1b652368-51c6-483d-91c5-aef9aba0b74c","timestamp":"2026-08-23T21:10:53.050Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/track7-prompt.md","content":"Continue the callisto release-engineering remediation plan at `.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md` — read it\nfirst for full history and conventions. Every track through Phase 3 is done (Track 3a/3b1, 1, 2, 9,\n4, 6-mechanical, 5). This session picks up **Track 7 — git revwalk bounding & redundant I/O**, the\nnext item in Phase 4 of the plan file loaded at session start (`.claude/plans/shimmying-giggling-hickey.md`\nif still present, or ask the user for it — otherwise the scope below is self-contained).\n\nTier: **lighter TDD loop, one finding per commit** (red test confirmed failing → minimal fix → green\n→ independent read-only review agent, explicitly told not to run destructive git commands → full\n`just ci` → commit). Do not batch unrelated findings into one commit. This matches how Track 9 and\nTrack 6-mechanical were done — see ACTIVE.md for the exact precedent.\n\n## Findings, verified live in code as of 2026-08-23 (re-verify before trusting further — code may\nhave moved)\n\n**1. Unbounded double revwalk — `crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:312`,\n`commits_since_with_pathspec`.** Confirmed still doing two full, unbounded `rev_walk(...).all()`\ncalls: one from HEAD, one from `since`, then building a `HashSet` of the `since`-reachable side and\nfiltering by exclusion. This walks the *entire* repo history every time regardless of how close\n`since` is to HEAD. Original audit measured ~2.05s vs ~13ms (100 packages/50k commits) — over 99%\nwasted work. `gix` exposes a real bounded-walk API (stop the HEAD walk once every commit reachable\nfrom `since` has been excluded, rather than walking to the repo's first commit) — use it instead of\nthe two-full-walks-then-exclude approach.\n\nImportant: a separate correctness bug in this exact function (a `break` vs `continue` bug losing\ncommits from branchy history — see the comment already in the function and commit `7e3391bc`) is\n**already fixed**. Don't re-litigate it — but the bounded-walk rewrite must preserve that fix's\ninvariant (topological walk can visit `since` before emitting all in-queue commits on branches that\ndiverged before it), which is exactly why the original audit flagged this as needing an independent\nreview + before/after re-measurement pass rather than a naive bound. Get a second pair of eyes\n(review agent) specifically on this invariant before merging.\n\n**2. Per-package glob-matcher recompile — `crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs`, `matching_tags`\n(called from `select_from_tags`, called once per package in `TagIndex::build`'s loop).** The tag\n*list fetch* itself was already deduplicated in a prior session (`fetch_all_tags` is called once for\nthe whole build, not per package — see the comment at `tags.rs:111-118`). What's still live: every\ncall to `matching_tags` compiles a fresh `globset::Glob::new(...).compile_matcher()` and does a full\nlinear scan of the shared tag list, once per package. At 1000 packages / 41k tags the original audit\nmeasured ~640ms wasted here. Fix: compile each package's glob matcher once (or cache by template\nstring, since multiple packages may share a template) rather than per package per build.\n\n**3. Commit-inference pathspec bug — `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:177`.** Confirmed:\npathspecs passed to inference are built from `pkg.manifests.iter().map(|m| m.path.clone())` — the\nmanifest *file* path (e.g. `crates/foo/Cargo.toml`), not the package's source *directory*. This means\ncommit-based inference only ever matches commits that touch the manifest file itself, never real\nsource changes under the package directory — making the `inference` feature a near-total no-op for\nits actual purpose. Fix the pathspec to cover the package's directory (mirroring how\n`commits_since_with_pathspec`'s other callers scope pathspecs), regardless of whether `inference`\nbecomes default-on (that's a separate, deliberately-unresolved product decision — don't touch feature\ndefaults as part of this fix).\n\n## Not yet re-verified this session — check before acting, may be stale\n\n- Workspace-root `Cargo.toml` read up to 3× per command; npm/cargo manifests re-read 2-3× per graph\n  build (redundant I/O, smaller than findings 1-2 above).\n- Explicitly out of scope regardless: Cargo workspace-inherited dependency rewrites bypassing\n  write-batching is a known, deliberately-deferred prior design decision (see Spec A/Spec B in\n  ACTIVE.md) — don't re-plan it, just don't touch it.\n\n## Process\n\n1. Re-verify each finding against current code before starting (line numbers drift).\n2. One finding, one red test, one fix, one commit — in the order listed above (1 and 2 are\n   independent of each other; 3 is independent of both).\n3. For finding 1 specifically: get an independent review pass on the branchy-history invariant\n   before considering it done, and re-measure before/after (packages/commits/tags counts matching\n   the original audit's methodology if possible, so the improvement is a real number, not a guess).\n4. `just ci` must pass clean before any commit.\n5. Update `.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md` with Track 7's outcome when done, matching the existing\n   Track 9 / Track 6-mechanical entry format (what was found, what was fixed, commits, measured\n   before/after where applicable).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c4ee6492-be09-4278-a285-f114049bb0df","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
